    (39, 'ruby', 'Jigglypuff''s vocal chords can freely adjust the wavelength of its voice. This {{ScPkmn}} uses this ability to sing at precisely the right wavelength to make its foes most drowsy.'),
    (39, 'sapphire', 'When this {{ScPkmn}} sings, it never pauses to breathe. If it is in a battle against an opponent that does not easily fall asleep, Jigglypuff cannot breathe, endangering its life.'),
    (39, 'scarlet', 'When its huge eyes waver, it sings a mysteriously soothing melody that lulls its enemies to sleep.'),
    (39, 'shield', 'By freely changing the wavelength of its voice, Jigglypuff sings a mysterious melody sure to make any listener sleepy.'),
    (39, 'shining-pearl', 'When it wavers its big, round eyes, it begins singing a lullaby that makes everyone drowsy.'),
    (39, 'silver', 'Looking into its cute, round eyes causes it to sing a relaxing melody, inducing its enemies to sleep.'),
    (39, 'soulsilver', 'Looking into its cute, round eyes causes it to sing a relaxing melody, inducing its enemies to sleep.'),
    (39, 'sun', 'It hugely inflates its stomach and sings a mysterious melody. If you hear this melody, you''ll become sleepy right away.'),
    (39, 'sword', 'Jigglypuff has top-notch lung capacity, even by comparison to other Pokémon. It won''t stop singing its lullabies until its foes fall asleep.'),
    (39, 'ultra-moon', 'The songs they sing are totally different depending on the region they live in. Some even sound like they''re shouting!'),
    (39, 'ultra-sun', 'Recordings of Jigglypuff''s strange lullabies can be purchased from department stores. These CDs can be found near the bedding area.'),
    (39, 'violet', 'If it inflates to sing a lullaby, it can perform longer and cause sure drowsiness in its audience.'),
