    (55, 'alpha-sapphire', 'Golduck is the fastest swimmer among all Pokémon. It swims effortlessly, even in a rough, stormy sea. It sometimes rescues people from wrecked ships floundering in high seas.'),
    (55, 'black', 'It is seen swimming dynamically and elegantly using its well-developed limbs and flippers.'),
    (55, 'black-2', 'When its forehead shines mysteriously, Golduck can use the full extent of its power.'),
    (55, 'blue', 'Often seen swimming elegantly by lake shores. It is often mistaken for the Japanese monster, {{wp|Kappa (folklore)|Kappa}}.'),
    (55, 'brilliant-diamond', 'This Pokémon lives in lakes. It swims faster than any world-class swimmer.'),
    (55, 'crystal', 'It swims gracefully along on the quiet, slow-moving rivers and lakes of which it is so fond.'),
    (55, 'diamond', 'A Pokémon that lives in lakes. It swims faster than any human swimming champion.'),
    (55, 'emerald', 'A Golduck is an adept swimmer. It sometimes joins competitive swimmers in training. It uses psychic powers when its forehead shimmers with light.'),
    (55, 'firered', 'The forelegs are webbed, helping to make it an adept swimmer. It can be seen swimming elegantly in lakes, etc.'),
    (55, 'gold', 'When it swims at full speed using its long, webbed limbs, its forehead somehow begins to glow.'),
    (55, 'heartgold', 'When it swims at full speed using its long, webbed limbs, its forehead somehow begins to glow.'),
    (55, 'leafgreen', 'Often seen swimming elegantly by lakeshores. It is often mistaken for the Japanese monster Kappa.'),
    (55, 'legends-arceus', 'Its body is strong, and it has webbing on its hands and feet. Golduck can swim easily through rough seas, clawing its way through the high waves.'),
    (55, 'moon', 'It swims along the banks of lakes and catches fish Pokémon. It takes them to the shore and quietly eats them up.'),
    (55, 'omega-ruby', 'The webbed flippers on its forelegs and hind legs and the streamlined body of Golduck give it frightening speed. This Pokémon is definitely much faster than even the most athletic swimmer.'),
    (55, 'pearl', 'The flippers of its well-developed limbs give it shocking speed. It is the best swimmer among Pokémon.'),
    (55, 'platinum', 'It is seen swimming dynamically and elegantly using its well-developed limbs and flippers.'),
    (55, 'red', 'Often seen swimming elegantly by lake shores. It is often mistaken for the Japanese monster, {{wp|Kappa (folklore)|Kappa}}.'),
    (55, 'ruby', 'The webbed flippers on its forelegs and hind legs and the streamlined body of Golduck give it frightening speed. This {{ScPkmn}} is definitely much faster than even the most athletic swimmer.'),
    (55, 'sapphire', 'Golduck is the fastest swimmer among all {{ScPkmn}}. It swims effortlessly, even in a rough, stormy sea. It sometimes rescues people from wrecked ships floundering in high seas.'),
