    (72, 'yellow', 'It can sometimes be found all dry and shriveled up on a beach. Toss it back into the sea to revive it.'),
    (73, 'alpha-sapphire', 'Tentacruel has tentacles that can be freely elongated and shortened at will. It ensnares prey with its tentacles and weakens the prey by dosing it with a harsh toxin. It can catch up to 80 prey at the same time.'),
    (73, 'black', 'It extends its 80 tentacles to form an encircling poisonous net that is difficult to escape.'),
    (73, 'black-2', 'It extends its 80 tentacles to form an encircling poisonous net that is difficult to escape.'),
    (73, 'blue', 'The tentacles are normally kept short. On hunts, they are extended to ensnare and immobilize prey.'),
    (73, 'brilliant-diamond', 'With 80 tentacles for ensnaring victims, it prevents escape until the prey is weakened by poison.'),
    (73, 'crystal', 'When its 80 feelers absorb water, it stretches to become like a net to entangle its prey.'),
    (73, 'diamond', 'With 80 tentacles for ensnaring victims, it prevents escape until the prey is weakened by poison.'),
    (73, 'emerald', 'It lives in complex rock formations on the ocean floor and traps prey using its 80 tentacles. Its red orbs glow when it grows excited or agitated.'),
    (73, 'firered', 'It has 80 tentacles that move about freely. They can sting, causing poisoning and sharp, stabbing pain.'),
    (73, 'gold', 'Its 80 tentacles absorb water and stretch almost endlessly to Constrict its prey and enemies.'),
    (73, 'heartgold', 'Its 80 tentacles absorb water and stretch almost endlessly to constrict its prey and enemies.'),
    (73, 'leafgreen', 'The tentacles are normally kept short. On hunts, they are extended to ensnare and immobilize prey.'),
    (73, 'legends-arceus', 'It has 80 tentacles, each with a venomous tip. These tentacles are also extendible, lengthening when Tentacruel attempts to catch prey. Use caution.'),
    (73, 'moon', 'Although these Pokémon are rare, when a large outbreak of them occurs, all fish Pokémon disappear from the surrounding sea.'),
    (73, 'omega-ruby', 'Tentacruel has large red orbs on its head. The orbs glow before lashing the vicinity with a harsh ultrasonic blast. This Pokémon''s outburst creates rough waves around it.'),
    (73, 'pearl', 'It alerts others to danger by stridently flashing the red orbs on its head.'),
    (73, 'platinum', 'It extends its 80 tentacles to form an encircling poisonous net that is difficult to escape.'),
    (73, 'red', 'The tentacles are normally kept short. On hunts, they are extended to ensnare and immobilize prey.'),
    (73, 'ruby', 'Tentacruel has large red orbs on its head. The orbs glow before lashing the vicinity with a harsh ultrasonic blast. This {{ScPkmn}}''s outburst creates rough waves around it.'),
    (73, 'sapphire', 'Tentacruel has tentacles that can be freely elongated and shortened at will. It ensnares prey with its tentacles and weakens the prey by dosing it with a harsh toxin. It can catch up to 80 prey at the same time.'),
    (73, 'scarlet', 'On the rare occasions that large outbreaks of Tentacruel occur, all fish Pokémon disappear from the surrounding sea.'),
    (73, 'shield', 'Its 80 tentacles can stretch and shrink freely. Tentacruel ensnares prey in a net of spread-out tentacles, delivering venomous stings to its catch.'),
    (73, 'shining-pearl', 'It alerts others to danger by stridently flashing the red orbs on its head.'),
