    (74, 'alpha-sapphire', 'When Geodude sleeps deeply, it buries itself halfway into the ground. It will not awaken even if hikers step on it unwittingly. In the morning, this Pokémon rolls downhill in search of food.'),
    (74, 'black', 'At rest, it looks just like a rock. Carelessly stepping on it will make it swing its fists angrily.'),
    (74, 'black-2', 'At rest, it looks just like a rock. Carelessly stepping on it will make it swing its fists angrily.'),
    (74, 'blue', 'Found in fields and mountains. Mistaking them for boulders, people often step or trip on them.'),
    (74, 'crystal', 'Proud of their sturdy bodies, they bash against each other in a contest to prove whose is harder.'),
    (74, 'diamond', 'Many live on mountain trails and remain half buried while keeping an eye on climbers.'),
    (74, 'emerald', 'It climbs mountain paths using only the power of its arms. Because they look just like boulders lining paths, hikers may step on them without noticing.'),
    (74, 'firered', 'Its round form makes it easy to pick up. Some people have used them to hurl at each other in a snowball fight.'),
    (74, 'gold', 'Most people may not notice, but a closer look should reveal that there are many Geodude around.'),
    (74, 'heartgold', 'Most people may not notice, but a closer look should reveal that there are many Geodude around.'),
    (74, 'leafgreen', 'Found in fields and mountains. Mistaking them for boulders, people often step or trip on them.'),
    (74, 'moon', 'There are plenty of them to be found along any road. A scholar with too much free time once counted a hundred of them along a single route.'),
    (74, 'omega-ruby', 'The longer a Geodude lives, the more its edges are chipped and worn away, making it more rounded in appearance. However, this Pokémon''s heart will remain hard, craggy, and rough always.'),
    (74, 'pearl', 'It is impossible to distinguish from rocks. It slams against others in contests of hardness.'),
    (74, 'platinum', 'At rest, it looks just like a rock. Carelessly stepping on it will make it swing its fists angrily.'),
    (74, 'red', 'Found in fields and mountains. Mistaking them for boulders, people often step or trip on them.'),
    (74, 'ruby', 'The longer a Geodude lives, the more its edges are chipped and worn away, making it more rounded in appearance. However, this {{ScPkmn}}''s heart will remain hard, craggy, and rough always.'),
    (74, 'sapphire', 'When Geodude sleeps deeply, it buries itself halfway into the ground. It will not awaken even if hikers step on it unwittingly. In the morning, this {{ScPkmn}} rolls downhill in search of food.'),
    (74, 'silver', 'It uses its arms to steadily climb steep mountain paths. It swings its fists around if angered.'),
    (74, 'soulsilver', 'It uses its arms to steadily climb steep mountain paths. It swings its fists around if angered.'),
    (74, 'sun', 'Its round body makes it easy to pick up, but it is hard and heavy. It''s dangerous to play with them as if they were snowballs.'),
    (74, 'ultra-moon', 'It uses both hands to climb precipitous cliffs. People who see it in action have been known to take up bouldering.'),
    (74, 'ultra-sun', 'Geodude that have lived a long life have had all their edges smoothed out until they''re totally round. They also have a calm, quiet disposition.'),
    (74, 'white', 'At rest, it looks just like a rock. Carelessly stepping on it will make it swing its fists angrily.'),
    (74, 'white-2', 'At rest, it looks just like a rock. Carelessly stepping on it will make it swing its fists angrily.'),
    (74, 'x', 'Found in fields and mountains. Mistaking them for boulders, people often step or trip on them.'),
    (74, 'y', 'It is impossible to distinguish from rocks. It slams against others in contests of hardness.'),
    (74, 'yellow', 'Commonly found near mountain trails, etc. If you step on one by accident, it gets angry.'),
    (75, 'alpha-sapphire', 'Rocks are Graveler''s favorite food. This Pokémon will climb a mountain from the base to the summit, crunchingly feasting on rocks all the while. Upon reaching the peak, it rolls back down to the bottom.'),
    (75, 'black', 'It rolls on mountain paths to move. Once it builds momentum, no Pokémon can stop it without difficulty.'),
    (75, 'black-2', 'It rolls on mountain paths to move. Once it builds momentum, no Pokémon can stop it without difficulty.'),
    (75, 'blue', 'Rolls down slopes to move. It rolls over any obstacle without slowing or changing its direction.'),
    (75, 'crystal', 'It travels by rolling on mountain paths. If it gains too much speed, it stops by running into huge rocks.'),
    (75, 'diamond', 'Graveler make their homes on sheer cliff faces by gouging out numerous horizontal holes.'),
    (75, 'emerald', 'They descend from mountains by tumbling down steep slopes. They are so brutal, they smash aside obstructing trees and massive boulders with thunderous tackles.'),
    (75, 'firered', 'Be careful while hiking on mountain trails. Graveler may come rolling down the path without slowing.'),
    (75, 'gold', 'With a free and uncaring nature, it doesn''t mind if pieces break off while it rolls down mountains.'),
    (75, 'heartgold', 'With a free and uncaring nature, it doesn''t mind if pieces break off while it rolls down mountains.'),
    (75, 'leafgreen', 'Rolls down slopes to move. It rolls over any obstacle without slowing or changing its direction.'),
    (75, 'moon', 'This slow-footed Pokémon moves by curling up and rolling instead of walking. With enough momentum, its speed can exceed 60 mph.'),
    (75, 'omega-ruby', 'Graveler grows by feeding on rocks. Apparently, it prefers to eat rocks that are covered in moss. This Pokémon eats its way through a ton of rocks on a daily basis.'),
    (75, 'pearl', 'It tumbles down slopes, heedless of any body parts chipping off. It eats a ton of rocks daily.'),
    (75, 'platinum', 'It rolls on mountain paths to move. Once it builds momentum, no {{OBP|Pokémon|species}} can stop it without difficulty.'),
    (75, 'red', 'Rolls down slopes to move. It rolls over any obstacle without slowing or changing its direction.'),
    (75, 'ruby', 'Graveler grows by feeding on rocks. Apparently, it prefers to eat rocks that are covered in moss. This {{ScPkmn}} eats its way through a ton of rocks on a daily basis.'),
    (75, 'sapphire', 'Rocks are Graveler''s favorite food. This {{ScPkmn}} will climb a mountain from the base to the summit, crunchingly feasting on rocks all the while. Upon reaching the peak, it rolls back down to the bottom.'),
    (75, 'silver', 'A slow walker, it rolls to move. It pays no attention to any object that happens to be in its path.'),
    (75, 'soulsilver', 'A slow walker, it rolls to move. It pays no attention to any object that happens to be in its path.'),
    (75, 'sun', 'Mossy rocks are its favorite food. It can devour a ton a day while crunching loudly.'),
    (75, 'ultra-moon', 'It travels by rolling down cliffs. If it falls into a river, it will Explosion with its last gasp.'),
    (75, 'ultra-sun', 'It climbs up cliffs as it heads toward the peak of a mountain. As soon as it reaches the summit, it rolls back down the way it came.'),
    (75, 'white', 'It rolls on mountain paths to move. Once it builds momentum, no Pokémon can stop it without difficulty.'),
    (75, 'white-2', 'It rolls on mountain paths to move. Once it builds momentum, no Pokémon can stop it without difficulty.'),
    (75, 'x', 'With a free and uncaring nature, it doesn''t mind if pieces break off while it rolls down mountains.'),
    (75, 'y', 'Rolls down slopes to move. It rolls over any obstacle without slowing or changing its direction.'),
    (75, 'yellow', 'Often seen rolling down mountain trails. Obstacles are just things to roll straight over, not avoid.'),
    (76, 'alpha-sapphire', 'Golem is known for rolling down from mountains. To prevent them from rolling into the homes of people downhill, grooves have been dug into the sides of mountains to serve as guideways for diverting this Pokémon''s course.'),
    (76, 'black', 'Even dynamite can''t harm its hard, boulderlike body. It sheds its hide just once a year.'),
    (76, 'black-2', 'Even dynamite can''t harm its hard, boulder-like body. It sheds its hide just once a year.'),
    (76, 'blue', 'Its boulder-like body is extremely hard. It can easily withstand dynamite blasts without damage.'),
    (76, 'crystal', 'Its rock-like body is so durable, even high-powered dynamite blasts fail to scratch its rugged hide.'),
    (76, 'diamond', 'It sheds its hide once a year. Its boulderlike body is so tough, even dynamite can''t harm it.'),
    (76, 'emerald', 'It is said to live in volcanic craters on mountain peaks. Once a year, it sheds its hide and grows larger. The shed hide crumbles and returns to the soil.'),
    (76, 'firered', 'It is enclosed in a hard shell that is as rugged as slabs of rock. It sheds skin once a year to grow larger.'),
    (76, 'gold', 'It sheds its skin once a year. The discarded shell immediately hardens and crumbles away.'),
    (76, 'heartgold', 'It sheds its skin once a year. The discarded shell immediately hardens and crumbles away.'),
    (76, 'leafgreen', 'Its boulder-like body is extremely hard. It can easily withstand dynamite blasts without taking damage.'),
    (76, 'moon', 'Once a year, this Pokémon molts, and its shed shell returns to the soil. This process creates enriched soil, so farmers collect the shells.'),
    (76, 'omega-ruby', 'Golem live up on mountains. If there is a large earthquake, these Pokémon will come rolling down off the mountains en masse to the foothills below.'),
    (76, 'pearl', 'It tumbles down mountains, leaving grooves from peak to base. Stay clear of these grooves.'),
    (76, 'platinum', 'Even dynamite can''t harm its hard, boulderlike body. It sheds its hide just once a year.'),
    (76, 'red', 'Its boulder-like body is extremely hard. It can easily withstand dynamite blasts without damage.'),
    (76, 'ruby', 'Golem live up on mountains. If there is a large earthquake, these {{ScPkmn}} will come rolling down off the mountains en masse to the foothills below.'),
    (76, 'sapphire', 'Golem is known for rolling down from mountains. To prevent them from rolling into the homes of people downhill, grooves have been dug into the sides of mountains to serve as guideways for diverting this {{ScPkmn}}''s course.'),
    (76, 'silver', 'It is capable of blowing itself up. It uses this explosive force to jump from mountain to mountain.'),
    (76, 'soulsilver', 'It is capable of blowing itself up. It uses this explosive force to jump from mountain to mountain.'),
    (76, 'sun', 'Its body can survive dynamite blasts without a single scratch, but it hates rain and humidity.'),
    (76, 'ultra-moon', 'It detonates its own body. The power from that explosion can propel it up steep mountain paths with amazing speed.'),
    (76, 'ultra-sun', 'When Golem grow old, they stop shedding their shells. Those that have lived a long, long time have shells green with moss.'),
    (76, 'white', 'Even dynamite can''t harm its hard, boulderlike body. It sheds its hide just once a year.'),
    (76, 'white-2', 'Even dynamite can''t harm its hard, boulder-like body. It sheds its hide just once a year.'),
    (76, 'x', 'It tumbles down mountains, leaving grooves from peak to base. Stay clear of these grooves.'),
    (76, 'y', 'Even dynamite can''t harm its hard, boulder-like body. It sheds its hide just once a year.'),
    (76, 'yellow', 'Once it sheds its skin, its body turns tender and whitish. Its hide hardens when it''s exposed to air.'),
    (77, 'alpha-sapphire', 'Ponyta is very weak at birth. It can barely stand up. This Pokémon becomes stronger by stumbling and falling to keep up with its parent.'),
