    (127, 'alpha-sapphire', 'Pinsir has a pair of massive horns. Protruding from the surface of these horns are thorns. These thorns are driven deeply into the foe''s body when the pincer closes, making it tough for the foe to escape.'),
    (127, 'black', 'It grips prey with its pincers until the prey is torn in half. What it can''t tear, it tosses far.'),
    (127, 'black-2', 'It grips prey with its powerful pincers and will not let go until the prey is torn in half.'),
    (127, 'blue', 'If it fails to crush the victim in its pincers, it will swing it around and toss it hard.'),
    (127, 'crystal', 'When the temperature drops at night, it sleeps on treetops or among roots where it is well hidden.'),
    (127, 'diamond', 'It grips prey with its pincers until the prey is torn in half. What it can''t tear, it tosses far.'),
    (127, 'emerald', 'Their pincers are strong enough to shatter thick logs. Because they dislike cold, Pinsir burrow and sleep under the ground on chilly nights.'),
    (127, 'firered', 'Its two long pincer horns are powerful. Once they grip an enemy, they won''t release until the foe is torn.'),
    (127, 'gold', 'With its horns, it digs burrows to sleep in at night. In the morning, damp soil clings to its body.'),
    (127, 'heartgold', 'With its pincer horns, it digs burrows to sleep in at night. In the morning, damp soil clings to its body.'),
    (127, 'leafgreen', 'If it fails to crush the foe in its pincers, it will swing around and toss the opponent.'),
    (127, 'moon', 'One solid blow from its horns is enough to split apart a large tree. Its greatest rival in Alola is Vikavolt.'),
    (127, 'omega-ruby', 'Pinsir is astoundingly strong. It can grip a foe weighing twice its weight in its horns and easily lift it. This Pokémon''s movements turn sluggish in cold places.'),
    (127, 'pearl', 'It grips prey with its pincers until the prey is torn in half. What it can''t tear, it tosses far.'),
