    (168, 'sun', 'There are some areas where people use the string Ariados spins for their own weaving. The resulting cloth is popular for its strength.'),
    (168, 'ultra-moon', 'It spews threads from its mouth to catch its prey. When night falls, it leaves its web to go hunt aggressively.'),
    (168, 'ultra-sun', 'Every night, it wanders around in search of prey, whose movements it restrains by spewing threads before it bites into them with its fangs.'),
    (168, 'violet', 'It wanders in search of food after darkness falls, never nesting in a specific place.'),
    (168, 'white', 'It attaches silk to its prey and sets it free. Later, it tracks the silk to the prey and its friends.'),
