    (222, 'alpha-sapphire', 'Clusters of Corsola congregate in warm seas where they serve as ideal hiding places for smaller Pokémon. When the water temperature falls, this Pokémon migrates to the southern seas.'),
    (222, 'black', 'Many live in the clean seas of the south. They apparently can''t live in polluted waters.'),
    (222, 'black-2', 'They prefer unpolluted southern seas. Their coral branches lose their color and deteriorate in dirty water.'),
    (222, 'brilliant-diamond', 'Many live in the clean seas of the south. They apparently can''t live in polluted waters.'),
    (222, 'crystal', 'The points on its head absorb nutrients from clean water. They cannot survive in polluted water.'),
    (222, 'diamond', 'Many live in the clean seas of the south. They apparently can''t live in polluted waters.'),
    (222, 'emerald', 'Corsola live in warm southern seas. If the sea becomes polluted, the beautiful coral stalks become discolored and crumble away in tatters.'),
