    (421, 'alpha-sapphire', 'If it senses strong sunlight, it opens its folded petals to absorb the sun''s rays with its whole body.'),
    (421, 'black', 'If it senses strong sunlight, it opens its folded petals to absorb the sun''s rays with its whole body.'),
    (421, 'black-2', 'If it senses strong sunlight, it opens its folded petals to absorb the sun''s rays with its whole body.'),
    (421, 'brilliant-diamond', 'It blooms during times of strong sunlight. The Pokémon tries to make up for everything it endured as a bud.'),
    (421, 'diamond', 'It blooms during times of strong sunlight. It tries to make up for everything it endured as a bud.'),
    (421, 'heartgold', 'During times of strong sunlight, its bud blooms, its petals open fully, and it becomes very active.'),
    (421, 'legends-arceus', 'Cheerfully active on sunny days. Immediately closes its petals and becomes immobile once the sun becomes hidden, however.'),
    (421, 'legends-arceus', 'Motionless, save for the occasional quiver. A rich array of Pokémon can be found gathered around it, drawn by the scent exuded from Cherrim''s folded petals.'),
    (421, 'omega-ruby', 'During times of strong sunlight, its bud blooms, its petals open fully, and it becomes very active.'),
    (421, 'pearl', 'It is docile as a bud, but turns cheerful when it blooms. It folds back into a bud if sunlight wanes.'),
    (421, 'platinum', 'If it senses strong sunlight, it opens its folded petals to absorb the sun''s rays with its whole body.'),
    (421, 'shield', 'The faint scent that emanates from its full blossom entices bug Pokémon to it.'),
    (421, 'shield', 'Its folded petals are pretty tough. Bird Pokémon can peck at them all they want, and Cherrim won''t be bothered at all.'),
    (421, 'shining-pearl', 'It is docile as a bud and turns cheerful when it blooms. It folds back into a bud if sunlight wanes.'),
    (421, 'soulsilver', 'During times of strong sunlight, its bud blooms, its petals open fully, and it becomes very active.'),
    (421, 'sword', 'After absorbing plenty of sunlight, Cherrim takes this form. It''s full of energy while it''s like this, and its liveliness will go on until sundown.'),
    (421, 'sword', 'As a bud, it barely moves. It sits still, placidly waiting for sunlight to appear.'),
