    (426, 'shield', 'It grabs people and Pokémon and carries them off somewhere. Where do they go? Nobody knows.'),
    (426, 'shining-pearl', 'It carries people and Pokémon when it flies. But since it only drifts, it can end up anywhere.'),
    (426, 'soulsilver', 'It can generate and release gas within its body. That''s how it can control the altitude of its drift.'),
    (426, 'sun', 'There was once an incident in which a man took a trip riding a Drifblim, only to go missing.'),
    (426, 'sword', 'Some say this Pokémon is a collection of souls burdened with regrets, silently drifting through the dusk.'),
    (426, 'ultra-moon', 'The raw material for the gas inside its body is souls. When its body starts to deflate, it''s thought to carry away people and Pokémon.'),
    (426, 'ultra-sun', 'There''s a rumor that if you catch a Drifblim floating on the wind at dusk, you''ll be carried away to the afterlife.'),
    (426, 'violet', 'They carry people and Pokémon, but the wind can catch them, so there can''t be a fixed destination.'),
