    (545, 'y', 'With quick movements, it chases down its foes, attacking relentlessly with its horns until it prevails.'),
    (546, 'alpha-sapphire', 'Perhaps because they feel more at ease in a group, they stick to others they find. They end up looking like a cloud.'),
    (546, 'black', 'When attacked, it escapes by shooting cotton from its body. The cotton serves as a decoy to distract the attacker.'),
    (546, 'black-2', 'Perhaps because they feel more at ease in a group, they stick to others they find. They end up looking like a cloud.'),
    (546, 'moon', 'Pillows and beds stuffed with cotton exhaled by Cottonee are soft and puffy, light and airy—altogether top quality.'),
    (546, 'omega-ruby', 'When attacked, it escapes by shooting cotton from its body. The cotton serves as a decoy to distract the attacker.'),
    (546, 'scarlet', 'Pillows and beds stuffed with cotton exhaled by Cottonee are soft and puffy, light and airy— altogether top quality.'),
    (546, 'shield', 'Weaving together the cotton of both Cottonee and Eldegoss produces exquisite cloth that''s highly prized by many luxury brands.'),
    (546, 'sun', 'When it finds others of its kind, they all stick together. When enough of them have collected, the mass resembles a cumulonimbus cloud.'),
    (546, 'sword', 'It shoots cotton from its body to protect itself. If it gets caught up in hurricane-strength winds, it can get sent to the other side of the Earth.'),
    (546, 'ultra-moon', 'When attacked, it expels cotton from its body to create a diversion. The cotton it loses grows back in quickly.'),
    (546, 'ultra-sun', 'To protect itself, it shoots cotton from its body. When it gets wet in the rain, its cotton grows moist and heavy, and it can''t move as well.'),
    (546, 'violet', 'When attacked, it escapes by shooting cotton from its body. The cotton serves as a decoy to distract the attacker.'),
    (546, 'white', 'They go wherever the wind takes them. On rainy days, their bodies are heavier, so they take shelter beneath big trees.'),
    (546, 'white-2', 'Perhaps because they feel more at ease in a group, they stick to others they find. They end up looking like a cloud.'),
    (546, 'x', 'When attacked, it escapes by shooting cotton from its body. The cotton serves as a decoy to distract the attacker.'),
    (546, 'y', 'Perhaps because they feel more at ease in a group, they stick to others they find. They end up looking like a cloud.'),
    (547, 'alpha-sapphire', 'Like the wind, it can slip through any gap, no matter how small. It leaves balls of white fluff behind.'),
    (547, 'black', 'Like the wind, it can slip through any gap, no matter how small. It leaves balls of white fluff behind.'),
    (547, 'black-2', 'They appear along with whirlwinds. They pull pranks, such as moving furniture and leaving balls of cotton in homes.'),
    (547, 'moon', 'This Pokémon appears, riding upon the wind. But if the wind gusts up, it''ll blow the cotton on this Pokémon''s head clean off.'),
    (547, 'omega-ruby', 'They appear along with whirlwinds. They pull pranks, such as moving furniture and leaving balls of cotton in homes.'),
    (547, 'scarlet', 'Like the wind, it can slip through any gap, no matter how small. It leaves balls of white fluff behind.'),
    (547, 'shield', 'As long as this Pokémon bathes in sunlight, its cotton keeps growing. If too much cotton fluff builds up, Whimsicott tears it off and scatters it.'),
    (547, 'sun', 'It rides on the wind and slips into people''s homes. After it has turned a room into a cotton-filled mess, it giggles to itself and takes off.'),
    (547, 'sword', 'It scatters cotton all over the place as a prank. If it gets wet, it''ll become too heavy to move and have no choice but to answer for its mischief.'),
    (547, 'ultra-moon', 'Whimsicott doesn''t live in a fixed location. It floats around on whirling winds, appearing all over the place to perform its mischief.'),
    (547, 'ultra-sun', 'This nuisance sneaks into people''s homes, where it hides important things and scatters cotton all over the place.'),
    (547, 'violet', 'It rides on the wind and slips into people’s homes. After it has turned a room into a cotton- filled mess, it giggles to itself and takes off.'),
    (547, 'white', 'Riding whirlwinds, they appear. These Pokémon sneak through gaps into houses and cause all sorts of mischief.'),
    (547, 'white-2', 'They appear along with whirlwinds. They pull pranks, such as moving furniture and leaving balls of cotton in homes.'),
    (547, 'x', 'They appear along with whirlwinds. They pull pranks, such as moving furniture and leaving balls of cotton in homes.'),
    (547, 'y', 'Like the wind, it can slip through any gap, no matter how small. It leaves balls of white fluff behind.'),
    (548, 'alpha-sapphire', 'Since they prefer moist, nutrient-rich soil, the areas where Petilil live are known to be good for growing plants.'),
    (548, 'black', 'The leaves on its head are very bitter. Eating one of these leaves is known to refresh a tired body.'),
    (548, 'black-2', 'The leaves on its head grow right back even if they fall out. These bitter leaves refresh those who eat them.'),
    (548, 'legends-arceus', 'The leaves on its head are highly valued for medicinal purposes. Dry the leaves in the sun, boil them, and then drink the bitter decoction for remarkably effective relief from fatigue.'),
    (548, 'moon', 'By pruning the leaves on its head with regularity, this Pokémon can be grown into a fine plump shape.'),
    (548, 'omega-ruby', 'The leaves on its head are very bitter. Eating one of these leaves is known to refresh a tired body.'),
    (548, 'scarlet', 'The leaves on its head grow right back even if they fall out. These bitter leaves refresh those who eat them.'),
    (548, 'shield', 'The deeper the color of a Petilil''s leaves, the healthier the Pokémon is. Petilil sometimes make its home in a well-tended field or flowerbed.'),
    (548, 'sun', 'Although the leaves on its head are bitter enough to cause dizziness, they provide relief from weariness—even more so when boiled.'),
    (548, 'sword', 'Petilil appears around sources of clean water. Boiling leaves from this Pokémon''s head results in a liquid that''s sometimes used as a bug repellent.'),
    (548, 'ultra-moon', 'They prefer clean water and soil. When the environment they live in turns bad, the whole bunch will up and move to a new area.'),
    (548, 'ultra-sun', 'Some say if you dry the leaves on its head, boil them down, and drink the infusion, your vigor will return, so Petilil is popular with the elderly.'),
    (548, 'violet', 'If the leaves on its head are pruned with regularity, this Pokémon can be grown into a fine plump shape.'),
    (548, 'white', 'Since they prefer moist, nutrient-rich soil, the areas where Petilil live are known to be good for growing plants.'),
    (548, 'white-2', 'The leaves on its head grow right back even if they fall out. These bitter leaves refresh those who eat them.'),
    (548, 'x', 'The leaves on its head are very bitter. Eating one of these leaves is known to refresh a tired body.'),
    (548, 'y', 'Since they prefer moist, nutrient-rich soil, the areas where Petilil live are known to be good for growing plants.'),
    (549, 'alpha-sapphire', 'Even veteran Trainers face a challenge in getting its beautiful flower to bloom. This Pokémon is popular with celebrities.'),
    (549, 'black', 'Even veteran Trainers face a challenge in getting its beautiful flower to bloom. This Pokémon is popular with celebrities.'),
    (549, 'black-2', 'The fragrance of the garland on its head has a relaxing effect, but taking care of it is very difficult.'),
    (549, 'moon', 'As soon as it finds a male to be its partner, the beautiful flower on its head darkens, droops, and withers away.'),
    (549, 'omega-ruby', 'The fragrance of the garland on its head has a relaxing effect. It withers if a Trainer does not take good care of it.'),
    (549, 'shield', 'Essential oils made from Lilligant flowers have a sublime scent, but they''re also staggeringly expensive.'),
    (549, 'sun', 'No matter how much time and money is spent raising it, its flowers are the most beautiful when they bloom in the wild.'),
    (549, 'sword', 'It''s believed that even first-rate gardeners have a hard time getting the flower on a Lilligant''s head to bloom.'),
    (549, 'ultra-moon', 'It''s well liked by other Pokémon because of its beauty. The flower on its head needs constant care, or it will soon wither and rot.'),
    (549, 'ultra-sun', 'The fragrance of its flower differs slightly depending on the soil where it grew up. Sniffing the aroma calms your heart and mind.'),
    (549, 'white', 'The fragrance of the garland on its head has a relaxing effect. It withers if a Trainer does not take good care of it.'),
    (549, 'white-2', 'The fragrance of the garland on its head has a relaxing effect, but taking care of it is very difficult.'),
    (549, 'x', 'The fragrance of the garland on its head has a relaxing effect. It withers if a Trainer does not take good care of it.'),
    (549, 'y', 'Even veteran Trainers face a challenge in getting its beautiful flower to bloom. This Pokémon is popular with celebrities.'),
    (550, 'scarlet', 'Its temperament is vicious and aggressive. This Pokémon is also full of vitality and can multiply rapidly before anyone notices.'),
    (550, 'shield', 'In the past, it often appeared on the dinner table. The meat of red-striped Basculin is on the fatty side, and it''s more popular with the youth.'),
    (550, 'sword', 'Anglers love the fight this Pokémon puts up on the hook. And there are always more to catch— many people release them into lakes illicitly.'),
    (550, 'ultra-moon', 'When a school of Basculin appears in a lake, everything else disappears, except for Corphish and Crawdaunt. That''s how violent Basculin are.'),
    (550, 'ultra-sun', 'Savage, violent Pokémon, red and blue Basculin are always fighting each other over territory.'),
    (550, 'violet', 'It''s so vicious that it''s called the Thug of the River. Yet Basculin is still targeted by predators, such as Dondozo and Bombirdier.'),
    (551, 'alpha-sapphire', 'They live buried in the sands of the desert. The sun-warmed sands prevent their body temperature from dropping.'),
    (551, 'black', 'They live buried in the sands of the desert. The sun-warmed sands prevent their body temperature from dropping.'),
    (551, 'black-2', 'They live hidden under hot desert sands in order to keep their body temperature from dropping.'),
    (551, 'legends-za', 'It moves below the sand''s surface, exposing only its nose and eyes. A black membrane shields its eyes from the sun.'),
    (551, 'moon', 'It conceals itself in the sand and chomps down on the legs of any prey that unwarily walk over it. Its favorite food is Trapinch.'),
    (551, 'omega-ruby', 'It moves along below the sand''s surface, except for its nose and eyes. A dark membrane shields its eyes from the sun.'),
    (551, 'scarlet', 'It submerges itself in sand and moves as if swimming. This wise behavior keeps its enemies from finding it and maintains its temperature.'),
    (551, 'shield', 'Sandile is small, but its legs and lower body are powerful. Pushing sand aside as it goes, Sandile moves through the desert as if it''s swimming.'),
    (551, 'sun', 'It submerges itself in sand and moves as if swimming. This wise behavior keeps its enemies from finding it and maintains its temperature.'),
    (551, 'sword', 'The desert gets cold at night, so when the sun sets, this Pokémon burrows deep into the sand and sleeps until sunrise.'),
    (551, 'ultra-moon', 'Sandile''s still not good at hunting, so it mostly eats things that have collapsed in the desert. It''s called “the cleaner of the desert.”'),
    (551, 'ultra-sun', 'Alola, where it''s warm all year round, is a comfortable environment for this Pokémon. Sometimes you''ll even see it outside of deserts.'),
    (551, 'violet', 'They live hidden under hot desert sands in order to keep their body temperature from dropping.'),
    (551, 'white', 'It moves along below the sand''s surface, except for its nose and eyes. A dark membrane shields its eyes from the sun.'),
    (551, 'white-2', 'They live hidden under hot desert sands in order to keep their body temperature from dropping.'),
    (551, 'x', 'It moves along below the sand''s surface, except for its nose and eyes. A dark membrane shields its eyes from the sun.'),
    (551, 'y', 'They live buried in the sands of the desert. The sun-warmed sands prevent their body temperature from dropping.'),
    (552, 'alpha-sapphire', 'The special membrane covering its eyes can sense the heat of objects, so it can see its surroundings even in darkness.'),
    (552, 'black', 'They live in groups of a few individuals. Protective membranes shield their eyes from sandstorms.'),
    (552, 'black-2', 'Protected by thin membranes, their eyes can see even in the dead of night. They live in groups of a few individuals.'),
    (552, 'legends-za', 'The special membrane covering its eyes can sense the heat of objects, so it can see its surroundings even in darkness.'),
    (552, 'moon', 'Thanks to the special membrane covering its eyes, it can see its surroundings clearly, even in the middle of the night.'),
    (552, 'omega-ruby', 'They live in groups of a few individuals. Protective membranes shield their eyes from sandstorms.'),
    (552, 'scarlet', 'Protected by thin membranes, their eyes can see even in the dead of night. They live in groups of a few individuals.'),
    (552, 'shield', 'Although this Pokémon has specialized eyes that allow it to see in the dark, Krokorok won''t move much at night—the desert gets cold after sunset.'),
    (552, 'sun', 'They move in groups of a few individuals. A female is often the leader of the group, and the males will gather food.'),
    (552, 'sword', 'Krokorok has specialized eyes that enable it to see in the dark. This ability lets Krokorok hunt in the dead of night without getting lost.'),
    (552, 'ultra-moon', 'It buries some of its prey in the sand to use as emergency meals when its hunts are unsuccessful.'),
    (552, 'ultra-sun', 'Krokorok really hates it when its body gets cold. On nights when the temperature drops, it digs deep into the desert sands.'),
    (552, 'violet', 'Thanks to the special membrane covering its eyes, it can see its surroundings clearly, even in the middle of the night.'),
    (552, 'white', 'The special membrane covering its eyes can sense the heat of objects, so it can see its surroundings even in darkness.'),
    (552, 'white-2', 'Protected by thin membranes, their eyes can see even in the dead of night. They live in groups of a few individuals.'),
