    (563, 'alpha-sapphire', 'Grave robbers who mistake them for real coffins and get too close end up trapped inside their bodies.'),
    (563, 'black', 'It has been said that they swallow those who get too close and turn them into mummies. They like to eat gold nuggets.'),
    (563, 'black-2', 'Grave robbers who mistake them for real coffins and get too close end up trapped inside their bodies.'),
    (563, 'legends-za', 'Grave robbers sometimes mistake this Pokémon for a real coffin and get too close to it. They end up trapped within Cofagrigus''s body.'),
    (563, 'omega-ruby', 'It has been said that they swallow those who get too close and turn them into mummies. They like to eat gold nuggets.'),
    (563, 'shield', 'There are many depictions of Cofagrigus decorating ancient tombs. They''re symbols of the wealth that kings of bygone eras had.'),
    (563, 'sword', 'This Pokémon has a body of sparkling gold. People say it no longer remembers that it was once human.'),
    (563, 'white', 'They pretend to be elaborate coffins to teach lessons to grave robbers. Their bodies are covered in pure gold.'),
    (563, 'white-2', 'Grave robbers who mistake them for real coffins and get too close end up trapped inside their bodies.'),
    (563, 'x', 'It has been said that they swallow those who get too close and turn them into mummies. They like to eat gold nuggets.'),
    (563, 'y', 'Grave robbers who mistake them for real coffins and get too close end up trapped inside their bodies.'),
    (564, 'alpha-sapphire', 'Restored from a fossil, this Pokémon can dive to depths beyond half a mile.'),
    (564, 'black', 'Restored from a fossil, this Pokémon can dive to depths beyond half a mile.'),
    (564, 'black-2', 'This Pokémon was restored from a fossil. It swam skillfully and dove to depths beyond half a mile.'),
    (564, 'moon', 'Reputed to be the ancestor of most turtle Pokémon, it lived in warm seas approximately a hundred million years ago.'),
    (564, 'omega-ruby', 'About 100 million years ago, these Pokémon swam in oceans. It is thought they also went on land to attack prey.'),
    (564, 'shield', 'Tirtouga is considered to be the ancestor of many turtle Pokémon. It was restored to life from a fossil.'),
    (564, 'sun', 'Based on studies of its skeletal structure, it can apparently dive to ocean depths of over half a mile.'),
    (564, 'sword', 'This Pokémon inhabited ancient seas. Although it can only crawl, it still comes up onto land in search of prey.'),
    (564, 'ultra-moon', 'Its hunting grounds encompassed a broad area, from the land to more than half a mile deep in the ocean.'),
    (564, 'ultra-sun', 'It was restored from an ancient fossil. Tirtouga lived in the sea but came up onto the land to search for prey.'),
    (564, 'white', 'About 100 million years ago, these Pokémon swam in oceans. It is thought they also went on land to attack prey.'),
    (564, 'white-2', 'This Pokémon was restored from a fossil. It swam skillfully and dove to depths beyond half a mile.'),
    (564, 'x', 'About 100 million years ago, these Pokémon swam in oceans. It is thought they also went on land to attack prey.'),
    (564, 'y', 'Restored from a fossil, this Pokémon can dive to depths beyond half a mile.'),
    (565, 'alpha-sapphire', 'It could knock out a foe with a slap from one of its developed front appendages and chew it up, shell or bones and all.'),
    (565, 'black', 'They can live both in the ocean and on land. A slap from one of them is enough to open a hole in the bottom of a tanker.'),
    (565, 'black-2', 'It could knock out a foe with a slap from one of its developed front appendages and chew it up, shell or bones and all.'),
    (565, 'moon', 'Active both on land and in the sea, this Pokémon drags its land-based prey into the water to finish it off.'),
    (565, 'omega-ruby', 'They can live both in the ocean and on land. A slap from one of them is enough to open a hole in the bottom of a tanker.'),
    (565, 'shield', 'This Pokémon emerges from the water in search of prey despite the fact that it moves more slowly on land.'),
    (565, 'sun', 'It constructed its sturdy shell by crunching and swallowing the hard shells or bones of its prey.'),
    (565, 'sword', 'Carracosta completely devours its prey—bones, shells, and all. Because of this, Carracosta''s own shell grows thick and sturdy.'),
    (565, 'ultra-moon', 'Carracosta eats every last bit of the prey it catches, even the shells and bones, to further strengthen its sturdy shell.'),
    (565, 'ultra-sun', 'Its jaws are terrifyingly powerful. It could eat Omastar and Omanyte whole and not be bothered in the slightest by their shells.'),
    (565, 'white', 'Incredible jaw strength enables them to chew up steel beams and rocks along with their prey.'),
    (565, 'white-2', 'It could knock out a foe with a slap from one of its developed front appendages and chew it up, shell or bones and all.'),
    (565, 'x', 'They can live both in the ocean and on land. A slap from one of them is enough to open a hole in the bottom of a tanker.'),
    (565, 'y', 'It could knock out a foe with a slap from one of its developed front appendages and chew it up, shell or bones and all.'),
    (566, 'alpha-sapphire', 'Said to be an ancestor of bird Pokémon, they were unable to fly and moved about by hopping from one branch to another.'),
    (566, 'black', 'Said to be an ancestor of bird Pokémon, they were unable to fly and moved about by hopping from one branch to another.'),
    (566, 'black-2', 'It was revived from an ancient fossil. Not able to fly, it lived in treetops and hopped from one branch to another.'),
    (566, 'moon', 'To all appearances flightless, it was able to glide down from tall treetops to snag its prey.'),
    (566, 'omega-ruby', 'Revived from a fossil, this Pokémon is thought to be the ancestor of all bird Pokémon.'),
    (566, 'shield', 'Archen is said to be the ancestor of bird Pokémon. It lived in treetops, eating berries and bug Pokémon.'),
    (566, 'sun', 'It is the ancestor of all bird Pokémon. Archen itself could not actually fly but moved by hopping from treetop to treetop.'),
    (566, 'sword', 'This Pokémon was successfully restored from a fossil. As research suggested, Archen is unable to fly. But it''s very good at jumping.'),
    (566, 'ultra-moon', 'Restored from a fossil, this ancient bird Pokémon has wings but can''t yet fly.'),
    (566, 'ultra-sun', 'Once thought to be the ancestor of all bird Pokémon, some of the latest research suggests that may not be the case.'),
    (566, 'white', 'Revived from a fossil, this Pokémon is thought to be the ancestor of all bird Pokémon.'),
    (566, 'white-2', 'It was revived from an ancient fossil. Not able to fly, it lived in treetops and hopped from one branch to another.'),
    (566, 'x', 'Revived from a fossil, this Pokémon is thought to be the ancestor of all bird Pokémon.'),
    (566, 'y', 'Said to be an ancestor of bird Pokémon, they were unable to fly and moved about by hopping from one branch to another.'),
    (567, 'alpha-sapphire', 'It runs better than it flies. It takes off into the sky by running at a speed of 25 mph.'),
    (567, 'black', 'They are intelligent and will cooperate to catch prey. From the ground, they use a running start to take flight.'),
    (567, 'black-2', 'It runs better than it flies. It takes off into the sky by running at a speed of 25 mph.'),
    (567, 'moon', 'They hunted in flocks. When one Archeops had the prey cornered, another would swoop on it.'),
    (567, 'omega-ruby', 'They are intelligent and will cooperate to catch prey. From the ground, they use a running start to take flight.'),
    (567, 'shield', 'Though capable of flight, Archeops was apparently better at hunting on the ground.'),
    (567, 'sun', 'Although apparently able to fly, they tended to run along the ground, averaging speeds of roughly 25 mph.'),
    (567, 'sword', 'It needs a running start to take off. If Archeops wants to fly, it first needs to run nearly 25 mph, building speed over a course of about 2.5 miles.'),
    (567, 'ultra-moon', 'Said to be an ancestor of bird Pokémon, the muscles it uses to flap its wings are still weak, so it needs a long runway in order to take off.'),
    (567, 'ultra-sun', 'This ancient Pokémon''s plumage is delicate, so if anyone other than an experienced professional tries to restore it, they will fail.'),
    (567, 'white', 'It runs better than it flies. It catches prey by running at speeds comparable to those of an automobile.'),
    (567, 'white-2', 'It runs better than it flies. It takes off into the sky by running at a speed of 25 mph.'),
    (567, 'x', 'They are intelligent and will cooperate to catch prey. From the ground, they use a running start to take flight.'),
    (567, 'y', 'It runs better than it flies. It takes off into the sky by running at a speed of 25 mph.'),
    (568, 'alpha-sapphire', 'Inhaling the gas they belch will make you sleep for a week. They prefer unsanitary places.'),
    (568, 'black', 'Inhaling the gas they belch will make you sleep for a week. They prefer unsanitary places.'),
    (568, 'black-2', 'Wanting more garbage, they follow people who litter. They always belch poison gas.'),
    (568, 'legends-za', 'The combination of garbage bags and industrial waste caused the chemical reaction that created this Pokémon.'),
    (568, 'moon', 'It gorges on trash until its stomach is full. Then it belches toxic gas. An unlucky whiff of gas will put a person in the hospital.'),
    (568, 'omega-ruby', 'The combination of garbage bags and industrial waste caused the chemical reaction that created this Pokémon.'),
    (568, 'shield', 'This Pokémon was born from a bag stuffed with trash. Galarian Weezing relish the fumes belched by Trubbish.'),
    (568, 'sun', 'Unsanitary places are what they like best. They can be spotted in Alola, often with Grimer in hot pursuit.'),
    (568, 'sword', 'Its favorite places are unsanitary ones. If you leave trash lying around, you could even find one of these Pokémon living in your room.'),
    (568, 'ultra-moon', 'If a young Pokémon or child breathes in the toxic gas that Trubbish belches out, it could be a life-threatening situation.'),
    (568, 'ultra-sun', 'Poisonous gas leaks out of it when it breathes. Muk that catch a whiff of that stench will come drooling.'),
    (568, 'white', 'The combination of garbage bags and industrial waste caused the chemical reaction that created this Pokémon.'),
    (568, 'white-2', 'Wanting more garbage, they follow people who litter. They always belch poison gas.'),
    (568, 'x', 'The combination of garbage bags and industrial waste caused the chemical reaction that created this Pokémon.'),
    (568, 'y', 'Inhaling the gas they belch will make you sleep for a week. They prefer unsanitary places.'),
    (569, 'alpha-sapphire', 'Consuming garbage makes new kinds of poison gases and liquids inside their bodies.'),
    (569, 'black', 'It clenches opponents with its left arm and finishes them off with foul-smelling poison gas belched from its mouth.'),
    (569, 'black-2', 'Consuming garbage makes new kinds of poison gases and liquids inside their bodies.'),
    (569, 'moon', 'For a time, their numbers increased explosively in Alola. Since the arrival of Grimer, their population has decreased dramatically.'),
    (569, 'omega-ruby', 'It clenches opponents with its left arm and finishes them off with foul-smelling poison gas belched from its mouth.'),
    (569, 'shield', 'The toxic liquid it launches from its right arm is so virulent that it can kill a weakened creature instantly.'),
    (569, 'sun', 'Beware the poisonous liquid it shoots from its right arm. If even a little of it gets on you, you''ll experience the effects of the unidentified toxin.'),
    (569, 'sword', 'This Pokémon eats trash, which turns into poison inside its body. The main component of the poison depends on what sort of trash was eaten.'),
    (569, 'ultra-moon', 'Some say the reason Garbodor in Alola are a little stronger than their counterparts elsewhere is the presence of Muk, their natural enemy.'),
    (569, 'ultra-sun', 'It locks opponents in place with its left hand, immobilizing them by entirely dousing their bodies with poisonous liquid.'),
    (569, 'white', 'They absorb garbage and make it part of their bodies. They shoot a poisonous liquid from their right-hand fingertips.'),
    (569, 'white-2', 'Consuming garbage makes new kinds of poison gases and liquids inside their bodies.'),
    (569, 'x', 'It clenches opponents with its left arm and finishes them off with foul-smelling poison gas belched from its mouth.'),
    (569, 'y', 'Consuming garbage makes new kinds of poison gases and liquids inside their bodies.'),
    (570, 'alpha-sapphire', 'To protect themselves from danger, they hide their true identities by transforming into people and Pokémon.'),
    (570, 'black', 'It changes into the forms of others to surprise them. Apparently, it often transforms into a silent child.'),
    (570, 'black-2', 'It changes so it looks just like its foe, tricks it, and then uses that opportunity to flee.'),
    (570, 'omega-ruby', 'It changes so it looks just like its foe, tricks it, and then uses that opportunity to flee.'),
    (570, 'shield', 'Zorua sometimes transforms into a person and goes into cities to search for food. When Zorua does this, it usually takes on the form of a child.'),
    (570, 'sword', 'Zorua is a timid Pokémon. This disposition seems to be what led to the development of Zorua''s ability to take on the forms of other creatures.'),
    (570, 'ultra-moon', 'If a normally talkative child suddenly stops talking, it may have been replaced by Zorua.'),
    (570, 'ultra-sun', 'This Pokémon has a cowardly disposition, so when it''s not around friends, it basically always stays transformed as something else.'),
    (570, 'white', 'To protect themselves from danger, they hide their true identities by transforming into people and Pokémon.'),
    (570, 'white-2', 'It changes so it looks just like its foe, tricks it, and then uses that opportunity to flee.'),
    (570, 'x', 'It changes so it looks just like its foe, tricks it, and then uses that opportunity to flee.'),
    (570, 'y', 'To protect themselves from danger, they hide their true identities by transforming into people and Pokémon.'),
    (571, 'alpha-sapphire', 'Bonds between these Pokémon are very strong. It protects the safety of its pack by tricking its opponents.'),
    (571, 'black', 'Bonds between these Pokémon are very strong. It protects the safety of its pack by tricking its opponents.'),
    (571, 'black-2', 'Stories say those who tried to catch Zoroark were trapped in an illusion and punished.'),
    (571, 'omega-ruby', 'Each has the ability to fool a large group of people simultaneously. They protect their lair with illusory scenery.'),
    (571, 'shield', 'Seeking to ease the burden of solitude, lonely Trainers tell Zoroark to show illusions to them.'),
    (571, 'sword', 'This Pokémon cares deeply about others of its kind, and it will conjure terrifying illusions to keep its den and pack safe.'),
    (571, 'ultra-moon', 'If it thinks humans are going to discover its den, Zoroark shows them visions that make them wander around in the woods.'),
    (571, 'ultra-sun', 'It doesn''t just transform itself—it also has the power to make hundreds of people see its illusions.'),
    (571, 'white', 'Each has the ability to fool a large group of people simultaneously. They protect their lair with illusory scenery.'),
    (571, 'white-2', 'Stories say those who tried to catch Zoroark were trapped in an illusion and punished.'),
    (571, 'x', 'Each has the ability to fool a large group of people simultaneously. They protect their lair with illusory scenery.'),
    (571, 'y', 'Bonds between these Pokémon are very strong. It protects the safety of its pack by tricking its opponents.'),
    (572, 'alpha-sapphire', 'These Pokémon prefer a tidy habitat. They are always sweeping and dusting, using their tails as brooms.'),
    (572, 'black', 'They greet one another by rubbing each other with their tails, which are always kept well groomed and clean.'),
    (572, 'black-2', 'Minccino greet each other by grooming one another thoroughly with their tails.'),
    (572, 'omega-ruby', 'Minccino greet each other by grooming one another thoroughly with their tails.'),
    (572, 'scarlet', 'When its tail has gotten dirty from self-cleaning or from cleaning its nest, Minccino spends a whole day washing its tail in clean springwater.'),
    (572, 'shield', 'They pet each other with their tails as a form of greeting. Of the two, the one whose tail is fluffier is a bit more boastful.'),
    (572, 'sword', 'The way it brushes away grime with its tail can be helpful when cleaning. But its focus on spotlessness can make cleaning more of a hassle.'),
    (572, 'ultra-moon', 'When its tail has gotten dirty from self-cleaning or from cleaning its nest, Minccino spends a whole day washing its tail in clean spring water.'),
    (572, 'ultra-sun', 'A clean freak that will not allow even the slightest mess, it uses its tail like a mop to thoroughly clean any and all filth.'),
    (572, 'violet', 'These Pokémon like things neat and tidy. They are always sweeping and dusting their habitat, using their tails as brooms.'),
    (572, 'white', 'These Pokémon prefer a tidy habitat. They are always sweeping and dusting, using their tails as brooms.'),
    (572, 'white-2', 'Minccino greet each other by grooming one another thoroughly with their tails.'),
