    (582, 'alpha-sapphire', 'This Pokémon formed from icicles bathed in energy from the morning sun. It sleeps buried in snow.'),
    (582, 'black', 'The temperature of their breath is -58° F. They create snow crystals and make snow fall in the areas around them.'),
    (582, 'black-2', 'Theoretically, this Pokémon formed from icicles bathed in energy from the morning sun. Their breath is -58° F.'),
    (582, 'legends-za', 'The temperature of their breath is −58 degrees Fahrenheit. They create snow crystals and make snow fall in the areas around them.'),
    (582, 'moon', 'It feels pleasantly cool when embraced. This Pokémon is treasured by households in warm regions.'),
    (582, 'omega-ruby', 'The temperature of their breath is -58 degrees Fahrenheit. They create snow crystals and make snow fall in the areas around them.'),
    (582, 'shield', 'Supposedly, this Pokémon was born from an icicle. It spews out freezing air at −58 degrees Fahrenheit to make itself more comfortable.'),
    (582, 'sun', 'Born of an icicle, this Pokémon uses its frosty breath to make ice crystals, causing snow to fall.'),
    (582, 'sword', 'Unable to survive in hot areas, it makes itself comfortable by breathing out air cold enough to cause snow. It burrows into the snow to sleep.'),
    (582, 'ultra-moon', 'When the morning sun hit an icicle, it wished not to melt, and thus Vanillite was born. At night, it buries itself in snow to sleep.'),
    (582, 'ultra-sun', 'It exhales cold air that is at –58<!--U+2013 EN DASH in-game--> degrees Fahrenheit. When it''s in a warm place, it shrinks little by little.'),
    (582, 'white', 'This Pokémon formed from icicles bathed in energy from the morning sun. It sleeps buried in snow.'),
    (582, 'white-2', 'Theoretically, this Pokémon formed from icicles bathed in energy from the morning sun. Their breath is -58° F.'),
    (582, 'x', 'The temperature of their breath is -58 degrees Fahrenheit. They create snow crystals and make snow fall in the areas around them.'),
    (582, 'y', 'This Pokémon formed from icicles bathed in energy from the morning sun. It sleeps buried in snow.'),
    (583, 'alpha-sapphire', 'Snowy mountains are this Pokémon''s habitat. During an ancient ice age, they moved to southern areas.'),
    (583, 'black', 'Snowy mountains are this Pokémon''s habitat. During an ancient ice age, they moved to southern areas.'),
    (583, 'black-2', 'They cool down the surrounding air and create ice particles, which they use to freeze their foes.'),
    (583, 'legends-za', 'They cool down the surrounding air and create ice particles, which they use to freeze their foes.'),
    (583, 'moon', 'This Pokémon has existed since the Ice Age. It controls particles of ice, freezes its opponents, and then shatters them with a headbutt.'),
    (583, 'omega-ruby', 'They cool down the surrounding air and create ice particles, which they use to freeze their foes.'),
    (583, 'shield', 'It blasts enemies with cold air reaching −148 degrees Fahrenheit, freezing them solid. But it spares their lives afterward—it''s a kind Pokémon.'),
    (583, 'sun', 'Hot days cause its body to melt. It can be restored by refreezing it, but the process leaves its body slightly warped.'),
    (583, 'sword', 'By drinking pure water, it grows its icy body. This Pokémon can be hard to find on days with warm, sunny weather.'),
    (583, 'ultra-moon', 'This hearty Pokémon survived the Ice Age. It''s incredibly popular in very hot regions.'),
    (583, 'ultra-sun', 'It sprays its enemies with grains of ice to freeze them. Most Vanillish in Alola are smaller than average.'),
    (583, 'white', 'It conceals itself from enemy eyes by creating many small ice particles and hiding among them.'),
    (583, 'white-2', 'They cool down the surrounding air and create ice particles, which they use to freeze their foes.'),
    (583, 'x', 'They cool down the surrounding air and create ice particles, which they use to freeze their foes.'),
    (583, 'y', 'Snowy mountains are this Pokémon''s habitat. During an ancient ice age, they moved to southern areas.'),
    (584, 'alpha-sapphire', 'Swallowing large amounts of water, they make snow clouds inside their bodies and, when angry, cause violent blizzards.'),
    (584, 'black', 'Swallowing large amounts of water, they make snow clouds inside their bodies and attack their foes with violent blizzards.'),
    (584, 'black-2', 'Swallowing large amounts of water, they make snow clouds inside their bodies and, when angry, cause violent blizzards.'),
    (584, 'legends-za', 'If both heads get angry simultaneously, this Pokémon expels a blizzard from its horn, burying everything in snow.'),
    (584, 'moon', 'Even if it loses one of its heads, it can live relatively problem-free. It makes snow clouds inside its body.'),
    (584, 'omega-ruby', 'If both heads get angry simultaneously, this Pokémon expels a blizzard, burying everything in snow.'),
    (584, 'shield', 'People believe this Pokémon formed when two Vanillish stuck together. Its body temperature is roughly 21 degrees Fahrenheit.'),
    (584, 'sun', 'Each of its two heads has a brain, and when they are in agreement, it attacks its enemies by exhaling a violent blizzard.'),
    (584, 'sword', 'When its anger reaches a breaking point, this Pokémon unleashes a fierce blizzard that freezes every creature around it, be they friend or foe.'),
    (584, 'ultra-moon', 'Vanilluxe is born when two Vanillish, half-melted by the day''s light, stick to each other and freeze together in the cold return of night.'),
    (584, 'ultra-sun', 'It blasts blizzards from its two mouths. It can create snow anywhere, so it gets a lot of love from skiers and snowboarders.'),
    (584, 'white', 'If both heads get angry simultaneously, this Pokémon expels a blizzard, burying everything in snow.'),
    (584, 'white-2', 'Swallowing large amounts of water, they make snow clouds inside their bodies and, when angry, cause violent blizzards.'),
    (584, 'x', 'If both heads get angry simultaneously, this Pokémon expels a blizzard, burying everything in snow.'),
    (584, 'y', 'Swallowing large amounts of water, they make snow clouds inside their bodies and, when angry, cause violent blizzards.'),
    (585, 'alpha-sapphire', 'The turning of the seasons changes the color and scent of this Pokémon''s fur. People use it to mark the seasons.'),
    (585, 'black', 'The color and scent of their fur changes to match the mountain grass. When they sense hostility, they hide in the grass.'),
    (585, 'black-2', 'Their coloring changes according to the seasons and can be slightly affected by the temperature and humidity as well.'),
    (585, 'omega-ruby', 'Their coloring changes according to the seasons and can be slightly affected by the temperature and humidity as well.'),
    (585, 'scarlet', 'Deerling’s scent changes with the seasons, but when the Pokémon is in its Winter Form, it has hardly any scent at all.'),
    (585, 'scarlet', 'Deerling have different scents depending on the season. In early spring, these Pokémon give off a delicate, sweet, and calming scent.'),
    (585, 'scarlet', 'To prevent Deerling from entering their fields, many farmers will have several {{P|Lycanroc}} stand guard, as they are the natural enemy of Deerling.'),
    (585, 'scarlet', 'These Pokémon are not shy—they will behave as they please, even in front of people. If you feed one of them, it will quickly take a liking to you.'),
    (585, 'violet', 'This Pokémon will playfully headbutt those it gets along well with. It has antlers hidden under its flower, so the headbutts are a little painful.'),
    (585, 'violet', 'Deerling have different scents depending on the season. In this form, Deerling have a softly sweet scent that lingers in the nose.'),
    (585, 'violet', 'Despite Deerling''s adorable appearance, farmers consider it a nuisance since it loves plant shoots and will eat them all up.'),
    (585, 'violet', 'Deerling have different scents depending on the season. When a distinct grassy smell starts to waft from one, you know that summer has begun.'),
    (585, 'white', 'The turning of the seasons changes the color and scent of this Pokémon''s fur. People use it to mark the seasons.'),
    (585, 'white-2', 'Their coloring changes according to the seasons and can be slightly affected by the temperature and humidity as well.'),
    (585, 'x', 'Their coloring changes according to the seasons and can be slightly affected by the temperature and humidity as well.'),
    (585, 'y', 'The turning of the seasons changes the color and scent of this Pokémon''s fur. People use it to mark the seasons.'),
    (586, 'alpha-sapphire', 'They migrate according to the seasons, so some people call Sawsbuck the harbingers of spring.'),
    (586, 'black', 'They migrate according to the seasons. People can tell the season by looking at Sawsbuck''s horns.'),
    (586, 'black-2', 'They migrate according to the seasons, so some people call Sawsbuck the harbingers of spring.'),
    (586, 'omega-ruby', 'They migrate according to the seasons. People can tell the season by looking at Sawsbuck''s horns.'),
    (586, 'scarlet', 'It seems that a Sawsbuck with many flowers on its antlers will grow at a slightly slower pace because the flowers absorb the Pokémon’s nutrients.'),
    (586, 'scarlet', 'There are many Sawsbuck enthusiasts. The thicker and larger the branches and leaves on its antlers, the more majestic the Sawsbuck is thought to be.'),
    (586, 'scarlet', 'There are many Sawsbuck enthusiasts. The darker the red of the foliage that hangs from its antlers, the more stylish the Sawsbuck is thought to be.'),
    (586, 'scarlet', 'It’s said that Sawsbuck are calm and easy to tame during the season when they take on this form, so it’s the perfect time to make one your partner.'),
    (586, 'violet', 'Sawsbuck in their Autumn Form are known for having very short tempers. The males fight each other incessantly.'),
    (586, 'violet', 'This Pokémon''s leaves can be made into a black tea, the taste of which varies depending on the region of origin. Paldea''s is especially aromatic.'),
    (586, 'violet', 'There are many Sawsbuck enthusiasts. The paler the pink flowers that bloom on its antlers, the more beautiful the Sawsbuck is considered to be.'),
    (586, 'violet', 'Though there are many enthusiasts for Sawsbuck as a species, this seasonal form in particular is not very popular.'),
    (586, 'white', 'The plants growing on its horns change according to the season. The leaders of the herd possess magnificent horns.'),
    (586, 'white-2', 'They migrate according to the seasons, so some people call Sawsbuck the harbingers of spring.'),
    (586, 'x', 'They migrate according to the seasons. People can tell the season by looking at Sawsbuck''s horns.'),
    (586, 'y', 'They migrate according to the seasons, so some people call Sawsbuck the harbingers of spring.'),
    (587, 'alpha-sapphire', 'The energy made in its cheeks'' electric pouches is stored inside its membrane and released while it is gliding.'),
    (587, 'black', 'The energy made in its cheeks'' electric pouches is stored inside its membrane and released while it is gliding.'),
    (587, 'black-2', 'It glides on its outstretched membrane while shocking foes with the electricity stored in the pouches on its cheeks.'),
    (587, 'legends-za', 'The energy made in its cheeks'' electric pouches is stored inside its patagial membranes and released while it is gliding.'),
    (587, 'moon', 'It grills berries and bug Pokémon with electric shocks and makes a meal of them. It usually nests in the holes gouged in trees by Pikipek.'),
    (587, 'omega-ruby', 'They live on treetops and glide using the inside of a cape-like membrane while discharging electricity.'),
    (587, 'shield', 'This Pokémon absolutely loves sweet berries. Sometimes it stuffs its cheeks full of so much food that it can''t fly properly.'),
    (587, 'sun', 'It glides using its cape-like membrane. Electrical energy scatters from it, shocking its friends and foes alike.'),
    (587, 'sword', 'As Emolga flutters through the air, it crackles with electricity. This Pokémon is cute, but it can cause a lot of trouble.'),
    (587, 'ultra-moon', 'As it flies, it scatters electricity around, so bird Pokémon keep their distance. That''s why Emolga can keep all its food to itself.'),
    (587, 'ultra-sun', 'They store up electricity to fly through the air. When thunder cracks at night, sometimes there are almost enough of them to blot out the sky.'),
    (587, 'white', 'They live on treetops and glide using the inside of a cape-like membrane while discharging electricity.'),
    (587, 'white-2', 'It glides on its outstretched membrane while shocking foes with the electricity stored in the pouches on its cheeks.'),
    (587, 'x', 'They live on treetops and glide using the inside of a cape-like membrane while discharging electricity.'),
    (587, 'y', 'The energy made in its cheeks'' electric pouches is stored inside its membrane and released while it is gliding.'),
    (588, 'alpha-sapphire', 'For some reason they evolve when they receive electrical energy while they are attacking Shelmet.'),
    (588, 'black', 'These mysterious Pokémon evolve when they receive electrical stimulation while they are in the same place as Shelmet.'),
    (588, 'black-2', 'For some reason they evolve when they receive electrical energy while they are attacking Shelmet.'),
    (588, 'omega-ruby', 'These mysterious Pokémon evolve when they receive electrical stimulation while they are in the same place as Shelmet.'),
    (588, 'shield', 'It spits a liquid from its mouth to melt through Shelmet''s shell. Karrablast doesn''t eat the shell— it eats only the contents.'),
    (588, 'sword', 'Its strange physiology reacts to electrical energy in interesting ways. The presence of a Shelmet will cause this Pokémon to evolve.'),
    (588, 'white', 'When they feel threatened, they spit an acidic liquid to drive attackers away. This Pokémon targets Shelmet.'),
    (588, 'white-2', 'For some reason they evolve when they receive electrical energy while they are attacking Shelmet.'),
    (588, 'x', 'These mysterious Pokémon evolve when they receive electrical stimulation while they are in the same place as Shelmet.'),
    (588, 'y', 'For some reason they evolve when they receive electrical energy while they are attacking Shelmet.'),
    (589, 'alpha-sapphire', 'These Pokémon evolve by wearing the shell covering of a Shelmet. The steel armor protects their whole body.'),
    (589, 'black', 'They fly around at high speed, striking with their pointed spears. Even when in trouble, they face opponents bravely.'),
    (589, 'black-2', 'Wearing the shell covering they stole from Shelmet, they defend themselves and attack with two lances.'),
    (589, 'omega-ruby', 'Wearing the shell covering they stole from Shelmet, they defend themselves and attack with two lances.'),
    (589, 'shield', 'It charges its enemies, lances at the ready. An image of one of its duels is captured in a famous painting of Escavalier clashing with Sirfetch''d.'),
    (589, 'sword', 'They use shells they''ve stolen from Shelmet to arm and protect themselves. They''re very popular Pokémon in the Galar region.'),
    (589, 'white', 'These Pokémon evolve by wearing the shell covering of a Shelmet. The steel armor protects their whole body.'),
    (589, 'white-2', 'Wearing the shell covering they stole from Shelmet, they defend themselves and attack with two lances.'),
    (589, 'x', 'Wearing the shell covering they stole from Shelmet, they defend themselves and attack with two lances.'),
    (589, 'y', 'These Pokémon evolve by wearing the shell covering of a Shelmet. The steel armor protects their whole body.'),
    (590, 'alpha-sapphire', 'It lures Pokémon with its pattern that looks just like a Poké Ball, then releases poison spores.'),
    (590, 'black', 'It lures people in with its Poké Ball pattern, then releases poison spores. Why it resembles a Poké Ball is unknown.'),
    (590, 'black-2', 'It lures Pokémon with its pattern that looks just like a Poké Ball then releases poison spores.'),
    (590, 'legends-za', 'It lures targets in with its Poké Ball-like pattern and sprays poison spores at them. Why it resembles a Poké Ball is unknown.'),
    (590, 'omega-ruby', 'It lures people in with its Poké Ball pattern, then releases poison spores. Why it resembles a Poké Ball is unknown.'),
    (590, 'scarlet', 'There is a theory that the developer of the modern-day Poké Ball really liked Foongus, but this has not been confirmed.'),
    (590, 'shield', 'The spores released from this Pokémon''s hands are highly poisonous, but when thoroughly dried, the spores can be used as stomach medicine.'),
    (590, 'sword', 'No one knows what the Poké Ball-like pattern on Foongus means or why Foongus has it.'),
    (590, 'violet', 'This Pokémon prefers damp places. It spurts out poison spores to repel approaching enemies.'),
    (590, 'white', 'For some reason, this Pokémon resembles a Poké Ball. They release poison spores to repel those who try to catch them.'),
    (590, 'white-2', 'It lures Pokémon with its pattern that looks just like a Poké Ball then releases poison spores.'),
    (590, 'x', 'It lures people in with its Poké Ball pattern, then releases poison spores. Why it resembles a Poké Ball is unknown.'),
    (590, 'y', 'It lures Pokémon with its pattern that looks just like a Poké Ball, then releases poison spores.'),
    (591, 'alpha-sapphire', 'It lures prey close by dancing and waving its arm caps, which resemble Poké Balls, in a swaying motion.'),
    (591, 'black', 'It lures prey close by dancing and waving its arm caps, which resemble Poké Balls, in a swaying motion.'),
    (591, 'black-2', 'It moves the caps on both arms and does a dance to lure prey. It prefers damp places.'),
    (591, 'legends-za', 'They show off their Poké Ball caps in an attempt to lure prey close, but few Pokémon are fooled.'),
    (591, 'omega-ruby', 'They show off their Poké Ball caps to lure prey, but very few Pokémon are fooled by this.'),
    (591, 'scarlet', 'Be wary of the poisonous spores it releases. Mushrooms resembling Amoonguss’s caps will grow out of anywhere the spores touch.'),
    (591, 'shield', 'Amoonguss generally doesn''t move as much. It tends to stand still near Poké Balls that have been dropped on the ground.'),
    (591, 'sword', 'This Pokémon puffs poisonous spores at its foes. If the spores aren''t washed off quickly, they''ll grow into mushrooms wherever they land.'),
    (591, 'violet', 'Amoonguss mimics Poké Balls. It is not yet clear whether this mimicry is effective against other Pokémon.'),
    (591, 'white', 'They show off their Poké Ball caps to lure prey, but very few Pokémon are fooled by this.'),
    (591, 'white-2', 'It moves the caps on both arms and does a dance to lure prey. It prefers damp places.'),
    (591, 'x', 'They show off their Poké Ball caps to lure prey, but very few Pokémon are fooled by this.'),
    (591, 'y', 'It lures prey close by dancing and waving its arm caps, which resemble Poké Balls, in a swaying motion.'),
    (592, 'alpha-sapphire', 'If its veil-like arms stun and wrap a foe, that foe will be dragged miles below the surface, never to return.'),
    (592, 'black', 'With its thin, veil-like arms wrapped around the body of its opponent, it sinks to the ocean floor.'),
    (592, 'black-2', 'If its veil-like arms stun and wrap a foe, that foe will be dragged miles below the surface, never to return.'),
    (592, 'omega-ruby', 'They paralyze prey with poison, then drag them down to their lairs, five miles below the surface.'),
    (592, 'shield', 'Its thin, veillike arms have tens of thousands of poisonous stingers. Females have slightly longer stingers.*'),
    (592, 'shield', 'Legend has it that the residents of a sunken ancient city changed into these Pokémon.*'),
    (592, 'sword', 'It envelops its prey in its veillike arms and draws it down to the deeps, five miles below the ocean''s surface.'),
    (592, 'ultra-moon', 'Using the invisible poison spikes on its veillike arms and legs, it paralyzes its enemies and causes them to drown.'),
    (592, 'ultra-sun', 'It wraps its veillike arms and legs around prey swimming by and drags them down to the depths of the ocean.'),
    (592, 'white', 'They paralyze prey with poison, then drag them down to their lairs, five miles below the surface.'),
    (592, 'white-2', 'If its veil-like arms stun and wrap a foe, that foe will be dragged miles below the surface, never to return.'),
    (592, 'x', 'They paralyze prey with poison, then drag them down to their lairs, five miles below the surface.'),
    (592, 'y', 'If its veil-like arms stun and wrap a foe, that foe will be dragged miles below the surface, never to return.'),
    (593, 'alpha-sapphire', 'The fate of the ships and crew that wander into Jellicent''s habitat: all sunken, all lost, all vanished.'),
    (593, 'black', 'The fate of the ships and crew that wander into Jellicent''s habitat: all sunken, all lost, all vanished.'),
    (593, 'black-2', 'Its body is mostly seawater. It''s said there''s a castle of ships Jellicent have sunk on the seafloor.'),
    (593, 'omega-ruby', 'Its body is mostly seawater. It''s said there''s a castle of ships Jellicent have sunk on the seafloor.'),
    (593, 'shield', 'Whenever a full moon hangs in the night sky, schools of Jellicent gather near the surface of the sea, waiting for their prey to appear.*'),
    (593, 'shield', 'The crown on its head gets bigger and bigger as it absorbs more and more of the life-force of other creatures.*'),
    (593, 'sword', 'These Pokémon have body compositions that are mostly identical to seawater. They make their lairs from sunken ships.*'),
    (593, 'sword', 'Most of this Pokémon''s body composition is identical to sea water. It makes sunken ships its lair.*'),
    (593, 'ultra-moon', 'Fishermen are terrified of Jellicent. It''s rumored to drag them into the sea and steal their lives away.'),
    (593, 'ultra-sun', 'Jellicent is always hanging around fancy cruise ships and tankers, hoping to drag away its prey.'),
    (593, 'white', 'They propel themselves by expelling absorbed seawater from their bodies. Their favorite food is life energy.'),
    (593, 'white-2', 'Its body is mostly seawater. It''s said there''s a castle of ships Jellicent have sunk on the seafloor.'),
    (593, 'x', 'Its body is mostly seawater. It''s said there''s a castle of ships Jellicent have sunk on the seafloor.'),
