    (621, 'alpha-sapphire', 'It warms its body by absorbing sunlight with its wings. When its body temperature falls, it can no longer move.'),
    (621, 'black', 'It warms its body by absorbing sunlight with its wings. When its body temperature falls, it can no longer move.'),
    (621, 'black-2', 'It runs through the narrow tunnels formed by Excadrill and Onix. It uses its sharp claws to catch prey.'),
    (621, 'omega-ruby', 'It races through narrow caves, using its sharp claws to catch prey. The skin on its face is harder than a rock.'),
    (621, 'shield', 'Druddigon are vicious and cunning. They take up residence in nests dug out by other Pokémon, treating the stolen nests as their own lairs.'),
    (621, 'sword', 'Druddigon lives in caves, but it never skips sunbathing—it won''t be able to move if its body gets too cold.'),
    (621, 'ultra-moon', 'It infiltrates tunnels that Pokémon like Diglett and Dugtrio have dug and quietly waits for prey to pass through.'),
    (621, 'ultra-sun', 'The red skin on its face is harder than rock. In narrow caves, it squares off against its enemies and charges face-first right into them.'),
    (621, 'white', 'It races through narrow caves, using its sharp claws to catch prey. The skin on its face is harder than a rock.'),
    (621, 'white-2', 'It runs through the narrow tunnels formed by Excadrill and Onix. It uses its sharp claws to catch prey.'),
    (621, 'x', 'It races through narrow caves, using its sharp claws to catch prey. The skin on its face is harder than a rock.'),
    (621, 'y', 'It warms its body by absorbing sunlight with its wings. When its body temperature falls, it can no longer move.'),
    (622, 'alpha-sapphire', 'Ancient science fashioned this Pokémon from clay. It''s been active for thousands of years.'),
    (622, 'black', 'The energy that burns inside it enables it to move, but no one has yet been able to identify this energy.'),
    (622, 'black-2', 'Ancient science fashioned this Pokémon from clay. It''s been active for thousands of years.'),
    (622, 'legends-za', 'Ancient people apparently fashioned Golett out of clay to do their labor for them. What powers these Pokémon remains unclear.'),
    (622, 'omega-ruby', 'The energy that burns inside it enables it to move, but no one has yet been able to identify this energy.'),
    (622, 'scarlet', 'These Pokémon are thought to have been created by the science of an ancient and mysterious civilization.'),
    (622, 'shield', 'This Pokémon was created from clay. It received orders from its master many thousands of years ago, and it still follows those orders to this day.'),
    (622, 'sword', 'They were sculpted from clay in ancient times. No one knows why, but some of them are driven to continually line up boulders.'),
    (622, 'ultra-moon', 'Although ancient people apparently built it by working with clay, the source of its energy is unclear.'),
    (622, 'ultra-sun', 'Its movements are powered by a mysterious energy. It has continued to move since ancient times, so its power may soon run out.'),
    (622, 'violet', 'Its movements are powered by a mysterious energy. It has continued to move since ancient times, so its power may soon run out.'),
    (622, 'white', 'These Pokémon are thought to have been created by the science of an ancient and mysterious civilization.'),
    (622, 'white-2', 'Ancient science fashioned this Pokémon from clay. It''s been active for thousands of years.'),
    (622, 'x', 'The energy that burns inside it enables it to move, but no one has yet been able to identify this energy.'),
    (622, 'y', 'Ancient science fashioned this Pokémon from clay. It''s been active for thousands of years.'),
    (623, 'alpha-sapphire', 'It flies across the sky at Mach speeds. Removing the seal on its chest makes its internal energy go out of control.'),
    (623, 'black', 'It flies across the sky at Mach speeds. Removing the seal on its chest makes its internal energy go out of control.'),
    (623, 'black-2', 'Golurk were created to protect people and Pokémon. They run on a mysterious energy.'),
    (623, 'legends-za', 'It''s said that inside Golurk is a perpetual motion machine that produces energy, but the truth is not yet known.'),
    (623, 'omega-ruby', 'It is said that Golurk were ordered to protect people and Pokémon by the ancient people who made them.'),
    (623, 'scarlet', 'When the seal on its chest is removed, it rages indiscriminately. During such rampages, it can turn a whole town into a mountain of rubble.'),
    (623, 'shield', 'There''s a theory that inside Golurk is a perpetual motion machine that produces limitless energy, but this belief hasn''t been proven.'),
    (623, 'sword', 'Artillery platforms built into the walls of ancient castles served as perches from which Golurk could fire energy beams.'),
    (623, 'ultra-moon', 'When the seal on its chest is removed, it rages indiscriminately, turning the whole town around it into a mountain of rubble.'),
    (623, 'ultra-sun', 'Some say that ancient people invented Golurk to serve as a laborer. It follows its master''s orders faithfully.'),
    (623, 'violet', 'Golurk were created by ancient people to protect both people and Pokémon. They run on a mysterious energy.'),
    (623, 'white', 'It is said that Golurk were ordered to protect people and Pokémon by the ancient people who made them.'),
    (623, 'white-2', 'Golurk were created to protect people and Pokémon. They run on a mysterious energy.'),
    (623, 'x', 'It is said that Golurk were ordered to protect people and Pokémon by the ancient people who made them.'),
    (623, 'y', 'It flies across the sky at Mach speeds. Removing the seal on its chest makes its internal energy go out of control.'),
    (624, 'alpha-sapphire', 'Ignoring their injuries, groups attack by sinking the blades that cover their bodies into their prey.'),
    (624, 'black', 'Blades comprise this Pokémon''s entire body. If battling dulls the blades, it sharpens them on stones by the river.'),
    (624, 'black-2', 'Ignoring their injuries, groups attack by sinking the blades that cover their bodies into their prey.'),
    (624, 'omega-ruby', 'Blades comprise this Pokémon''s entire body. If battling dulls the blades, it sharpens them on stones by the river.'),
    (624, 'scarlet', 'Pawniard will fearlessly challenge even powerful foes. In a pinch, it will cling to opponents and pierce them with the blades all over its body.'),
    (624, 'shield', 'A pack of these Pokémon forms to serve a Bisharp boss. Each Pawniard trains diligently, dreaming of one day taking the lead.'),
    (624, 'sword', 'It uses river stones to maintain the cutting edges of the blades covering its body. These sharpened blades allow it to bring down opponents.'),
    (624, 'ultra-moon', 'It follows Bisharp''s orders to a tee when it attacks enemies. After slashing an opponent, Pawniard clangs both of its blades together.'),
    (624, 'ultra-sun', 'After shredding its prey, it sharpens its blades on a stone by the river. Each Pawniard has its own favorite sharpening stone.'),
    (624, 'violet', 'Any chips in its blades would prove fatal for it. After each battle, it diligently maintains its blades using its favorite sharpening stone.'),
    (624, 'white', 'They fight at Bisharp''s command. They cling to their prey and inflict damage by sinking their blades into it.'),
    (624, 'white-2', 'Ignoring their injuries, groups attack by sinking the blades that cover their bodies into their prey.'),
    (624, 'x', 'Blades comprise this Pokémon''s entire body. If battling dulls the blades, it sharpens them on stones by the river.'),
    (624, 'y', 'Ignoring their injuries, groups attack by sinking the blades that cover their bodies into their prey.'),
    (625, 'alpha-sapphire', 'Bisharp pursues prey in the company of a large group of Pawniard. Then Bisharp finishes off the prey.'),
    (625, 'black', 'It leads a group of Pawniard. It battles to become the boss, but will be driven from the group if it loses.'),
    (625, 'black-2', 'This pitiless Pokémon commands a group of Pawniard to hound prey into immobility. It then moves in to finish the prey off.'),
    (625, 'omega-ruby', 'This pitiless Pokémon commands a group of Pawniard to hound prey into immobility. It then moves in to finish the prey off.'),
    (625, 'scarlet', 'This Pokémon commands a group of several Pawniard. Groups that are defeated in territorial disputes are absorbed by the winning side.'),
    (625, 'shield', 'Violent conflicts erupt between Bisharp and Fraxure over places where sharpening stones can be found.'),
    (625, 'sword', 'It''s accompanied by a large retinue of Pawniard. Bisharp keeps a keen eye on its minions, ensuring none of them even think of double-crossing it.'),
    (625, 'ultra-moon', 'It leads a group of Pawniard. Bisharp doesn''t even change its expression when it deals the finishing blow to an opponent.'),
    (625, 'ultra-sun', 'No matter how strong the Bisharp, it''s said that if the blade on its head is chipped, it will retire from its position as the boss.'),
    (625, 'violet', 'Bisharp mercilessly cuts its opponents to pieces with the sharp blades covering its body. It will do anything to win.'),
    (625, 'white', 'Bisharp pursues prey in the company of a large group of Pawniard. Then Bisharp finishes off the prey.'),
    (625, 'white-2', 'This pitiless Pokémon commands a group of Pawniard to hound prey into immobility. It then moves in to finish the prey off.'),
    (625, 'x', 'This pitiless Pokémon commands a group of Pawniard to hound prey into immobility. It then moves in to finish the prey off.'),
    (625, 'y', 'Bisharp pursues prey in the company of a large group of Pawniard. Then Bisharp finishes off the prey.'),
    (626, 'alpha-sapphire', 'Their fluffy fur absorbs damage, even if they strike foes with a fierce headbutt.'),
    (626, 'black', 'Their fluffy fur absorbs damage, even if they strike foes with a fierce headbutt.'),
    (626, 'black-2', 'They are known to charge so wildly that if a train were to enter their territory, they would send it flying.'),
    (626, 'omega-ruby', 'They charge wildly and headbutt everything. Their headbutts have enough destructive force to derail a train.'),
    (626, 'shield', 'These Pokémon live in herds of about 20 individuals. Bouffalant that betray the herd will lose the hair on their heads for some reason.'),
    (626, 'sword', 'These Pokémon can crush a car with no more than a headbutt. Bouffalant with more hair on their heads hold higher positions within the herd.'),
    (626, 'white', 'They charge wildly and headbutt everything. Their headbutts have enough destructive force to derail a train.'),
    (626, 'white-2', 'They are known to charge so wildly that if a train were to enter their territory, they would send it flying.'),
    (626, 'x', 'They charge wildly and headbutt everything. Their headbutts have enough destructive force to derail a train.'),
    (626, 'y', 'Their fluffy fur absorbs damage, even if they strike foes with a fierce headbutt.'),
    (627, 'alpha-sapphire', 'They will challenge anything, even strong opponents, without fear. Their frequent fights help them become stronger.'),
    (627, 'black', 'They crush berries with their talons. They bravely stand up to any opponent, no matter how strong it is.'),
    (627, 'black-2', 'It stands up to massive opponents, not out of courage, but out of recklessness. But that is how it gets stronger.'),
    (627, 'legends-arceus', 'Its chick-like looks belie its hotheadedness. It challenges its parents at every opportunity, desperate to prove its strength.'),
    (627, 'moon', 'With its sharp claws, this Pokémon pierces its prey, and then it pecks at them. Although it also consumes berries, it''s a carnivore at heart.'),
    (627, 'omega-ruby', 'They crush berries with their talons. They bravely stand up to any opponent, no matter how strong it is.'),
    (627, 'scarlet', 'They pick fights indiscriminately. They grow stronger and more powerful each time they faint or are injured.'),
    (627, 'shield', 'A combative Pokémon, it''s ready to pick a fight with anyone. It has talons that can crush hard berries.'),
    (627, 'sun', 'They pick fights indiscriminately. They grow stronger and more powerful each time they faint or are injured.'),
    (627, 'sword', 'If it spies a strong Pokémon, Rufflet can''t resist challenging it to a battle. But if Rufflet loses, it starts bawling.'),
    (627, 'ultra-moon', 'Known as a natural-born warrior, soon after its hatching, it will challenge its parent to a fight in order to gain their acceptance.'),
    (627, 'ultra-sun', 'With its powerful legs and sturdy claws, it can crack even the hard shells of Shellder and pluck out their insides.'),
    (627, 'violet', 'With its sharp claws, this Pokémon pierces its prey, and then it pecks at them. Although it also consumes berries, it''s a carnivore at heart.'),
    (627, 'white', 'They will challenge anything, even strong opponents, without fear. Their frequent fights help them become stronger.'),
    (627, 'white-2', 'It stands up to massive opponents, not out of courage, but out of recklessness. But that is how it gets stronger.'),
    (627, 'x', 'They crush berries with their talons. They bravely stand up to any opponent, no matter how strong it is.'),
    (627, 'y', 'They will challenge anything, even strong opponents, without fear. Their frequent fights help them become stronger.'),
    (628, 'alpha-sapphire', 'They fight for their friends without any thought about danger to themselves. One can carry a car while flying.'),
    (628, 'black', 'They fight for their friends without any thought about danger to themselves. One can carry a car while flying.'),
    (628, 'black-2', 'For the sake of its friends, this brave warrior of the sky will not stop battling, even if injured.'),
    (628, 'moon', 'It''s thought that people disturbed their habitats in the past, so Braviary banded together to fight back.'),
    (628, 'omega-ruby', 'For the sake of its friends, this brave warrior of the sky will not stop battling, even if injured.'),
    (628, 'shield', 'Because this Pokémon is hotheaded and belligerent, it''s Corviknight that''s taken the role of transportation in Galar.'),
    (628, 'sun', 'With its brave disposition, it fears nothing—not even death. Ancient Alolan people respected it, referring to it as "the hero of the sky."'),
    (628, 'sword', 'Known for its bravery and pride, this majestic Pokémon is often seen as a motif for various kinds of emblems.'),
    (628, 'ultra-moon', 'Known as “the hero of the skies,” this Pokémon is so proud and so brave that it will never retreat, even when it''s injured.'),
    (628, 'ultra-sun', 'The more scars it has on its front, the more heroic it''s considered to be. Those with many scars on their back are mocked by the flock.'),
    (628, 'white', 'The more scars they have, the more respect these brave soldiers of the sky get from their peers.'),
    (628, 'white-2', 'For the sake of its friends, this brave warrior of the sky will not stop battling, even if injured.'),
    (628, 'x', 'For the sake of its friends, this brave warrior of the sky will not stop battling, even if injured.'),
    (628, 'y', 'They fight for their friends without any thought about danger to themselves. One can carry a car while flying.'),
    (629, 'alpha-sapphire', 'Their wings are too tiny to allow them to fly. They guard their posteriors with bones that were gathered by Mandibuzz.'),
    (629, 'black', 'Its wings are too tiny to allow it to fly. As the time approaches for it to evolve, it discards the bones it was wearing.'),
    (629, 'black-2', 'Their wings are too tiny to allow them to fly. They guard their posteriors with bones that were gathered by Mandibuzz.'),
    (629, 'moon', 'It can''t fly yet and must wait until its wings have developed more. Since it''s still at a playful age, it hops around friskily.'),
    (629, 'omega-ruby', 'Its wings are too tiny to allow it to fly. As the time approaches for it to evolve, it discards the bones it was wearing.'),
    (629, 'scarlet', 'They tend to guard their posteriors with suitable bones they have found. They pursue weak Pokémon.'),
    (629, 'shield', 'Vullaby grow quickly. Bones that have gotten too small for older Vullaby to wear often get passed down to younger ones in the nest.'),
    (629, 'sun', 'It protects its plump posterior with the bones of prey it has consumed. As it grows, it replaces the bones.'),
    (629, 'sword', 'It wears a bone to protect its rear. It often squabbles with others of its kind over particularly comfy bones.'),
    (629, 'ultra-moon', 'Its healthy appetite leads to visible growth spurts. It often has to replace the bones it wears as its size increases.'),
    (629, 'ultra-sun', 'Mandibuzz gives it the bones it wears. Vullaby''s wings are short, so it can''t fly yet, but it jumps around, dreaming of wide open skies.'),
    (629, 'violet', 'Its healthy appetite leads to visible growth spurts. It often has to replace the bones it wears as its size increases.'),
    (629, 'white', 'They tend to guard their posteriors with suitable bones they have found. They pursue weak Pokémon.'),
    (629, 'white-2', 'Their wings are too tiny to allow them to fly. They guard their posteriors with bones that were gathered by Mandibuzz.'),
    (629, 'x', 'Its wings are too tiny to allow it to fly. As the time approaches for it to evolve, it discards the bones it was wearing.'),
    (629, 'y', 'Their wings are too tiny to allow them to fly. They guard their posteriors with bones that were gathered by Mandibuzz.'),
    (630, 'alpha-sapphire', 'Watching from the sky, they swoop to strike weakened Pokémon on the ground. They decorate themselves with bones.'),
    (630, 'black', 'It makes a nest out of bones it finds. It grabs weakened prey in its talons and hauls it to its nest of bones.'),
    (630, 'black-2', 'They fly in circles around the sky. When they spot prey, they attack and carry it back to their nest with ease.'),
    (630, 'moon', 'It circles in the sky, keeping a keen eye out for Pokémon in a weakened state. Its choicest food is Cubone.'),
    (630, 'omega-ruby', 'They fly in circles around the sky. When they spot prey, they attack and carry it back to their nest with ease.'),
    (630, 'scarlet', 'It''s always searching for food for Vullaby. When it finds a weak Pokémon, Mandibuzz swoops it right off to its nest.'),
    (630, 'shield', 'They adorn themselves with bones. There seem to be fashion trends among them, as different bones come into and fall out of popularity.'),
    (630, 'sun', 'They adorn themselves beautifully with bones. This is supposedly an effort to attract males, but no male Mandibuzz have ever been found.'),
    (630, 'sword', 'Although it''s a bit of a ruffian, this Pokémon will take lost Vullaby under its wing and care for them till they''re ready to leave the nest.'),
    (630, 'ultra-moon', 'It''s always searching for food for Vullaby. When it finds a weak Pokémon, Mandibuzz swoops it right off to its nest.'),
    (630, 'ultra-sun', 'It skillfully arranges the bones of its prey to construct its nest. Most of the bones are Cubone.'),
    (630, 'violet', 'Watching from the sky, they attack weakened prey on the ground. They have a habit of decorating themselves with bones.'),
    (630, 'white', 'Watching from the sky, they swoop to strike weakened Pokémon on the ground. They decorate themselves with bones.'),
    (630, 'white-2', 'They fly in circles around the sky. When they spot prey, they attack and carry it back to their nest with ease.'),
    (630, 'x', 'They fly in circles around the sky. When they spot prey, they attack and carry it back to their nest with ease.'),
    (630, 'y', 'Watching from the sky, they swoop to strike weakened Pokémon on the ground. They decorate themselves with bones.'),
    (631, 'alpha-sapphire', 'It draws in air through its tail, transforms it into fire, and uses it like a tongue. It melts Durant and eats them.'),
    (631, 'black', 'It breathes through a hole in its tail while it burns with an internal fire. Durant is its prey.'),
    (631, 'black-2', 'It draws in air through its tail, transforms it into fire, and uses it like a tongue. It melts Durant and eats them.'),
    (631, 'omega-ruby', 'Using their very hot, flame-covered tongues, they burn through Durant''s steel bodies and consume their insides.'),
    (631, 'shield', 'A flame serves as its tongue, melting through the hard shell of Durant so that Heatmor can devour their insides.'),
    (631, 'sword', 'There''s a hole in its tail that allows it to draw in the air it needs to keep its fire burning. If the hole gets blocked, this Pokémon will fall ill.'),
    (631, 'white', 'Using their very hot, flame-covered tongues, they burn through Durant''s steel bodies and consume their insides.'),
    (631, 'white-2', 'It draws in air through its tail, transforms it into fire, and uses it like a tongue. It melts Durant and eats them.'),
    (631, 'x', 'Using their very hot, flame-covered tongues, they burn through Durant''s steel bodies and consume their insides.'),
    (631, 'y', 'It draws in air through its tail, transforms it into fire, and uses it like a tongue. It melts Durant and eats them.'),
    (632, 'alpha-sapphire', 'They attack in groups, covering themselves in steel armor to protect themselves from Heatmor.'),
    (632, 'black', 'They attack in groups, covering themselves in steel armor to protect themselves from Heatmor.'),
    (632, 'black-2', 'Individuals each play different roles in driving Heatmor, their natural predator, away from their colony.'),
    (632, 'omega-ruby', 'Individuals each play different roles in driving Heatmor, their natural predator, away from their colony.'),
    (632, 'shield', 'With their large mandibles, these Pokémon can crunch their way through rock. They work together to protect their eggs from Sandaconda.'),
    (632, 'sword', 'They lay their eggs deep inside their nests. When attacked by Heatmor, they retaliate using their massive mandibles.'),
    (632, 'white', 'Durant dig nests in mountains. They build their complicated, interconnected tunnels into mazes.'),
    (632, 'white-2', 'Individuals each play different roles in driving Heatmor, their natural predator, away from their colony.'),
    (632, 'x', 'Individuals each play different roles in driving Heatmor, their natural predator, away from their colony.'),
    (632, 'y', 'They attack in groups, covering themselves in steel armor to protect themselves from Heatmor.'),
    (633, 'alpha-sapphire', 'Lacking sight, it''s unaware of its surroundings, so it bumps into things and eats anything that moves.'),
    (633, 'black', 'It tends to bite everything, and it is not a picky eater. Approaching it carelessly is dangerous.'),
    (633, 'black-2', 'Lacking sight, it''s unaware of its surroundings, so it bumps into things and eats anything that moves.'),
    (633, 'omega-ruby', 'They cannot see, so they tackle and bite to learn about their surroundings. Their bodies are covered in wounds.'),
    (633, 'scarlet', 'It can’t see, so its first approach to examining things is to bite them. You will be covered in wounds until a Deino warms up to you.'),
    (633, 'shield', 'Because it can''t see, this Pokémon is constantly biting at everything it touches, trying to keep track of its surroundings.'),
    (633, 'sword', 'When it encounters something, its first urge is usually to bite it. If it likes what it tastes, it will commit the associated scent to memory.'),
    (633, 'violet', 'It nests deep inside a cave. Food there is scarce, so Deino will sink its teeth into anything that moves and attempt to eat it.'),
    (633, 'white', 'They cannot see, so they tackle and bite to learn about their surroundings. Their bodies are covered in wounds.'),
    (633, 'white-2', 'Lacking sight, it''s unaware of its surroundings, so it bumps into things and eats anything that moves.'),
    (633, 'x', 'They cannot see, so they tackle and bite to learn about their surroundings. Their bodies are covered in wounds.'),
    (633, 'y', 'Lacking sight, it''s unaware of its surroundings, so it bumps into things and eats anything that moves.'),
    (634, 'alpha-sapphire', 'After it has eaten up all the food in its territory, it moves to another area. Its two heads do not get along.'),
    (634, 'black', 'After it has eaten up all the food in its territory, it moves to another area. Its two heads do not get along.'),
    (634, 'black-2', 'The two heads do not get along. Whichever head eats more than the other gets to be the leader.'),
    (634, 'omega-ruby', 'The two heads do not get along. Whichever head eats more than the other gets to be the leader.'),
    (634, 'scarlet', 'The two heads do not get along at all. If you don’t give each head the same amount of attention, they’ll begin fighting out of jealousy.'),
    (634, 'shield', 'Their two heads will fight each other over a single piece of food. Zweilous are covered in scars even without battling others.'),
    (634, 'sword', 'While hunting for prey, Zweilous wanders its territory, its two heads often bickering over which way to go.'),
    (634, 'violet', 'The two heads have different likes and dislikes. Because the heads fight with each other, Zweilous gets stronger without needing to rely on others.'),
    (634, 'white', 'Since their two heads do not get along and compete with each other for food, they always eat too much.'),
    (634, 'white-2', 'The two heads do not get along. Whichever head eats more than the other gets to be the leader.'),
    (634, 'x', 'The two heads do not get along. Whichever head eats more than the other gets to be the leader.'),
    (634, 'y', 'After it has eaten up all the food in its territory, it moves to another area. Its two heads do not get along.'),
    (635, 'alpha-sapphire', 'It responds to movement by attacking. This scary, three-headed Pokémon devours everything in its path!'),
    (635, 'black', 'This brutal Pokémon travels the skies on its six wings. Anything that moves seems like a foe to it, triggering its attack.'),
    (635, 'black-2', 'It responds to movement by attacking. This scary, three-headed Pokémon devours everything in its path!'),
    (635, 'omega-ruby', 'The heads on their arms do not have brains. They use all three heads to consume and destroy everything.'),
    (635, 'scarlet', 'Only the central head has a brain. It is very intelligent, but it thinks only of destruction.'),
    (635, 'shield', 'The three heads take turns sinking their teeth into the opponent. Their attacks won''t slow until their target goes down.'),
    (635, 'sword', 'There are a slew of stories about villages that were destroyed by Hydreigon. It bites anything that moves.'),
    (635, 'violet', 'It''s said that Hydreigon grew ferocious because people in times long past loathed it, considering it to be evil incarnate and attacking it relentlessly.'),
    (635, 'white', 'The heads on their arms do not have brains. They use all three heads to consume and destroy everything.'),
    (635, 'white-2', 'It responds to movement by attacking. This scary, three-headed Pokémon devours everything in its path!'),
    (635, 'x', 'The heads on their arms do not have brains. They use all three heads to consume and destroy everything.'),
    (635, 'y', 'It responds to movement by attacking. This scary, three-headed Pokémon devours everything in its path!'),
    (636, 'alpha-sapphire', 'The base of volcanoes is where they make their homes. They shoot fire from their five horns to repel attacking enemies.'),
    (636, 'black', 'This Pokémon was believed to have been born from the sun. When it evolves, its entire body is engulfed in flames.'),
    (636, 'black-2', 'Said to have been born from the sun, it spews fire from its horns and encases itself in a cocoon of fire when it evolves.'),
    (636, 'omega-ruby', 'Said to have been born from the sun, it spews fire from its horns and encases itself in a cocoon of fire when it evolves.'),
    (636, 'scarlet', 'This Pokémon was called the Larva That Stole the Sun. The fire Larvesta spouts from its horns can cut right through a sheet of iron.'),
    (636, 'shield', 'Larvesta''s body is warm all over. It spouts fire from the tips of its horns to intimidate predators and scare prey.'),
    (636, 'sword', 'The people of ancient times believed that Larvesta fell from the sun.'),
    (636, 'ultra-moon', 'It protects itself with flame. Long years ago, people believed Larvesta had a nest on the sun.'),
    (636, 'ultra-sun', 'When battling opponents, it sprays fire from its five horns. The max temperature of the flames can reach nearly 5,500 degrees Fahrenheit.'),
    (636, 'violet', 'In ancient times, Larvesta was worshiped as the emissary of the sun. However, it was also viewed as a burden since it often caused forest fires.'),
    (636, 'white', 'The base of volcanoes is where they make their homes. They shoot fire from their five horns to repel attacking enemies.'),
    (636, 'white-2', 'Said to have been born from the sun, it spews fire from its horns and encases itself in a cocoon of fire when it evolves.'),
    (636, 'x', 'Said to have been born from the sun, it spews fire from its horns and encases itself in a cocoon of fire when it evolves.'),
    (636, 'y', 'The base of volcanoes is where they make their homes. They shoot fire from their five horns to repel attacking enemies.'),
    (637, 'alpha-sapphire', 'When volcanic ash darkened the atmosphere, it is said that Volcarona''s fire provided a replacement for the sun.'),
    (637, 'black', 'When volcanic ash darkened the atmosphere, it is said that Volcarona''s fire provided a replacement for the sun.'),
    (637, 'black-2', 'Thought to be an embodiment of the sun, it appeared during a bitterly cold winter and saved Pokémon from freezing.'),
    (637, 'omega-ruby', 'A sea of fire engulfs the surroundings of their battles, since they use their six wings to scatter their ember scales.'),
    (637, 'scarlet', 'Its burning body causes it to be unpopular in hot parts of the world, but in cold ones, Volcarona is revered as an embodiment of the sun.'),
    (637, 'shield', 'This Pokémon emerges from a cocoon formed of raging flames. Ancient murals depict Volcarona as a deity of fire.'),
    (637, 'sword', 'Volcarona scatters burning scales. Some say it does this to start fires. Others say it''s trying to rescue those that suffer in the cold.'),
    (637, 'ultra-moon', 'According to legends, it was hatched from a flaming cocoon to save people and Pokémon that were suffering from the cold.'),
    (637, 'ultra-sun', 'As it flies, it scatters its flaming scales. It was feared by ancient people, who referred to it as "the rage of the sun."'),
    (637, 'violet', 'This Pokémon scatters burning scales. Most of the danger of these scales is not in their heat—it''s in the way they rob the surrounding air of oxygen.'),
    (637, 'white', 'A sea of fire engulfs the surroundings of their battles, since they use their six wings to scatter their ember scales.'),
    (637, 'white-2', 'Thought to be an embodiment of the sun, it appeared during a bitterly cold winter and saved Pokémon from freezing.'),
    (637, 'x', 'A sea of fire engulfs the surroundings of their battles, since they use their six wings to scatter their ember scales.'),
    (637, 'y', 'When volcanic ash darkened the atmosphere, it is said that Volcarona''s fire provided a replacement for the sun.'),
    (638, 'alpha-sapphire', 'It has a body and heart of steel. It worked with its allies to punish people when they hurt Pokémon.'),
    (638, 'black', 'This legendary Pokémon battled against humans to protect Pokémon. Its personality is calm and composed.'),
    (638, 'black-2', 'It has a body and heart of steel. It worked with its allies to punish people when they hurt Pokémon.'),
    (638, 'legends-za', 'It has a body and heart of steel. One glare from Cobalion can bring even the most ferocious of Pokémon to heel.'),
    (638, 'omega-ruby', 'It has a body and heart of steel. Its glare is sufficient to make even an unruly Pokémon obey it.'),
    (638, 'shield', 'From the moment it''s born, this Pokémon radiates the air of a leader. Its presence will calm even vicious foes.'),
    (638, 'sword', 'This Pokémon appears in a legend alongside Terrakion and Virizion, fighting against humans in defense of the Unova region''s Pokémon.'),
    (638, 'white', 'It has a body and heart of steel. Its glare is sufficient to make even an unruly Pokémon obey it.'),
    (638, 'white-2', 'It has a body and heart of steel. It worked with its allies to punish people when they hurt Pokémon.'),
    (638, 'x', 'It has a body and heart of steel. Its glare is sufficient to make even an unruly Pokémon obey it.'),
    (638, 'y', 'It has a body and heart of steel. It worked with its allies to punish people when they hurt Pokémon.'),
    (639, 'alpha-sapphire', 'Spoken of in legend, this Pokémon used its phenomenal power to destroy a castle in its effort to protect Pokémon.'),
    (639, 'black', 'This Pokémon came to the defense of Pokémon that had lost their homes in a war among humans.'),
    (639, 'black-2', 'Spoken of in legend, this Pokémon used its phenomenal power to destroy a castle in its effort to protect Pokémon.'),
    (639, 'legends-za', 'It charges with enough force to break through a giant castle wall in one blow. This Pokémon is spoken of in legends.'),
    (639, 'omega-ruby', 'Its charge is strong enough to break through a giant castle wall in one blow. This Pokémon is spoken of in legends.'),
    (639, 'shield', 'In Unovan legend, Terrakion battled against humans in an effort to protect other Pokémon.'),
    (639, 'sword', 'It has phenomenal power. It will mercilessly crush anyone or anything that bullies small Pokémon.'),
    (639, 'white', 'Its charge is strong enough to break through a giant castle wall in one blow. This Pokémon is spoken of in legends.'),
