    (650, 'alpha-sapphire', 'Such a thick shell of wood covers its head and back that even a direct hit from a truck wouldn''t faze it.'),
    (650, 'legends-za', 'The quills on its head are usually soft. When it flexes them, the points become so hard and sharp that they can pierce rock.'),
    (650, 'omega-ruby', 'The quills on its head are usually soft. When it flexes them, the points become so hard and sharp that they can pierce rock.'),
    (650, 'scarlet', 'When Chespin tenses up just before landing a headbutt, the spikes on its head sharpen to points, piercing the enemy’s body on contact.'),
    (650, 'violet', 'Eating lots of berries makes the bark shell that covers Chespin’s head and body grow sturdier.'),
    (650, 'x', 'The quills on its head are usually soft. When it flexes them, the points become so hard and sharp that they can pierce rock.'),
    (650, 'y', 'Such a thick shell of wood covers its head and back that even a direct hit from a truck wouldn''t faze it.'),
    (651, 'alpha-sapphire', 'They strengthen their lower bodies by running into one another. They are very kind and won''t start fights.'),
    (651, 'legends-za', 'They strengthen their lower bodies by running into one another. They are very kind and won''t start fights.'),
    (651, 'omega-ruby', 'It relies on its sturdy shell to deflect predators'' attacks. It counterattacks with its sharp quills.'),
    (651, 'scarlet', 'It’s protected by a sturdy shell. The shell is also very heavy, which naturally strengthens Quilladin’s lower body.'),
    (651, 'violet', 'It can send a trailer flying with a tackle. It’s numb to pain, so even violent collisions don’t faze it.'),
    (651, 'x', 'It relies on its sturdy shell to deflect predators'' attacks. It counterattacks with its sharp quills.'),
    (651, 'y', 'They strengthen their lower bodies by running into one another. They are very kind and won''t start fights.'),
    (652, 'alpha-sapphire', 'When it takes a defensive posture with its fists guarding its face, it could withstand a bomb blast.'),
    (652, 'legends-za', 'Its tackle is forceful enough to flip a 50-ton tank. It shields its allies from danger with its own body.'),
    (652, 'omega-ruby', 'Its Tackle is forceful enough to flip a 50-ton tank. It shields its allies from danger with its own body.'),
    (652, 'scarlet', 'When its allies are in trouble, Chesnaught creates a shield with its arms and uses its own body to block attacks.'),
    (652, 'violet', 'Its gentle disposition would have it avoid conflict, but it gives opponents a thrashing with its thorned fists when the situation calls for it.'),
    (652, 'x', 'Its Tackle is forceful enough to flip a 50-ton tank. It shields its allies from danger with its own body.'),
    (652, 'y', 'When it takes a defensive posture with its fists guarding its face, it could withstand a bomb blast.'),
    (653, 'alpha-sapphire', 'As it walks, it munches on a twig in place of a snack. It intimidates opponents by puffing hot air out of its ears.'),
    (653, 'legends-za', 'Eating a twig fills it with energy, and its roomy ears give vent to air hotter than 390 degrees Fahrenheit.'),
    (653, 'omega-ruby', 'Eating a twig fills it with energy, and its roomy ears give vent to air hotter than 390 degrees Fahrenheit.'),
    (653, 'scarlet', 'This Pokémon gets worked up easily. Its body can also overheat, so it uses its ears to dissipate the heat and calm down.'),
    (653, 'violet', 'Twigs make for Fennekin’s snacks. When it nibbles on twigs, it finds the courage to face strong foes.'),
    (653, 'x', 'Eating a twig fills it with energy, and its roomy ears give vent to air hotter than 390 degrees Fahrenheit.'),
    (653, 'y', 'As it walks, it munches on a twig in place of a snack. It intimidates opponents by puffing hot air out of its ears.'),
    (654, 'alpha-sapphire', 'When the twig is plucked from its tail, friction sets the twig alight. The flame is used to send signals to its allies.'),
    (654, 'legends-za', 'It keeps a twig in its tail. Using friction from its tail fur, it sets the twig on fire and launches into battle.'),
    (654, 'omega-ruby', 'It has a twig stuck in its tail. With friction from its tail fur, it sets the twig on fire and launches into battle.'),
    (654, 'scarlet', 'It ignites the twig from its tail and waves the twig around to signal its allies. To indicate danger, it draws circles in the air with the twig’s flame.'),
    (654, 'violet', 'Braixen’s branch ignites as it’s pulled from the Pokémon’s tail. Braixen then uses the flame to spark powerful attacks.'),
    (654, 'x', 'It has a twig stuck in its tail. With friction from its tail fur, it sets the twig on fire and launches into battle.'),
    (654, 'y', 'When the twig is plucked from its tail, friction sets the twig alight. The flame is used to send signals to its allies.'),
    (655, 'alpha-sapphire', 'Using psychic power, it generates a fiery vortex of 5,400 degrees Fahrenheit, incinerating foes swept into this whirl of flame.'),
    (655, 'legends-za', 'Using psychic power, it generates a fiery vortex of 5,400 degrees Fahrenheit, incinerating foes swept into this whirl of flame.'),
    (655, 'omega-ruby', 'It gazes into the flame at the tip of its branch to achieve a focused state, which allows it to see into the future.'),
    (655, 'scarlet', 'It leaves burn marks in the ground with the flame at the tip of its wand. Long ago, people used the shapes of these burn marks for divination.'),
    (655, 'violet', 'It controls flames telekinetically, trapping its foes in a fiery vortex surpassing 5,400 degrees Fahrenheit and burning them to a crisp.'),
    (655, 'x', 'It gazes into the flame at the tip of its branch to achieve a focused state, which allows it to see into the future.'),
    (655, 'y', 'Using psychic power, it generates a fiery vortex of 5,400 degrees Fahrenheit, incinerating foes swept into this whirl of flame.'),
    (656, 'alpha-sapphire', 'It protects its skin by covering its body in delicate bubbles. Beneath its happy-go-lucky air, it keeps a watchful eye on its surroundings.'),
    (656, 'legends-za', 'It protects its skin by covering its body in delicate bubbles. Beneath its happy-go-lucky air, it keeps a watchful eye on its surroundings.'),
    (656, 'omega-ruby', 'It secretes flexible bubbles from its chest and back. The bubbles reduce the damage it would otherwise take when attacked.'),
    (656, 'scarlet', 'Its happy-go-lucky look is an act intended to fool its enemies. It will suddenly drop the facade and overwhelm its foes with its blinding speed.'),
    (656, 'violet', 'It utilizes its extraordinary jumping abilities to flummox its foes, throwing springy bubbles at them from above their heads.'),
    (656, 'x', 'It secretes flexible bubbles from its chest and back. The bubbles reduce the damage it would otherwise take when attacked.'),
    (656, 'y', 'It protects its skin by covering its body in delicate bubbles. Beneath its happy-go-lucky air, it keeps a watchful eye on its surroundings.'),
    (657, 'alpha-sapphire', 'Its swiftness is unparalleled. It can scale a tower of more than 2,000 feet in a minute''s time.'),
    (657, 'legends-za', 'Its swiftness is unparalleled. It can scale a tower of more than 2,000 feet in a minute''s time.'),
    (657, 'omega-ruby', 'It can throw bubble-covered pebbles with precise control, hitting empty cans up to a hundred feet away.'),
    (657, 'scarlet', 'It excels at devising battle strategies that make use of the terrain, and it never misses its mark when throwing bubble-covered pebbles.'),
    (657, 'violet', 'The tips of its fingers and toes stick firmly to vertical surfaces. Frogadier can scale skyscrapers with ease.'),
    (657, 'x', 'It can throw bubble-covered pebbles with precise control, hitting empty cans up to a hundred feet away.'),
    (657, 'y', 'Its swiftness is unparalleled. It can scale a tower of more than 2,000 feet in a minute''s time.'),
    (658, 'alpha-sapphire', 'It appears and vanishes with a ninja''s grace. It toys with its enemies using swift movements, while slicing them with throwing stars of sharpest water.'),
    (658, 'legends-za', 'It creates throwing stars out of compressed water. When it spins them and throws them at high speed, these stars can split metal in two.'),
    (658, 'omega-ruby', 'It creates throwing stars out of compressed water. When it spins them and throws them at high speed, these stars can split metal in two.'),
    (658, 'scarlet', 'The movement of air against the long tongue Greninja keeps wrapped around its neck allows it to sense enemies it can’t see.'),
    (658, 'violet', 'It makes shuriken out of mucus excreted from its thighs. These shuriken can cut cleanly through steel cables.'),
    (658, 'x', 'It creates Water Shuriken. When it spins them and throws them at high speed, these stars can split metal in two.'),
    (658, 'y', 'It appears and vanishes with a ninja''s grace. It toys with its enemies using swift movements, while slicing them with throwing stars of sharpest water.'),
    (659, 'alpha-sapphire', 'It has ears like shovels. Digging holes strengthens its ears so much that they can sever thick roots effortlessly.'),
    (659, 'legends-za', 'They use their large ears to dig burrows. They will dig the whole night through without rest.'),
    (659, 'omega-ruby', 'They use their large ears to dig burrows. They will dig the whole night through.'),
    (659, 'shield', 'It''s very sensitive to danger. The sound of Corviknight''s flapping will have Bunnelby digging a hole to hide underground in moments.'),
    (659, 'sword', 'It excels at digging holes. Using its ears, it can dig a nest 33 feet deep in one night.'),
    (659, 'x', 'They use their large ears to dig burrows. They will dig the whole night through.'),
    (659, 'y', 'It has ears like shovels. Digging holes strengthens its ears so much that they can sever thick roots effortlessly.'),
    (660, 'alpha-sapphire', 'As powerful as an excavator, its ears can reduce dense bedrock to rubble. When it''s finished digging, it lounges lazily.'),
    (660, 'legends-za', 'With their powerful ears, they can heft boulders of a ton or more with ease. They can be a big help at construction sites.'),
    (660, 'omega-ruby', 'With their powerful ears, they can heft boulders of a ton or more with ease. They can be a big help at construction sites.'),
    (660, 'shield', 'The fur on its belly retains heat exceptionally well. People used to make heavy winter clothing from fur shed by this Pokémon.'),
    (660, 'sword', 'With power equal to an excavator, it can dig through dense bedrock. It''s a huge help during tunnel construction.'),
    (660, 'x', 'With their powerful ears, they can heft boulders of a ton or more with ease. They can be a big help at construction sites.'),
    (660, 'y', 'As powerful as an excavator, its ears can reduce dense bedrock to rubble. When it''s finished digging, it lounges lazily.'),
    (661, 'alpha-sapphire', 'Despite the beauty of its lilting voice, it''s merciless to intruders that enter its territory.'),
    (661, 'legends-za', 'Despite the beauty of its lilting voice, it''s merciless to intruders that enter its territory.'),
    (661, 'moon', 'When it''s excited, its temperature can double, spiking hormone production in its body.'),
    (661, 'omega-ruby', 'These friendly Pokémon send signals to one another with beautiful chirps and tail-feather movements.'),
    (661, 'scarlet', 'This Pokémon is normally calm, but once it enters battle, its hormonal balance changes and it becomes aggressive.'),
    (661, 'shield', 'When this Pokémon gets excited, its body temperature increases sharply. If you touch a Fletchling with bare hands, you might get burned.'),
    (661, 'sun', 'This amiable Pokémon is easy to train. But when battle is joined, it shows its ferocious side.'),
    (661, 'sword', 'Its melodious cries are actually warnings. Fletchling will mercilessly peck at anything that enters its territory.'),
    (661, 'ultra-moon', 'Its body is always warm. Trainers who live in cold areas apparently sleep with it in their bed.'),
    (661, 'ultra-sun', 'While it''s an amiable Pokémon, if you touch it unexpectedly, it will heat up its body in an instant, and you''ll be burned.'),
    (661, 'violet', 'Fletchling can be found in both rural and urban areas. They once had a huge territorial dispute with Squawkabilly. Fights broke out all over town.'),
    (661, 'x', 'These friendly Pokémon send signals to one another with beautiful chirps and tail-feather movements.'),
    (661, 'y', 'Despite the beauty of its lilting voice, it''s merciless to intruders that enter its territory.'),
    (662, 'alpha-sapphire', 'The hotter the flame sac on its belly, the faster it can fly, but it takes some time to get the fire going.'),
    (662, 'legends-za', 'The hotter the flame sac in its belly, the faster it can fly, but it takes some time to get the fire going.'),
    (662, 'moon', 'It will not tolerate other Fletchinder entering its territory, which has a radius of several miles.'),
    (662, 'omega-ruby', 'From its beak, it expels embers that set the tall grass on fire. Then it pounces on the bewildered prey that pop out of the grass.'),
    (662, 'scarlet', 'Fletchinder scatters embers in tall grass where bug Pokémon might be hiding and then catches them as they come leaping out.'),
    (662, 'shield', 'Fletchinder are exceedingly territorial and aggressive. These Pokémon fight among themselves over feeding grounds.'),
    (662, 'sun', 'From its beak, it fires embers at its prey. Once it has caught them, it grills them at high heat before feasting upon them.'),
    (662, 'sword', 'Fletchinder launches embers into the den of its prey. When the prey comes leaping out, Fletchinder''s sharp talons finish it off.'),
    (662, 'ultra-moon', 'Its speed right after takeoff already puts it in the top speed class of all bird Pokémon.'),
    (662, 'ultra-sun', 'It scatters embers in the tall grass. Then bug Pokémon, frightened by the flames, come flying out, and Fletchinder gobbles them up.'),
    (662, 'violet', 'Its territory has a radius of just over a mile. If any bird Pokémon should enter, it will show them no mercy.'),
    (662, 'x', 'From its beak, it expels embers that set the tall grass on fire. Then it pounces on the bewildered prey that pop out of the grass.'),
    (662, 'y', 'The hotter the flame sac on its belly, the faster it can fly, but it takes some time to get the fire going.'),
    (663, 'alpha-sapphire', 'When attacking prey, it can reach speeds of up to 310 mph. It finishes its prey off with a colossal kick.'),
    (663, 'legends-za', 'In the fever of an exciting battle, it showers embers from the gaps between its feathers as it flies.'),
    (663, 'moon', 'It zooms directly at its prey at flight speeds of close to 310 mph, while fiery embers scatter from gaps in its feathers.'),
    (663, 'omega-ruby', 'In the fever of an exciting battle, it showers embers from the gaps between its feathers and takes to the air.'),
    (663, 'scarlet', 'It has top-notch flying capabilities. It flies around easily, even while carrying prey that weighs more than 220 lbs.'),
    (663, 'shield', 'Talonflame dives toward prey at speeds of up to 310 mph and assaults them with powerful kicks, giving the prey no chance to escape.'),
    (663, 'sun', 'Its favorite foods are Wingull and Pikipek. It attacks with a powerful kick and grasps them firmly in its talons.'),
    (663, 'sword', 'Talonflame mainly preys upon other bird Pokémon. To intimidate opponents, it sends embers spewing from gaps between its feathers.'),
    (663, 'ultra-moon', 'Bird Pokémon make up most of its diet. It approaches at high speeds and smacks them down to the ground with its powerful kick.'),
    (663, 'ultra-sun', 'Its tough wings don''t allow fire to pass through them. A long time ago, firefighters'' outfits were made from Talonflame wings.'),
    (663, 'violet', 'When it gets excited, it vents sparks from the gaps between its feathers. These unburnable feathers are used as a fireproof material.'),
    (663, 'x', 'In the fever of an exciting battle, it showers embers from the gaps between its feathers and takes to the air.'),
    (663, 'y', 'When attacking prey, it can reach speeds of up to 310 mph. It finishes its prey off with a colossal kick.'),
    (664, 'alpha-sapphire', 'The powder that covers its body regulates its temperature, so it can live in any region or climate.'),
    (664, 'legends-za', 'The powder that covers its body regulates its temperature, so it can live in any region or climate.'),
    (664, 'omega-ruby', 'When under attack from bird Pokémon, it spews a poisonous black powder that causes paralysis on contact.'),
    (664, 'scarlet', 'Any poison this Pokémon takes in is converted into a black powder and secreted. That''s why Scatterbug can eat poisonous leaves and roots.'),
    (664, 'violet', 'This Pokémon scatters poisonous powder to repel enemies. It will eat different plants depending on where it lives.'),
    (664, 'x', 'When under attack from bird Pokémon, it spews a poisonous black powder that causes paralysis on contact.'),
    (664, 'y', 'The powder that covers its body regulates its temperature, so it can live in any region or climate.'),
    (665, 'alpha-sapphire', 'The beaks of bird Pokémon can''t begin to scratch its stalwart body. To defend itself, it spews powder.'),
    (665, 'legends-za', 'It lives hidden within thicket shadows. When predators attack, it bristles the fur covering its body in an effort to threaten them.'),
    (665, 'omega-ruby', 'It lives hidden within thicket shadows. When predators attack, it quickly bristles the fur covering its body in an effort to threaten them.'),
    (665, 'scarlet', 'If Rufflet attacks this Pokémon by pecking at it, it will retaliate with its sharp fur and poisonous black powder.'),
    (665, 'violet', 'Spewpa doesn''t live in a fixed location. It roams where it pleases across the fields and mountains, building up the energy it needs to evolve.'),
    (665, 'x', 'It lives hidden within thicket shadows. When predators attack, it quickly bristles the fur covering its body in an effort to threaten them.'),
    (665, 'y', 'The beaks of bird Pokémon can''t begin to scratch its stalwart body. To defend itself, it spews powder.'),
