    (667, 'alpha-sapphire', 'They set off on their own from their pride and live by themselves to become stronger. These hot-blooded Pokémon are quick to fight.'),
    (667, 'legends-za', 'They set off on their own from their pride and live by themselves to become stronger. These hot-blooded Pokémon are quick to fight.'),
    (667, 'omega-ruby', 'The stronger the opponent it faces, the more heat surges from its mane and the more power flows through its body.'),
    (667, 'scarlet', 'When Litleo are young, female Pyroar will teach them how to hunt. Once the Litleo mature, they will leave the pride and set out on their own.'),
    (667, 'ultra-moon', 'This hot-blooded Pokémon is filled with curiosity. When it gets angry or starts fighting, its short mane gets hot.'),
    (667, 'ultra-sun', 'When they''re young, they live with a pride. Once they''re able to hunt prey on their own, they''re kicked out and have to make their own way.'),
    (667, 'violet', 'The more a Litleo trains its body and spirit by battling mighty enemies, the hotter its mane will grow.'),
    (667, 'x', 'The stronger the opponent it faces, the more heat surges from its mane and the more power flows through its body.'),
    (667, 'y', 'They set off on their own from their pride and live by themselves to become stronger. These hot-blooded Pokémon are quick to fight.'),
    (668, 'alpha-sapphire', 'With fiery breath of more than 10,000 degrees Fahrenheit, they viciously threaten any challenger. The females protect the pride''s cubs.'),
    (668, 'legends-za', 'The male with the largest mane of fire is the leader of the pride.'),
    (668, 'omega-ruby', 'The male with the largest mane of fire is the leader of the pride.'),
    (668, 'scarlet', 'The females of a pride work together to bring down prey. It’s thanks to them that their pride doesn’t starve.'),
    (668, 'ultra-moon', 'The temperature of its breath is over 10,000 degrees Fahrenheit, but Pyroar doesn''t use it on its prey. This Pokémon prefers to eat raw meat.'),
    (668, 'ultra-sun', 'The males are usually lazy, but when attacked by a strong foe, a male will protect its friends with no regard for its own safety.'),
    (668, 'violet', 'The mane of a male Pyroar heats up to over 3,600 degrees Fahrenheit during battle. Merely approaching it will cause severe burns.'),
    (668, 'x', 'The male with the largest mane of fire is the leader of the pride.'),
    (668, 'y', 'With fiery breath of more than 10,000 degrees Fahrenheit, they viciously threaten any challenger. The females protect the pride''s cubs.'),
    (669, 'alpha-sapphire', 'When it finds a flower it likes, it dwells on that flower its whole life long. It floats in the wind''s embrace with an untroubled heart.'),
    (669, 'legends-za', 'It receives strength from flowers and gives them some of its energy in return. This Pokémon likes orange flowers best of all.'),
    (669, 'legends-za', 'This Pokémon can draw forth the power hidden within blooming wild flowers. It is particularly fond of red flowers.'),
    (669, 'legends-za', 'This Pokémon likes blue flowers best of all. It floats upward using the power emanating from its flower and bobs along lightly through the air.'),
    (669, 'legends-za', 'When evening falls, it searches out a place blooming with flowers of the same white color as its own flower, and then it goes to sleep.'),
    (669, 'legends-za', 'This Flabébé rides a yellow flower. The Pokémon is defenseless and vulnerable before it has found and received power from a flower.'),
    (669, 'omega-ruby', 'It draws out and controls the hidden power of flowers. The flower Flabébé holds is most likely part of its body.'),
    (669, 'scarlet', 'This Flabébé rides an orange flower. On its head, it wears a crown of pollen that has healing properties.'),
    (669, 'scarlet', 'This Flabébé rides a yellow flower. The Pokémon is defenseless and vulnerable before it has found and received power from a flower.'),
    (669, 'scarlet', 'This Flabébé rides a white flower. The wind blows this Pokémon around as it drifts in search of flower gardens.'),
    (669, 'scarlet', 'Once it finds a flower it likes, this Pokémon will spend the rest of its life taking care of its flower. This Flabébé rides a blue flower.'),
    (669, 'scarlet', 'This Pokémon can draw forth the power hidden within blooming wild flowers. It is particularly fond of red flowers.'),
    (669, 'ultra-moon', 'Flabébé wears a crown made from pollen it''s collected from its flower. The crown has hidden healing properties.'),
    (669, 'ultra-sun', 'It''s not safe without the power of a flower, but it will keep traveling around until it finds one with the color and shape it wants.'),
    (669, 'violet', 'This Flabébé rides a red flower. Immediately after birth, this Pokémon begins flying around in search of a flower it likes.'),
    (669, 'violet', 'When evening falls, it searches out a place blooming with flowers of the same white color as itself, and then it goes to sleep.'),
    (669, 'violet', 'It unleashes a variety of moves by drawing forth the power hidden within flowers. This Pokémon is particularly fond of yellow flowers.'),
    (669, 'violet', 'It receives strength from flowers and gives them some of its energy in return. This Pokémon likes orange flowers best of all.'),
    (669, 'violet', 'This Pokémon likes blue flowers best of all. It floats upward using the power emanating from its flower and bobs along lightly through the air.'),
    (669, 'x', 'It draws out and controls the hidden power of flowers. The flower Flabébé holds is most likely part of its body.'),
    (669, 'y', 'When it finds a flower it likes, it dwells on that flower its whole life long. It floats in the wind''s embrace with an untroubled heart.'),
    (670, 'alpha-sapphire', 'When the flowers of a well-tended flower bed bloom, it appears and celebrates with an elegant dance.'),
    (670, 'omega-ruby', 'It flutters around fields of flowers and cares for flowers that are starting to wilt. It draws out the hidden power of flowers to battle.'),
    (670, 'ultra-moon', 'It gives its own power to flowers, pouring its heart into caring for them. Floette never forgives anyone who messes up a flower bed.'),
    (670, 'ultra-sun', 'It raises flowers and uses them as weapons. The more gorgeous the blossom, the more power it contains.'),
    (670, 'x', 'It flutters around fields of flowers and cares for flowers that are starting to wilt. It draws out the hidden power of flowers to battle.'),
    (670, 'y', 'When the flowers of a well-tended flower bed bloom, it appears and celebrates with an elegant dance.'),
    (671, 'alpha-sapphire', 'In times long past, governors of castles would invite Florges to create flower gardens to embellish the castle domains.'),
    (671, 'legends-za', 'It is said that there was once a Florges that protected the garden of a castle for over 300 years.'),
    (671, 'legends-za', 'Blue pigments were tremendously expensive in the past, so paintings of blue Florges are highly valuable.'),
    (671, 'legends-za', 'When Florges attacks, its orange flowers fire off powerful beams as if they were a battery of artillery.'),
    (671, 'legends-za', 'A flower garden made by a white-flowered Florges will be beautifully decorated with flowering plants of many different colors.'),
    (671, 'legends-za', 'They say that flower gardens created by Florges constantly emit a power that can heal both body and spirit.'),
    (671, 'omega-ruby', 'It claims exquisite flower gardens as its territory, and it obtains power from basking in the energy emitted by flowering plants.'),
    (671, 'scarlet', 'It is said that there was once a Florges that protected the garden of a castle for over 300 years.'),
    (671, 'scarlet', 'A flower garden made by a white-flowered Florges will be beautifully decorated with flowering plants of many different colors.'),
    (671, 'scarlet', 'This Pokémon creates an impressive flower garden in its territory. It draws forth the power of the red flowers around its neck.'),
    (671, 'scarlet', 'Its orange flowers fire off powerful beams, attacking as if they were a battery of artillery.'),
    (671, 'scarlet', 'Though usually compassionate, Florges will hunt down anyone who vandalizes its flower garden, showing no mercy even if they beg for their lives.'),
    (671, 'ultra-moon', 'Its life can span several hundred years. It''s said to devote its entire life to protecting gardens.'),
    (671, 'ultra-sun', 'It controls the flowers it grows. The petal blizzards that Florges triggers are overwhelming in their beauty and power.'),
    (671, 'violet', 'In times long past, castle governors would lovingly raise Florges to care for their castles'' exquisite gardens.'),
    (671, 'violet', 'This Pokémon battles by drawing forth the power of yellow flowers. It ruthlessly punishes anyone who tramples on flowering plants.'),
    (671, 'violet', 'A Florges adorned with white flowers can sync with the wavelengths of various colors to draw forth their power.'),
    (671, 'violet', 'Blue pigments were tremendously expensive in the past, so paintings of blue Florges are highly valuable.'),
    (671, 'violet', 'They say that flower gardens created by Florges are constantly showered with a power that can heal both body and spirit.'),
    (671, 'x', 'It claims exquisite flower gardens as its territory, and it obtains power from basking in the energy emitted by flowering plants.'),
    (671, 'y', 'In times long past, governors of castles would invite Florges to create flower gardens to embellish the castle domains.'),
    (672, 'alpha-sapphire', 'If it has sunshine and water, it doesn''t need to eat, because it can generate energy from the leaves on its back.'),
    (672, 'legends-za', 'If it has sunshine and water, it doesn''t need to eat, because it can generate energy from the leaves on its back.'),
    (672, 'omega-ruby', 'Thought to be one of the first Pokémon to live in harmony with humans, it has a placid disposition.'),
    (672, 'scarlet', 'Until recently, people living in the mountains would ride on the back of these Pokémon to traverse the mountain paths.'),
    (672, 'violet', 'As long as it has sunlight and water, Skiddo can make energy with the leaves on its body, allowing it to live on rocky mountains barren of food.'),
    (672, 'x', 'Thought to be one of the first Pokémon to live in harmony with humans, it has a placid disposition.'),
    (672, 'y', 'If it has sunshine and water, it doesn''t need to eat, because it can generate energy from the leaves on its back.'),
    (673, 'alpha-sapphire', 'They inhabit mountainous regions. The leader of the herd is decided by a battle of clashing horns.'),
    (673, 'legends-za', 'It can tell how its Trainer is feeling by subtle shifts in their grip on its horns. This empathic sense lets human and Pokémon run as if one being.'),
    (673, 'omega-ruby', 'It can tell how its Trainer is feeling by subtle shifts in the grip on its horns. This empathic sense lets them run as if one being.'),
    (673, 'scarlet', 'It can sense the feelings of others by touching them with its horns. This species has assisted people with their work since 5,000 years ago.'),
    (673, 'violet', 'These Pokémon live in herds in mountainous places. The victor in their contests of clashing horns will become the leader of the herd.'),
    (673, 'x', 'It can tell how its Trainer is feeling by subtle shifts in the grip on its horns. This empathic sense lets them run as if one being.'),
    (673, 'y', 'They inhabit mountainous regions. The leader of the herd is decided by a battle of clashing horns.'),
    (674, 'alpha-sapphire', 'It does its level best to glare and pull a scary face, but it can''t help grinning if anyone pats its head.'),
    (674, 'legends-za', 'It does its level best to glare and pull a scary face, but it can''t help grinning if anyone pats its head.'),
    (674, 'moon', 'There''s no point to the leaf in its mouth, aside from an effort to look cool. It''s mischievous, so it''s not well suited to inexperienced Trainers.'),
    (674, 'omega-ruby', 'It does its best to be taken seriously by its enemies, but its glare is not sufficiently intimidating. Chewing on a leaf is its trademark.'),
    (674, 'shield', 'Wanting to make sure it''s taken seriously, Pancham''s always giving others a glare. But if it''s not focusing, it ends up smiling.'),
    (674, 'sun', 'It grows up imitating the behavior of Pangoro, which it looks up to as a leader.'),
    (674, 'sword', 'It chooses a Pangoro as its master and then imitates its master''s actions. This is how it learns to battle and hunt for prey.'),
    (674, 'ultra-moon', 'It''s desperate to intimidate its opponents. Be nice and pretend to be scared if you catch it glaring at you intensely.'),
    (674, 'ultra-sun', 'It follows Pangoro around like a henchman. When Pancham makes a big mistake, its leaf gets taken away.'),
    (674, 'x', 'It does its best to be taken seriously by its enemies, but its glare is not sufficiently intimidating. Chewing on a leaf is its trademark.'),
    (674, 'y', 'It does its level best to glare and pull a scary face, but it can''t help grinning if anyone pats its head.'),
    (675, 'alpha-sapphire', 'It charges ahead and bashes its opponents like a berserker, uncaring about any hits it might take. Its arms are mighty enough to snap a telephone pole.'),
    (675, 'legends-za', 'Although it has a violent temperament, it won''t put up with those who bully the weak. It senses foes'' movements with its leaf.'),
    (675, 'moon', 'From the slight twitches of its bamboo leaf, it deduces its opponent''s movements. It''s eager to tussle but kindhearted toward its companions.'),
    (675, 'omega-ruby', 'Although it possesses a violent temperament, it won''t put up with bullying. It uses the leaf in its mouth to sense the movements of its enemies.'),
    (675, 'shield', 'Using its leaf, Pangoro can predict the moves of its opponents. It strikes with punches that can turn a dump truck into scrap with just one hit.'),
    (675, 'sun', 'It boasts superb physical strength. Those who wish to become Pangoro''s Trainer have no choice but to converse with their fists.'),
    (675, 'sword', 'This Pokémon is quick to anger, and it has no problem using its prodigious strength to get its way. It lives for duels against Obstagoon.'),
    (675, 'ultra-moon', 'Pangoro is the type to talk with its fists. It doesn''t say much as it pummels opponents with enough force to send a dump truck flying.'),
    (675, 'ultra-sun', 'This rowdy Pokémon boasts great physical strength. Many Trainers are also smitten by its lively character.'),
    (675, 'x', 'Although it possesses a violent temperament, it won''t put up with bullying. It uses the leaf in its mouth to sense the movements of its enemies.'),
    (675, 'y', 'It charges ahead and bashes its opponents like a berserker, uncaring about any hits it might take. Its arms are mighty enough to snap a telephone pole.'),
    (676, 'alpha-sapphire', 'Historically, in the Kalos region, these Pokémon were the designated guardians of the king.'),
    (676, 'legends-za', 'Historically, in the Kalos region, these Pokémon were the designated guardians of the king.'),
    (676, 'omega-ruby', 'Trimming its fluffy fur not only makes it more elegant but also increases the swiftness of its movements.'),
    (676, 'ultra-moon', 'Left alone, its fur will grow longer and longer, but it will only allow someone it trusts to cut it.'),
    (676, 'ultra-sun', 'There was an era when aristocrats would compete to see who could trim their Furfrou''s fur into the most exquisite style.'),
    (676, 'x', 'Trimming its fluffy fur not only makes it more elegant but also increases the swiftness of its movements.'),
    (676, 'y', 'Historically, in the Kalos region, these Pokémon were the designated guardians of the king.'),
    (677, 'alpha-sapphire', 'It has enough psychic energy to blast everything within 300 feet of itself, but it has no control over its power.'),
    (677, 'legends-za', 'It keeps its intense psychic power from leaking out by using its ears to cover the organs emitting that power.'),
    (677, 'omega-ruby', 'The organ that emits its intense psychic power is sheltered by its ears to keep power from leaking out.'),
    (677, 'scarlet', 'It keeps its ears covered to prevent the intense psychic power in its body from escaping, but it falls unconscious if this power builds too much.'),
    (677, 'shield', 'There''s enough psychic power in Espurr to send a wrestler flying, but because this power can''t be controlled, Espurr finds it troublesome.'),
    (677, 'sword', 'Though Espurr''s expression never changes, behind that blank stare is an intense struggle to contain its devastating psychic power.'),
    (677, 'violet', 'Behind an Espurr’s expressionless face is a frantic struggle to contain psychic power.'),
    (677, 'x', 'The organ that emits its intense psychic power is sheltered by its ears to keep power from leaking out.'),
    (677, 'y', 'It has enough psychic energy to blast everything within 300 feet of itself, but it has no control over its power.'),
    (678, 'legends-za', 'When in danger, it raises its ears and releases enough psychic power to grind a 10-ton truck into dust.'),
    (678, 'scarlet', 'Though it has enough psychic power to blast away any opponent, Meowstic prefers to support its allies rather than attack.'),
    (678, 'shield', 'The defensive instinct of the males is strong. It''s when they''re protecting themselves or their partners that they unleash their full power.'),
    (678, 'sword', 'Revealing the eyelike patterns on the insides of its ears will unleash its psychic powers. It normally keeps the patterns hidden, however.'),
    (678, 'violet', 'If Meowstic continuously emits its powerful psychic energy, it will damage its own body.'),
    (679, 'alpha-sapphire', 'If anyone dares to grab its hilt, it wraps a blue cloth around that person''s arm and drains that person''s life energy completely.'),
    (679, 'legends-za', 'Apparently Honedge was born when a departed spirit began inhabiting an ancient sword. It attaches itself to people and drinks their life force.'),
    (679, 'omega-ruby', 'Apparently this Pokémon is born when a departed spirit inhabits a sword. It attaches itself to people and drinks their life force.'),
    (679, 'shield', 'The blue eye on the sword''s handguard is the true body of Honedge. With its old cloth, it drains people''s lives away.'),
    (679, 'sword', 'Honedge''s soul once belonged to a person who was killed a long time ago by the sword that makes up Honedge''s body.'),
    (679, 'x', 'Apparently this Pokémon is born when a departed spirit inhabits a sword. It attaches itself to people and drinks their life force.'),
    (679, 'y', 'If anyone dares to grab its hilt, it wraps a blue cloth around that person''s arm and drains that person''s life energy completely.'),
    (680, 'alpha-sapphire', 'The complex attack patterns of its two swords are unstoppable, even for an opponent greatly accomplished at swordplay.'),
    (680, 'legends-za', 'When Honedge evolves, it divides into two swords that cooperate via telepathy to coordinate attacks and slash their enemies to ribbons.'),
    (680, 'omega-ruby', 'When Honedge evolves, it divides into two swords, which cooperate via telepathy to coordinate attacks and slash their enemies to ribbons.'),
    (680, 'shield', 'The two swords employ a strategy of rapidly alternating between offense and defense to bring down their prey.'),
    (680, 'sword', 'Honedge evolves into twins. The two blades rub together to emit a metallic sound that unnerves opponents.'),
    (680, 'x', 'When Honedge evolves, it divides into two swords, which cooperate via telepathy to coordinate attacks and slash their enemies to ribbons.'),
    (680, 'y', 'The complex attack patterns of its two swords are unstoppable, even for an opponent greatly accomplished at swordplay.'),
    (681, 'legends-za', 'Apparently, it can detect the innate qualities of leadership. According to legend, whoever it recognizes is destined to rule.'),
    (681, 'shield', 'Its potent spectral powers allow it to manipulate others. It once used its powers to force people and Pokémon to build a kingdom to its liking.'),
    (681, 'sword', 'In this defensive stance, Aegislash uses its steel body and a force field of spectral power to reduce the damage of any attack.'),
    (682, 'alpha-sapphire', 'In the past, rather than using perfume, royal ladies carried a Spritzee that would waft a fragrance they liked.'),
    (682, 'legends-za', 'In the past, rather than using perfume, royal ladies carried a Spritzee that would waft a fragrance they liked.'),
    (682, 'omega-ruby', 'It emits a scent that enraptures those who smell it. This fragrance changes depending on what it has eaten.'),
    (682, 'shield', 'The scent its body gives off enraptures those who smell it. Noble ladies had no shortage of love for Spritzee.'),
    (682, 'sword', 'A scent pouch within this Pokémon''s body allows it to create various scents. A change in its diet will alter the fragrance it produces.'),
    (682, 'x', 'It emits a scent that enraptures those who smell it. This fragrance changes depending on what it has eaten.'),
    (682, 'y', 'In the past, rather than using perfume, royal ladies carried a Spritzee that would waft a fragrance they liked.'),
    (683, 'alpha-sapphire', 'Its scent is so overpowering that, unless a Trainer happens to really enjoy the smell, he or she will have a hard time walking alongside it.'),
    (683, 'legends-za', 'Its scent is so overpowering that, unless they happen to really enjoy the smell, Trainers will have a hard time walking alongside it.'),
    (683, 'omega-ruby', 'It devises various scents, pleasant and unpleasant, and emits scents that its enemies dislike in order to gain an edge in battle.'),
    (683, 'shield', 'The scents Aromatisse can produce range from sweet smells that bolster allies to foul smells that sap an opponent''s will to fight.'),
    (683, 'sword', 'The scent that constantly emits from its fur is so powerful that this Pokémon''s companions will eventually lose their sense of smell.'),
    (683, 'x', 'It devises various scents, pleasant and unpleasant, and emits scents that its enemies dislike in order to gain an edge in battle.'),
    (683, 'y', 'Its scent is so overpowering that, unless a Trainer happens to really enjoy the smell, he or she will have a hard time walking alongside it.'),
    (684, 'alpha-sapphire', 'Because it eats nothing but sweets, its fur is as sticky sweet as cotton candy.'),
    (684, 'legends-za', 'To entangle and immobilize its opponents in battle, it extrudes white threads as sweet and sticky as cotton candy.'),
    (684, 'omega-ruby', 'To entangle its opponents in battle, it extrudes white threads as sweet and sticky as cotton candy.'),
    (684, 'shield', 'The sweet smell of cotton candy perfumes Swirlix''s fluffy fur. This Pokémon spits out sticky string to tangle up its enemies.'),
    (684, 'sword', 'It eats its own weight in sugar every day. If it doesn''t get enough sugar, it becomes incredibly grumpy.'),
    (684, 'x', 'To entangle its opponents in battle, it extrudes white threads as sweet and sticky as cotton candy.'),
    (684, 'y', 'Because it eats nothing but sweets, its fur is as sticky sweet as cotton candy.'),
    (685, 'alpha-sapphire', 'Its sense of smell is 100 million times better than a human''s, so even the faintest scent tells it about everything in the area. It''s like it can see with its nose!'),
    (685, 'legends-za', 'It can distinguish the faintest of scents. It puts its sensitive sense of smell to use by helping pastry chefs in their work.'),
    (685, 'omega-ruby', 'It can distinguish the faintest of scents. It puts its sensitive sense of smell to use by helping pastry chefs in their work.'),
    (685, 'shield', 'Slurpuff''s fur contains a lot of air, making it soft to the touch and lighter than it looks.'),
    (685, 'sword', 'By taking in a person''s scent, it can sniff out their mental and physical condition. It''s hoped that this skill will have many medical applications.'),
    (685, 'x', 'It can distinguish the faintest of scents. It puts its sensitive sense of smell to use by helping pastry chefs in their work.'),
    (685, 'y', 'Its sense of smell is 100 million times better than a human''s, so even the faintest scent tells it about everything in the area. It''s like it can see with its nose!'),
    (686, 'alpha-sapphire', 'It flashes the light-emitting spots on its body, which drains its opponent''s will to fight. It takes the opportunity to scuttle away and hide.'),
    (686, 'legends-za', 'It drains foes'' will to fight by flashing light at them. It then takes the opportunity to hide itself away.'),
    (686, 'omega-ruby', 'Opponents who stare at the flashing of the light-emitting spots on its body become dazed and lose their will to fight.'),
    (686, 'scarlet', 'It protects itself from tough foes by flashing its luminescent spots to discourage them.'),
    (686, 'shield', 'By exposing foes to the blinking of its luminescent spots, Inkay demoralizes them, and then it seizes the chance to flee.'),
    (686, 'sword', 'It spins while making its luminescent spots flash. These spots allow it to communicate with others by using different patterns of light.'),
    (686, 'ultra-moon', 'When exchanging information with others of its kind, it flashes the light-emitting spots on its body in a complex rhythm.'),
    (686, 'ultra-sun', 'It draws prey near with its blinking lights and then wraps them up in its long tentacles and holds them in place.'),
    (686, 'violet', 'Being upside-down improves its blood flow and clears its mind, causing the power of its psychic moves to increase dramatically.'),
    (686, 'x', 'Opponents who stare at the flashing of the light-emitting spots on its body become dazed and lose their will to fight.'),
    (686, 'y', 'It flashes the light-emitting spots on its body, which drains its opponent''s will to fight. It takes the opportunity to scuttle away and hide.'),
    (687, 'alpha-sapphire', 'It lures its prey close with hypnotic motions, then wraps its tentacles around it before finishing it off with digestive fluids.'),
    (687, 'legends-za', 'It wields the most compelling hypnotic powers of any Pokémon, and it forces others to do whatever it wants.'),
    (687, 'omega-ruby', 'It wields the most compelling hypnotic powers of any Pokémon, and it forces others to do whatever it wants.'),
    (687, 'scarlet', 'Its hypnotic powers are dangerously strong. Anyone who falls under Malamar’s control loses their memories surrounding the event.'),
    (687, 'shield', 'It''s said that Malamar''s hypnotic powers played a role in certain history-changing events.'),
    (687, 'sword', 'Gazing at its luminescent spots will quickly induce a hypnotic state, putting the observer under Malamar''s control.'),
    (687, 'ultra-moon', 'It flashes the pattern on its torso to control its prey and draw them in. The edges of its fins are supremely sharp.'),
    (687, 'ultra-sun', 'When it comes to strong hypnosis, there''s an endless number of people who utilize Malamar for their nefarious deeds.'),
    (687, 'violet', 'It flashes the luminescent spots on its body to hypnotize its opponents, gaining total control over them.'),
    (687, 'x', 'It wields the most compelling hypnotic powers of any Pokémon, and it forces others to do whatever it wants.'),
    (687, 'y', 'It lures its prey close with hypnotic motions, then wraps its tentacles around it before finishing it off with digestive fluids.'),
    (688, 'alpha-sapphire', 'They stretch and then contract, yanking their rocks along with them in bold hops. They eat seaweed that washes up on the shoreline.'),
    (688, 'legends-za', 'Two Binacle live together on one rock. When they fight, one of them will move to a different rock.'),
    (688, 'omega-ruby', 'Two Binacle live together on one rock. When they fight, one of them will move to a different rock.'),
    (688, 'shield', 'If the two don''t work well together, both their offense and defense fall apart. Without good teamwork, they won''t survive.'),
    (688, 'sword', 'After two Binacle find a suitably sized rock, they adhere themselves to it and live together. They cooperate to gather food during high tide.'),
    (688, 'x', 'Two Binacle live together on one rock. When they fight, one of them will move to a different rock.'),
    (688, 'y', 'They stretch and then contract, yanking their rocks along with them in bold hops. They eat seaweed that washes up on the shoreline.'),
    (689, 'alpha-sapphire', 'Barbaracle''s legs and hands have minds of their own, and they will move independently. But they usually follow the head''s orders.'),
    (689, 'legends-za', 'Barbaracle''s legs and hands have minds of their own, and they will move independently. But they usually follow the head''s orders.'),
    (689, 'omega-ruby', 'When they evolve, two Binacle multiply into seven. They fight with the power of seven Binacle.'),
    (689, 'shield', 'Having an eye on each palm allows it to keep watch in all directions. In a pinch, its limbs start to act on their own to ensure the enemy''s defeat.'),
    (689, 'sword', 'Seven Binacle come together to form one Barbaracle. The Binacle that serves as the head gives orders to those serving as the limbs.'),
    (689, 'x', 'When they evolve, two Binacle multiply into seven. They fight with the power of seven Binacle.'),
    (689, 'y', 'Barbaracle''s legs and hands have minds of their own, and they will move independently. But they usually follow the head''s orders.'),
    (690, 'alpha-sapphire', 'It looks just like rotten kelp. It hides from foes while storing up power for its evolution.'),
    (690, 'legends-za', 'Camouflaged as rotten kelp, this Pokémon sprays liquid poison to take down prey that approach unawares.'),
    (690, 'omega-ruby', 'Camouflaged as rotten kelp, they spray liquid poison on prey that approaches unawares and then finish it off.'),
    (690, 'scarlet', 'Skrelp evades its enemies by hiding amid drifting seaweed. It eats rotten seaweed to create its poison.'),
    (690, 'shield', 'Skrelp looks like a piece of rotten seaweed, so it can blend in with seaweed drifting on the ocean and avoid being detected by enemies.'),
    (690, 'sword', 'It drifts in the ocean, blending in with floating seaweed. When other Pokémon come to feast on the seaweed, Skrelp feasts on them instead.'),
    (690, 'ultra-moon', 'It''s not good at swimming, so it clings to the seaweed. In the Alola region, it''s often found near {{P|Dhelmise}}.'),
    (690, 'ultra-sun', 'It vanishes into seaweed and remains perfectly still to avoid attacks from large Pokémon. Rotten seaweed is its main food source.'),
    (690, 'violet', 'This Pokémon is a poor swimmer. If it''s caught in a fierce storm, it will sometimes get washed far away and become unable to return to its home.'),
    (690, 'x', 'Camouflaged as rotten kelp, they spray liquid poison on prey that approaches unawares and then finish it off.'),
    (690, 'y', 'It looks just like rotten kelp. It hides from foes while storing up power for its evolution.'),
    (691, 'alpha-sapphire', 'Tales are told of ships that wander into seas where Dragalge live, never to return.'),
    (691, 'legends-za', 'Their poison is strong enough to eat through the hull of a tanker, and they spit it indiscriminately at anything that enters their territory.'),
    (691, 'omega-ruby', 'Their poison is strong enough to eat through the hull of a tanker, and they spit it indiscriminately at anything that enters their territory.'),
    (691, 'scarlet', 'Using a liquid poison, Dragalge indiscriminately attacks anything that wanders into its territory. This poison can corrode the undersides of boats.'),
    (691, 'shield', 'Dragalge generates dragon energy by sticking the plume on its head out above the ocean''s surface and bathing it in sunlight.'),
    (691, 'sword', 'Dragalge uses a poisonous liquid capable of corroding metal to send tankers that enter its territory to the bottom of the sea.'),
    (691, 'ultra-moon', 'It blends in with seaweed to ambush its prey and then takes them down with a poisonous liquid strong enough to melt metal.'),
    (691, 'ultra-sun', 'This vicious Pokémon sprays a poisonous liquid on opponents that come near. For whatever reason, it gets along really well with Dhelmise.'),
    (691, 'violet', 'Since Finizen is the better swimmer, Dragalge will approach it under the cover of seaweed, then immobilize it with a poisonous attack.'),
    (691, 'x', 'Their poison is strong enough to eat through the hull of a tanker, and they spit it indiscriminately at anything that enters their territory.'),
    (691, 'y', 'Tales are told of ships that wander into seas where Dragalge live, never to return.'),
    (692, 'alpha-sapphire', 'Through controlled explosions of internal gas, it can expel water like a pistol shot. At close distances, it can shatter rock.'),
    (692, 'legends-za', 'They knock down flying prey by firing compressed water from their massive claws like shooting a pistol.'),
    (692, 'omega-ruby', 'They knock down flying prey by firing compressed water from their massive claws like shooting a pistol.'),
    (692, 'scarlet', 'This Pokémon launches water by detonating gas inside its right claw. It snipes flying Pokémon.'),
    (692, 'shield', 'By detonating gas that accumulates in its right claw, this Pokémon launches water like a bullet. This is how Clauncher defeats its enemies.'),
    (692, 'sword', 'Clauncher''s claws can fall off during battle, but they''ll regenerate. The meat inside the claws is popular as a delicacy in Galar.'),
    (692, 'ultra-moon', 'It moves around by jetting water from its right pincer. It has a poor sense of balance, so it''s terrible at swimming straight.'),
    (692, 'ultra-sun', 'Its claws occasionally fall off, and it keeps a low profile until they grow back. The meat of its claws is so delicious!'),
    (692, 'violet', 'Clauncher''s claws will regrow if they fall off. The meat inside the claws is edible, but it has a distinct flavor that doesn''t appeal to all tastes.'),
    (692, 'x', 'They knock down flying prey by firing compressed water from their massive claws like shooting a pistol.'),
    (692, 'y', 'Through controlled explosions of internal gas, it can expel water like a pistol shot. At close distances, it can shatter rock.'),
    (693, 'alpha-sapphire', 'By expelling water from the nozzle in the back of its claw, it can move at a speed of 60 knots.'),
    (693, 'legends-za', 'By expelling water from the nozzle in the back of its claw, it can move at a speed of 60 knots.'),
    (693, 'omega-ruby', 'Their enormous claws launch cannonballs of water powerful enough to pierce tanker hulls.'),
    (693, 'scarlet', 'Clawitzer can move through the water at a speed of 60 knots by using gas inside its body to expel water from the back of its claw.'),
    (693, 'shield', 'Clawitzer''s right arm is a cannon that launches projectiles made of seawater. Shots from a Clawitzer''s cannon arm can sink a tanker.'),
    (693, 'sword', 'After using the feelers on its oversized claw to detect the location of prey, Clawitzer launches a cannonball of water at its target.'),
    (693, 'ultra-moon', 'Its right arm is packed with meat. When its pincer falls off, it''s exported to be used as a cooking ingredient.'),
    (693, 'ultra-sun', 'It compresses the water it has sucked up and then projects it with enough power to punch a hole right through a thick sheet of iron.'),
    (693, 'violet', 'The cannonballs of seawater that Clawitzer launches from its claw are powerful enough to punch through tanker hulls.'),
    (693, 'x', 'Their enormous claws launch cannonballs of water powerful enough to pierce tanker hulls.'),
    (693, 'y', 'By expelling water from the nozzle in the back of its claw, it can move at a speed of 60 knots.'),
    (694, 'alpha-sapphire', 'The frills on either side of its head have cells that generate electricity when exposed to sunlight.'),
    (694, 'legends-za', 'The frills on either side of its head have cells that generate electricity when exposed to sunlight.'),
    (694, 'omega-ruby', 'They make their home in deserts. They can generate their energy from basking in the sun, so eating food is not a requirement.'),
    (694, 'shield', 'The sun powers this Pokémon''s electricity generation. Interruption of that process stresses Helioptile to the point of weakness.'),
    (694, 'sword', 'When spread, the frills on its head act like solar panels, generating the power behind this Pokémon''s electric moves.'),
    (694, 'x', 'They make their home in deserts. They can generate their energy from basking in the sun, so eating food is not a requirement.'),
    (694, 'y', 'The frills on either side of its head have cells that generate electricity when exposed to sunlight.'),
    (695, 'alpha-sapphire', 'It stimulates its muscles with electricity, boosting the strength in its legs and enabling it to run 100 yards in five seconds.'),
    (695, 'legends-za', 'They flare their frills and generate energy. A single Heliolisk can generate sufficient electricity to power a skyscraper.'),
    (695, 'omega-ruby', 'They flare their frills and generate energy. A single Heliolisk can generate sufficient electricity to power a skyscraper.'),
    (695, 'shield', 'One Heliolisk basking in the sun with its frill outspread is all it would take to produce enough electricity to power a city.'),
    (695, 'sword', 'A now-vanished desert culture treasured these Pokémon. Appropriately, when Heliolisk came to the Galar region, treasure came with them.'),
    (695, 'x', 'They flare their frills and generate energy. A single Heliolisk can generate sufficient electricity to power a skyscraper.'),
    (695, 'y', 'It stimulates its muscles with electricity, boosting the strength in its legs and enabling it to run 100 yards in five seconds.'),
    (696, 'alpha-sapphire', 'Its immense jaws have enough destructive force that it can chew up an automobile. It lived 100 million years ago.'),
    (696, 'legends-za', 'This Pokémon was restored from a fossil. If something happens that it doesn''t like, it throws a tantrum and runs wild.'),
    (696, 'omega-ruby', 'This Pokémon was restored from a fossil. If something happens that it doesn''t like, it throws a tantrum and runs wild.'),
    (696, 'shield', 'This Pokémon is selfish and likes to be pampered. It can also inflict grievous wounds on its Trainer just by playing around.'),
    (696, 'sword', 'This is an ancient Pokémon, revived in modern times. It has a violent disposition, and it''ll tear apart anything it gets between its hefty jaws.'),
    (696, 'ultra-moon', 'Tyrunt is spoiled and selfish. It may just be trying to frolic, but sometimes the ones it''s trying to frolic with are gravely injured.'),
    (696, 'ultra-sun', 'Its large jaw has incredible destructive power. Some theories suggest that its restored form is different from its form of long ago.'),
    (696, 'x', 'This Pokémon was restored from a fossil. If something happens that it doesn''t like, it throws a tantrum and runs wild.'),
    (696, 'y', 'Its immense jaws have enough destructive force that it can chew up an automobile. It lived 100 million years ago.'),
    (697, 'alpha-sapphire', 'Nothing could stop this Pokémon 100 million years ago, so it behaved like a king.'),
    (697, 'legends-za', 'This Pokémon behaved like a king 100 million years ago. Nothing could stop it.'),
    (697, 'omega-ruby', 'Thanks to its gargantuan jaws, which could shred thick metal plates as if they were paper, it was invincible in the ancient world it once inhabited.'),
    (697, 'shield', 'A single bite of Tyrantrum''s massive jaws will demolish a car. This Pokémon was the king of the ancient world.'),
    (697, 'sword', 'This Pokémon is from about 100,000,000 years ago. It has the presence of a king, vicious but magnificent.'),
    (697, 'ultra-moon', 'The king of the ancient world, it can easily crunch a car with the devastating strength of its enormous jaws.'),
    (697, 'ultra-sun', 'Complete restoration is impossible, allowing room for theories that its entire body was once covered in a feather-like coat.'),
    (697, 'x', 'Thanks to its gargantuan jaws, which could shred thick metal plates as if they were paper, it was invincible in the ancient world it once inhabited.'),
    (697, 'y', 'Nothing could stop this Pokémon 100 million years ago, so it behaved like a king.'),
    (698, 'alpha-sapphire', 'This calm Pokémon lived in a cold land where there were no violent predators like Tyrantrum.'),
    (698, 'legends-za', 'This ancient Pokémon was restored from a part of its body that had been frozen in ice for 100 million years.'),
    (698, 'omega-ruby', 'This ancient Pokémon was restored from part of its body that had been frozen in ice for over 100 million years.'),
    (698, 'shield', 'Amaura is an ancient Pokémon that has gone extinct. Specimens of this species can sometimes be found frozen in ice.'),
    (698, 'sword', 'This Pokémon was successfully restored from a fossil. In the past, it lived with others of its kind in cold lands where there were fewer predators.'),
    (698, 'ultra-moon', 'Amaura was restored successfully, but it''s not expected to live long because of the heat of the current environment.'),
    (698, 'ultra-sun', 'It lived in cold areas in ancient times. It''s said that when Amaura whinnies, auroras appear in the night sky.'),
    (698, 'x', 'This ancient Pokémon was restored from part of its body that had been frozen in ice for over 100 million years.'),
    (698, 'y', 'This calm Pokémon lived in a cold land where there were no violent predators like Tyrantrum.'),
    (699, 'alpha-sapphire', 'Using its diamond-shaped crystals, it can instantly create a wall of ice to block an opponent''s attack.'),
    (699, 'legends-za', 'The diamond-shaped crystals on its body expel air as cold as −240 degrees Fahrenheit, surrounding its enemies and encasing them in ice.'),
    (699, 'omega-ruby', 'The diamond-shaped crystals on its body expel air as cold as -240 degrees Fahrenheit, surrounding its enemies and encasing them in ice.'),
    (699, 'shield', 'When gripped by rage, Aurorus will emanate freezing air, covering everything around it in ice.'),
    (699, 'sword', 'Aurorus was restored from a fossil. It''s said that when this Pokémon howls, auroras appear in the night sky.'),
    (699, 'ultra-moon', 'This usually quiet and kindly Pokémon has a surface temperature of around –240<!--U+2013 EN DASH in-game--> degrees Fahrenheit.'),
    (699, 'ultra-sun', 'An Aurorus was found frozen solid within a glacier, just as it appeared long ago, which became quite a big event in the news.'),
    (699, 'x', 'The diamond-shaped crystals on its body expel air as cold as -240 degrees Fahrenheit, surrounding its enemies and encasing them in ice.'),
    (699, 'y', 'Using its diamond-shaped crystals, it can instantly create a wall of ice to block an opponent''s attack.'),
    (700, 'alpha-sapphire', 'It wraps its ribbonlike feelers around the arm of its beloved Trainer and walks with him or her.'),
    (700, 'legends-arceus', 'It emits a soothing aura from its ribbon-shaped organs. It wraps these appendages around quarrelers to instantly restore calm to the situation.'),
    (700, 'legends-za', 'It wraps its ribbonlike feelers around the arm of its beloved Trainer and walks with them.'),
    (700, 'moon', 'When this Pokémon sights its prey, it swirls its ribbonlike feelers as a distraction. A moment later, it pounces.'),
    (700, 'omega-ruby', 'It sends a soothing aura from its ribbonlike feelers to calm fights.'),
    (700, 'scarlet', 'This Pokémon uses its ribbonlike feelers to send a soothing aura into its opponents, erasing their hostility.'),
    (700, 'shield', 'There''s a [[Galar]]ian fairy tale that describes a beautiful Sylveon vanquishing a dreadful dragon Pokémon.'),
    (700, 'sun', 'Its ribbonlike feelers give off an aura that weakens hostility in its prey, causing them to let down their guard. Then it attacks.'),
    (700, 'sword', 'By releasing enmity-erasing waves from its ribbonlike feelers, Sylveon stops any conflict.'),
    (700, 'ultra-moon', 'Sylveon wraps its ribbonlike feelers around its Trainer''s arm because this touch enables it to read its Trainer''s feelings.'),
    (700, 'ultra-sun', 'Once a fight breaks out, it will unflinchingly charge at dragon {{OBP|Pokémon|species}} that are many times larger than itself.'),
    (700, 'violet', 'Sylveon cuts an elegant figure as it dances lightly around, feelers fluttering, but its piercing moves aim straight for its opponents'' weak spots.'),
    (700, 'x', 'It sends a soothing aura from its ribbonlike feelers to calm fights.'),
    (700, 'y', 'It wraps its ribbonlike feelers around the arm of its beloved {{pkmn|Trainer}} and walks with him or her.'),
    (701, 'alpha-sapphire', 'With its wings, it controls its position in the air. It likes to attack from above, a maneuver that is difficult to defend against.'),
    (701, 'legends-za', 'With its wings, it controls its position in the air. It likes to attack from above, a maneuver that is difficult to defend against.'),
    (701, 'omega-ruby', 'Although its body is small, its proficient fighting skills enable it to keep up with big bruisers like Machamp and Hariyama.'),
    (701, 'scarlet', 'Its elegant finishing moves—performed by nimbly leaping around using its wings—are polished in the forest where it was born and raised.'),
    (701, 'shield', 'It always strikes a pose before going for its finishing move. Sometimes opponents take advantage of that time to counterattack.'),
    (701, 'sword', 'It drives its opponents to exhaustion with its agile maneuvers, then ends the fight with a flashy finishing move.'),
    (701, 'ultra-moon', 'In combat, Hawlucha leaps nimbly about, taking advantage of its opponents'' blind spots. It''s also skilled at using superb submission holds.'),
    (701, 'ultra-sun', 'It overwhelms opponents with quick moves, but sometimes it showboats for too long when it''s using a special move and gets itself into a pinch.'),
    (701, 'violet', 'Hawlucha live quietly without flocking together. They fight constantly with their natural enemies: noisy groups of Primeape.'),
    (701, 'x', 'Although its body is small, its proficient fighting skills enable it to keep up with big bruisers like Machamp and Hariyama.'),
    (701, 'y', 'With its wings, it controls its position in the air. It likes to attack from above, a maneuver that is difficult to defend against.'),
    (702, 'alpha-sapphire', 'It uses its tail to absorb electricity from power plants or from outlets in houses, and then it fires the electricity from its whiskers.'),
    (702, 'legends-za', 'Its whiskers serve as antennas. By sending and receiving electrical waves, it can communicate with others over vast distances.'),
    (702, 'omega-ruby', 'Its whiskers serve as antennas. By sending and receiving electrical waves, it can communicate with others over vast distances.'),
    (702, 'scarlet', 'It’s small and its electricity-generating organ is not fully developed, so it uses its tail to absorb electricity from people’s homes and charge itself.'),
    (702, 'shield', 'Since Dedenne can''t generate as much electricity on its own, it steals electricity from outlets or other electric Pokémon.'),
    (702, 'sword', 'A Dedenne''s whiskers pick up electrical waves other Dedenne send out. These Pokémon share locations of food or electricity with one another.'),
    (702, 'ultra-moon', 'Its upper whiskers are sensors that survey its surroundings. Its lower whiskers are organs that shoot electricity.'),
    (702, 'ultra-sun', 'It sneaks into people''s homes and steals electricity from their outlets. When your electric bill seems off, it''s the handiwork of this rascal.'),
    (702, 'violet', 'Dedenne emit electrical waves from the whiskers on their cheeks to communicate with each other. When low on electricity, they curl up and sleep.'),
    (702, 'x', 'Its whiskers serve as antennas. By sending and receiving electrical waves, it can communicate with others over vast distances.'),
    (702, 'y', 'It uses its tail to absorb electricity from power plants or from outlets in houses, and then it fires the electricity from its whiskers.'),
    (703, 'alpha-sapphire', 'It has slept underground for hundreds of millions of years since its birth. It''s occasionally found during the excavation of caves.'),
    (703, 'legends-za', 'Born from the high temperatures and pressures deep underground, it releases energy from the stone in its head.'),
    (703, 'moon', 'Although this Pokémon is not especially rare, its glittering, jewel-draped body draws attention from people.'),
    (703, 'omega-ruby', 'Born from the temperatures and pressures deep underground, it fires beams from the stone in its head.'),
    (703, 'scarlet', 'It has slept underground for hundreds of millions of years since its birth. It''s occasionally found during the excavation of caves.'),
    (703, 'shield', 'It''s said that somewhere in the world, there''s a mineral vein housing a large pack of slumbering Carbink. It''s also said that this pack has a Diancie.'),
    (703, 'sun', 'Born from the high temperatures and pressures deep underground, it defends itself by firing beams from the jewel part of its body.'),
    (703, 'sword', 'When beset by attackers, Carbink wipes them all out by firing high-energy beams from the gems embedded in its body.'),
    (703, 'ultra-moon', 'To keep the jewels on their bodies free of tarnish, packs of Carbink use their soft manes to polish one another''s jewels.'),
    (703, 'ultra-sun', 'Some say that deep beneath the surface of the world, a pack of Carbink live with Diancie in a kingdom of jewels.'),
    (703, 'violet', 'Born from the high temperatures and pressures deep underground, it defends itself by firing beams from the jewel part of its body.'),
    (703, 'x', 'Born from the temperatures and pressures deep underground, it fires beams from the stone in its head.'),
    (703, 'y', 'It has slept underground for hundreds of millions of years since its birth. It''s occasionally found during the excavation of caves.'),
    (704, 'alpha-sapphire', 'It''s covered in a slimy membrane that makes any punches or kicks slide off it harmlessly.'),
    (704, 'legends-arceus', 'Goomy hides away in the shade of trees, where it''s nice and humid. If the slime coating its body dries out, the Pokémon instantly becomes lethargic.'),
    (704, 'legends-za', 'Thanks to the slimy membrane covering its body, punches or kicks from its enemies slide right off it.'),
    (704, 'moon', 'Its source of protection is its slimy, germ-laden mucous membrane. Anyone who touches it needs some thorough hand-washing.'),
    (704, 'omega-ruby', 'The weakest Dragon-type Pokémon, it lives in damp, shady places, so its body doesn''t dry out.'),
    (704, 'scarlet', 'Most of a Goomy’s body is water. A membrane covers the whole Pokémon to prevent it from shriveling up in dry weather.'),
    (704, 'shield', 'Their horns are powerful sensors. As soon as Goomy pick up any sign of enemies, they go into hiding. This is how they''ve survived.'),
    (704, 'sun', 'The weakest of all Dragon-type Pokémon, it''s unable to breathe if its skin dries out, so it sticks to shady places.'),
    (704, 'sword', 'Because most of its body is water, it will dry up if the weather becomes too arid. It''s considered the weakest dragon Pokémon.'),
    (704, 'ultra-moon', 'Its body is mostly water. If it dries out, it will die, so it''s always sitting with perfect stillness in the shade.'),
    (704, 'ultra-sun', 'It uses its horns to check out its surroundings. They''re very sensitive, so if you grab them, it will feel a strong shock and be unable to move.'),
    (704, 'violet', 'Goomy''s horns are excellent sensory organs that cover all five of Goomy''s senses. Goomy picks up on danger from the movement of the air.'),
    (704, 'x', 'The weakest Dragon-type Pokémon, it lives in damp, shady places, so its body doesn''t dry out.'),
    (704, 'y', 'It''s covered in a slimy membrane that makes any punches or kicks slide off it harmlessly.'),
    (705, 'alpha-sapphire', 'Its four horns are a high-performance radar system. It uses them to sense sounds and smells, rather than using ears or a nose.'),
    (705, 'moon', 'This Pokémon''s mucous can dissolve anything. Toothless, it sprays mucous on its prey. Once they''re nicely dissolved, it slurps them up.'),
    (705, 'omega-ruby', 'It drives away opponents by excreting a sticky liquid that can dissolve anything. Its eyes devolved, so it can''t see anything.'),
    (705, 'shield', 'The lump on its back contains its tiny brain. It thinks only of food and escaping its enemies.'),
    (705, 'sun', 'It has trouble drawing a line between friends and food. It will calmly try to melt and eat even those it gets along well with.'),
    (705, 'sword', 'Although this Pokémon isn''t very strong, its body is coated in a caustic slime that can melt through anything, so predators steer clear of it.'),
    (705, 'ultra-moon', 'Its entire body is covered with gooey mucus that can dissolve anything. Be sure to put gloves on if you''re going to touch it.'),
    (705, 'ultra-sun', 'It crawls along sluggishly. The swirly protrusion on its back is filled with its brain and other organs.'),
    (705, 'x', 'It drives away opponents by excreting a sticky liquid that can dissolve anything. Its eyes devolved, so it can''t see anything.'),
    (705, 'y', 'Its four horns are a high-performance radar system. It uses them to sense sounds and smells, rather than using ears or a nose.'),
    (706, 'alpha-sapphire', 'It attacks with retractable horns. It throws a punch that''s the equivalent of the force of a hundred pro boxers.'),
    (706, 'moon', 'It gets picked on because it''s meek. But then, whoever teased it gets to feel the full force of its horns and a good swatting from its thick tail.'),
    (706, 'omega-ruby', 'This very friendly Dragon-type Pokémon will hug its beloved Trainer, leaving that Trainer covered in sticky slime.'),
    (706, 'shield', 'Its form of offense is forcefully stretching out its horns. The strikes land 100 times harder than any blow from a heavyweight boxer.'),
    (706, 'sun', 'An amazingly friendly Pokémon, but if left to itself, loneliness overcomes it, and it oozes gooey tears.'),
    (706, 'sword', 'Sometimes it misunderstands instructions and appears dazed or bewildered. Many Trainers don''t mind, finding this behavior to be adorable.'),
    (706, 'ultra-moon', 'Underneath its slimy skin is a thick layer of fat, and the combination of the two makes enemies'' attacks slide right off.'),
    (706, 'ultra-sun', 'It''s very friendly toward people. If you grow close to it, Goodra will hug you with its sticky, slime-covered body. Don''t get mad.'),
    (706, 'x', 'This very friendly Dragon-type Pokémon will hug its beloved Trainer, leaving that Trainer covered in sticky slime.'),
    (706, 'y', 'It attacks with retractable horns. It throws a punch that''s the equivalent of the force of a hundred pro boxers.'),
    (707, 'alpha-sapphire', 'It never lets go of a key that it likes, so people give it the keys to vaults and safes as a way to prevent crime.'),
    (707, 'legends-za', 'It never lets go of a key that it likes, so people give it the keys to vaults and safes as a way to prevent crime.'),
    (707, 'moon', 'It inserts its horn into chinks in metal, absorbing metal ions. For some reason, it collects keys.'),
    (707, 'omega-ruby', 'These key collectors threaten any attackers by fiercely jingling their keys at them.'),
    (707, 'scarlet', 'Once it absorbs a key’s metal ions, it discards the key without a second thought. However, it will hang on to keys it favors for decades.'),
    (707, 'shield', 'Klefki sucks in metal ions with the horn topping its head. It seems this Pokémon loves keys so much that its head needed to look like one, too.'),
    (707, 'sun', 'This even-tempered Pokémon has a habit of collecting keys. It will sneak into people''s homes to steal their keys.'),
    (707, 'sword', 'This Pokémon is constantly collecting keys. Entrust a Klefki with important keys, and the Pokémon will protect them no matter what.'),
    (707, 'ultra-moon', 'Long ago it lived in mines, but once the minerals that make up its diet became scarcer, Klefki began appearing in human settlements.'),
    (707, 'ultra-sun', 'Although it''s unclear why it collects keys, giving it a key makes Klefki very happy. However, it apparently only likes master keys.'),
    (707, 'violet', 'In the past, noble families entrusted their vault keys to a Klefki. They passed the Klefki down through the generations, taking good care of it.'),
    (707, 'x', 'These key collectors threaten any attackers by fiercely jingling their keys at them.'),
    (707, 'y', 'It never lets go of a key that it likes, so people give it the keys to vaults and safes as a way to prevent crime.'),
    (708, 'alpha-sapphire', 'According to old tales, these Pokémon are stumps possessed by the spirits of children who died while lost in the forest.'),
    (708, 'legends-za', 'According to old tales, these Pokémon are stumps possessed by the spirits of children who died while lost in the forest.'),
    (708, 'moon', 'According to legend, medicine to cure any illness can be made by plucking the green leaves on its head, brewing them, and boiling down the liquid.'),
    (708, 'omega-ruby', 'These Pokémon are created when spirits possess rotten tree stumps. They prefer to live in abandoned forests.'),
    (708, 'scarlet', 'Legend tells that its green leaves can cure any illness. When plucked, however, the leaves will instantly wither away.'),
    (708, 'shield', 'With a voice like a human child''s, it cries out to lure adults deep into the forest, getting them lost among the trees.'),
    (708, 'sun', 'These Pokémon are stumps possessed by the spirits of children who died in the forest. Their cries sound like eerie screams.'),
    (708, 'sword', 'After a lost child perished in the forest, their spirit possessed a tree stump, causing the spirit''s rebirth as this Pokémon.'),
    (708, 'ultra-moon', 'An unknown spirit came to lodge in a tree stump, creating this Pokémon. A cure-all can be made from an infusion of its green leaves.'),
    (708, 'ultra-sun', 'By imitating the voice of a child, it causes people to get hopelessly lost deep in the forest. It''s trying to make friends with them.'),
    (708, 'violet', 'This Pokémon came to be when the spirit of a deceased child possessed a tree stump. It now wanders the forest searching for friends.'),
    (708, 'x', 'These Pokémon are created when spirits possess rotten tree stumps. They prefer to live in abandoned forests.'),
    (708, 'y', 'According to old tales, these Pokémon are stumps possessed by the spirits of children who died while lost in the forest.'),
    (709, 'alpha-sapphire', 'Using its roots as a nervous system, it controls the trees in the forest. It''s kind to the Pokémon that reside in its body.'),
    (709, 'legends-za', 'Using its roots as a nervous system, it controls the trees in the forest. It''s kind to the Pokémon that reside in its body.'),
    (709, 'moon', 'Through its roots, it exerts control over other trees. A deadly curse falls upon anyone cutting down trees in forests where Trevenant dwell.'),
    (709, 'omega-ruby', 'It can control trees at will. It will trap people who harm the forest, so they can never leave.'),
    (709, 'scarlet', 'Using its roots, Trevenant connects itself to trees and monitors every corner of its forest. It uses curses to drive intruders away.'),
    (709, 'shield', 'Small roots that extend from the tips of this Pokémon''s feet can tie into the trees of the forest and give Trevenant control over them.'),
    (709, 'sun', 'This Pokémon is said to devour anyone daring to ravage the forest. To the creatures dwelling in the forest, it offers great kindness.'),
    (709, 'sword', 'People fear it due to a belief that it devours any who try to cut down trees in its forest, but to the Pokémon it shares its woods with, it''s kind.'),
    (709, 'ultra-moon', 'This Pokémon controls trees via roots stretching from its feet, and it will attack anyone that dares to ravage the forest.'),
    (709, 'ultra-sun', 'It''s feared as a ghost of the forest. Lumberjacks bring along Fire types, which Trevenant hates, when they enter the forest.'),
    (709, 'violet', 'Trevenant is very kind to Pokémon living in the forest. It doesn''t even care if these Pokémon take up residence in the greenery on its head.'),
    (709, 'x', 'It can control trees at will. It will trap people who harm the forest, so they can never leave.'),
    (709, 'y', 'Using its roots as a nervous system, it controls the trees in the forest. It''s kind to the Pokémon that reside in its body.'),
    (710, 'alpha-sapphire', 'It is said to carry wandering spirits to the place where they belong so they can move on.'),
    (710, 'legends-za', 'It was recently discovered that the different varieties of Pumpkaboo vary not only in size but also in the size of the souls they collect.'),
    (710, 'legends-za', 'In keeping with the size of its body, this variety of Pumpkaboo takes the small spirits of children to the afterlife.'),
    (710, 'legends-za', 'In keeping with the size of its body, this variety of Pumpkaboo takes the large spirits of adults to the afterlife.'),
    (710, 'legends-za', 'In keeping with the size of its body, this variety of Pumpkaboo takes jumbo spirits to the afterlife.'),
    (710, 'omega-ruby', 'The pumpkin body is inhabited by a spirit trapped in this world. As the sun sets, it becomes restless and active.'),
    (710, 'shield', 'Large Pumpkaboo are said to be the product of areas where many lost souls lingered.'),
    (710, 'shield', 'Small Pumpkaboo are said to be the product of areas where few lost souls lingered.'),
    (710, 'shield', 'The light that streams out from the holes in the pumpkin can hypnotize and control the people and Pokémon that see it.'),
    (710, 'shield', 'Massive Pumpkaboo are said to be the product of areas where a great number of lost souls lingered.'),
    (710, 'sword', 'When taking spirits to the afterlife, small Pumpkaboo prefer the spirits of children to those of adults.'),
    (710, 'sword', 'Spirits that wander this world are placed into Pumpkaboo''s body. They''re then moved on to the afterlife.'),
    (710, 'sword', 'When taking spirits to the afterlife, large Pumpkaboo prefer the spirits of adults to those of children.'),
    (710, 'sword', 'Supersized Pumpkaboo are very partial to the spirits of people who were of similarly superior proportions.'),
    (710, 'x', 'The pumpkin body is inhabited by a spirit trapped in this world. As the sun sets, it becomes restless and active.'),
    (710, 'y', 'It is said to carry wandering spirits to the place where they belong so they can move on.'),
    (711, 'alpha-sapphire', 'It enwraps its prey in its hairlike arms. It sings joyfully as it observes the suffering of its prey.'),
    (711, 'legends-za', 'Small Gourgeist pretend to be children to fool adults. Anyone who falls for the act gets carried away to the hereafter.'),
    (711, 'legends-za', 'Jumbo Gourgeist aren''t picky. They will forcefully drag anyone off to the afterlife.'),
    (711, 'legends-za', 'Large Gourgeist put on the guise of adults, taking the hands of children to lead them to the afterlife.'),
    (711, 'legends-za', 'Singing in eerie voices, they wander town streets on the night of the new moon. Anyone who hears their song is cursed.'),
    (711, 'omega-ruby', 'Singing in eerie voices, they wander town streets on the night of the new moon. Anyone who hears their song is cursed.'),
    (711, 'shield', 'A large-sized Pumpkaboo evolves into a large-sized Gourgeist. Its bodily proportions also get passed on to its descendants.'),
    (711, 'shield', 'A small-sized Pumpkaboo evolves into a small-sized Gourgeist. Its bodily proportions also get passed on to its descendants.'),
    (711, 'shield', 'In the darkness of a new-moon night, Gourgeist will come knocking. Whoever answers the door will be swept off to the afterlife.'),
    (711, 'shield', 'A supersized Pumpkaboo evolves into a supersized Gourgeist. Its bodily proportions also get passed on to its descendants.'),
    (711, 'sword', 'Supersized Gourgeist aren''t picky. They will forcefully drag anyone off to the afterlife.'),
    (711, 'sword', 'Eerie cries emanate from its body in the dead of night. The sounds are said to be the wails of spirits who are suffering in the afterlife.'),
    (711, 'sword', 'Large Gourgeist put on the guise of adults, taking the hands of children to lead them to the afterlife.'),
    (711, 'sword', 'Small Gourgeist pretend to be children to fool adults. Anyone who falls for the act gets carried away to the hereafter.'),
    (711, 'x', 'Singing in eerie voices, they wander town streets on the night of the new moon. Anyone who hears their song is cursed.'),
    (711, 'y', 'It enwraps its prey in its hairlike arms. It sings joyfully as it observes the suffering of its prey.'),
    (712, 'alpha-sapphire', 'Using air of -150 degrees Fahrenheit, they freeze opponents solid. They live in herds above the snow line on mountains.'),
    (712, 'legends-arceus', 'Lives on mountains blanketed in perennial snow. It freezes water vapor in the air to make the ice helmet that it dons for defense.'),
    (712, 'legends-za', 'It blocks opponents'' attacks with the ice that shields its body. If the ice breaks, this Pokémon uses cold air to quickly create new ice.'),
    (712, 'omega-ruby', 'It blocks opponents'' attacks with the ice that shields its body. It uses cold air to repair any cracks with new ice.'),
    (712, 'scarlet', 'They live in mountainous regions of frigid cold. On rare occasions, they ride on the back of an Avalugg to cross seas and move to new habitats.'),
    (712, 'shield', 'This Pokémon lives in areas of frigid cold. It secures itself to the back of an Avalugg by freezing its feet in place.'),
    (712, 'sword', 'They chill the air around them to -150 degrees Fahrenheit, freezing the water in the air into ice that they use as armor.'),
    (712, 'violet', 'Bergmite protects itself by coating its body in ice formed by frigid air of -148 degrees Fahrenheit. It fights with Frigibax whenever they meet.'),
    (712, 'x', 'It blocks opponents'' attacks with the ice that shields its body. It uses cold air to repair any cracks with new ice.'),
    (712, 'y', 'Using air of -150 degrees Fahrenheit, they freeze opponents solid. They live in herds above the snow line on mountains.'),
    (713, 'alpha-sapphire', 'The way several Bergmite huddle on its back makes it look like an aircraft carrier made of ice.'),
    (713, 'omega-ruby', 'Its ice-covered body is as hard as steel. Its cumbersome frame crushes anything that stands in its way.'),
    (713, 'shield', 'As Avalugg moves about during the day, the cracks in its body deepen. The Pokémon''s body returns to a pristine state overnight.'),
    (713, 'sword', 'At high latitudes, this Pokémon can be found with clusters of Bergmite on its back as it swims among the icebergs.'),
    (713, 'x', 'Its ice-covered body is as hard as steel. Its cumbersome frame crushes anything that stands in its way.'),
    (713, 'y', 'The way several Bergmite huddle on its back makes it look like an aircraft carrier made of ice.'),
    (714, 'alpha-sapphire', 'Even a robust wrestler will become dizzy and unable to stand when exposed to its 200,000-hertz ultrasonic waves.'),
    (714, 'legends-za', 'Even a robust wrestler will become dizzy and unable to stand when exposed to its 200,000-hertz ultrasonic waves.'),
    (714, 'omega-ruby', 'They live in pitch-black caves. Their enormous ears can emit ultrasonic waves of 200,000 hertz.'),
    (714, 'scarlet', 'This Pokémon emits ultrasonic waves from its large ears to search for fruit to eat. It mistakes Applin for its food.'),
    (714, 'shield', 'No wavelength of sound is beyond Noibat''s ability to produce. The ultrasonic waves it generates can overcome much larger Pokémon.'),
    (714, 'sword', 'After nightfall, they emerge from the caves they nest in during the day. Using their ultrasonic waves, they go on the hunt for ripened fruit.'),
    (714, 'ultra-moon', 'It flies around in search of fruit to eat. It uses ultrasonic waves to detect which fruits are ripe.'),
    (714, 'ultra-sun', 'Fruits are its favorite foods. This gourmet carefully picks out just the ripe ones using its sonar.'),
    (714, 'violet', 'Noibat can change the frequency of its sound waves at will, and it generates ultrasonic waves of up to 200,000 hertz.'),
    (714, 'x', 'They live in pitch-black caves. Their enormous ears can emit ultrasonic waves of 200,000 hertz.'),
    (714, 'y', 'Even a robust wrestler will become dizzy and unable to stand when exposed to its 200,000-hertz ultrasonic waves.'),
    (715, 'alpha-sapphire', 'The ultrasonic waves it emits from its ears can reduce a large boulder to pebbles. It swoops out of the dark to attack.'),
    (715, 'legends-za', 'They fly around on moonless nights and attack careless prey. Nothing can beat them in a battle in the dark.'),
    (715, 'omega-ruby', 'They fly around on moonless nights and attack careless prey. Nothing can beat them in a battle in the dark.'),
    (715, 'scarlet', 'Ultrasonic waves emitted by a Noivern can pulverize a large boulder. This Pokémon has a cruel disposition.'),
    (715, 'shield', 'Flying through the darkness, it weakens enemies with ultrasonic waves that could crush stone. Its fangs finish the fight.'),
    (715, 'sword', 'Aggressive and cruel, this Pokémon will ruthlessly torment enemies that are helpless in the dark.'),
    (715, 'ultra-moon', 'This hot-blooded Pokémon attacks anything it sees with ultrasonic waves that can crush boulders.'),
    (715, 'ultra-sun', 'Although it has a violent disposition, if you give it a nice ripe fruit that it loves, Noivern will suddenly become tame.'),
    (715, 'violet', 'In the dark, even Hydreigon are terrified of this Pokémon. But in the light, Noivern is the one that avoids battle.'),
    (715, 'x', 'They fly around on moonless nights and attack careless prey. Nothing can beat them in a battle in the dark.'),
    (715, 'y', 'The ultrasonic waves it emits from its ears can reduce a large boulder to pebbles. It swoops out of the dark to attack.'),
    (716, 'alpha-sapphire', 'When the horns on its head shine in seven colors, it is said to be sharing everlasting life.'),
    (716, 'legends-za', 'When the horns on its head shine in seven colors, it is said to be sharing everlasting life.'),
    (716, 'omega-ruby', 'Legends say it can share eternal life. It slept for a thousand years in the form of a tree before its revival.'),
    (716, 'x', 'Legends say it can share eternal life. It slept for a thousand years in the form of a tree before its revival.'),
    (716, 'y', 'When the horns on its head shine in seven colors, it is said to be sharing everlasting life.'),
    (717, 'alpha-sapphire', 'When its life comes to an end, it absorbs the life energy of every living thing and turns into a cocoon once more.'),
    (717, 'legends-za', 'It''s said that when its life comes to an end, it absorbs the life energy of every living thing and turns into a cocoon once more.'),
    (717, 'omega-ruby', 'When this legendary Pokémon''s wings and tail feathers spread wide and glow red, it absorbs the life force of living creatures.'),
    (717, 'x', 'When this legendary Pokémon''s wings and tail feathers spread wide and glow red, it absorbs the life force of living creatures.'),
    (717, 'y', 'When its life comes to an end, it absorbs the life energy of every living thing and turns into a cocoon once more.'),
    (718, 'legends-za', 'It''s hypothesized that it''s monitoring those who destroy the ecosystem from deep in the cave where it lives.'),
    (718, 'moon', 'It''s thought to be monitoring the ecosystem. There are rumors that even greater power lies hidden within it.'),
    (718, 'sun', 'This is Zygarde''s form when it has gathered 50% of its cells. It wipes out all those who oppose it, showing not a shred of mercy.'),
    (718, 'ultra-moon', 'Some say it can change to an even more powerful form when battling those who threaten the ecosystem.'),
    (718, 'ultra-sun', 'This is Zygarde''s form when about half of its pieces have been assembled. It plays the role of monitoring the ecosystem.'),
    (719, 'alpha-sapphire', 'It can instantly create many diamonds by compressing the carbon in the air between its hands.'),
    (719, 'legends-za', 'Diancie is a spontaneous mutation of Carbink. Its pink, glimmering body is said to be the loveliest sight in the whole world.'),
    (719, 'omega-ruby', 'A sudden transformation of Carbink, its pink, glimmering body is said to be the loveliest sight in the whole world.'),
    (719, 'x', 'A sudden transformation of Carbink, its pink, glimmering body is said to be the loveliest sight in the whole world.'),
    (719, 'y', 'It can instantly create many diamonds by compressing the carbon in the air between its hands.'),
    (720, 'alpha-sapphire', 'It is said to be able to seize anything it desires with its six rings and six huge arms. With its power sealed, it is transformed into a much smaller form.'),
    (720, 'legends-za', 'It uses loops to gather things it likes and take them to its secret home. It also teleports through a loop.'),
    (720, 'omega-ruby', 'In its true form, it possess a huge amount of power. Legends of its avarice tell how it once carried off an entire castle to gain the treasure hidden within.'),
    (720, 'x', 'This troublemaker sends anything and everything to faraway places using its loop, which can warp space.'),
    (720, 'y', 'It gathers things it likes and passes them through its loop to teleport them to a secret place.'),
    (721, 'alpha-sapphire', 'It expels its internal steam from the arms on its back. It has enough power to blow away a mountain.'),
    (721, 'legends-za', 'It expels its internal steam from the arms on its back. It has enough power to blow away a mountain.'),
    (721, 'omega-ruby', 'It lets out billows of steam and disappears into the dense fog. It''s said to live in mountains where humans do not tread.'),
    (721, 'x', 'It lets out billows of steam and disappears into the dense fog. It''s said to live in mountains where humans do not tread.'),
    (721, 'y', 'It expels its internal steam from the arms on its back. It has enough power to blow away a mountain.'),
    (722, 'legends-arceus', 'Flies noiselessly on delicate wings. It has mastered the art of deftly launching dagger-sharp feathers from those same wings.'),
    (722, 'moon', 'Silently it glides, drawing near its targets. Before they even notice it, it begins to pelt them with vicious kicks.'),
    (722, 'scarlet', 'Silently it glides, streaking toward its targets to get close to them. Before they even notice it, it begins to pelt them with vicious kicks.'),
    (722, 'shield', 'During the day, it builds up energy via photosynthesis. At night, it flies silently through the sky, on the prowl for prey.*'),
    (722, 'sun', 'This wary Pokémon uses photosynthesis to store up energy during the day, while becoming active at night.'),
    (722, 'sword', 'At a distance, it launches its sharp feathers while flying about. If the enemy gets too close, Rowlet switches tactics and delivers vicious kicks.*'),
    (722, 'ultra-moon', 'It feels relaxed in tight, dark places and has been known to use its Trainer''s pocket or bag as a nest.'),
    (722, 'ultra-sun', 'It sends its feathers, which are as sharp as blades, flying in attack. Its legs are strong, so its kicks are also formidable.'),
    (722, 'violet', 'It feels relaxed in tight, dark places and has been known to nestle into its Trainer’s bag or the front of their jacket.'),
    (723, 'legends-arceus', 'Regularly basks in sunlight to gather power—presumably due to the frigid climate. Nonetheless, the edges of the blade quills set into its wings are keen as ever.'),
    (723, 'moon', 'It throws sharp feathers called blade quills at enemies or prey. It seldom misses.'),
    (723, 'scarlet', 'This narcissistic Pokémon is a clean freak. If you don’t groom it diligently, it may stop listening to you.'),
    (723, 'shield', 'It never slacks when it comes to the task of cleaning its feathers. Thorough preening keeps it looking spiffy and its blade quills nice and sharp.*'),
    (723, 'sun', 'A bit of a dandy, it spends its free time preening its wings. Its preoccupation with any dirt on its plumage can leave it unable to battle.'),
    (723, 'sword', 'It throws one knifelike feather after another at its enemies, and each one precisely strikes a weak point. These feathers are known as blade quills.*'),
    (723, 'ultra-moon', 'Supremely sensitive to the presence of others, it can detect opponents standing behind it, flinging its sharp feathers to take them out.'),
    (723, 'ultra-sun', 'This narcissistic Pokémon is a clean freak. If you don''t groom it diligently, it will stop listening to you.'),
    (723, 'violet', 'It throws sharp feathers called blade quills at enemies or prey. It seldom misses.'),
    (724, 'moon', 'Although basically cool and cautious, when it''s caught by surprise, it''s seized by panic.'),
    (724, 'shield', 'In a tenth of a second, it can nock and fire an arrow quill, piercing an opponent''s weak point before they notice what''s happening.*'),
    (724, 'sun', 'It fires arrow quills from its wings with such precision, they can pierce a pebble at distances over a hundred yards.'),
    (724, 'sword', 'As if wielding a bow, it launches the arrow quills hidden among the feathers of its wings. Decidueye''s shots never miss.*'),
    (724, 'ultra-moon', 'Decidueye can nock and fire an arrow at an enemy in a tenth of a second, so its battles are decided in the blink of an eye.'),
    (724, 'ultra-sun', 'It nocks its arrow quills and shoots them at opponents. When it simply can''t afford to miss, it tugs the vine on its head to improve its focus.'),
    (725, 'moon', 'It doesn''t allow its emotions to be easily seen. Earning its trust takes time. It prefers solitude.'),
    (725, 'scarlet', 'If you try too hard to get close to it, it won’t open up to you. Even if you do grow close, giving it too much affection is still a no-no.'),
    (725, 'shield', 'Trying to pet Litten before it trusts you will result in a nasty scratch from its sharp claws. Be careful.*'),
    (725, 'sun', 'While grooming itself, it builds up fur inside its stomach. It sets the fur alight and spews fiery attacks, which change based on how it coughs.'),
    (725, 'sword', 'It spends even the smallest amount of downtime grooming its fur with its tongue. Loose fur gathers in its stomach and serves as fuel for fiery moves.*'),
    (725, 'ultra-moon', 'Its coat regrows twice a year. When the time comes, Litten sets its own body on fire and burns away the old fur.'),
    (725, 'ultra-sun', 'If you try too hard to get close to it, it won''t open up to you. Even if you do grow close, giving it too much affection is still a no-no.'),
    (725, 'violet', 'While grooming itself, it builds up fur inside its stomach. It sets the fur alight and spews fiery attacks, which change based on how it coughs.'),
    (726, 'moon', 'It boasts powerful front legs. With a single punch, it can bend an iron bar right over.'),
    (726, 'scarlet', 'At its throat, it bears a bell of fire. The bell rings brightly whenever fire spews out.'),
    (726, 'shield', 'When facing a powerful enemy, Torracat''s fighting spirit gets pumped up, and its fire bell blazes hotter.*'),
    (726, 'sun', 'At its throat, it bears a bell of fire. The bell rings brightly whenever this Pokémon spits fire.'),
    (726, 'sword', 'In the midst of battle, the fire pouch on Torracat''s neck rings like a bell and produces stronger flames than usual.*'),
    (726, 'ultra-moon', 'When its mane is standing on end, you can tell it''s feeling good. When it isn''t feeling well, its fur will lie down flat.'),
    (726, 'ultra-sun', 'It can act spoiled if it grows close to its Trainer. A powerful Pokémon, its sharp claws can leave its Trainer''s whole body covered in scratches.'),
    (726, 'violet', 'Torracat will let its Trainer coddle it once they’ve grown close, but it’s a powerful, sharp-clawed Pokémon, so its Trainer gets covered in scratches.'),
    (727, 'moon', 'After hurling ferocious punches and flinging furious kicks, it finishes opponents off by spewing fire from around its navel.'),
    (727, 'scarlet', 'When its fighting spirit is set alight, the flames around its waist become especially intense.'),
    (727, 'shield', 'Incineroar''s rough and aggressive behavior is its most notable trait, but the way it helps out small Pokémon shows that it has a kind side as well.*'),
    (727, 'sun', 'This Pokémon has a violent, selfish disposition. If it''s not in the mood to listen, it will ignore its Trainer''s orders with complete nonchalance.'),
    (727, 'sword', 'It excels at violent, no-holds-barred battles. The temperature of the flames that issue from its navel exceeds 3,600 degrees Fahrenheit.*'),
    (727, 'ultra-moon', 'When its fighting spirit is set alight, the flames around its waist become especially intense.'),
    (727, 'ultra-sun', 'Although it''s rough mannered and egotistical, it finds beating down unworthy opponents boring. It gets motivated for stronger opponents.'),
    (727, 'violet', 'After hurling ferocious punches and flinging furious kicks, it finishes opponents off by spewing fire from around its navel.'),
    (728, 'moon', 'This Pokémon can control water bubbles. It practices diligently so it can learn to make big bubbles.'),
    (728, 'scarlet', 'This Pokémon can control balloons made of water. It practices diligently so it can learn to make big balloons.'),
    (728, 'shield', 'If Popplio want to create big, powerful balloons, they must be persistent. It takes daily practice for these Pokémon to develop their skills.*'),
    (728, 'sun', 'This Pokémon snorts body fluids from its nose, blowing balloons to smash into its foes. It''s famous for being a hard worker.'),
    (728, 'sword', 'It creates special bouncy balloons to send at its opponents. When the balloons pop, the sheer force of their bursting is what deals damage.*'),
    (728, 'ultra-moon', 'Popplio gets on top of its bouncy water balloons to jump higher. It''s quite the acrobatic fighter!'),
    (728, 'ultra-sun', 'The balloons it inflates with its nose grow larger and larger as it practices day by day.'),
    (728, 'violet', 'The balloons it inflates with its nose grow larger and larger as it practices day by day.'),
    (729, 'moon', 'It cares deeply for its companions. When its Trainer is feeling down, it performs a cheery dance to try and help.'),
    (729, 'scarlet', 'A skillful dancer, it creates a sequence of water balloons as it dances, then briskly bombards its enemies.'),
    (729, 'shield', 'On nights when the sea is calm, Brionne dance with one another to the singing of the Primarina that''s leading them.*'),
    (729, 'sun', 'A skillful dancer, it creates a sequence of water balloons as it dances, and briskly bombards its enemies.'),
    (729, 'sword', 'As if dancing, it artfully dodges the attacks of its enemies. All the while, it''s busy forming a bunch of balloons to overwhelm its foes.*'),
    (729, 'ultra-moon', 'It attacks by smacking its enemies with the exploding water balloons that it creates.'),
    (729, 'ultra-sun', 'It gets excited when it sees a dance it doesn''t know. This hard worker practices diligently until it can learn that dance.'),
    (729, 'violet', 'It cares deeply for its companions. When its Trainer is feeling down, it performs a cheery dance to try to help.'),
    (730, 'moon', 'Its singing voice is its chief weapon in battle. This Pokémon''s Trainer must prioritize the daily maintenance of its throat at all costs.'),
    (730, 'scarlet', 'To Primarina, every battle is a stage. It takes down its prey with beautiful singing and dancing.'),
    (730, 'shield', 'For Primarina, every battle''s a stage. Its singing and the dancing of its balloons will mesmerize the audience.*'),
    (730, 'sun', 'It Sparkling Aria. The melody is learned from others of its kind and is passed down from one generation to the next.'),
    (730, 'sword', 'With its mouth, it makes sonic waves that sound like beautiful singing. It uses the sonic waves to control its water balloons.*'),
    (730, 'ultra-moon', 'Also known as a songstress, it has a fantastical look on moonlit nights when it leads its colony in song.'),
    (730, 'ultra-sun', 'To Primarina, every battle is a stage. It takes down its prey with beautiful singing and dancing.'),
    (730, 'violet', 'Also known as a songstress, it is a sight to behold on moonlit nights when it sings in front of the colony it leads.'),
    (731, 'moon', 'This Pokémon feeds on berries, whose leftover seeds become the ammunition for the attacks it fires off from its mouth.'),
    (731, 'scarlet', 'Using its beak to strike 16 times per second, it opens holes in even the hardest of trees.'),
    (731, 'sun', 'It can peck at a rate of 16 times a second to drill holes in trees. It uses the holes for food storage and for nesting.'),
    (731, 'ultra-moon', 'It may look spindly, but its neck muscles are heavy-duty. It can peck at a tree 16 times per second!'),
    (731, 'ultra-sun', 'It pecks at trees with its hard beak. You can get some idea of its mood or condition from the rhythm of its pecking.'),
    (731, 'violet', 'Pikipek has strong muscles in its neck, so it won’t hurt itself even if it violently shakes its head.'),
    (732, 'moon', 'By bending its beak, it can produce a variety of calls and brand itself a noisy nuisance for its neighbors.'),
    (732, 'scarlet', 'It flies around using a hundred different cries in various ways to declare its territory to others.'),
    (732, 'sun', 'It eats berries and stores their seeds in its beak. When it encounters enemies or prey, it fires off all the seeds in a burst.'),
    (732, 'ultra-moon', 'From its mouth, it fires the seeds of berries it has eaten. The scattered seeds give rise to new plants.'),
    (732, 'ultra-sun', 'It can bend the tip of its beak to produce over a hundred different cries at will.'),
    (732, 'violet', 'When it encounters foes, it launches the many seeds stored in its beak in a radial burst.'),
    (733, 'moon', 'Within its beak, its internal gas ignites, explosively launching seeds with enough power to pulverize boulders.'),
    (733, 'scarlet', 'The compressed gas in Toucannon’s beak launches seeds with such force that they can shatter large boulders.'),
    (733, 'sun', 'When it battles, Beak Blast. The temperature can easily exceed 212 degrees Fahrenheit, causing severe burns when it hits.'),
    (733, 'ultra-moon', 'Known for forming harmonious couples, this Pokémon is brought to wedding ceremonies as a good luck charm.'),
    (733, 'ultra-sun', 'They smack beaks with others of their kind to communicate. The strength and number of hits tell each other how they feel.'),
    (733, 'violet', 'Pairs of Toucannon are considered symbols of companionship, as these Pokémon will raise the temperature of their beaks to warm each other.'),
    (734, 'moon', 'It wanders around in a never-ending search for food. At dusk, it collapses from exhaustion and falls asleep on the spot.'),
    (734, 'scarlet', 'Its stomach fills most of its torso. It wanders the same path every day, searching for fresh food.'),
    (734, 'sun', 'With its sharp fangs, it will bite anything. It did not originally live in Alola but was imported from another region.'),
    (734, 'ultra-moon', 'Although it will eat anything, it prefers fresh living things, so it marches down streets in search of prey.'),
    (734, 'ultra-sun', 'Its stomach takes up most of its long torso. It''s a big eater, so the amount Trainers have to spend on its food is no laughing matter.'),
    (734, 'violet', 'It spends its waking hours searching for food. When Yungoos is hungry, its ferocity gains a certain edge.'),
    (735, 'moon', 'It adores having Rattata and Raticate for dinner, but as it''s {{pkmn2|diurnal}}, it never encounters them. This Pokémon boasts incredible patience.'),
    (735, 'scarlet', 'Once it finds signs of prey, it will patiently stake out the location, waiting until the sun goes down.'),
    (735, 'sun', 'When it finds a trace of its prey, it patiently stakes out the location...but it''s always snoozing by nightfall.'),
    (735, 'ultra-moon', 'Patient by nature, this Pokémon loses control of itself and pounces when it spots its favorite meal—Rattata!'),
    (735, 'ultra-sun', 'Although it wasn''t originally found in Alola, this Pokémon was brought over a long time ago when there was a huge Rattata outbreak.'),
    (735, 'violet', 'Gumshoos specializes in relentlessly tracking down prey. The simple-minded Skwovet doesn''t seem to provide Gumshoos enough challenge.'),
    (736, 'moon', 'They often gather near places frequented by electric Pokémon in order to avoid being attacked by bird Pokémon.'),
    (736, 'scarlet', 'Grubbin normally live underground, but if they get unearthed by {{P|Hoothoot}}, they may be found gathered around electric Pokémon.'),
    (736, 'shield', 'It uses its big jaws to dig nests into the forest floor, and it loves to feed on sweet tree sap.'),
    (736, 'sun', 'Its strong jaw enables it to scrape trees and slurp out the sap. It normally lives underground.'),
    (736, 'sword', 'Its natural enemies, like {{P|Rookidee}}, may flee rather than risk getting caught in its large mandibles that can snap thick tree branches.'),
    (736, 'ultra-moon', 'It spits a sticky thread to stop opponents in their tracks, and then it grabs them in its sharp, sturdy mandibles to take them down.'),
    (736, 'ultra-sun', 'If you find its nest, you shouldn''t stick your hand inside. You''ll get bitten by an irritated Grubbin.'),
    (736, 'violet', 'It spits sticky thread and winds them around branches, then swings nimbly from tree to tree in a pendulum-like motion.'),
    (737, 'moon', 'From the food it digests, it generates electricity, and it stores this energy in its electric sac.'),
    (737, 'scarlet', 'Protected by a sturdy shell, Charjabug eats large quantities of fresh and decomposing leaf litter in order to evolve.'),
    (737, 'shield', 'Its digestive processes convert the leaves it eats into electricity. An electric sac in its belly stores the electricity for later use.'),
    (737, 'sun', 'Its body is capable of storing electricity. On camping trips, people are grateful to have one around.'),
    (737, 'sword', 'While its durable shell protects it from attacks, Charjabug strikes at enemies with jolts of electricity discharged from the tips of its jaws.'),
    (737, 'ultra-moon', 'Its stout shell provides excellent defense from attacks. It uses electricity on persistent opponents.'),
    (737, 'ultra-sun', 'It buries itself in fallen leaves and barely moves, munching away on humus. If you accidentally step on one, you''ll get a shock!'),
    (737, 'violet', 'As it digests fallen leaves, it generates and stores electricity, which it can discharge from the tips of its jaws.'),
    (738, 'moon', 'It produces electricity via an electrical organ in its abdomen. It overwhelms bird Pokémon with shocking beams of electrical energy.'),
    (738, 'scarlet', 'Displaying exceptional mobility, it weaves between trees and shoots down bird Pokémon with its electromagnetic beams.'),
    (738, 'shield', 'If it carries a Charjabug to use as a spare battery, a flying Vikavolt can rapidly fire high-powered beams of electricity.'),
    (738, 'sun', 'It zips around, on sharp lookout for an opening. It concentrates electrical energy within its large jaws and uses it to zap its enemies.'),
    (738, 'sword', 'It builds up electricity in its abdomen, focuses it through its jaws, and then fires the electricity off in concentrated beams.'),
    (738, 'ultra-moon', 'Vikavolt flusters opponents with acrobatic flying maneuvers. This creates an opening for it to deliver an electric beam attack.'),
    (738, 'ultra-sun', 'It has an organ that generates electricity in its abdomen. It concentrates energy in its strong jaws and fires off powerful jolts of electricity.'),
    (738, 'violet', 'When carrying a Charjabug, Vikavolt can receive electricity from it and then rapidly fire powerful electromagnetic beams from its large jaws.'),
    (739, 'legends-za', 'Its hard pincers are well-suited to both offense and defense. Fights between two Crabrawler are like boxing matches.'),
    (739, 'moon', 'It punches so much, its pincers often come off from overuse, but they grow back quickly. What little meat they contain is rich and delicious.'),
    (739, 'scarlet', 'This Pokémon punches trees and eats the berries that drop down, training itself and getting food at the same time.'),
    (739, 'sun', 'While guarding its weak points with its pincers, it looks for an opening and unleashes punches. When it loses, it foams at the mouth and faints.'),
    (739, 'ultra-moon', 'Crabrawler has been known to mistake Exeggutor for a coconut tree and climb it. The enraged Exeggutor shakes it off and stomps it.'),
    (739, 'ultra-sun', 'Its hard pincers are well suited to both offense and defense. Fights between two Crabrawler are like boxing matches.'),
    (739, 'violet', 'If it loses its pincers, they''ll quickly regrow. The pincers are popular ingredients in paella since their shells produce a tasty soup stock.'),
    (740, 'legends-za', 'It punches things without pausing to think. There are even records of Crabominable forcing back an avalanche with a flurry of punches.'),
    (740, 'moon', 'It just throws punches indiscriminately. In times of desperation, it can lop off its own pincers and fire them like rockets.'),
    (740, 'scarlet', 'The detached pincers of these Pokémon are delicious. Some Trainers bring Lechonk into the mountains just to search for them.'),
    (740, 'sun', 'It aimed for the top but got lost and ended up on a snowy mountain. Being forced to endure the cold, this Pokémon evolved and grew fur.'),
    (740, 'ultra-moon', 'Before it stops to think, it just starts pummeling. There are records of its turning back avalanches with a flurry of punches.'),
    (740, 'ultra-sun', 'It stores coldness in its pincers and pummels its foes. It can even smash thick walls of ice to bits!'),
    (740, 'violet', 'Though its punches are powerful, this Pokémon''s movements are sluggish. It blows icy bubbles from its mouth to immobilize its opponents.'),
    (741, 'moon', 'This Oricorio has sipped red nectar. Its passionate dance moves cause its enemies to combust in both body and mind.'),
    (741, 'scarlet', 'This Pokémon is incredibly popular, possibly because its passionate dancing is a great match with the temperament of Paldean people.'),
    (741, 'sun', 'It beats its wings together to create fire. As it moves in the steps of its beautiful dance, it bathes opponents in intense flames.'),
    (741, 'ultra-moon', 'This Oricorio has drunk red nectar. If its Trainer gives the wrong order, this passionate Pokémon becomes fiercely angry.'),
    (741, 'ultra-sun', 'It wins the hearts of its enemies with its passionate dancing and then uses the opening it creates to burn them up with blazing flames.'),
    (741, 'violet', 'This form of Oricorio has sipped red nectar. It whips up blazing flames as it moves to the steps of its passionate dance.'),
    (742, 'moon', 'Myriads of Cutiefly flutter above the heads of people who have auras resembling those of flowers.'),
    (742, 'scarlet', 'When it senses the auras of people or Pokémon who are having fun, it will draw close and give them a painful poke with its long proboscis.'),
    (742, 'shield', 'An opponent''s aura can tell Cutiefly what that opponent''s next move will be. Then Cutiefly can glide around the attack and strike back.'),
    (742, 'sun', 'It feeds on the nectar and pollen of flowers. Because it''s able to sense auras, it can identify which flowers are about to bloom.'),
    (742, 'sword', 'Nectar and pollen are its favorite fare. You can find Cutiefly hovering around Gossifleur, trying to get some of Gossifleur''s pollen.'),
    (742, 'ultra-moon', 'Cutiefly can pick up the auras of living things. It skillfully reads those auras to predict its foes'' movements and make fools of them.'),
    (742, 'ultra-sun', 'Nectar and pollen are its favorite fare. In fields of flowers, it gets into skirmishes with Butterfree over food.'),
    (742, 'violet', 'Cutiefly sucks up pollen and nectar with its long proboscis. It stores any pollen it doesn''t finish eating in its fur.'),
    (743, 'moon', 'Some of Ribombee''s pollen puffs are highly nutritious. They are sometimes sold as supplements.'),
    (743, 'scarlet', 'Ribombee can sense when people or Pokémon are feeling down, and it will cheer them up with handmade pollen puffs.'),
    (743, 'shield', 'Ribombee absolutely hate getting wet or rained on. In the cloudy [[Galar]] region, they are very seldom seen.'),
    (743, 'sun', 'It rolls up pollen into puffs. It makes many different varieties, some used as food and others used in battle.'),
    (743, 'sword', 'It makes pollen puffs from pollen and nectar. The puffs'' effects depend on the type of ingredients and how much of each one is used.'),
    (743, 'ultra-moon', 'It can predict the weather from moisture levels and wind direction. Ribombee only reveals itself when there are a few clear days in a row.'),
    (743, 'ultra-sun', 'Rain makes pollen damp, so Ribombee hates rain. When it sees ominous clouds, it finds a hollow in a tree, where it waits stock-still.'),
    (743, 'violet', 'Pollen puffs created by skilled Ribombee can relieve fatigue, making the puffs a popular commodity.'),
    (744, 'moon', 'This Pokémon has lived with people since times long ago. It can sense when its Trainer is in the dumps and will stick close by its Trainer''s side.'),
    (744, 'scarlet', 'This Pokémon is very friendly when it''s young. Its disposition becomes vicious once it matures, but it never forgets the kindness of its master.'),
    (744, 'shield', 'This Pokémon intimidates opponents by striking the ground with the rocks on its neck. The moment an opponent flinches, Rockruff attacks.'),
    (744, 'sun', 'It''s considered to be a good Pokémon for beginners because of its friendliness, but its disposition grows rougher as it grows up.'),
    (744, 'sword', 'This Pokémon can bond very strongly with its Trainer, but it also has a habit of biting. Raising a Rockruff for a long time can be challenging.'),
    (744, 'ultra-moon', 'When it rubs the rocks on its neck against you, that''s proof of its love for you. However, the rocks are sharp, so the gesture is quite painful!'),
    (744, 'ultra-sun', 'As they develop, their disposition grows more violent and aggressive. Many Trainers find them too much to handle and abandon them.'),
    (744, 'violet', 'This Pokémon travels in a pack with others until it grows up. When its mood turns sour, it starts striking the ground with the rocks on its neck.'),
    (745, 'moon', 'When properly raised from a young age, it will become a trustworthy partner that will absolutely never betray its {{pkmn|Trainer}}.'),
    (745, 'scarlet', 'Lycanroc attacks its prey with its sharp claws and fangs. It loyally obeys the instructions of a {{pkmn|Trainer}} it trusts.'),
    (745, 'shield', 'With swift movements, this Pokémon gradually backs its prey into a corner. Lycanroc''s fangs are always aimed toward opponents'' weak spots.'),
    (745, 'sun', 'Its quick movements confuse its enemies. Well equipped with claws and fangs, it also uses the sharp rocks in its mane as weapons.'),
    (745, 'sword', 'This Lycanroc is calm and cautious. The rocks jutting from its mane are razor sharp.'),
    (745, 'ultra-moon', 'The rocks in its mane are sharper than a knife. Fragments that break off are treasured as good luck charms.'),
    (745, 'ultra-sun', 'The sharp rocks in its mane can cut like knives. Lycanroc wears its prey down by degrees before finishing them off.'),
    (745, 'violet', 'It has a calm and collected demeanor. It swiftly closes in on its prey, then slices them with the rocks in its mane.'),
    (746, 'moon', 'It''s awfully weak and notably tasty, so everyone is always out to get it. As it happens, anyone trying to bully it receives a painful lesson.'),
    (746, 'shield', 'When it senses danger, its eyes tear up. The sparkle of its tears signals other Wishiwashi to gather.'),
    (746, 'sun', 'When it''s in trouble, its eyes moisten and begin to shine. The shining light attracts its comrades, and they stand together against their enemies.'),
    (746, 'sword', 'Individually, they''re incredibly weak. It''s by gathering up into schools that they''re able to confront opponents.'),
    (746, 'ultra-moon', 'When it''s in a jam, its shining eyes attract others of its kind. The light from its eyes is visible almost 25 miles away.'),
    (746, 'ultra-sun', 'They''re weak, so they move in schools. However, they can also often be seen all alone, having strayed from the school.'),
    (747, 'moon', 'It''s found crawling on beaches and seafloors. The coral that grows on Corsola''s head is as good as a five-star banquet to this Pokémon.'),
    (747, 'scarlet', 'This Pokémon wanders the seaside looking for food. It often gets electric shocks from broken Pincurchin spines that it tries to eat.'),
    (747, 'shield', 'Unlike their Alolan counterparts, the Mareanie of the Galar region have not yet figured out that the branches of Corsola are delicious.'),
    (747, 'sun', 'It plunges the poison spike on its head into its prey. When the prey has weakened, Mareanie deals the finishing blow with its 10 tentacles.'),
    (747, 'sword', 'The first symptom of its sting is numbness. The next is an itching sensation so intense that it''s impossible to resist the urge to claw at your skin.'),
    (747, 'ultra-moon', 'Aside from its head, its body parts regenerate quickly if they''re cut off. After a good night''s sleep, Mareanie is back to normal.'),
    (747, 'ultra-sun', 'They eat Corsola branches, so Mareanie are hated by craftsmen who work with Corsola branches that have naturally fallen off.'),
    (747, 'violet', 'It has excellent regenerative capabilities. Legs that a Mareanie has lost have a very bitter, astringent flavor—they''re not suitable as food.'),
    (748, 'moon', 'Those attacked by Toxapex''s poison will suffer intense pain for three days and three nights. Post-recovery, there will be some aftereffects.'),
    (748, 'scarlet', 'This Pokémon lives within a dome made by its own legs. Toxapex monitors its surroundings by sensing the flow of the tide through its spikes.'),
    (748, 'shield', 'Within the poison sac in its body is a poison so toxic that Pokémon as large as Wailord will still be suffering three days after it first takes effect.'),
    (748, 'sun', 'Toxapex crawls along the ocean floor on its 12 legs. It leaves a trail of Corsola bits scattered in its wake.'),
    (748, 'sword', 'To survive in the cold waters of Galar, this Pokémon forms a dome with its legs, enclosing its body so it can capture its own body heat.'),
    (748, 'ultra-moon', 'With its 12 legs, it creates a dome to shelter within. The flow of the tides doesn''t affect Toxapex in there, so it''s very comfortable.'),
    (748, 'ultra-sun', 'To attack, this Pokémon sends toxic spikes flying at its enemies. Ones that come close get mown down by the claws on its feet.'),
    (748, 'violet', 'Toxapex gets into fierce battles with Bruxish over areas where warm ocean currents flow, but the odds are always against it.'),
    (749, 'moon', 'It has a stubborn, individualistic disposition. Eating dirt, making mud, and playing in the mire all form part of its daily routine.'),
    (749, 'scarlet', 'This Pokémon covers itself in mud that it has regurgitated. The mud won’t dry out even if it’s exposed to the sun for a long time.'),
    (749, 'shield', 'It eats dirt to create mud and smears this mud all over its feet, giving them the grip needed to walk on rough terrain without slipping.'),
    (749, 'sun', 'The mud stuck to Mudbray''s hooves enhances its grip and its powerful running gait.'),
    (749, 'sword', 'Loads weighing up to 50 times as much as its own body weight pose no issue for this Pokémon. It''s skilled at making use of mud.'),
    (749, 'ultra-moon', 'Possessing mighty power, Mudbray can be loaded with 50 times its own body weight and will be totally fine.'),
    (749, 'ultra-sun', 'It loves playing in the mud. If it isn''t showered with mud on a daily basis, it gets stressed out and stops listening to its Trainer.'),
    (749, 'violet', 'Though a slow walker, Mudbray is plenty strong. Its pace doesn''t change even when it''s loaded with 50 times its own body weight.'),
    (750, 'moon', 'Its heavy, mud-covered kicks are its best means of attack, and it can reduce large trucks to scrap without breaking a sweat.'),
    (750, 'scarlet', 'This Pokémon has been treasured not just for its physical labor but also because it produces high-quality mud used for making pottery.'),
    (750, 'shield', 'Mudsdale has so much stamina that it could carry over 10 tons across the Galar region without rest or sleep.'),
    (750, 'sun', 'It spits a mud that provides resistance to both wind and rain, so the walls of old houses were often coated with it.'),
    (750, 'sword', 'Mud that hardens around a Mudsdale''s legs sets harder than stone. It''s so hard that it allows this Pokémon to scrap a truck with a single kick.'),
    (750, 'ultra-moon', 'It can trudge mountain roads without rest for three days and three nights, all the while dragging a 10-ton load.'),
    (750, 'ultra-sun', 'It remains calm and unmoving no matter the situation. It mixes dirt with the saliva in its mouth to make a special kind of mud.'),
    (750, 'violet', 'Its legs are fortified with mud and harder than stone, and they can reduce a large truck to scrap with one kick.'),
    (751, 'moon', 'When it comes across enemies or potential prey, this Pokémon smashes its water-bubble-covered head into them.'),
    (751, 'scarlet', 'Dewpider uses sticky threads to create the water bubble that covers its head, so the bubble very rarely bursts.'),
    (751, 'shield', 'Dewpider normally lives underwater. When it comes onto land in search of food, it takes water with it in the form of a bubble on its head.'),
    (751, 'sun', 'It crawls onto the land in search of food. Its water bubble allows it to breathe and protects its soft head.'),
    (751, 'sword', 'It forms a water bubble at the rear of its body and then covers its head with it. Meeting another Dewpider means comparing water-bubble sizes.'),
    (751, 'ultra-moon', 'It can only breathe oxygen that has dissolved in water, so it wears a water bubble on its head when it walks around on land.'),
    (751, 'ultra-sun', 'When two Dewpider meet, they display their water bubbles to each other. Then the one with the smaller bubble gets out of the other''s way.'),
    (751, 'violet', 'It supports the water bubble that envelops its head with three of its legs. Sometimes it secretly swaps which legs are holding up the bubble.'),
    (752, 'moon', 'Despite what its appearance suggests, it cares for others. If it finds vulnerable, weak Pokémon, it protectively brings them into its water bubble.'),
    (752, 'scarlet', 'A caring Pokémon, Araquanid carries Dewpider around inside its water bubble to protect them as it walks. It protects its food in its bubble too.'),
    (752, 'shield', 'It acts as a caretaker for Dewpider, putting them inside its bubble and letting them eat any leftover food.'),
    (752, 'sun', 'It delivers headbutts with the water bubble on its head. Small Pokémon get sucked into the bubble, where they drown.'),
    (752, 'sword', 'It launches water bubbles with its legs, drowning prey within the bubbles. This Pokémon can then take its time to savor its meal.'),
    (752, 'ultra-moon', 'It has a habit of storing things it values in its water bubble. If its Trainer doesn''t watch out, Araquanid will try to put them in its bubble!'),
    (752, 'ultra-sun', 'It usually passes its time in the water. When its belly is full, it stores its subdued prey in the water bubble on its head.'),
    (752, 'violet', 'It launches sticky water bubbles. Foes who lose consciousness while trapped inside these bubbles will get torn apart by Araquanid’s gnashing jaws.'),
    (753, 'moon', 'They give off a sweet and refreshing scent. {{P|Cutiefly}} often gather near the tall grass where Fomantis are hiding.'),
    (753, 'scarlet', 'Fomantis hates having its naps interrupted. It fires off beams using energy it gathers by bathing in the sun.'),
    (753, 'shield', 'During the day, Fomantis basks in sunlight and sleeps peacefully. It wakes and moves around at night.'),
    (753, 'sun', 'During the day, it sleeps and soaks up light. When night falls, it walks around looking for a safer place to sleep.'),
    (753, 'sword', 'When bathed in sunlight, this Pokémon emits a pleasantly sweet scent, which causes bug Pokémon to gather around it.'),
    (753, 'ultra-moon', 'It loves the sunshine. When it basks in the sunlight regularly, it grows up with vivid coloration.'),
    (753, 'ultra-sun', 'When the sun rises, Fomantis spreads its four leaves and bathes in the sunlight. The tip of its head has a pleasant aroma.'),
    (753, 'violet', 'Many Trainers give their Fomantis their own flowerpots so they can sunbathe in peace and quiet.'),
    (754, 'moon', 'It fires beams from its sickle-shaped petals. These beams are powerful enough to cleave through thick metal plates.'),
    (754, 'scarlet', 'By masquerading as a bug Pokémon, it lowers the guard of actual bug Pokémon lured in by a scent of sweet flowers. Its sickles bring them down.'),
    (754, 'shield', 'The petals on this Pokémon''s arms are thin and super sharp, and they can fire laser beams if Lurantis gathers light first.'),
    (754, 'sun', 'It requires a lot of effort to maintain Lurantis''s vivid coloring, but some collectors enjoy this work and treat it as their hobby.'),
    (754, 'sword', 'This Pokémon resembles a beautiful flower. A properly raised Lurantis will have gorgeous, brilliant colors.'),
    (754, 'ultra-moon', 'As it slashes into its enemies, it looks like it''s dancing. Its elegant appearance has led some to call it the most glamorous Grass Pokémon.'),
    (754, 'ultra-sun', 'For self-protection, it pretends to be a bug Pokémon. Both of its arms bear keen-edged petals.'),
    (754, 'violet', 'A lot of time and effort is required to maintain the vivid colors of its petals. This Pokémon puts its Trainer''s attentiveness to the test.'),
    (755, 'moon', 'As it drowses the day away, it nourishes itself by sucking from tree roots. It wakens at the fall of night, wandering off in search of a new tree.'),
    (755, 'shield', 'Morelull live in forests that stay dark even during the day. They scatter flickering spores that put enemies to sleep.'),
    (755, 'sun', 'It scatters spores that flicker and glow. Anyone seeing these lights falls into a deep slumber.'),
    (755, 'sword', 'Pokémon living in the forest eat the delicious caps on Morelull''s head. The caps regrow overnight.'),
    (755, 'ultra-moon', 'It likes damp dark places. When night falls, the spores filling the caps of its mushrooms glow.'),
    (755, 'ultra-sun', 'It scatters its shining spores around itself. Even though they''re dangerous, nighttime tours of forests where Morelull live are popular.'),
    (756, 'moon', 'It emits flickering spores that cause drowsiness. When its prey succumb to sleep, this Pokémon feeds on them by sucking in their energy.'),
    (756, 'shield', 'If you see a light deep in a forest at night, don''t go near. Shiinotic will make you fall fast asleep.'),
    (756, 'sun', 'Forests where Shiinotic live are treacherous to enter at night. People confused by its strange lights can never find their way home again.'),
    (756, 'sword', 'Its flickering spores lure in prey and put them to sleep. Once this Pokémon has its prey snoozing, it drains their vitality with its fingertips.'),
    (756, 'ultra-moon', 'When it starts fighting for territory with Parasect, the entire area gets completely coated in spores!'),
    (756, 'ultra-sun', 'It puts its prey to sleep and siphons off their vitality through the tip of its arms. If one of its kind is weakened, it helps by sending it vitality.'),
    (757, 'moon', 'Volcanoes or dry, craggy places are its home. It emanates a sweet-smelling poisonous gas that attracts bug Pokémon, then attacks them.'),
    (757, 'scarlet', 'It taunts its prey and lures them into narrow, rocky areas where it then sprays them with toxic gas to make them dizzy and take them down.'),
    (757, 'shield', 'This sneaky Pokémon will slink behind its prey and immobilize it with poisonous gas before the prey even realizes Salandit is there.'),
    (757, 'sun', 'It burns its bodily fluids to create a poisonous gas. When its enemies become disoriented from inhaling the gas, it attacks them.'),
    (757, 'sword', 'Its venom sacs produce a fluid that this Pokémon then heats up with the flame in its tail. This process creates Salandit''s poisonous gas.'),
    (757, 'ultra-moon', 'It weakens opponents and sends them reeling with its poisonous gas. Salandit doesn''t deal well with Spinda, since it''s always reeling.'),
    (757, 'ultra-sun', 'The males will do whatever the females tell them. They give the females most of their food. Due to malnutrition, the males can''t evolve.'),
    (757, 'violet', 'Only female Salandit can produce gas laden with pheromones. Males entranced by this gas will do whatever the females tell them.'),
    (758, 'moon', 'Filled with pheromones, its poisonous gas can be diluted to use in the production of luscious perfumes.'),
    (758, 'scarlet', 'Salazzle makes its opponents light-headed with poisonous gas, then captivates them with alluring movements to turn them into loyal servants.'),
    (758, 'shield', 'The winner of competitions between Salazzle is decided by which one has the most male Salandit with it.'),
    (758, 'sun', 'For some reason, only females have been found. It creates a reverse harem of male Salandit that it lives with.'),
    (758, 'sword', 'Only female Salazzle exist. They emit a gas laden with pheromones to captivate male Salandit.'),
    (758, 'ultra-moon', 'It punishes Salandit that couldn''t bring it food with a fierce slap of its flame-spewing palm.'),
    (758, 'ultra-sun', 'Salazzle lives deep in caves and forces the Salandit it has attracted with its pheromones to serve it.'),
    (758, 'violet', 'When two Salazzle meet, they will use their pheromone gas to fight over the males in each other''s group.'),
    (759, 'moon', 'A touch from anyone except a known friend sends it into a surging frenzy. It''s an incredibly dangerous Pokémon.'),
    (759, 'shield', 'The way it protects itself by flailing its arms may be an adorable sight, but stay well away. This is flailing that can snap thick tree trunks.'),
    (759, 'sun', 'Despite its adorable appearance, when it gets angry and flails about, its arms and legs could knock a pro wrestler sprawling.'),
    (759, 'sword', 'Its fluffy fur is a delight to pet, but carelessly reaching out to touch this Pokémon could result in painful retaliation.'),
    (759, 'ultra-moon', 'Stufful hates to be hugged or touched in any way. It will squirm, thrash, and resist with amazing power.'),
    (759, 'ultra-sun', 'It boasts power enough to split large trees in half. The organ on its rear releases an odor that it uses to communicate with others of its kind.'),
    (760, 'moon', 'This Pokémon has the habit of hugging its companions. Many Trainers have left this world after their spines were squashed by its hug.'),
    (760, 'shield', 'The moves it uses to take down its prey would make a martial artist jealous. It tucks subdued prey under its arms to carry them to its nest.'),
    (760, 'sun', 'This immensely dangerous Pokémon possesses overwhelming physical strength. Its habitat is generally off-limits.'),
    (760, 'sword', 'Once it accepts you as a friend, it tries to show its affection with a hug. Letting it do that is dangerous—it could easily shatter your bones.'),
    (760, 'ultra-moon', 'It boasts tremendous physical strength. Many people call it the most dangerous Pokémon in the Alola region.'),
    (760, 'ultra-sun', 'It waves its hands wildly in intimidation and warning. Life is over for anyone who doesn''t run away as fast as possible.'),
    (761, 'moon', 'Although it''s too sugary for human consumption, Bounsweet''s sweat can be watered down into a juice with just the right amount of sweetness.'),
    (761, 'scarlet', 'Its sweat is sweet, like syrup made from boiled-down fruit. Because of this, Bounsweet was highly valued in the past, when sweeteners were scarce.'),
    (761, 'shield', 'When under attack, it secretes a sweet and delicious sweat. The scent only calls more enemies to it.'),
    (761, 'sun', 'A delectable aroma pours from its body. They are often swallowed whole by Toucannon lured by that wafting deliciousness.'),
    (761, 'sword', 'Its body gives off a sweet, fruity scent that is extremely appetizing to bird Pokémon.'),
    (761, 'ultra-moon', 'It tries to resist being swallowed by a bird Pokémon by spinning the sepals on its head. It''s usually a fruitless attempt.'),
    (761, 'ultra-sun', 'Because of its sweet, delicious aroma, bird Pokémon are always after it, but it''s not intelligent enough to care.'),
    (761, 'violet', 'A Greedent drawn in by the sweet scent of these Pokémon will tuck the Bounsweet in among the berries in its tail and carry them all away.'),
    (762, 'moon', 'This Pokémon is always bouncing around energetically. Other Pokémon are attracted by its lively appearance and pleasant aroma.'),
    (762, 'scarlet', 'Steenee spreads a sweet scent that makes others feel invigorated. This same scent is popular for antiperspirants.'),
    (762, 'shield', 'Any {{P|Corvisquire}} that pecks at this Pokémon will be greeted with a smack from its sepals followed by a sharp kick.'),
    (762, 'sun', 'The sepals on its head developed to protect its body. These are quite hard, so even if pecked by bird Pokémon, this Pokémon is totally fine.'),
    (762, 'sword', 'As it twirls like a dancer, a sweet smell spreads out around it. Anyone who inhales the scent will feel a surge of happiness.'),
    (762, 'ultra-moon', 'It bounces around, swinging the sepals on its head with abandon. They''re quite painful when they smack you!'),
    (762, 'ultra-sun', 'It''s protected by its hard sepals, so it plays with bird Pokémon without worry. They peck it relentlessly, but it doesn''t care.'),
    (762, 'violet', 'Steenee bounces energetically through forests. If the rind that peels off its body is pulverized, it can be used to treat stomach pains.'),
    (763, 'moon', 'A Pokémon known for the beauty of its well-shaped legs, it sometimes appears as a mascot in advertisements for beauty salons.'),
    (763, 'scarlet', 'This Pokémon is proud and aggressive. However, it is said that a Tsareena will instantly become calm if someone touches the crown on its calyx.'),
    (763, 'shield', 'A kick from the hardened tips of this Pokémon''s legs leaves a wound in the opponent''s body and soul that will never heal.'),
    (763, 'sun', 'Its long, striking legs aren''t just for show but to be used to kick with skill. In victory, it shows off by kicking the defeated, laughing boisterously.'),
    (763, 'sword', 'This feared Pokémon has long, slender legs and a cruel heart. It shows no mercy as it stomps on its opponents.'),
    (763, 'ultra-moon', 'A Pokémon with an aggressive personality and a mastery of kicking, it cackles every time it kicks an opponent.'),
    (763, 'ultra-sun', 'A master of grand and beautiful kicks, it can knock out even kickboxing champions with a single blow.'),
    (763, 'violet', 'This Pokémon launches fierce yet elegant kicks with its long, slender legs. It views Quaquaval as its rival.'),
    (764, 'moon', 'Baths prepared with the flowers from its vine have a relaxing effect, so this Pokémon is a hit with many people.'),
    (764, 'scarlet', 'It uses its vine to pick flowers. The flowers that Comfey attaches to itself develop healing properties.'),
    (764, 'shield', 'These Pokémon smell very nice. All Comfey wear different flowers, so each of these Pokémon has its own individual scent.'),
    (764, 'sun', 'It attaches flowers to its highly nutritious vine. This revitalizes the flowers, and they give off an aromatic scent.'),
    (764, 'sword', 'Comfey picks flowers with its vine and decorates itself with them. For some reason, flowers won''t wither once they''re attached to a Comfey.'),
    (764, 'ultra-moon', 'It picks flowers and sticks them to its body with fluids it produces. The aroma that wafts from its petals has a healing effect.'),
    (764, 'ultra-sun', 'It stretches sticky vines out from its head and picks flowers to adorn itself with. When it doesn''t have any flowers, it feels uneasy.'),
    (764, 'violet', 'It prefers areas with lots of flowers. A Comfey adorned with flowers is a happy Comfey, and the flowers gain healing effects.'),
    (765, 'moon', 'Deep in the jungle, high in the lofty canopy, this Pokémon abides. On rare occasions, it shows up at the beach to match wits with Slowking.'),
    (765, 'scarlet', 'People used to mistake Oranguru for a human when they saw it issue command after command to the other Pokémon of the forest.'),
    (765, 'shield', 'It knows the forest inside and out. If it comes across a wounded Pokémon, Oranguru will gather medicinal herbs to treat it.'),
    (765, 'sun', 'Known for its extreme intelligence, this Pokémon will look down on inexperienced Trainers, so it''s best suited to veteran Trainers.'),
    (765, 'sword', 'With waves of its fan—made from leaves and its own fur—Oranguru skillfully gives instructions to other Pokémon.'),
    (765, 'ultra-moon', 'Oranguru don''t get along with each other, so they''re always engaging in battles of wits to decide which one is superior.'),
    (765, 'ultra-sun', 'It normally spends its time meditating in the treetops. It throws [[Poké Ball]]s and gives other Pokémon orders as it pleases.'),
    (765, 'violet', 'This Pokémon lives quietly in the depths of the forest. The purple, cape-like fur gets longer and longer as Oranguru ages.'),
    (766, 'moon', 'They battle with hard berries for weapons. Their techniques are passed from the boss to the group, generation upon generation.'),
    (766, 'scarlet', 'This Pokémon battles by throwing hard berries. It won’t obey a Trainer who throws Poké Balls without skill.'),
    (766, 'shield', 'Passimian live in groups of about 20, with each member performing an assigned role. Through cooperation, the group survives.'),
    (766, 'sun', 'They form groups of roughly 20 individuals. Their mutual bond is remarkable—they will never let down a comrade.'),
    (766, 'sword', 'Displaying amazing teamwork, they follow the orders of their boss as they all help out in the search for their favorite berries.'),
    (766, 'ultra-moon', 'Berries are its weapons as well as the staple of its diet. The one that can throw a berry the farthest is the boss of the troop.'),
    (766, 'ultra-sun', 'They use their saliva to stick leaves to their shoulders. You can tell what troop they belong to from the position of the leaves.'),
    (766, 'violet', 'The boss chooses 10 members of the group to go out hunting. The hunting party will evenly split the food they find with the rest of the group.'),
    (767, 'legends-za', 'Its habitat includes everything from beaches to seabeds. It is happy to eat up even rotten scraps, providing a sort of natural cleaning service.'),
    (767, 'moon', 'Its habitat varies from beaches to seabeds. A natural scavenger, it will gleefully chow down on anything edible, no matter how rotten.'),
    (767, 'shield', 'Wimpod gather in swarms, constantly on the lookout for danger. They scatter the moment they detect an enemy''s presence.'),
    (767, 'sun', 'This Pokémon is a coward. As it desperately dashes off, the flailing of its many legs leaves a sparkling clean path in its wake.'),
    (767, 'sword', 'It''s nature''s cleaner—it eats anything and everything, including garbage and rotten things. The ground near its nest is always clean.'),
    (767, 'ultra-moon', 'An astonishingly cowardly Pokémon, Wimpod will whir its legs at high speeds to run away if anything comes near it.'),
    (767, 'ultra-sun', 'It will pick up anything it finds on the ground. Sometimes it finds coins, so Murkrow and Meowth will go after it.'),
    (768, 'legends-za', 'It has the skill to cleave even air or seawater in two with a flash of its giant, sharp claws.'),
    (768, 'moon', 'It battles skillfully with its six arms, but spends most of its time peacefully meditating in caves deep beneath the sea.'),
    (768, 'shield', 'They live in sunken ships or in holes in the seabed. When Golisopod and {{P|Grapploct}} battle, the loser becomes the winner''s meal.'),
    (768, 'sun', 'With a flashing slash of its giant sharp claws, it cleaves seawater—or even air—right in two.'),
    (768, 'sword', 'It will do anything to win, taking advantage of every opening and finishing opponents off with the small claws on its front legs.'),
    (768, 'ultra-moon', 'Its claws, which it can extend and retract at will, are its greatest weapons. Golisopod is sometimes accompanied by Wimpod.'),
    (768, 'ultra-sun', 'The shell covering its body is as hard as diamond. This Pokémon will do anything it takes to win.'),
    (769, 'legends-za', 'Grudges of the dead have possessed a mound of sand and become a Pokémon. Sandygast is fond of the shovel on its head.'),
    (769, 'moon', 'It takes control of anyone who puts a hand in its mouth. And so it adds to the accumulation of its sand-mound body.'),
    (769, 'scarlet', 'If it loses its shovel, it will stick something else— like a branch—in its head to make do until it finds another shovel.'),
    (769, 'shield', 'Sandygast mainly inhabits beaches. It takes control of anyone who puts their hand into its mouth, forcing them to make its body bigger.'),
    (769, 'sun', 'Born from a sand mound playfully built by a child, this Pokémon embodies the grudges of the departed.'),
    (769, 'sword', 'Grudges of the dead have possessed a mound of sand and become a Pokémon. Sandygast is fond of the shovel on its head.'),
    (769, 'ultra-moon', 'If you build sand mounds when you''re playing, destroy them before you go home, or they may get possessed and become Sandygast.'),
    (769, 'ultra-sun', 'It likes the shovel on its head, so Sandygast will get serious and fight any children who come to take it back.'),
    (769, 'violet', 'It flings sand into the eyes of its prey and tries to close in on them while they''re blinded, but since Sandygast is so slow, the prey tends to escape.'),
    (770, 'legends-za', 'Heaps of bones lie buried beneath its castle. They came from those whom Palossand drained of vitality and left all dried up.'),
    (770, 'moon', 'Buried beneath the castle are masses of dried-up bones from those whose vitality it has drained.'),
    (770, 'scarlet', 'The terrifying Palossand drags smaller Pokémon into its sandy body. Once its victims are trapped, it drains them of their vitality whenever it pleases.'),
    (770, 'shield', 'This Pokémon lives on beaches, but it hates water. Palossand can''t maintain its castle-like shape if it gets drenched by a heavy rain.'),
    (770, 'sun', 'Possessed people controlled by this Pokémon transformed its sand mound into a castle. As it evolved, its power to curse grew ever stronger.'),
    (770, 'sword', 'Palossand is known as the Beach Nightmare. It pulls its prey down into the sand by controlling the sand itself, and then it sucks out their souls.'),
    (770, 'ultra-moon', 'Once it has whipped up a sandstorm to halt its opponents in their tracks, this terrifying Pokémon snatches away their vitality.'),
    (770, 'ultra-sun', 'Each of its grains of sand has its own will. Palossand eats small Pokémon and siphons away their vital essence while they''re still alive.'),
    (770, 'violet', 'From the hollows in its arms, it fires the bones of its victims, which are all dried up after being drained of their vitality.'),
    (771, 'moon', 'These Pokémon line the beaches. The sticky mucous that covers their bodies can be used to soothe sunburned skin. How convenient!'),
    (771, 'shield', 'It''s covered in a slime that keeps its skin moist, allowing it to stay on land for days without drying up.'),
    (771, 'sun', 'It lives in shallow seas, such as areas near a beach. It can eject its internal organs, which it uses to engulf its prey or battle enemies.'),
    (771, 'sword', 'It lives in warm, shallow waters. If it encounters a foe, it will spit out its internal organs as a means to punch them.'),
    (771, 'ultra-moon', 'Its entire body is covered in its own slime. If you accidentally step on one, you''ll slip, and it will get mad and smack you!'),
    (771, 'ultra-sun', 'The tradition known as Pyukumuku chucking started from the custom of throwing Pyukumuku back into the sea after they wash onshore.'),
    (772, 'moon', 'Due to the danger that this synthetic Pokémon may go on a rampage, it wears a control mask to restrain its power.'),
    (772, 'shield', 'It was modeled after Arceus. The mask placed upon it limits its power in order to keep it under control.'),
    (772, 'sun', 'The heavy control mask it wears suppresses its intrinsic capabilities. This Pokémon has some hidden special power.'),
    (772, 'sword', 'Rumor has it that the theft of top-secret research notes led to a new instance of this Pokémon being created in the Galar region.'),
    (772, 'ultra-moon', 'There''s danger of its going on a rampage, so its true power is sealed away beneath its control mask.'),
    (772, 'ultra-sun', 'A Pokémon weapon developed for a specific mission, it went berserk during an experiment, so it was cryogenically frozen.'),
    (773, 'moon', 'Although its name was Type: Null at first, the [[Gladion|boy]] who [[Evolution|evolved]] it into this form gave it the name by which it is now known.'),
    (773, 'moon', 'Upon awakening, its {{a|RKS System}} is activated. By employing specific [[Memory|memories]], this Pokémon can adapt its type to confound its enemies.'),
    (773, 'shield', 'The final factor needed to release this Pokémon''s true power was a strong bond with a Trainer it trusts.'),
    (773, 'shield', 'It has the ability to change its type based on the memory it''s holding. This is its <Type>-type form.'),
    (773, 'sun', 'Its trust in its partner is what awakens it. This {{OBP|Pokémon|species}} is capable of changing its [[type]], a flexibility that is well displayed in battle.'),
    (773, 'sun', 'It destroyed its own control mask. It has become capable of changing its type by equipping special memories.'),
    (773, 'sword', 'Thanks to its awakened powers, it can change to the <Type> type to match the memory it has equipped.'),
    (773, 'sword', 'A solid bond of trust between this Pokémon and its Trainer awakened the strength hidden within Silvally. It can change its type at will.'),
    (773, 'ultra-moon', 'Through the bond it formed with its [[Pokémon Trainer|Trainer]], its will was strengthened, and it was able to destroy its control mask.'),
    (773, 'ultra-moon', 'Its capacity to change types unleashed, it shines silver due to the energy springing forth from within.'),
    (773, 'ultra-sun', 'This is its form once it has awakened and evolved. Freed from its heavy mask, its speed is greatly increased.'),
    (773, 'ultra-sun', 'Having been awakened successfully, it can change its type and battle—just like Arceus.'),
    (774, 'moon', 'Strong impacts can knock it out of its shell. This Pokémon was born from mutated nanoparticles.'),
    (774, 'scarlet', 'This Pokémon is born in the ozone layer. It falls to the ground once the outer shell enclosing its core grows heavy.'),
    (774, 'sun', 'Originally making its home in the ozone layer, it hurtles to the ground when the shell enclosing its body grows too heavy.'),
    (774, 'ultra-moon', 'Although its outer shell is uncommonly durable, the shock of falling to the ground smashes the shell to smithereens.'),
    (774, 'ultra-sun', 'It lives in the ozone layer, where it becomes food for stronger Pokémon. When it tries to run away, it falls to the ground.'),
    (774, 'violet', 'It will react when touched or called to, but it’s unknown whether such responses indicate consciousness.'),
    (775, 'moon', 'The log it holds was given to it by its parents at birth. It has also been known to cling to the arm of a friendly Trainer.'),
    (775, 'scarlet', 'Komala spends its entire life sleeping. It feeds on leaves that contain a potent poison only Komala can break down.'),
    (775, 'sun', 'It is born asleep, and it dies asleep. All its movements are apparently no more than the results of it tossing and turning in its dreams.'),
    (775, 'ultra-moon', 'It remains asleep from birth to death as a result of the sedative properties of the leaves that form its diet.'),
    (775, 'ultra-sun', 'It stays asleep from the moment it''s born. When it falls into a deep sleep, it stops moving altogether.'),
    (775, 'violet', 'A potent anesthetic can be made by diluting Komala''s drool. This anesthetic was used for surgeries in the past.'),
    (776, 'moon', 'It gushes fire and poisonous gases from its nostrils. Its dung is an explosive substance and can be put to various uses.'),
    (776, 'shield', 'Eating sulfur in its volcanic habitat is what causes explosive compounds to develop in its shell. Its droppings are also dangerously explosive.'),
    (776, 'sun', 'The shell on its back is chemically unstable and Shell Trap. The hole in its stomach is its weak point.'),
    (776, 'sword', 'Explosive substances coat the shell on its back. Enemies that dare attack it will be blown away by an immense detonation.'),
    (776, 'ultra-moon', 'Its exploding shell poses a real danger but is sensitive to moisture. On rainy days, Turtonator takes silent refuge in caves.'),
    (776, 'ultra-sun', 'It lives in volcanoes and eats sulfur and other minerals. Materials from the food it eats form the basis of its explosive shell.'),
    (777, 'moon', 'The long hairs on its back act as lightning rods. The bolts of lightning it attracts are stored as energy in its electric sac.'),
    (777, 'shield', 'When it''s in trouble, it curls up into a ball, makes its fur spikes stand on end, and then discharges electricity indiscriminately.'),
    (777, 'sun', 'The spiny fur on its back is normally at rest. When this Pokémon becomes agitated, its fur stands on end and stabs into its attackers.'),
    (777, 'sword', 'With the long hairs on its back, this Pokémon takes in electricity from other electric Pokémon. It stores what it absorbs in an electric sac.'),
    (777, 'ultra-moon', 'Its capacity to produce electricity is somewhat limited, so it gets charged up by letting lightning strike it!'),
    (777, 'ultra-sun', 'When it''s surprised or agitated, the 14 fur spikes on its back will stand up involuntarily.'),
    (778, 'legends-za', 'Mimikyu is sad that it may be exposed for what it really is. It will take revenge on whoever broke the neck of its disguise-no forgiveness.'),
    (778, 'legends-za', 'A lonely Pokémon, it conceals its terrifying appearance beneath an old rag so it can get closer to people and other Pokémon.'),
    (778, 'moon', 'A lonely Pokémon, it conceals its terrifying appearance beneath an old rag so it can get closer to people and other Pokémon.'),
    (778, 'moon', 'If its neck is broken or its rag torn during an attack, it works through the night to patch it.'),
    (778, 'scarlet', 'This Pokémon lives in dark places untouched by sunlight. When it appears before humans, it hides itself under a cloth that resembles a {{P|Pikachu}}.'),
    (778, 'scarlet', 'Even as it struggles beneath the cloth to repair the broken neck of its disguise, Mimikyu keeps up its impersonation of {{P|Pikachu}}.'),
    (778, 'shield', 'There was a scientist who peeked under Mimikyu''s old rag in the name of research. The scientist died of a mysterious disease.'),
    (778, 'shield', 'Its disguise made from an old rag allowed it to avoid an attack, but the impact broke the neck of the disguise. Now everyone knows it''s a Mimikyu.'),
    (778, 'sun', 'Its actual appearance is unknown. A scholar who saw what was under its rag was overwhelmed by terror and died from the shock.'),
    (778, 'sun', 'After going to all the effort of disguising itself, its neck was broken. Whatever is inside is probably unharmed, but it''s still feeling sad.'),
    (778, 'sword', 'It wears a rag fashioned into a {{P|Pikachu}} costume in an effort to look less scary. Unfortunately, the costume only makes it creepier.'),
    (778, 'sword', 'There will be no forgiveness for any who reveal that it was pretending to be {{P|Pikachu}}. It will bring the culprit down, even at the cost of its own life.'),
    (778, 'ultra-moon', 'Sad that its true identity may be exposed, Mimikyu will mercilessly seek revenge on any opponent that breaks its neck.'),
    (778, 'ultra-moon', 'A gust of wind revealed what hides under this Pokémon''s rag to a passing Trainer, who went home and died painfully that very night.'),
    (778, 'ultra-sun', 'Although it''s a quiet, lonely Pokémon, if you try to look at what''s under its rag, it will become agitated and resist violently.'),
    (778, 'ultra-sun', 'It stands in front of a mirror, trying to fix its broken neck as if its life depended on it. It has a hard time getting it right, so it''s crying inside.'),
    (778, 'violet', 'It has taken damage and can no longer hold the head of its cloth disguise upright. For as long as it lives, Mimikyu will never forget its attacker.'),
    (778, 'violet', 'Mimikyu was only recently identified as a Pokémon. Previously, people thought it was just a ghost wearing a cloth.'),
    (779, 'moon', 'It stuns its prey with psychokinesis and then grinds them to mush with its strong teeth. Even {{P|Shellder}}''s shell is no match for it.'),
    (779, 'scarlet', 'It grinds its teeth with great force to stimulate its brain. It fires the psychic energy created by this process from the protuberance on its head.'),
    (779, 'sun', 'When it unleashes its psychic power from the protuberance on its head, the grating sound of grinding teeth echoes through the area.'),
    (779, 'ultra-moon', 'Its skin is thick enough to fend off {{P|Mareanie}}''s spikes. With its robust teeth, Bruxish crunches up the spikes and eats them.'),
    (779, 'ultra-sun', 'It burrows beneath the sand, radiating psychic power from the protuberance on its head. It waits for prey as it surveys the area.'),
    (779, 'violet', 'When sunlight reflects on the ripples created by a Bruxish grinding its teeth, the water all around sparkles brilliantly.'),
    (780, 'legends-za', 'It has a compassionate personality, but if it is angered, it completely destroys its surroundings with its intense breath.'),
    (780, 'moon', 'This Pokémon is friendly to people and loves children most of all. It comes from deep in the mountains to play with children it likes in town.'),
    (780, 'shield', 'Drampa is a kind and friendly Pokémon—up until it''s angered. When that happens, it stirs up a gale and flattens everything around.'),
    (780, 'sun', 'It has a compassionate personality, but if it is angered, it completely destroys its surroundings with its intense breath.'),
    (780, 'sword', 'The mountains it calls home are nearly two miles in height. On rare occasions, it descends to play with the children living in the towns below.'),
    (780, 'ultra-moon', 'It appears in towns and plays with the children. Drampa will protect kids when they''re in danger, so their moms don''t have to worry.'),
    (780, 'ultra-sun', 'If a child it has made friends with is bullied, Drampa will find the bully''s house and burn it to the ground.'),
    (781, 'moon', 'The soul of seaweed adrift in the waves became reborn as this Pokémon. It maintains itself with new infusions of seabed detritus and seaweed.'),
    (781, 'shield', 'After lowering its anchor, it waits for its prey. It catches large Wailord and drains their life-force.'),
    (781, 'sun', 'Swinging its massive anchor, it can KO Wailord in a single blow. What appears to be green seaweed is actually its body.'),
    (781, 'sword', 'After a piece of seaweed merged with debris from a sunken ship, it was reborn as this {{t|ghost}} Pokémon.'),
    (781, 'ultra-moon', 'Its chain-like green seaweed can stretch outward for hundreds of yards. For some reason, it gets along well with Skrelp.'),
    (781, 'ultra-sun', 'It wraps its prey in green seaweed and sucks away their vitality. It only likes to go after big prey like Wailord.'),
    (782, 'moon', 'They live in mountains where no trace of humans can be detected. Jangmo-o grow little by little as they battle one another.'),
    (782, 'scarlet', 'The scale atop its head is useful for both offense and defense. It bravely stands and faces its foes rather than turning tail, even if its foes are strong.'),
    (782, 'shield', 'Jangmo-o strikes its scales to communicate with others of its kind. Its scales are actually fur that''s become as hard as metal.'),
    (782, 'sun', 'It expresses its feelings by smacking its scales. Metallic sounds echo through the tall mountains where Jangmo-o lives.'),
    (782, 'sword', 'They learn to fight by smashing their head scales together. The dueling strengthens both their skills and their spirits.'),
    (782, 'ultra-moon', 'It will never show an enemy its back in battle. Ancient warriors liked Jangmo-o for its valiant disposition and made it one of their own.'),
    (782, 'ultra-sun', 'It smacks the scales on its head against rocks or against the ground to frighten its opponents. It can also contact its friends with these noises.'),
    (782, 'violet', 'They communicate with their allies using the sounds their scales make when struck. A group of these Pokémon causes quite a racket.'),
    (783, 'moon', 'It sheds and regrows its scales on a continuous basis. The scales become harder and sharper each time they''re regrown.'),
    (783, 'scarlet', 'It gets into fistfights so intense that the scales on its arms peel off. Bare arms are a sign of valiance.'),
    (783, 'shield', 'Before attacking its enemies, it clashes its scales together and roars. Its sharp claws shred the opposition.'),
    (783, 'sun', 'It leaps at its prey with a courageous shout. Its scaly punches tear its opponents to shreds.'),
    (783, 'sword', 'The scaleless, scarred parts of its body are signs of its strength. It shows them off to defeated opponents.'),
    (783, 'ultra-moon', 'The scales it sheds can be molded and processed to make pots and pans. They conduct heat well, so they''re a popular item.'),
    (783, 'ultra-sun', 'It makes noise by clanging its scales together. When the rhythm has reached its peak, Hakamo-o attacks.'),
    (783, 'violet', 'It fires itself up by striking its scales with force as it dances. Its roar is a battle cry.'),
    (784, 'moon', 'Its rigid scales function as offense and defense. In the past, its scales were processed and used to make weapons and other commodities.'),
    (784, 'scarlet', 'It lets its arm hang, and then "quick as a flash" swings upward to land its specialty punch and send the opponent flying high into the sky.'),
    (784, 'shield', 'Certain ruins have paintings of ancient warriors wearing armor made of Kommo-o scales.'),
    (784, 'sun', 'When it spots enemies, it threatens them by jingling the scales on its tail. Weak opponents will crack and flee in panic.'),
    (784, 'sword', 'It clatters its tail scales to unnerve opponents. This Pokémon will battle only those who stand steadfast in the face of this display.'),
    (784, 'ultra-moon', 'It battles valiantly with its fists, which are armored in steel scales. Kommo-o specializes in uppercuts.'),
    (784, 'ultra-sun', 'When it howls after finishing off its prey, the metallic sounds of its celebrating comrades can be heard from all around.'),
    (784, 'violet', 'It bashes its scales to test its opponents'' mettle. The sound of struck Kommo-o scales frightens weaker foes and sends them running.'),
    (785, 'moon', 'It confuses its enemies by flying too quickly for the eye to follow. It has a hair-trigger temper but forgets what made it angry an instant later.'),
    (785, 'sun', 'This guardian deity of Melemele is brimming with curiosity. It summons thunderclouds and stores their lightning inside its body.'),
    (785, 'ultra-moon', 'The lightning-wielding guardian deity of Melemele, Tapu Koko is brimming with curiosity and appears before people from time to time.'),
    (785, 'ultra-sun', 'Although it''s called a guardian deity, if a person or Pokémon puts it in a bad mood, it will become a malevolent deity and attack.'),
    (786, 'moon', 'As it flutters about, it scatters its strangely glowing scales. Touching them is said to restore good health on the spot.'),
    (786, 'sun', 'This guardian deity of Akala is guilelessly cruel. The fragrant aroma of flowers is the source of its energy.'),
    (786, 'ultra-moon', 'Although called a guardian deity, Tapu Lele is devoid of guilt about its cruel disposition and can be described as nature incarnate.'),
    (786, 'ultra-sun', 'It heals the wounds of people and Pokémon by sprinkling them with its sparkling scales. This guardian deity is worshiped on Akala.'),
    (787, 'moon', 'The guardian deity of Ula''ula is a lazy Pokémon. It commands plants to immobilize its foes and then deals them a savage blow with its horns.'),
    (787, 'sun', 'It pulls large trees up by the roots and swings them around. It causes vegetation to grow, and then it absorbs energy from the growth.'),
    (787, 'ultra-moon', 'It makes ringing sounds with its tail to let others know where it is, avoiding unneeded conflicts. This guardian deity of Ula''ula controls plants.'),
    (787, 'ultra-sun', 'Although it''s called a guardian deity, it''s violent enough to crush anyone it sees as an enemy.'),
    (788, 'moon', 'The guardian deity of Poni, it can control water. People say it can create pure water that will wash away any uncleanness.'),
    (788, 'sun', 'The dense fog it creates brings the downfall and destruction of its confused enemies. Ocean currents are the source of its energy.'),
    (788, 'ultra-moon', 'Although it''s called a guardian deity, terrible calamities sometimes befall those who recklessly approach Tapu Fini.'),
    (788, 'ultra-sun', 'This guardian deity of Poni Island manipulates water. Because it lives deep within a thick fog, it came to be both feared and revered.'),
    (789, 'moon', 'In ages past, it was called the child of the stars. It''s said to be a Pokémon from another world, but no specific details are known.'),
    (789, 'shield', 'Cosmog is very curious but not very cautious, often placing itself in danger. If things start to look dicey, it teleports away.*'),
    (789, 'sun', 'Its body is gaseous and frail. It slowly grows as it collects dust from the atmosphere.'),
    (789, 'sword', 'This Pokémon came from another universe. Its gaseous body is so light that even a gentle breeze can blow it away.*'),
    (789, 'ultra-moon', 'Whether or not it''s a Pokémon from this world is a mystery. When it''s in a jam, it warps away to a safe place to hide.'),
    (789, 'ultra-sun', 'Even though its helpless, gaseous body can be blown away by the slightest breeze, it doesn''t seem to care.'),
    (790, 'moon', 'There''s something accumulating around the black core within its hard shell. People think this Pokémon may come from another world.'),
    (790, 'shield', 'It sucks in dust from the air at an astounding rate, frantically building up energy within its core as preparation for evolution.*'),
    (790, 'sun', 'Motionless as if dead, its body is faintly warm to the touch. In the distant past, it was called the cocoon of the stars.'),
    (790, 'sword', 'The absorption of starlight fuels this Pokémon''s growth. The shell that encases it is harder than any known material.*'),
    (790, 'ultra-moon', 'As it absorbs light, Cosmoem continues to grow. Its golden shell is surprisingly solid.'),
    (790, 'ultra-sun', 'The king who ruled Alola in times of antiquity called it the “cocoon of the stars” and built an altar to worship it.'),
    (791, 'moon', 'This {{OBP|Pokémon|species}} is said to be a male [[evolution]] of Cosmog. At the activation of its third eye, it departs for another world.'),
    (791, 'shield', 'Solgaleo was once known as the Beast That Devours the Sun. Energy in the form of light radiates boundlessly from it.*'),
    (791, 'sun', 'It is said to live in [[Ultra Space|another world]]. The intense light it radiates from the surface of its body can make the darkest of nights light up like midday.'),
    (791, 'sword', 'When light radiates from its body, this Pokémon could almost appear to be the sun. It will dispel any darkness and light up the world.*'),
    (791, 'ultra-moon', 'In writings from the distant past, it''s called by the name “the beast that devours the sun.”'),
    (791, 'ultra-sun', 'Sometimes the result of its opening an [[Ultra Wormhole]] is that energy and life-forms from other worlds are called here to this world.'),
    (792, 'moon', 'Said to live in another world, this {{OBP|Pokémon|species}} devours light, drawing the moonless dark veil of night over the brightness of day.'),
    (792, 'shield', 'It steals the light from its surroundings and then becomes the full moon, showering its own light across the night sky.*'),
    (792, 'sun', 'It is said to be a female [[evolution]] of Cosmog. When its third eye activates, away it flies to [[Ultra Space|another world]].'),
    (792, 'sword', 'Known as the Beast That Calls the Moon, this Pokémon lives by taking in any and all light and converting it into its own energy.*'),
    (792, 'ultra-moon', 'It sometimes summons unknown powers and [[Ultra Beasts|life-forms]] here to this world from [[Ultra Wormhole|holes]] that lead to other worlds.'),
    (792, 'ultra-sun', 'Records of it exist in writings from long, long ago, where it was known by the name “the beast that calls the moon.”'),
    (793, 'moon', 'One of the Ultra Beasts. It''s unclear whether or not this Pokémon is sentient, but sometimes it can be observed behaving like a young girl.'),
    (793, 'sun', 'One of several mysterious Ultra Beasts. People on the street report observing those infested by it suddenly becoming violent.'),
    (793, 'ultra-moon', 'It appeared in this world from an Ultra Wormhole. Nihilego appears to be a parasite that lives by feeding on people and Pokémon.'),
    (793, 'ultra-sun', 'A life-form from another world, it was dubbed a UB and is thought to produce a strong neurotoxin.'),
    (794, 'moon', 'A mysterious life-form called an Ultra Beast. Witnesses saw it pulverize a dump truck with a single punch.'),
    (794, 'sun', 'This Ultra Beast appeared from another world. It shows off its body, but whether that display is a boast or a threat remains unclear.'),
    (794, 'ultra-moon', 'Buzzwole goes around showing off its abnormally swollen muscles. It is one kind of Ultra Beast.'),
    (794, 'ultra-sun', 'Although it''s alien to this world and a danger here, it''s apparently a common organism in the world where it normally lives.'),
    (795, 'moon', 'One of the Ultra Beasts. It refuses to touch anything, perhaps because it senses some uncleanness in this world.'),
    (795, 'sun', 'One of the dangerous Ultra Beasts, it has been spotted running across the land at terrific speeds.'),
    (795, 'ultra-moon', 'Although it''s alien to this world and a danger here, it''s apparently a common organism in the world where it normally lives.'),
    (795, 'ultra-sun', 'A life-form that lives in another world, its body is thin and supple, but it also possesses great power.'),
    (796, 'moon', 'It appeared from the Ultra Wormhole. It raided a power plant, so people think it energizes itself with electricity.'),
    (796, 'sun', 'One of the mysterious life-forms known as Ultra Beasts. Astonishing electric shocks emanate from its entire body, according to witnesses.'),
    (796, 'ultra-moon', 'They''ve been dubbed Ultra Beasts. Some of them stand unmoving, like trees, with their arms and legs stuck into the ground.'),
    (796, 'ultra-sun', 'Although it''s alien to this world and a danger here, it''s apparently a common organism in the world where it normally lives.'),
    (797, 'moon', 'One kind of Ultra Beast. Witnesses have seen it burn down a forest by expelling gas from its two arms.'),
    (797, 'sun', 'It appeared from the Ultra Wormhole. Witnesses observed it flying across the sky at high speed.'),
    (797, 'ultra-moon', 'Although it''s alien to this world and a danger here, it''s apparently a common organism in the world where it normally lives.'),
    (797, 'ultra-sun', 'One of the dangerous UBs, high energy readings can be detected coming from both of its huge arms.'),
    (798, 'moon', 'One of the Ultra Beast life-forms, it was observed cutting down a gigantic steel tower with one stroke of its blade.'),
    (798, 'sun', 'This Ultra Beast came from the Ultra Wormhole. It seems not to attack enemies on its own, but its sharp body is a dangerous weapon in itself.'),
    (798, 'ultra-moon', 'Although it''s alien to this world and a danger here, it''s apparently a common organism in the world where it normally lives.'),
    (798, 'ultra-sun', 'This Ultra Beast''s body, which is as thin as paper, is like a sharpened sword.'),
    (799, 'moon', 'A dangerous Ultra Beast, it appears to be eating constantly, but for some reason its droppings have never been found.'),
    (799, 'sun', 'It has gobbled mountains and swallowed whole buildings, according to reports. It''s one of the Ultra Beasts.'),
    (799, 'ultra-moon', 'An unknown life-form called a UB. It may be constantly hungry—it is certainly always devouring something.'),
    (799, 'ultra-sun', 'Although it''s alien to this world and a danger here, it''s apparently a common organism in the world where it normally lives.'),
    (800, 'moon', 'Light is apparently the source of its energy. It has an extraordinarily vicious disposition and is constantly firing off Prismatic Laser.'),
    (800, 'sun', 'Reminiscent of the [[Ultra Beast]]s, this life-form, apparently asleep underground, is thought to have come from [[Ultra Space|another world]] in ancient times.'),
    (800, 'ultra-moon', 'Light is the source of its energy. If it isn''t devouring light, impurities build up in it and on it, and Necrozma darkens and stops moving.'),
    (800, 'ultra-sun', 'It looks somehow pained as it rages around in search of light, which serves as its energy. It''s apparently from another world.'),
    (801, 'moon', 'Its mechanized body is merely a vessel. Its true self is its Soul-Heart, an artificial soul.'),
    (801, 'sun', 'This artificial Pokémon, constructed more than 500 years ago, can understand human speech but cannot itself speak.'),
    (801, 'ultra-moon', 'Built roughly 500 years ago by a scientist, the part called the Soul-Heart is the actual life-form.'),
    (801, 'ultra-sun', 'It synchronizes its consciousness with others to understand their feelings. This faculty makes it useful for taking care of people.'),
    (802, 'legends-za', 'It slips into others'' shadows and mimics their movements and powers. With time, its prowess will surpass that of those it originally imitated.'),
    (802, 'moon', 'It lurks in the shadows of others, copying their movements and powers. This Pokémon is craven and cowering.'),
    (802, 'shield', 'This Pokémon can conceal itself in any shadow, so it went undiscovered for a long time.*'),
    (802, 'sun', 'Able to conceal itself in shadows, it never appears before humans, so its very existence was the stuff of myth.'),
    (802, 'sword', 'By slipping into the shadow of a martial arts master and copying their movements, this Pokémon learned the ultimate techniques.*'),
    (802, 'ultra-moon', 'It sinks into the shadows of people and Pokémon, where it can understand their feelings and copy their capabilities.'),
    (802, 'ultra-sun', 'It slips into the shadows of others and mimics their powers and movements. As it improves, it becomes stronger than those it''s imitating.'),
    (803, 'ultra-moon', 'An Ultra Beast that lives in a different world, it cackles wildly as it sprays its opponents with poison from the needles on its head.'),
    (803, 'ultra-sun', 'This Ultra Beast is well enough liked to be chosen as a first partner in its own world.'),
    (804, 'ultra-moon', 'One kind of Ultra Beast, it fires a glowing, venomous liquid from its needles. This liquid is also immensely adhesive.'),
    (804, 'ultra-sun', 'It stores hundreds of liters of poisonous liquid inside its body. It is one of the organisms known as UBs.'),
    (805, 'ultra-moon', 'When stone walls started moving and attacking, the brute''s true identity was this mysterious life-form, which brings to mind an Ultra Beast.'),
    (805, 'ultra-sun', 'It appeared from an Ultra Wormhole. Each one appears to be made up of many life-forms stacked one on top of each other.'),
    (806, 'ultra-moon', 'A UB that appeared from an Ultra Wormhole, it causes explosions, then takes advantage of opponents'' surprise to rob them of their vitality.'),
    (806, 'ultra-sun', 'It slithers toward people. Then, without warning, it triggers the Mind Blown. It''s apparently one kind of Ultra Beast.'),
    (807, 'legends-za', 'Electricity sparks from the pads on its limbs. Wherever Zeraora runs, lightning flashes and thunder echoes.'),
    (807, 'shield', 'Electricity sparks from the pads on its limbs. Wherever Zeraora runs, lightning flashes and thunder echoes.*'),
    (807, 'sword', 'It runs as fast as lightning strikes, shredding its opponents with its high-voltage claws.*'),
    (807, 'ultra-moon', 'It approaches its enemies at the speed of lightning, then tears them limb from limb with its sharp claws.'),
    (807, 'ultra-sun', 'It electrifies its claws and tears its opponents apart with them. Even if they dodge its attack, they''ll be electrocuted by the flying sparks.'),
    (808, 'legends-za', 'Its body is made up of molten steel. It melts particles of iron and other metals it finds in the ground and absorbs them into itself.'),
    (808, 'shield', 'They live as a group, but when the time comes, one strong Meltan will absorb all the others and evolve.*'),
    (808, 'sword', 'It dissolves and eats metal. Circulating liquid metal within its body is how it generates energy.*'),
    (809, 'shield', 'Centrifugal force is behind the punches of Melmetal''s heavy hex-nut arms. Melmetal is said to deliver the strongest punches of all Pokémon.*'),
    (809, 'sword', 'At the end of its life-span, Melmetal will rust and fall apart. The small shards left behind will eventually be reborn as Meltan.*'),
    (810, 'scarlet', 'The stick Grookey holds has grown harder and more flexible after soaking in the energy that emanates from inside Grookey’s body.'),
    (810, 'shield', 'It attacks with rapid beats of its stick. As it strikes with amazing speed, it gets more and more pumped.'),
    (810, 'sword', 'When it uses its special stick to strike up a beat, the sound waves produced carry revitalizing energy to the plants and flowers in the area.'),
    (810, 'violet', 'As Grookey strikes everything in sight with its stick, it has more and more fun, and its rhythm becomes livelier.'),
    (811, 'scarlet', 'It skillfully uses its two sticks not only for drumming out rapid beats but also for pummeling opponents during battle.'),
    (811, 'shield', 'When it''s drumming out rapid beats in battle, it gets so caught up in the rhythm that it won''t even notice that it''s already knocked out its opponent.'),
    (811, 'sword', 'The faster a Thwackey can beat out a rhythm with its two sticks, the more respect it wins from its peers.'),
    (811, 'violet', 'It becomes intensely focused while it drums out vigorous beats—so much so that sometimes it won’t listen to its Trainer’s commands.'),
    (812, 'shield', 'The one with the best drumming techniques becomes the boss of the troop. It has a gentle disposition and values harmony among its group.'),
    (812, 'sword', 'By drumming, it taps into the power of its special tree stump. The roots of the stump follow its direction in battle.'),
    (813, 'scarlet', 'Once its body has heated up, Scorbunny can use the full extent of its power. That’s why it does warm-up exercises.'),
    (813, 'shield', 'It has special pads on the backs of its feet, and one on its nose. Once it''s raring to fight, these pads radiate tremendous heat.'),
    (813, 'sword', 'A warm-up of running around gets fire energy coursing through this Pokémon''s body. Once that happens, it''s ready to fight at full power.'),
    (813, 'violet', 'Fire energy gathers in the pads of its feet, raising their temperature. Once hot, Scorbunny’s footpads can deal heavy damage to opponents.'),
    (814, 'scarlet', 'Thanks to its soft and fluffy fur, Raboot can easily heat up its fire energy and produce flames with more power.'),
    (814, 'shield', 'It kicks berries right off the branches of trees and then juggles them with its feet, practicing its footwork.'),
    (814, 'sword', 'Its thick and fluffy fur protects it from the cold and enables it to use hotter fire moves.'),
    (814, 'violet', 'While it prides itself on its varied kicking moves, it can also deliver powerful headbutts once its flames have heated up its forehead.'),
    (815, 'shield', 'It''s skilled at both offense and defense, and it gets pumped up when cheered on. But if it starts showboating, it could put itself in a tough spot.'),
    (815, 'sword', 'It juggles a pebble with its feet, turning it into a Pyro Ball. Its shots strike opponents hard and leave them {{status|burn|scorched}}.'),
    (816, 'scarlet', 'It gets berries to eat by shooting them down with bullets of water it spurts from its mouth. Its aim is perfect.'),
    (816, 'shield', 'When it gets wet, its skin changes color, and this Pokémon becomes invisible as if it were camouflaged.'),
    (816, 'sword', 'When scared, this Pokémon cries. Its tears pack the chemical punch of 100 onions, and attackers won''t be able to resist weeping.'),
    (816, 'violet', 'It’s a very cautious Pokémon. When it has no choice but to battle, it hides itself before attacking.'),
    (817, 'scarlet', 'It extends its long, slimy tongue at blinding speeds and finishes off its prey with great skill.'),
    (817, 'shield', 'Highly intelligent but also very lazy, it keeps enemies out of its territory by laying traps everywhere.'),
    (817, 'sword', 'A clever combatant, this Pokémon battles using water balloons created with moisture secreted from its palms.'),
    (817, 'violet', 'Highly intelligent but also very lazy, it defends its home by laying traps.'),
    (818, 'shield', 'Its nictitating membranes let it pick out foes'' weak points so it can precisely blast them with water that shoots from its fingertips at Mach 3.'),
    (818, 'sword', 'It has many hidden capabilities, such as fingertips that can shoot water and a membrane on its back that it can use to glide through the air.'),
    (819, 'scarlet', 'It stores berries in its cheeks. When there are no berries to be found, Skwovet will stuff pebbles into its cheeks to stave off its cravings.'),
    (819, 'shield', 'It eats berries nonstop—a habit that has made it more resilient than it looks. It''ll show up on farms, searching for yet more berries.'),
    (819, 'sword', 'Found throughout the Galar region, this Pokémon becomes uneasy if its cheeks are ever completely empty of berries.'),
    (819, 'violet', 'No matter how much it stuffs its belly with food, it is always anxious about getting hungry again. So, it stashes berries in its cheeks and tail.'),
    (820, 'scarlet', 'If it spots a berry tree, it will immediately go to gather berries without a sideways glance—even if it’s in the middle of a battle.'),
    (820, 'shield', 'Common throughout the Galar region, this Pokémon has strong teeth and can chew through the toughest of berry shells.'),
    (820, 'sword', 'It stashes berries in its tail—so many berries that they fall out constantly. But this Pokémon is a bit slow-witted, so it doesn''t notice the loss.'),
    (820, 'violet', 'This Pokémon makes off with heaps of fallen berries by wrapping them in its tail, which is roughly twice the length of its body.'),
    (821, 'legends-za', 'This valiant Pokémon will challenge any foe, no matter how mighty. Even if that backfires and Rookidee loses, it grows from the experience.'),
    (821, 'scarlet', 'This Pokémon is brave and reckless. The white markings around a Rookidee''s eyes intimidate fainthearted Pokémon.'),
    (821, 'shield', 'Jumping nimbly about, this small-bodied Pokémon takes advantage of even the slightest opportunity to disorient larger opponents.'),
    (821, 'sword', 'It will bravely challenge any opponent, no matter how powerful. This Pokémon benefits from every battle—even a defeat increases its strength a bit.'),
    (821, 'violet', 'The females are fussier than the males. If another creature dirties a female Rookidee''s wings, it''ll peck the offender relentlessly in a burning rage.'),
    (822, 'legends-za', 'Corvisquire are intelligent enough to use tools. They''ll use their feet to pick up and fling pebbles or wrap their enemies in ropes.'),
    (822, 'scarlet', 'It’s said that the reason behind Corvisquire’s high level of intelligence is the large size of its brain relative to those of other bird Pokémon.'),
    (822, 'shield', 'The lessons of many harsh battles have taught it how to accurately judge an opponent''s strength.'),
    (822, 'sword', 'Smart enough to use tools in battle, these Pokémon have been seen picking up rocks and flinging them or using ropes to wrap up enemies.'),
    (822, 'violet', 'This intelligent Pokémon will quickly learn how to use any tool it can hold in its beak or its talons.'),
    (823, 'shield', 'With their great intellect and flying skills, these Pokémon very successfully act as the Galar region''s airborne taxi service.'),
    (823, 'sword', 'This Pokémon reigns supreme in the skies of the [[Galar]] region. The black luster of its steel body could drive terror into the heart of any foe.'),
    (824, 'shield', 'Often found in gardens, this Pokémon has hairs on its body that it uses to assess its surroundings.'),
    (824, 'sword', 'A constant collector of information, this Pokémon is very smart. Very strong is what it isn''t.'),
    (825, 'shield', 'As it grows inside its shell, it uses its psychic abilities to monitor the outside world and prepare for evolution.'),
    (825, 'sword', 'It barely moves, but it''s still alive. Hiding in its shell without food or water seems to have awakened its psychic powers.'),
    (826, 'shield', 'It emits psychic energy to observe and study what''s around it—and what''s around it can include things over six miles away.'),
    (826, 'sword', 'It''s famous for its high level of intelligence, and the large size of its brain is proof that it also possesses immense psychic power.'),
    (827, 'legends-za', 'It filches food from people and Pokémon alike. While fleeing the scene, it wipes its tracks away with its tail to throw off pursuers.'),
    (827, 'shield', 'Cunning and cautious, this Pokémon survives by stealing food from others. It erases its tracks with swipes of its tail as it makes off with its plunder.'),
    (827, 'sword', 'Aided by the soft pads on its feet, it silently raids the food stores of other Pokémon. It survives off its ill-gotten gains.'),
    (828, 'legends-za', 'This clever Pokémon marks potential targets with its scent, then follows its nose to locate their nests.'),
    (828, 'shield', 'With a lithe body and sharp claws, it goes around stealing food and eggs. {{P|Boltund}} is its natural enemy.'),
    (828, 'sword', 'It secretly marks potential targets with a scent. By following the scent, it stalks its targets and steals from them when they least expect it.'),
    (829, 'shield', 'It whirls around in the wind while singing a joyous song. This delightful display has charmed many into raising this Pokémon.'),
    (829, 'sword', 'It anchors itself in the ground with its single leg, then basks in the sun. After absorbing enough sunlight, its petals spread as it blooms brilliantly.'),
    (830, 'shield', 'The cotton on the head of this Pokémon can be spun into a glossy, gorgeous yarn—a Galar regional specialty.'),
    (830, 'sword', 'The seeds attached to its cotton fluff are full of nutrients. It spreads them on the wind so that plants and other Pokémon can benefit from them.'),
    (831, 'shield', 'If its fleece grows too long, Wooloo won''t be able to move. Cloth made with the wool of this Pokémon is surprisingly strong.'),
    (831, 'sword', 'Its curly fleece is such an effective cushion that this Pokémon could fall off a cliff and stand right back up at the bottom, unharmed.'),
    (832, 'shield', 'Its majestic horns are meant only to impress the opposite gender. They never see use in battle.'),
    (832, 'sword', 'Weave a carpet from its springy wool, and you end up with something closer to a trampoline. You''ll start to bounce the moment you set foot on it.'),
    (833, 'scarlet', 'Its large front tooth is still growing in. When the tooth itches, this Pokémon will bite another Chewtle’s horn, and the two Pokémon will tussle.'),
    (833, 'shield', 'It starts off battles by attacking with its rock-hard horn, but as soon as the opponent flinches, this Pokémon bites down and never lets go.'),
    (833, 'sword', 'Apparently the itch of its teething impels it to snap its jaws at anything in front of it.'),
    (833, 'violet', 'A popular game among children is to lift up sticks that Chewtle have bitten onto to see whose Chewtle can hang on the longest.'),
    (834, 'shield', 'This Pokémon rapidly extends its retractable neck to sink its sharp fangs into distant enemies and take them down.'),
    (834, 'sword', 'With jaws that can shear through steel rods, this highly aggressive Pokémon chomps down on its unfortunate prey.'),
    (835, 'shield', 'This gluttonous Pokémon only assists people with their work because it wants treats. As it runs, it crackles with electricity.'),
    (835, 'sword', 'This Pokémon is very popular as a herding dog in the Galar region. As it runs, it generates electricity from the base of its tail.'),
    (836, 'shield', 'It sends electricity through its legs to boost their strength. Running at top speed, it easily breaks 50 mph.'),
    (836, 'sword', 'This Pokémon generates electricity and channels it into its legs to keep them going strong. Boltund can run nonstop for three full days.'),
    (837, 'scarlet', 'On sunny days, Rolycoly will come out onto grassy plains and roll around. Then it will eat the grass that gets tangled in its wheel-like leg.'),
    (837, 'shield', 'It can race around like a unicycle, even on rough, rocky terrain. Burning coal sustains it.'),
    (837, 'sword', 'Most of its body has the same composition as coal. Fittingly, this Pokémon was first discovered in coal mines about 400 years ago.'),
    (837, 'violet', 'Chunks of the surface of this Pokémon''s body that have grown old and flaked off have long been used for fuel as an alternative to coal.'),
    (838, 'scarlet', 'The temperature inside its body increases when it experiences strong emotions. It rolls around frantically while spewing flames.'),
    (838, 'shield', 'By rapidly rolling its legs, it can travel at over 18 mph. The temperature of the flames it breathes exceeds 1,800 degrees Fahrenheit.'),
    (838, 'sword', 'It forms coal inside its body. Coal dropped by this Pokémon once helped fuel the lives of people in the Galar region.'),
    (838, 'violet', 'Due to the coal tar created inside it, the heap of coal on Carkol''s back never falls apart, even when the Pokémon rolls around at high speeds.'),
    (839, 'shield', 'While it''s engaged in battle, its mountain of coal will burn bright red, sending off sparks that scorch the surrounding area.'),
    (839, 'sword', 'It''s usually peaceful, but the vandalism of mines enrages it. Offenders will be incinerated with flames that reach 2,700 degrees Fahrenheit.'),
    (840, 'scarlet', 'It grows by eating the flesh of an apple. Applin uses its own body fluid to strengthen the apple’s skin and prevent it from rotting.'),
    (840, 'shield', 'As soon as it''s born, it burrows into an apple. Not only does the apple serve as its food source, but the flavor of the fruit determines its evolution.'),
    (840, 'sword', 'It spends its entire life inside an apple. It hides from its natural enemies, bird Pokémon, by pretending it''s just an apple and nothing more.'),
    (840, 'violet', 'Applin lives inside an apple. When an Applin is separated from its apple, its body loses moisture and the Pokémon grows weak.'),
    (841, 'shield', 'It flies on wings of apple skin and spits a powerful acid. It can also change its shape into that of an apple.'),
    (841, 'sword', 'It ate a sour apple, and that induced its evolution. In its cheeks, it stores an acid capable of causing chemical burns.'),
    (842, 'shield', 'Its body is covered in sweet nectar, and the skin on its back is especially yummy. Children used to have it as a snack.'),
    (842, 'sword', 'Eating a sweet apple caused its evolution. A nectarous scent wafts from its body, luring in the bug Pokémon it preys on.'),
    (843, 'scarlet', 'Silicobra’s neck pouch, which can inflate and deflate like a balloon, gets more elastic each time Silicobra sheds its skin.'),
    (843, 'shield', 'It spews sand from its nostrils. While the enemy is blinded, it burrows into the ground to hide.'),
    (843, 'sword', 'As it digs, it swallows sand and stores it in its neck pouch. The pouch can hold more than 17 pounds of sand.'),
    (843, 'violet', 'Silicobra''s large nostrils are specialized for spraying sand, so this Pokémon is not very good at telling apart different smells.'),
    (844, 'shield', 'Its unique style of coiling allows it to blast sand out of its sand sac more efficiently.'),
    (844, 'sword', 'When it contracts its body, over 220 pounds of sand sprays from its nose. If it ever runs out of sand, it becomes disheartened.'),
    (845, 'shield', 'This hungry Pokémon swallows Arrokuda whole. Occasionally, it makes a mistake and tries to swallow a Pokémon other than its preferred prey.'),
    (845, 'sword', 'It''s so strong that it can knock out some opponents in a single hit, but it also may forget what it''s battling midfight.'),
    (846, 'scarlet', 'Arrokuda can swim quickly only in a straight line. The ones that become sluggish from overeating are the first to be targeted by flocks of Wattrel.'),
    (846, 'shield', 'After it''s eaten its fill, its movements become extremely sluggish. That''s when Cramorant swallows it up.'),
    (846, 'sword', 'If it sees any movement around it, this Pokémon charges for it straightaway, leading with its sharply pointed jaw. It''s very proud of that jaw.'),
    (846, 'violet', 'It takes down prey by charging into them with its hard, pointed jaw. But Arrokuda''s eyesight is poor, so this tactic has a low success rate.'),
    (847, 'scarlet', 'It spins its tail fins to leap from the water, then viciously bites down on Wingull flying close to the water’s surface.'),
    (847, 'shield', 'It spins its tail fins to propel itself, surging forward at speeds of over 100 knots before ramming prey and spearing into them.'),
    (847, 'sword', 'This Pokémon has a jaw that''s as sharp as a spear and as strong as steel. Apparently Barraskewda''s flesh is surprisingly tasty, too.'),
    (847, 'violet', 'It swims at speeds of over 100 knots and battles fiercely with pods of Finizen over prey.'),
    (848, 'legends-za', 'It manipulates the chemical makeup of its poison to produce electricity. The wattage is weak, but it can cause a tingling numbness.'),
    (848, 'scarlet', 'It has no problem drinking dirty water. An organ inside Toxel''s body filters such water into a poisonous liquid that is harmless to Toxel.'),
    (848, 'shield', 'It manipulates the chemical makeup of its poison to produce electricity. The voltage is weak, but it can cause a tingling paralysis.'),
    (848, 'sword', 'It stores poison in an internal poison sac and secretes that poison through its skin. If you touch this Pokémon, a tingling sensation follows.'),
    (848, 'violet', 'This selfish, attention-seeking Pokémon stores poison and electricity in two different sacs inside its body.'),
    (849, 'legends-za', 'When Toxtricity claws at the protrusions on its chest to generate electricity, a sound like that of a guitar echoes through the air.'),
    (849, 'scarlet', 'As it scatters toxic sweat and emits electricity, a melody that sounds like it came from a guitar reverberates through the surrounding area.'),
    (849, 'shield', 'This short-tempered and aggressive Pokémon chugs stagnant water to absorb any toxins it might contain.'),
    (849, 'sword', 'When this Pokémon sounds as if it''s strumming a guitar, it''s actually clawing at the protrusions on its chest to generate electricity.'),
    (849, 'violet', 'The jolts of electricity it launches by violently strumming the protrusions on its chest easily exceed 15,000 volts.'),
    (850, 'shield', 'It wraps prey up with its heated body, cooking them in its coils. Once they''re well-done, it will voraciously nibble them down to the last morsel.'),
    (850, 'sword', 'It stores flammable gas in its body and uses it to generate heat. The yellow sections on its belly get particularly hot.'),
    (851, 'shield', 'While its burning body is already dangerous on its own, this excessively hostile Pokémon also has large and very sharp fangs.'),
    (851, 'sword', 'When it heats up, its body temperature reaches about 1,500 degrees Fahrenheit. It lashes its body like a whip and launches itself at enemies.'),
    (852, 'legends-za', 'The bulbous ends of its tentacles are perfect for pummeling but next to useless for gripping.'),
    (852, 'shield', 'Its tentacles tear off easily, but it isn''t alarmed when that happens—it knows they''ll grow back. It''s about as smart as a three-year-old.'),
    (852, 'sword', 'It''s very curious, but its means of investigating things is to try to punch them with its tentacles. The search for food is what brings it onto land.'),
    (853, 'legends-za', 'Grapploct pins opponents to the ground with its prized tentacles. Not even monstrously strong Pokémon can wrestle free from its hold.'),
    (853, 'shield', 'Searching for an opponent to test its skills against, it emerges onto land. Once the battle is over, it returns to the sea.'),
    (853, 'sword', 'A body made up of nothing but muscle makes the grappling moves this Pokémon performs with its tentacles tremendously powerful.'),
    (854, 'scarlet', 'Some fanatics will go to great pains to prepare the perfect tea and teacup, eagerly waiting for a Sinistea to come and possess their selections.'),
    (854, 'scarlet', 'The soul of someone who died alone possessed some leftover tea. This Pokémon appears in hotels and houses.'),
    (854, 'shield', 'It absorbs the life-force of those who drink it. It waits patiently, but opportunities are fleeting—it tastes so bad that it gets spat out immediately.'),
    (854, 'shield', 'The teacup in which this Pokémon makes its home is a famous piece of antique tableware. Many forgeries are in circulation.'),
    (854, 'sword', 'The swirl pattern in this Pokémon''s body is its weakness. If it gets stirred, the swirl loses its shape, and Sinistea gets dizzy.'),
    (854, 'sword', 'This Pokémon is said to have been born when a lonely spirit possessed a cold, leftover cup of tea.'),
    (854, 'violet', 'This Sinistea lives in an antique teacup. As valuable as this Pokémon is, its awful taste remains unchanged.'),
    (854, 'violet', 'Sinistea gets into your body when you drink it, and then it steals your vitality from within. It also tastes awful.'),
    (855, 'scarlet', 'The tea that composes Polteageist’s body has a distinct and enjoyable flavor. Drinking too much, however, can be fatal.'),
    (855, 'scarlet', 'Apparently a Polteageist’s disposition is affected by the type of tea the Pokémon came from. What teapot it inhabits makes no difference.'),
    (855, 'shield', 'When angered, it launches tea from its body at the offender''s mouth. The tea causes strong chills if swallowed.'),
    (855, 'shield', 'Leaving leftover black tea unattended is asking for this Pokémon to come along and pour itself into it, turning the tea into a new Polteageist.'),
    (855, 'sword', 'Trainers Polteageist trusts will be allowed to experience its distinctive flavor and aroma firsthand by sampling just a tiny bit of its tea.'),
    (855, 'sword', 'This species lives in antique teapots. Most pots are forgeries, but on rare occasions, an authentic work is found.'),
    (855, 'violet', 'Though risky to drink, this Pokémon''s tea tastes delicious. Gourmets who have no fear of danger drink Polteageist tea day after day.'),
    (855, 'violet', 'These Pokémon multiply by creeping into teapots and pouring themselves into leftover tea.'),
    (856, 'scarlet', 'Because the emotions of others constantly flow into its head, this Pokémon prefers environments where no other creatures live.'),
    (856, 'shield', 'If this Pokémon senses a strong emotion, it will run away as fast as it can. It prefers areas without people.'),
    (856, 'sword', 'Via the protrusion on its head, it senses other creatures'' emotions. If you don''t have a calm disposition, it will never warm up to you.'),
    (856, 'violet', 'It senses the feelings of other living creatures. Be careful not to expose it to strong emotions for too long, or it will end up exhausted.'),
    (857, 'scarlet', 'To this Pokémon, strong emotions apparently feel like incredibly loud noises—even if the emotions are happy ones.'),
    (857, 'shield', 'Using the braids on its head, it pummels foes to get them to quiet down. One blow from those braids would knock out a professional boxer.'),
    (857, 'sword', 'No matter who you are, if you bring strong emotions near this Pokémon, it will silence you violently.'),
    (857, 'violet', 'The moment this Pokémon finds someone who''s emitting strong emotions, it will pummel them senseless with its braids to silence them.'),
    (858, 'shield', 'If you''re too loud around it, you risk being torn apart by the claws on its tentacle. This Pokémon is also known as the Forest Witch.'),
    (858, 'sword', 'It emits psychic power strong enough to cause headaches as a deterrent to the approach of others.'),
    (859, 'scarlet', 'The reason this Pokémon causes trouble for those it feels close to is because Impidimp itself gets irritable if it can’t absorb negative emotions.'),
    (859, 'shield', 'It sneaks into people''s homes, stealing things and feasting on the negative energy of the frustrated occupants.'),
    (859, 'sword', 'Through its nose, it sucks in the emanations produced by people and Pokémon when they feel annoyed. It thrives off this negative energy.'),
    (859, 'violet', 'They live in groups, pestering and playing pranks on each other to polish their troublemaking skills.'),
    (860, 'scarlet', 'Morgrem prefers dirty tactics, like ambushing, because it doesn’t have confidence in its brawn.'),
    (860, 'shield', 'With sly cunning, it tries to lure people into the woods. Some believe it to have the power to make crops grow.'),
    (860, 'sword', 'When it gets down on all fours as if to beg for forgiveness, it''s trying to lure opponents in so that it can False Surrender.'),
    (860, 'violet', 'This Pokémon absorbs negative emotions and turns them into energy. It''s popular with people who tend to think gloomy thoughts.'),
    (861, 'shield', 'Its hairs work like muscle fibers. When its hairs unfurl, they latch on to opponents, ensnaring them as tentacles would.'),
    (861, 'sword', 'With the hair wrapped around its body helping to enhance its muscles, this Pokémon can overwhelm even Machamp.'),
    (862, 'shield', 'It evolved after experiencing numerous fights. While crossing its arms, it lets out a shout that would make any opponent flinch.'),
    (862, 'sword', 'Its voice is staggering in volume. Obstagoon has a tendency to take on a threatening posture and shout—this move is known as Obstruct.'),
    (863, 'legends-za', 'In battle, Perrserker boasts unrivaled strength, and many epic sagas tell of its valor. But in its home, it leaves garbage everywhere.'),
    (863, 'shield', 'After many battles, it evolved dangerous claws that come together to form daggers when extended.'),
    (863, 'sword', 'What appears to be an iron helmet is actually hardened hair. This Pokémon lives for the thrill of battle.'),
    (864, 'shield', 'Be cautious of the ectoplasmic body surrounding its soul. You''ll become stiff as stone if you touch it.'),
    (864, 'sword', 'Its shell is overflowing with its heightened otherworldly energy. The ectoplasm serves as protection for this Pokémon''s core spirit.'),
    (865, 'legends-za', 'Sirfetch''d has put its soul into nurturing its leek, which it treasures like life itself. It wields the leek splendidly, performing great feats of combat.'),
    (865, 'shield', 'After deflecting attacks with its hard leaf shield, it strikes back with its sharp leek stalk. The leek stalk is both weapon and food.'),
    (865, 'sword', 'Only Farfetch''d that have survived many battles can attain this evolution. When this Pokémon''s leek withers, it will retire from combat.'),
    (866, 'legends-za', 'Its comical dancing is its calling card. When its enemies laugh, it seizes the chance to blast them with frigid air of −328 degrees Fahrenheit.'),
    (866, 'shield', 'Its amusing movements make it very popular. It releases its psychic power from the pattern on its belly.'),
    (866, 'sword', 'It''s highly skilled at tap-dancing. It waves its cane of ice in time with its graceful movements.'),
    (867, 'legends-za', 'The scattered pieces of its clay slab have been reassembled, allowing the malicious power contained within to be fully unleashed.'),
    (867, 'shield', 'Never touch its shadowlike body, or you''ll be shown the horrific memories behind the picture carved into it.'),
    (867, 'sword', 'A powerful curse was woven into an ancient painting. After absorbing the spirit of a Yamask, the painting began to move.'),
    (868, 'scarlet', 'The more sweet aromas it absorbs, the more its body swells. Milcery will deflate when its energy level drops.'),
    (868, 'shield', 'They say that any patisserie visited by Milcery is guaranteed success and good fortune.'),
    (868, 'sword', 'This Pokémon was born from sweet-smelling particles in the air. Its body is made of cream.'),
    (868, 'violet', 'When attacked, it tackles its foe and covers them in cream. With its foe either blinded or astonished by deliciousness, Milcery flees.'),
    (870, 'legends-za', 'Five of them are troopers, and one is the brass. The brass''s orders are absolute.'),
    (870, 'scarlet', 'The brass, which is the one that stands at the front and issues orders, is the strongest and smartest of the six.'),
    (870, 'shield', 'The six of them work together as one Pokémon. Teamwork is also their battle strategy, and they constantly change their formation as they fight.'),
    (870, 'sword', 'Five of them are troopers, and one is the brass. The brass''s orders are absolute.'),
    (870, 'violet', 'The leader, known as the brass, uses its extendible horn to issue orders to the others when it''s time to change formation.'),
    (871, 'scarlet', 'This Pokémon generates electricity when it digests food. It uses its five hard teeth to scrape seaweed off surfaces and eat it.'),
    (871, 'shield', 'It stores electricity in each spine. Even if one gets broken off, it still continues to emit electricity for at least three hours.'),
    (871, 'sword', 'It feeds on seaweed, using its teeth to scrape it off rocks. Electric current flows from the tips of its spines.'),
    (871, 'violet', 'This Pokémon is so timid that even brushing against seaweed will make it discharge electricity in surprise. Its lips do not conduct electricity.'),
    (872, 'scarlet', 'It eats snow that has accumulated on the ground. It prefers soft, freshly fallen snow, so it will eat its way up a mountain, aiming for the peak.'),
    (872, 'shield', 'It eats snow that piles up on the ground. The more snow it eats, the bigger and more impressive the spikes on its back grow.'),
    (872, 'sword', 'It spits out thread imbued with a frigid sort of energy and uses it to tie its body to branches, disguising itself as an icicle while it sleeps.'),
    (872, 'violet', 'Within its internal organs, Snom amplifies the frigid air it gets from eating snow and then uses this amplified air to create icicle-like spikes.'),
    (873, 'scarlet', 'Frosmoth senses air currents with its antennae. It sends its scales drifting on frigid air, making them fall like snow.'),
    (873, 'shield', 'It shows no mercy to any who desecrate fields and mountains. It will fly around on its icy wings, causing a blizzard to chase offenders away.'),
    (873, 'sword', 'Icy scales fall from its wings like snow as it flies over fields and mountains. The temperature of its wings is less than −290 degrees Fahrenheit.'),
    (873, 'violet', 'It causes blizzards as it flies around with its huge, chill-emanating wings. Clean meltwater is its favorite thing to drink.'),
    (874, 'scarlet', 'The elemental composition of the rocks that form its body were found to match the bedrock of a land far away from this Pokémon’s habitat.'),
    (874, 'shield', 'Once a year, on a specific date and at a specific time, they gather out of nowhere and form up in a circle.'),
    (874, 'sword', 'It stands in grasslands, watching the sun''s descent from zenith to horizon. This Pokémon has a talent for delivering dynamic kicks.'),
    (874, 'violet', 'This Pokémon spends its life gazing at the setting sun. It strides leisurely across grassy plains on legs of rock that weigh over 400 pounds each.'),
    (875, 'scarlet', 'On hot days, these Pokémon press their ice cube heads together and pass the time cooling each other down.'),
    (875, 'shield', 'This Pokémon keeps its heat-sensitive head cool with ice. It fishes for its food, dangling its single hair into the sea to lure in prey.'),
    (875, 'sword', 'It drifted in on the flow of ocean waters from a frigid place. It keeps its head iced constantly to make sure it stays nice and cold.'),
    (875, 'violet', 'If you lick the ice covering its face, you''ll find it has a faintly salty taste. This species rode here on ocean currents from a cold, faraway land.'),
    (876, 'legends-za', 'Through its horns, it can pick up on the emotions of creatures around it. Positive emotions are the source of its strength.'),
    (876, 'scarlet', 'This Pokémon picks up on the positive emotions of other creatures via its horns and uses those emotions to fuel itself.'),
    (876, 'shield', 'Through its horns, it can pick up on the emotions of creatures around it. Positive emotions are the source of its strength.'),
    (876, 'sword', 'It uses the horns on its head to sense the emotions of others. Males will act as valets for those they serve, looking after their every need.'),
    (876, 'violet', 'This Pokémon never leaves its Trainer''s side. It predicts their actions with its psychic power and takes care of their day-to-day needs.'),
    (877, 'legends-za', 'This Pokémon is always hungry. It generates electricity by eating seeds it has stored up in its pocket-like pouches.'),
    (877, 'scarlet', 'Morpeko eats seeds constantly to keep its hunger at bay. If it''s hungry for too long, it grows wild and brutish.'),
    (877, 'shield', 'It carries electrically roasted seeds with it as if they''re precious treasures. No matter how much it eats, it always gets hungry again in short order.'),
    (877, 'sword', 'As it eats the seeds stored up in its pocket-like pouches, this {{OBP|Pokémon|species}} is not just satisfying its constant hunger. It''s also generating electricity.'),
    (877, 'violet', 'It has a small stomach. If it isn''t constantly eating the seeds it keeps in its pockets, it will get hungry immediately.'),
    (878, 'scarlet', 'Using the pointy tip of its trunk, it carves off chunks of hard rocks to eat. It is very docile and helps people with physical labor.'),
    (878, 'shield', 'If a job requires serious strength, this Pokémon will excel at it. Its copper body tarnishes in the rain, turning a vibrant green color.'),
    (878, 'sword', 'It digs up the ground with its trunk. It''s also very strong, being able to carry loads of over five tons without any problem at all.'),
    (878, 'violet', 'Cufant can lift loads weighing five tons. In the mornings, it heads into caves with its herd, in search of the ore on which these Pokémon feed.'),
    (879, 'shield', 'These Pokémon live in herds. Their trunks have incredible grip strength, strong enough to crush giant rocks into powder.'),
    (879, 'sword', 'They came over from another region long ago and worked together with humans. Their green skin is resistant to water.'),
    (880, 'shield', 'The powerful muscles in its tail generate its electricity. Compared to its lower body, its upper half is entirely too small.'),
    (880, 'sword', 'In ancient times, it was unbeatable thanks to its powerful lower body, but it went extinct anyway after it depleted all its plant-based food sources.'),
    (881, 'shield', 'This Pokémon lived on prehistoric seashores and was able to preserve food with the ice on its body. It went extinct because it moved so slowly.'),
    (881, 'sword', 'The shaking of its freezing upper half is what generates its electricity. It has a hard time walking around.'),
    (882, 'shield', 'Its mighty legs are capable of running at speeds exceeding 40 mph, but this Pokémon can''t breathe unless it''s underwater.'),
    (882, 'sword', 'Powerful legs and jaws made it the apex predator of its time. Its own overhunting of its prey was what drove it to extinction.'),
    (883, 'shield', 'The skin on its face is impervious to attack, but breathing difficulties made this Pokémon go extinct anyway.'),
    (883, 'sword', 'Though it''s able to capture prey by freezing its surroundings, it has trouble eating the prey afterward because its mouth is on top of its head.'),
    (884, 'shield', 'The special metal that composes its body is very light, so this Pokémon has considerable agility. It lives in caves because it dislikes the rain.'),
    (884, 'sword', 'Its body resembles polished metal, and it''s both lightweight and strong. The only drawback is that it rusts easily.'),
    (885, 'scarlet', 'In the evening, groups of Dreepy will fly at high speeds over the ocean and poke at Pokémon in the water for fun.'),
    (885, 'shield', 'If this weak Pokémon is by itself, a mere child could defeat it. But if Dreepy has friends to help it train, it can evolve and become much stronger.'),
    (885, 'sword', 'After being reborn as a ghost Pokémon, Dreepy wanders the areas it used to inhabit back when it was alive in prehistoric seas.'),
    (885, 'violet', 'It has a habit of biting at Clauncher even though it doesn''t feed on them. This is said to be vestigial behavior from when Dreepy was alive.'),
    (886, 'scarlet', 'This Pokémon flies around at over 120 miles per hour. If a Drakloak is defeated in a battle, its Dreepy will wander off without a second thought.'),
    (886, 'shield', 'Without a Dreepy to place on its head and care for, it gets so uneasy it''ll try to substitute any Pokémon it finds for the missing Dreepy.'),
    (886, 'sword', 'It''s capable of flying faster than 120 mph. It battles alongside Dreepy and dotes on them until they successfully evolve.'),
    (886, 'violet', 'This Pokémon stores up energy in its lungs, then shoots it out. It takes care of Dreepy and battles alongside them until they''re all grown up.'),
    (887, 'scarlet', 'Dragapult can make its whole body transparent by clearing its mind and focusing. Even the Dreepy in Dragapult’s horns become invisible.'),
    (887, 'shield', 'Apparently the Dreepy inside Dragapult''s horns eagerly look forward to being launched out at Mach speeds.'),
    (887, 'sword', 'When it isn''t battling, it keeps Dreepy in the holes on its horns. Once a fight starts, it Dragon Darts.'),
    (887, 'violet', 'The fastest Dragapult of the group is always surrounded by Dreepy that want to fly at sonic speed.'),
    (888, 'shield', 'This Pokémon has slumbered for many years. Some say it''s Zamazenta''s elder sister—others say the two Pokémon are rivals.'),
    (888, 'sword', 'Known as a legendary hero, this Pokémon absorbs metal particles, transforming them into a weapon it uses to battle.'),
    (889, 'shield', 'This Pokémon slept for aeons while in the form of a statue. It was asleep for so long, people forgot that it ever existed.'),
    (889, 'sword', 'In times past, it worked together with a king of the people to save the [[Galar]] [[region]]. It absorbs metal that it then uses in battle.'),
    (890, 'shield', 'It was inside a meteorite that fell 20,000 years ago. There seems to be a connection between this Pokémon and the [[Dynamax]] phenomenon.'),
    (890, 'sword', 'The core on its chest absorbs energy emanating from the lands of the [[Galar]] [[region]]. This energy is what allows Eternatus to stay active.'),
    (891, 'shield', 'If Kubfu pulls the long white hair on its head, its fighting spirit heightens and power wells up from the depths of its belly.'),
    (891, 'sword', 'Kubfu trains hard to perfect its moves. The moves it masters will determine which form it takes when it evolves.'),
    (892, 'shield', 'Inhabiting the mountains of a distant region, this {{OBP|Pokémon|species}} races across sheer cliffs, training its legs and refining its [[move]]s.'),
    (892, 'sword', 'This form of Urshifu is a strong believer in the one-hit KO. Its strategy is to leap in close to foes and land a devastating blow with a hardened fist.'),
    (893, 'shield', 'Once the vines on Zarude''s body tear off, they become nutrients in the soil. This helps the plants of the forest grow.'),
    (893, 'sword', 'Within dense forests, this Pokémon lives in a pack with others of its kind. It''s incredibly aggressive, and the other Pokémon of the forest fear it.'),
    (894, 'shield', 'Its entire body is made up of a single organ that generates electrical energy. Regieleki is capable of creating all [[Galar]]''s electricity.'),
    (894, 'sword', 'This Pokémon is a cluster of electrical energy. It''s said that removing the rings on Regieleki''s body will unleash the Pokémon''s latent power.'),
    (895, 'shield', 'Its body is composed of crystallized dragon energy. Regidrago is said to have the powers of every dragon Pokémon.'),
    (895, 'sword', 'An academic theory proposes that Regidrago''s arms were once the head of an ancient dragon Pokémon. The theory remains unproven.'),
    (896, 'shield', 'Glastrier has tremendous physical strength, and the mask of ice covering its face is 100 times harder than diamond.'),
    (896, 'sword', 'Glastrier emits intense cold from its hooves. It''s also a belligerent Pokémon—anything it wants, it takes by force.'),
    (897, 'shield', 'As it dashes through the night, Spectrier absorbs the life-force of sleeping creatures. It craves silence and solitude.'),
    (897, 'sword', 'It probes its surroundings with all its senses save one—it doesn''t use its sense of sight. Spectrier''s kicks are said to separate soul from body.'),
    (898, 'shield', 'Calyrex is known in legend as a king that ruled over Galar in ancient times. It has the power to cause hearts to mend and plants to spring forth.'),
    (898, 'sword', 'Calyrex is a merciful Pokémon, capable of providing healing and blessings. It reigned over the [[Galar]] region in times of yore.'),
    (899, 'legends-arceus', 'The black orbs shine with an uncanny light when the Pokémon is erecting invisible barriers. The fur shed from its beard retains heat well and is a highly useful material for winter clothing.'),
    (900, 'legends-arceus', 'A violent creature that fells towering trees with its crude axes and shields itself with hard stone. If one should chance upon this Pokémon in the wilds, one''s only recourse is to flee.'),
    (900, 'legends-za', 'Its stone axes get chipped away here and there during ferocious battles, but the process serves to make them sharper and sharper.'),
    (900, 'scarlet', 'Parts of its body turned to stone when it evolved thanks to an extremely rare ore found in volcanic areas.'),
    (900, 'violet', 'This Pokémon is a rough, crude, and violent sort. It swings around its large, heavy stone axes to finish off its prey.'),
    (901, 'legends-arceus', 'I believe it was Hisui''s swampy terrain that gave Ursaluna its burly physique and newfound capacity to manipulate peat at will.'),
    (902, 'scarlet', 'This Pokémon is cloaked in the souls of its comrades who perished during a punishing journey to the river of their birth.'),
    (902, 'violet', 'It can jump with incredible power. Parts of its body are tinged red by the rage of its fallen friends.'),
    (903, 'legends-arceus', 'Because of Sneasler''s virulent poison and daunting physical prowess, no other species could hope to best it on the frozen highlands. Preferring solitude, this species does not form packs.'),
    (904, 'legends-arceus', 'Its lancelike spikes and savage temperament have earned it the nickname "sea fiend." It slurps up poison to nourish itself.'),
    (904, 'legends-za', 'Overqwil''s poisonous spikes-now thicker, longer, and stronger-will automatically strike toward anything that moves.'),
    (904, 'scarlet', 'Overqwil’s poisonous spikes will reflexively react even while Overqwil sleeps, stabbing any moving thing that approaches.'),
    (904, 'violet', 'It’s ferocious and has a short temper. The ends of its spikes are barbed, and they can’t be easily removed once they’ve punctured something.'),
    (905, 'legends-arceus', 'When it flies to this land from across the sea, the bitter winter comes to an end. According to legend, this Pokémon''s love gives rise to the budding of fresh life across Hisui.'),
    (906, 'scarlet', 'Its fluffy fur is similar in composition to plants. This Pokémon frequently washes its face to keep it from drying out.'),
    (906, 'violet', 'The sweet scent its body gives off mesmerizes those around it. The scent grows stronger when this Pokémon is in the sun.'),
    (907, 'scarlet', 'Floragato deftly wields the vine hidden beneath its long fur, slamming the hard flower bud against its opponents.'),
    (907, 'violet', 'The hardness of Floragato''s fur depends on the Pokémon''s mood. When Floragato is prepared to battle, its fur becomes pointed and needle sharp.'),
    (908, 'scarlet', 'This Pokémon uses the reflective fur lining in its cape to camouflage the stem of its flower, creating the illusion that the flower is floating.'),
    (908, 'violet', 'With skillful misdirection, it rigs foes with pollen-packed flower bombs. Meowscarada sets off the bombs before its foes realize what''s going on.'),
    (909, 'scarlet', 'It lies on warm rocks and uses the heat absorbed by its square-shaped scales to create fire energy.'),
    (909, 'violet', 'Its flame sac is small, so energy is always leaking out. This energy is released from the dent atop Fuecoco''s head and flickers to and fro.'),
    (910, 'scarlet', 'The combination of Crocalor’s fire energy and overflowing vitality has caused an egg-shaped fireball to appear on the Pokémon’s head.'),
    (910, 'violet', 'The valve in Crocalor''s flame sac is closely connected to its vocal cords. This Pokémon utters a guttural cry as it spews flames every which way.'),
    (911, 'scarlet', 'The fiery bird changes shape when Skeledirge sings. Rumor has it that the bird was born when the fireball on Skeledirge’s head gained a soul.'),
    (911, 'violet', 'Skeledirge’s gentle singing soothes the souls of all that hear it. It burns its enemies to a crisp with flames of over 5,400 degrees Fahrenheit.'),
    (912, 'scarlet', 'This Pokémon migrated to Paldea from distant lands long ago. The gel secreted by its feathers repels water and grime.'),
    (912, 'violet', 'Its strong legs let it easily swim around in even fast-flowing rivers. It likes to keep things tidy and is prone to overthinking things.'),
    (913, 'scarlet', 'These Pokémon constantly run through shallow waters to train their legs, then compete with each other to see which of them kicks most gracefully.'),
    (913, 'violet', 'The hardworking Quaxwell observes people and Pokémon from various regions and incorporates their movements into its own dance routines.'),
    (914, 'scarlet', 'A single kick from a Quaquaval can send a truck rolling. This Pokémon uses its powerful legs to perform striking dances from far-off lands.'),
    (914, 'violet', 'Dancing in ways that evoke far-away places, this Pokémon mesmerizes all that see it. Flourishes of its decorative water feathers slice into its foes.'),
    (915, 'scarlet', 'It searches for food all day. It possesses a keen sense of smell but doesn’t use it for anything other than foraging.'),
    (915, 'violet', 'This Pokémon spurns all but the finest of foods. Its body gives off an herblike scent that bug Pokémon detest.'),
    (916, 'scarlet', 'Oinkologne is proud of its fine, glossy skin. It emits a concentrated scent from the tip of its tail.'),
    (916, 'violet', 'It entrances female Pokémon with the sweet, alluring scent that wafts from all over its body.'),
    (917, 'scarlet', 'The ball of threads wrapped around its body is elastic enough to deflect the scythes of Scyther, this Pokémon’s natural enemy.'),
    (917, 'violet', 'The thread it secretes from its rear is as strong as wire. The secret behind the thread''s strength is the topic of ongoing research.'),
    (918, 'scarlet', 'It clings to branches and ceilings using its threads and moves without a sound. It takes out its prey before the prey even notices it.'),
    (918, 'violet', 'Spidops covers its territory in tough, sticky threads to set up traps for intruders.'),
    (919, 'scarlet', 'It has its third set of legs folded up. When it’s in a tough spot, this Pokémon jumps over 30 feet using the strength of its legs.'),
    (919, 'violet', 'It''s highly skilled at a fighting style in which it uses its jumping capabilities to dodge incoming attacks while also dealing damage to opponents.'),
    (920, 'scarlet', 'When it decides to fight all out, it stands on its previously folded legs to enter Showdown Mode. It neutralizes its enemies in short order.'),
    (920, 'violet', 'It uses its normally folded third set of legs when in Showdown Mode. This places a huge burden on its body, so it can''t stay in this mode for long.'),
    (921, 'scarlet', 'It has underdeveloped electric sacs on its cheeks. These sacs can produce electricity only if Pawmi rubs them furiously with the pads on its forepaws.'),
    (921, 'violet', 'The pads of its paws are electricity-discharging organs. Pawmi fires electricity from its forepaws while standing unsteadily on its hind legs.'),
    (922, 'scarlet', 'When its group is attacked, Pawmo is the first to leap into battle, defeating enemies with a fighting technique that utilizes electric shocks.'),
    (922, 'violet', 'Pawmo uses a unique fighting technique in which it uses its forepaws to strike foes and zap them with electricity from its paw pads simultaneously.'),
    (923, 'scarlet', 'This Pokémon normally is slow to react, but once it enters battle, it will strike down its enemies with lightning-fast movements.'),
    (923, 'violet', 'Pawmot''s fluffy fur acts as a battery. It can store the same amount of electricity as an electric car.'),
    (924, 'scarlet', 'Exhibiting great teamwork, they use their incisors to cut pieces out of any material that might be useful for a nest, then make off with them.'),
    (924, 'violet', 'The pair sticks together no matter what. They split any food they find exactly in half and then eat it together.'),
    (926, 'legends-za', 'This Pokémon cultivates yeast within its body. It has lived with humans—and helped enrich their diets—since ancient times.'),
    (926, 'scarlet', 'This Pokémon is smooth and moist to the touch. Yeast in Fidough’s breath induces fermentation in the Pokémon’s vicinity.'),
    (926, 'violet', 'The yeast in Fidough''s breath is useful for cooking, so this Pokémon has been protected by people since long ago.'),
    (927, 'legends-za', 'The appetizing scent of Dachsbun''s body sends opponents'' hunger into overdrive, wearing down their willpower and stamina.'),
    (927, 'scarlet', 'The pleasant aroma that emanates from this Pokémon’s body helps wheat grow, so Dachsbun has been treasured by farming villages.'),
    (927, 'violet', 'The surface of this Pokémon''s skin hardens when exposed to intense heat, and its body has an appetizing aroma.'),
    (928, 'scarlet', 'It protects itself from enemies by emitting oil from the fruit on its head. This oil is bitter and astringent enough to make someone flinch.'),
    (928, 'violet', 'This Pokémon converts nutrients into oil, which it stores in the fruit on its head. It can easily go a whole week without eating or drinking.'),
    (929, 'scarlet', 'Dolliv shares its tasty, fresh-scented oil with others. This species has coexisted with humans since times long gone.'),
    (929, 'violet', 'It basks in the sun to its heart''s content until the fruits on its head ripen. After that, Dolliv departs from human settlements and goes on a journey.'),
    (930, 'scarlet', 'This calm Pokémon is very compassionate. It will share its delicious, nutrient-rich oil with weakened Pokémon.'),
    (930, 'violet', 'This Pokémon drives back enemies by launching its rich, aromatic oil at them with enough force to smash a boulder.'),
    (932, 'legends-za', 'As Nacli treads along the ground, grains of rock salt are left behind. These trails have been called "salt roads" since long ago.'),
    (932, 'scarlet', 'It was born in a layer of rock salt deep under the earth. This species was particularly treasured in the old days, as they would share precious salt.'),
    (932, 'violet', 'The ground scrapes its body as it travels, causing it to leave salt behind. Salt is constantly being created and replenished inside Nacli''s body.'),
    (933, 'legends-za', 'This absent-minded Pokémon tends to forget about the prey it has salt-cured. It''s even prone to forgetting the orders its Trainer has given it.'),
    (933, 'scarlet', 'This Pokémon dry cures its prey by spraying salt over them. The curing process steals away the water in the prey’s body.'),
    (933, 'violet', 'It compresses rock salt inside its body and shoots out hardened salt pellets with enough force to perforate an iron sheet.'),
    (934, 'legends-za', 'Rock salt obtained from Garganacl has many restorative elements and is helpful for maintaining one''s health.'),
    (934, 'scarlet', 'Garganacl will rub its fingertips together and sprinkle injured Pokémon with salt. Even severe wounds will promptly heal afterward.'),
    (934, 'violet', 'Many Pokémon gather around Garganacl, hoping to lick at its mineral-rich salt.'),
    (935, 'legends-za', 'This Pokémon is skilled at manipulating flames. Humans have prized it highly since ancient times.'),
    (935, 'scarlet', 'Burnt charcoal came to life and became a {{OBP|Pokémon|species}}. Possessing a fiery fighting spirit, Charcadet will {{pkmn|battle}} even tough opponents.'),
    (935, 'violet', 'Its firepower increases when it fights, reaching over 1,800 degrees Fahrenheit. It likes {{Berries}} that are rich in fat.'),
    (936, 'legends-za', 'Though Armarouge pledges loyalty to its Trainer, it repeatedly leaves to go train on its own to strengthen its psychic energy.'),
    (936, 'scarlet', 'Armarouge evolved through the use of a set of armor that belonged to a distinguished warrior. This Pokémon is incredibly loyal.'),
    (936, 'violet', 'This Pokémon clads itself in armor that has been fortified by psychic and fire energy, and it shoots blazing fireballs.'),
    (937, 'legends-za', 'It swears loyalty to its Trainer. Should anyone dare to show that Trainer hostility, Ceruledge will cut the offender down without a second thought.'),
    (937, 'scarlet', 'The fiery blades on its arms burn fiercely with the lingering resentment of a sword wielder who fell before accomplishing their goal.'),
    (937, 'violet', 'An old set of armor steeped in grudges caused this Pokémon''s evolution. Ceruledge cuts its enemies to pieces without mercy.'),
    (938, 'scarlet', 'Tadbulb shakes its tail to generate electricity. If it senses danger, it will make its head blink on and off to alert its allies.'),
    (938, 'violet', 'It floats using the electricity stored in its body. When thunderclouds are around, Tadbulb will float higher off the ground.'),
    (939, 'scarlet', 'When this Pokémon expands and contracts its wobbly body, the belly-button dynamo in its stomach produces a huge amount of electricity.'),
    (939, 'violet', 'What appear to be eyeballs are actually organs for discharging the electricity generated by Bellibolt''s belly-button dynamo.'),
    (940, 'scarlet', 'When its wings catch the wind, the bones within produce electricity. This Pokémon dives into the ocean, catching prey by electrocuting them.'),
    (940, 'violet', 'These Pokémon make their nests on coastal cliffs. The nests have a strange, crackling texture, and they''re a popular delicacy.'),
    (941, 'scarlet', 'Kilowattrel inflates its throat sac to amplify its electricity. By riding the wind, this Pokémon can fly over 430 miles in a day.'),
    (941, 'violet', 'It uses its throat sac to store electricity generated by its wings. There''s hardly any oil in its feathers, so it is a poor swimmer.'),
    (942, 'legends-za', 'Packs of these Pokémon are incredibly close-knit. In order to be taken seriously, Maschiff intimidate others by wearing a grumpy expression.'),
    (942, 'scarlet', 'It always scowls in an attempt to make opponents take it seriously, but even crying children will burst into laughter when they see Maschiff’s face.'),
    (942, 'violet', 'Its well-developed jaw and fangs are strong enough to crunch through boulders, and its thick fat makes for an excellent defense.'),
    (943, 'legends-za', 'Contrary to appearances, Mabosstiff has a kind heart-but it will relentlessly chase down and put an end to any foe that dares threaten its family.'),
    (943, 'scarlet', 'This Pokémon can store energy in its large dewlap. Mabosstiff unleashes this energy all at once to blow away enemies.'),
    (943, 'violet', 'Mabosstiff loves playing with children. Though usually gentle, it takes on an intimidating look when protecting its family.'),
    (944, 'legends-za', 'Shroodle protects itself from foes using both its poisonous saliva and its front teeth, which are disproportionately big and long for its small body.'),
    (944, 'scarlet', 'Though usually a mellow Pokémon, it will sink its sharp, poison-soaked front teeth into any that anger it, causing paralysis in the object of its ire.'),
    (944, 'violet', 'To keep enemies away from its territory, it paints markings around its nest using a poisonous liquid that has an acrid odor.'),
    (945, 'legends-za', 'What Grafaiai eats affects the color of its saliva. With this saliva, it paints patterns on rocks and trees in order to protect its territory.'),
    (945, 'scarlet', 'The color of the poisonous saliva depends on what the Pokémon eats. Grafaiai covers its fingers in its saliva and draws patterns on trees in forests.'),
    (945, 'violet', 'Each Grafaiai paints its own individual pattern, and it will paint that same pattern over and over again throughout its life.'),
    (946, 'scarlet', 'A soul unable to move on to the afterlife was blown around by the wind until it got tangled up with dried grass and became a Pokémon.'),
    (946, 'violet', 'Not even Bramblin knows where it is headed as it tumbles across the wilderness, blown by the wind. It loathes getting wet.'),
    (947, 'scarlet', 'It will open the branches of its head to envelop its prey. Once it absorbs all the life energy it needs, it expels the prey and discards it.'),
    (947, 'violet', 'Brambleghast wanders around arid regions. On rare occasions, mass outbreaks of these Pokémon will bury an entire town.'),
    (948, 'scarlet', 'Toedscool lives in muggy forests. The flaps that fall from its body are chewy and very delicious.'),
    (948, 'violet', 'Though it looks like Tentacool, Toedscool is a completely different species. Its legs may be thin, but it can run at a speed of 30 mph.'),
    (949, 'scarlet', 'These Pokémon gather into groups and form colonies deep within forests. They absolutely hate it when strangers approach.'),
    (949, 'violet', 'It coils its 10 tentacles around prey and sucks out their nutrients, causing the prey pain. The folds along the rim of its head are a popular delicacy.'),
    (950, 'scarlet', 'Klawf hangs upside-down from cliffs, waiting for prey. But Klawf can’t remain in this position for long because its blood rushes to its head.'),
    (950, 'violet', 'This Pokémon lives on sheer cliffs. It sidesteps opponents'' attacks, then lunges for their weak spots with its claws.'),
    (951, 'legends-za', 'Capsakid is prone to intense mood swings, perhaps influenced by the spicy chemicals inside it. It will bite anything it takes a disliking to.'),
    (951, 'scarlet', 'The more sunlight this Pokémon bathes in, the more spicy chemicals are produced by its body, and thus the spicier its moves become.'),
    (951, 'violet', 'Traditional Paldean dishes can be extremely spicy because they include the shed front teeth of Capsakid among their ingredients.'),
    (952, 'legends-za', 'Its two heads have different temperaments and excel at different fighting styles. Nevertheless, they act in perfect harmony on the battlefield.'),
    (952, 'scarlet', 'The red head converts spicy chemicals into fire energy and blasts the surrounding area with a super spicy stream of flame.'),
    (952, 'violet', 'The green head has turned vicious due to the spicy chemicals stimulating its brain. Once it goes on a rampage, there is no stopping it.'),
    (953, 'scarlet', 'This Pokémon creates a mud ball by mixing sand and dirt with psychic energy. It treasures its mud ball more than its own life.'),
    (953, 'violet', 'It rolls its mud ball around while the energy it needs for evolution matures. Eventually the time comes for it to evolve.'),
    (954, 'scarlet', 'The body that supports the ball barely moves. Therefore, it is thought that the true body of this Pokémon is actually inside the ball.'),
    (954, 'violet', 'An infant sleeps inside the ball. Rabsca rolls the ball soothingly with its legs to ensure the infant sleeps comfortably.'),
    (955, 'scarlet', 'Flittle’s toes levitate about half an inch above the ground because of the psychic power emitted from the frills on the Pokémon’s belly.'),
    (955, 'violet', 'It spends its time running around wastelands. If anyone steals its beloved berries, it will chase them down and exact its revenge.'),
    (956, 'scarlet', 'It immobilizes opponents by bathing them in psychic power from its large eyes. Despite its appearance, it has a vicious temperament.'),
    (956, 'violet', 'It emits psychic power from the gaps between its multicolored frills and sprints at speeds greater than 120 mph.'),
    (957, 'legends-za', 'Tinkatink cobbles together a suitable hammer for itself using tools and metal fragments it finds in mines.'),
    (957, 'scarlet', 'It swings its handmade hammer around to protect itself, but the hammer is often stolen by Pokémon that eat metal.'),
    (957, 'violet', 'This Pokémon pounds iron scraps together to make a hammer. It will remake the hammer again and again until it''s satisfied with the result.'),
    (958, 'legends-za', 'Tinkatuff sometimes come to human settlements, where they rummage through factories and warehouses to gather metal.'),
    (958, 'scarlet', 'This Pokémon will attack groups of Pawniard and Bisharp, gathering metal from them in order to create a large and sturdy hammer.'),
    (958, 'violet', 'These Pokémon make their homes in piles of scrap metal. They test the strength of each other''s hammers by smashing them together.'),
    (959, 'legends-za', 'A Tinkaton leader teaches the Tinkatink in its group the skills needed for pounding and shaping metal.'),
    (959, 'scarlet', 'This intelligent Pokémon has a very daring disposition. It knocks rocks into the sky with its hammer, aiming for flying Corviknight.'),
    (959, 'violet', 'The hammer tops 220 pounds, yet it gets swung around easily by Tinkaton as it steals whatever it pleases and carries its plunder back home.'),
    (960, 'scarlet', 'This Pokémon can pick up the scent of a Veluza just over 65 feet away and will hide itself in the sand.'),
    (960, 'violet', 'Though it looks like Diglett, Wiglett is an entirely different species. The resemblance seems to be a coincidental result of environmental adaptation.'),
    (961, 'scarlet', 'It has a vicious temperament, contrary to what its appearance may suggest. It wraps its long bodies around prey, then drags the prey into its den.'),
    (961, 'violet', 'A variety of fish Pokémon, Wugtrio was once considered to be a [[regional form]] of Dugtrio.'),
    (962, 'scarlet', 'It gathers things up in an apron made from shed feathers added to the Pokémon’s chest feathers, then drops those things from high places for fun.'),
    (962, 'violet', 'Bombirdier uses the apron on its chest to bundle up food, which it carries back to its nest. It enjoys dropping things that make loud noises.'),
    (963, 'scarlet', 'It likes playing with others of its kind using the water ring on its tail. It uses ultrasonic waves to sense the emotions of other living creatures.'),
    (963, 'violet', 'Its water ring is made from seawater mixed with a sticky fluid that Finizen secretes from its blowhole.'),
    (964, 'scarlet', 'This {{OBP|Pokémon|species}} changes its appearance if it hears its allies calling for help. Palafin will never show anybody its moment of transformation.'),
    (964, 'violet', 'Its physical capabilities are no different than a Finizen''s, but when its allies are in danger, it transforms and powers itself up.'),
    (965, 'scarlet', 'It is said that this Pokémon was born when an unknown poison Pokémon entered and inspirited an engine left at a scrap-processing factory.'),
    (965, 'violet', 'The steel section is Varoom''s actual body. This Pokémon clings to rocks and converts the minerals within into energy to fuel its activities.'),
    (966, 'scarlet', 'It creates a gas out of poison and minerals from rocks. It then detonates the gas in its cylinders—now numbering eight—to generate energy.'),
    (966, 'violet', 'Revavroom viciously threatens others with the sound of its exhaust. It sticks its tongue out from its cylindrical mouth and sprays toxic fluids.'),
    (967, 'legends-za', 'Cyclizar keeps energy stored in the folds of its throat, allowing it to run nonstop over very long distances while carrying someone.'),
    (967, 'scarlet', 'Apparently Cyclizar has been allowing people to ride on its back since ancient times. Depictions of this have been found in 10,000-year-old murals.'),
    (967, 'violet', 'It can sprint at over 70 mph while carrying a human. The rider''s body heat warms Cyclizar''s back and lifts the Pokémon''s spirit.'),
    (968, 'scarlet', 'When attacked, this Pokémon will wield the tendrils on its body like fists and pelt the opponent with a storm of punches.'),
    (968, 'violet', 'This Pokémon lives in arid deserts. It maintains its metal body by consuming iron from the soil.'),
    (969, 'legends-za', 'Glimmet clings to the ceilings of caves. It defends itself by striking enemies with its bud, which is packed with poisonous components.'),
    (969, 'scarlet', 'It absorbs nutrients from cave walls. The petals it wears are made of crystallized poison.'),
    (969, 'violet', 'Glimmet''s toxic mineral crystals look just like flower petals. This Pokémon scatters poisonous powder like pollen to protect itself.'),
    (970, 'legends-za', 'Glimmora blooms into a large flower made of poisonous components. It works together with groups of Glimmet to repel enemies.'),
    (970, 'scarlet', 'When this Pokémon detects danger, it will open up its crystalline petals and fire beams from its conical body.'),
    (970, 'violet', 'Glimmora''s petals are made of crystallized poison energy. It has recently become evident that these petals resemble Tera Jewels.'),
    (971, 'legends-za', 'This Pokémon loves to gambol and roughhouse. It rubs its fur up against others and absorbs their life force until they''re utterly drained.'),
    (971, 'scarlet', 'It is said that a dog Pokémon that died in the wild without ever interacting with a human was reborn as this Pokémon.'),
    (971, 'violet', 'This friendly Pokémon doesn''t like being alone. Pay it even the slightest bit of attention, and it will follow you forever.'),
    (972, 'legends-za', 'At some point during the many years it spent guarding the gravestone of its dearly departed master, it was reborn as a ghost Pokémon.'),
    (972, 'scarlet', 'Houndstone spends most of its time sleeping in graveyards. Among all the dog Pokémon, this one is most loyal to its master.'),
    (972, 'violet', 'A lovingly mourned Pokémon was reborn as Houndstone. It doesn''t like anyone touching the protuberance atop its head.'),
    (973, 'legends-za', 'A flock of Flamigo can reach numbers of over 10,000. The sight of one of these massive flocks moving together in sync is incredible to behold.'),
    (973, 'scarlet', 'This Pokémon apparently ties the base of its neck into a knot so that energy stored in its belly does not escape from its beak.'),
    (973, 'violet', 'Thanks to a behavior of theirs known as “synchronizing,” an entire flock of these Pokémon can attack simultaneously in perfect harmony.'),
    (974, 'scarlet', 'This species left the ocean and began living on land a very long time ago. It seems to be closely related to Wailmer.'),
    (974, 'violet', 'It lives in frigid regions in pods of five or so individuals. It loves the minerals found in snow and ice.'),
    (975, 'scarlet', 'This Pokémon wanders around snowy, icy areas. It protects its body with powerful muscles and a {{a|Thick Fat|thick layer of fat}} under its skin.'),
    (975, 'violet', 'Ice energy builds up in the horn on its upper jaw, causing the horn to reach cryogenic temperatures that freeze its surroundings.'),
    (976, 'scarlet', 'When Veluza discards unnecessary flesh, its mind becomes honed and its psychic power increases. The spare flesh has a mild but delicious flavor.'),
    (976, 'violet', 'Veluza has excellent regenerative capabilities. It sheds spare flesh from its body to boost its agility, then charges at its prey.'),
    (977, 'legends-za', 'Although it boasts fantastic strength and a huge body that stirs up great waves when it thrashes, Dondozo struggles at catching prey.'),
    (977, 'scarlet', 'This Pokémon is a glutton, but it''s bad at getting food. It teams up with a Tatsugiri to catch prey.'),
    (977, 'violet', 'It treats Tatsugiri like its boss and follows it loyally. Though powerful, Dondozo is apparently not very smart.'),
    (979, 'legends-za', 'Primeape evolved into Annihilape after repeatedly using a move with enough force to burst the blood vessels in its head.'),
    (979, 'scarlet', 'When its anger rose beyond a critical point, this Pokémon gained power that is unfettered by the limits of its physical body.'),
    (979, 'violet', 'It imbues its fists with the power of the rage that it kept hidden in its heart. Opponents struck by these imbued fists will be shattered to their core.'),
    (980, 'scarlet', 'When attacked, this Pokémon will retaliate by sticking thick spines out from its body. It’s a risky move that puts everything on the line.'),
    (980, 'violet', 'It lives at the bottom of ponds and swamps. It will carry Wooper on its back and ferry them across water from one shore to the other.'),
    (981, 'scarlet', 'Now that the brain waves from the head and tail are synced up, the psychic power of this Pokémon is 10 times stronger than Girafarig’s.'),
    (981, 'violet', 'The hardened head from the tail protects the head of the main body as Farigiraf whips its long neck around to headbutt enemies.'),
    (983, 'scarlet', 'Only a Bisharp that stands above all others in its vast army can evolve into Kingambit.'),
    (983, 'violet', 'Though it commands a massive army in battle, it''s not skilled at devising complex strategies. It just uses brute strength to keep pushing.'),
    (984, 'scarlet', 'Sightings of this Pokémon have occurred in recent years. The name Great Tusk was taken from a creature listed in a certain book.'),
    (984, 'violet', 'This creature resembles a mysterious Pokémon that, according to a paranormal magazine, has lived since ancient times.'),
    (985, 'scarlet', 'There has been only one reported sighting of this Pokémon. It resembles a mysterious creature depicted in an old expedition journal.'),
    (985, 'violet', 'It resembles a mysterious Pokémon described in a paranormal magazine as a Jigglypuff from one billion years ago.'),
    (986, 'scarlet', 'It is possible that the creature listed as Brute Bonnet in a certain book could actually be this Pokémon.'),
    (986, 'violet', 'It bears a slight resemblance to a Pokémon described in a dubious magazine as a cross between a dinosaur and a mushroom.'),
    (987, 'scarlet', 'This Pokémon has characteristics similar to those of Flutter Mane, a creature mentioned in a certain book.'),
    (987, 'violet', 'It has similar features to a ghostly pterosaur that was covered in a paranormal magazine, but the two have little else in common.'),
    (988, 'scarlet', 'This mysterious Pokémon has some similarities to a creature that an old book introduced as Slither Wing.'),
    (988, 'violet', 'This Pokémon somewhat resembles an ancient form of Volcarona that was introduced in a dubious magazine.'),
    (989, 'scarlet', 'No records exist of this Pokémon being caught. Data is lacking, but the Pokémon’s traits match up with a creature shown in an expedition journal.'),
    (989, 'violet', 'It slightly resembles a Magneton that lived for 10,000 years and was featured in an article in a paranormal magazine.'),
    (990, 'scarlet', 'This Pokémon closely resembles a scientific weapon that a paranormal magazine claimed was sent to this planet by aliens.'),
    (990, 'violet', 'Sightings of this Pokémon have occurred in recent years. It resembles a mysterious object described in an old expedition journal.'),
    (991, 'scarlet', 'Its shape is similar to a robot featured in a paranormal magazine article. The robot was said to have been created by an ancient civilization.'),
    (991, 'violet', 'It resembles a mysterious object mentioned in an old book. There are only two reported sightings of this Pokémon.'),
    (992, 'scarlet', 'It is very similar to a cyborg covered exclusively by a paranormal magazine. The cyborg was said to be the modified form of a certain athlete.'),
    (992, 'violet', 'This Pokémon shares many similarities with Iron Hands, an object mentioned in a certain expedition journal.'),
    (993, 'scarlet', 'It resembles a certain Pokémon introduced in a paranormal magazine, described as the offspring of a Hydreigon that fell in love with a robot.'),
    (993, 'violet', 'It''s possible that Iron Jugulis, an object described in an old book, may actually be this Pokémon.'),
    (994, 'scarlet', 'This Pokémon resembles an unknown object described in a paranormal magazine as a UFO sent to observe humanity.'),
    (994, 'violet', 'No records exist of this species being caught. Data is lacking, but the Pokémon''s traits match up with an object described in an old book.'),
    (995, 'scarlet', 'It has some similarities to a Pokémon introduced in a dubious magazine as a Tyranitar from one billion years into the future.'),
    (995, 'violet', 'Some of its notable features match those of an object named within a certain expedition journal as Iron Thorns.'),
    (996, 'legends-za', 'Frigibax''s dorsal fin can convert heat from fiery moves into Ice-type energy to freeze the air.'),
    (996, 'scarlet', 'Frigibax absorbs heat through its dorsal fin and converts the heat into ice energy. The higher the temperature, the more energy Frigibax stores.'),
    (996, 'violet', 'This Pokémon lives in forests and craggy areas. Using the power of its dorsal fin, it cools the inside of its nest like a refrigerator.'),
    (997, 'legends-za', 'Arctibax is armed with a bladed dorsal fin and a mask made of ice. It is agile in its movements, springing upon foes to deliver slashing attacks.'),
    (997, 'scarlet', 'Arctibax freezes the air around it, protecting its face with an ice mask and turning its dorsal fin into a blade of ice.'),
    (997, 'violet', 'It attacks with the blade of its frozen dorsal fin by doing a front flip in the air. Arctibax''s strong back and legs allow it to pull off this technique.'),
    (998, 'legends-za', 'Baxcalibur exhales air cold enough to freeze lava. It uses its breath to freeze foes, then pulverizes them with a blow from its tail.'),
    (998, 'scarlet', 'This Pokémon blasts cryogenic air out from its mouth. This air can instantly freeze even liquid-hot lava.'),
    (998, 'violet', 'It launches itself into battle by flipping upside down and spewing frigid air from its mouth. It finishes opponents off with its dorsal blade.'),
    (999, 'legends-za', 'It lurks inside a sturdy treasure chest and possesses solid defenses, but it''s so heavy that it has difficulty moving around.'),
    (999, 'scarlet', 'This Pokémon was born inside a treasure chest about 1,500 years ago. It sucks the life-force out of scoundrels who try to steal the treasure.'),
    (999, 'violet', 'It lives inside an old treasure chest. Sometimes it gets left in shop corners since no one realizes it''s actually a Pokémon.'),
    (1000, 'legends-za', 'This Pokémon likes lively places. Some wild Gholdengo even live in cities.'),
    (1000, 'scarlet', 'Its body seems to be made up of 1,000 coins. This Pokémon gets along well with others and is quick to make friends with anybody.'),
    (1000, 'violet', 'It has a sturdy body made up of stacked coins. Gholdengo overwhelms its enemies by firing coin after coin at them in quick succession.'),
    (1001, 'scarlet', 'The grudge of a person punished for writing the king’s evil deeds upon wooden tablets has clad itself in dead leaves to become a Pokémon.'),
    (1001, 'violet', 'It drains the life-force from vegetation, causing nearby forests to instantly wither and fields to turn barren.'),
    (1002, 'scarlet', 'This Pokémon can control 100 tons of fallen snow. It plays around innocently by leaping in and out of avalanches it has caused.'),
    (1002, 'violet', 'The hatred of those who perished by the sword long ago has clad itself in snow and become a Pokémon.'),
    (1003, 'scarlet', 'The fear poured into an ancient ritual vessel has clad itself in rocks and dirt to become a Pokémon.'),
    (1003, 'violet', 'It slowly brings its exceedingly heavy head down upon the ground, splitting the earth open with huge fissures that run over 160 feet deep.'),
    (1004, 'scarlet', 'It controls flames burning at over 5,400 degrees Fahrenheit. It casually swims through the sea of lava it creates by melting rock and sand.'),
    (1004, 'violet', 'The envy accumulated within curved beads that sparked multiple conflicts has clad itself in fire and become a Pokémon.'),
    (1005, 'scarlet', 'It is possible that this is the creature listed as Roaring Moon in [[Scarlet Book|an expedition journal]] that still holds many mysteries.'),
    (1005, 'violet', 'According to an article in a dubious magazine, this Pokémon has some connection to a [[Mega Evolution|phenomenon]] that occurs in [[Kalos|a certain region]].'),
    (1006, 'scarlet', 'It has some similarities to a mad scientist’s invention covered in a paranormal magazine.'),
    (1006, 'violet', 'It''s possible that this is the object listed as Iron Valiant in a [[Violet Book|certain expedition journal.]]'),
    (1007, 'scarlet', 'The ecology and other data about this Pokémon are unknown. It was named Koraidon by the [[Professor Sada|professor]] who discovered it.*'),
    (1007, 'scarlet', 'This seems to be the Winged King mentioned in an [[Scarlet Book|old expedition journal]]. It was said to have split the land with its bare fists.'),
    (1007, 'violet', 'It has similar characteristics to a creature described in an old book as the Winged King.*'),
    (1007, 'violet', 'This {{OBP|Pokémon|species}} resembles Cyclizar, but it is far burlier and more ferocious. Nothing is known about its ecology or other features.'),
    (1008, 'scarlet', 'Much remains unknown about this creature. It resembles Cyclizar, but it is far more ruthless and powerful.'),
    (1008, 'scarlet', 'Its characteristics match those of a mysterious object recorded in an old expedition journal as the Iron Serpent.*'),
    (1008, 'violet', 'It was given the name Miraidon by the [[Professor Turo|professor]] who discovered it. Its ecology and other details are unknown.*'),
    (1008, 'violet', 'This seems to be the Iron Serpent mentioned in an [[Violet Book|old book]]. The Iron Serpent is said to have turned the land to ash with its lightning.'),
    (1009, 'scarlet', 'This ferocious creature is shrouded in mystery. It''s named after an aquatic monster mentioned in an old expedition journal.'),
    (1009, 'violet', 'It resembles an illustration published in a paranormal magazine, said to be a depiction of a super-ancient Suicune.'),
    (1010, 'scarlet', 'Many of its physical characteristics match those of a Virizion from the future that was covered in a paranormal magazine.'),
    (1010, 'violet', 'According to the few eyewitness accounts that exist, it used its shining blades to julienne large trees and boulders.'),
    (1011, 'scarlet', 'Dipplin is two creatures in one Pokémon. Its evolution was triggered by a special apple grown only in one place.'),
    (1011, 'violet', 'The head sticking out belongs to the fore-wyrm, while the tail belongs to the core-wyrm. The two share one apple and help each other out.'),
    (1012, 'scarlet', 'Supposedly, the regrets of a tea ceremony master who died before perfecting his craft lingered in some matcha and became a Pokémon.'),
    (1012, 'scarlet', 'It sprinkles some of its powdery body onto food and drains the life-force from those who so much as lick it.'),
    (1012, 'violet', 'Poltchageist looks like a [[regional form]] of Sinistea, but it was recently discovered that the two Pokémon are entirely unrelated.'),
    (1012, 'violet', 'It has taken up residence in a very expensive tea caddy. It takes an expert to distinguish the expensive tea caddies from the cheap ones.'),
    (1013, 'scarlet', 'It lives inside a superb teacup that was crafted by a potter of great renown. Collectors positively adore this Pokémon.'),
    (1013, 'scarlet', 'It pretends to be tea, trying to fool people into drinking it so it can drain their life-force. Its ruse is generally unsuccessful.'),
    (1013, 'violet', 'It prefers cool, dark places, such as the back of a shelf or the space beneath a home''s floorboards. It wanders in search of prey after sunset.'),
    (1013, 'violet', 'The more stirring it does with the tea whisk on its head, the more energy it builds up. It does this to prepare for battle.'),
    (1014, 'scarlet', 'After all its muscles were stimulated by the toxic chain around its neck, Okidogi transformed and gained a powerful physique.'),
    (1014, 'violet', 'Okidogi is a ruffian with a short temper. It can pulverize anything by swinging around the chain on its neck.'),
    (1015, 'scarlet', 'The chain is made from toxins that enhance capabilities. It stimulated Munkidori''s brain and caused the Pokémon''s psychic powers to bloom.'),
    (1015, 'violet', 'Munkidori keeps itself somewhere safe while it toys with its foes, using psychokinesis to induce intense dizziness.'),
    (1016, 'scarlet', 'Fezandipiti owes its beautiful looks and lovely voice to the toxic stimulants emanating from the chain wrapped around its body.'),
    (1016, 'violet', 'Fezandipiti beats its glossy wings to scatter pheromones that captivate people and Pokémon.'),
    (1017, 'scarlet', 'This {{OBP|Pokémon|species}}''s [[type]] changes based on which mask it''s wearing. It confounds its enemies with nimble movements and kicks.'),
    (1017, 'violet', 'This mischief-loving Pokémon is full of curiosity. It {{pkmn|battle}}s by drawing out the type-based energy contained within its masks.'),
    (1018, 'scarlet', 'It gathers static electricity from its surroundings. The beams it launches when down on all fours are tremendously powerful.'),
    (1018, 'violet', 'It digs holes on mountains, searching for food. It’s so durable that being caught in a cave-in won’t faze it.'),
    (1019, 'scarlet', 'Seven syrpents live inside an apple made of syrup. The syrpent in the center is the commander.'),
    (1019, 'violet', 'These capricious syrpents have banded together. On the rare occasion that their moods align, their true power is unleashed.'),
    (1020, 'scarlet', 'There are scant few reports of this creature being sighted. One short video shows it rampaging and spouting pillars of flame.'),
    (1020, 'violet', 'It resembles an eerie Pokémon once shown in a paranormal magazine. That Pokémon was said to be an Entei regenerated from a fossil.'),
    (1021, 'scarlet', 'It''s said to incinerate everything around it with lightning launched from its fur. Very little is known about this creature.'),
    (1021, 'violet', 'It bears resemblance to a Pokémon that became a hot topic for a short while after a paranormal magazine touted it as Raikou''s ancestor.'),
    (1022, 'scarlet', 'It resembles a Pokémon described in a dubious magazine as a Terrakion that had been modified by an evil organization.'),
    (1022, 'violet', 'It was named after a mysterious object recorded in an old book. Its body seems to be metallic.'),
    (1023, 'scarlet', 'It resembles a mysterious object introduced in a paranormal magazine as a cutting-edge weapon shaped like a Cobalion.'),
    (1023, 'violet', 'There was supposedly an incident in which it launched shining blades to cut everything around it to pieces. Little else is known about it.'),
    (1024, 'scarlet', 'Terapagos protects itself using its power to transform energy into hard crystals. This {{OBP|Pokémon|species}} is the source of the [[Terastal phenomenon]].'),
    (1024, 'violet', 'It''s thought that this Pokémon lived in ancient [[Paldea]] until it got caught in seismic shifts and went extinct.'),
    (1025, 'scarlet', 'It feeds others toxic mochi that draw out desires and capabilities. Those who eat the mochi fall under Pecharunt’s control, chained to its will.'),
    (1025, 'violet', 'Its peach-shaped shell serves as storage for a potent poison. It makes poisonous mochi and serves them to people and Pokémon.'),
    (10001, 'firered', 'This Deoxys has transformed into its aggressive guise. It can fool enemies by altering its appearance.'),
    (10002, 'leafgreen', 'When it changes form, an aurora appears. It absorbs attacks by altering its cellular structure.'),
    (10003, 'alpha-sapphire', 'Deoxys emerged from a virus that came from space. It is highly intelligent and wields psychokinetic powers. This Pokémon shoots lasers from the crystalline organ on its chest.'),
    (10003, 'black', 'An alien virus that fell to earth on a meteor underwent a DNA mutation to become this Pokémon.'),
    (10003, 'black-2', 'An alien virus that fell to earth on a meteor underwent a DNA mutation to become this Pokémon.'),
    (10003, 'brilliant-diamond', 'An alien virus that fell to earth on a meteorite underwent a DNA mutation to become this Pokémon.'),
    (10003, 'diamond', 'An alien virus that fell to earth on a meteor underwent a DNA mutation to become this Pokémon.'),
    (10003, 'emerald', 'A {{ScPkmn}} that mutated from an extraterrestrial virus exposed to a laser beam. Its body is configured for superior agility and speed.'),
    (10003, 'heartgold', 'DNA from a space virus mutated and became a Pokémon. It appears where auroras are seen.'),
    (10003, 'omega-ruby', 'The DNA of a space virus underwent a sudden mutation upon exposure to a laser beam and resulted in Deoxys. The crystalline organ on this Pokémon''s chest appears to be its brain.'),
    (10003, 'pearl', 'An alien virus that fell to earth on a meteor underwent a DNA mutation to become this Pokémon.'),
    (10003, 'platinum', 'An alien virus that fell to earth on a meteor underwent a DNA mutation to become this Pokémon.'),
    (10003, 'shining-pearl', 'An alien virus that fell to earth on a meteorite underwent a DNA mutation to become this Pokémon.'),
    (10003, 'soulsilver', 'DNA from a space virus mutated and became a Pokémon. It appears where auroras are seen.'),
    (10003, 'white', 'An alien virus that fell to earth on a meteor underwent a DNA mutation to become this Pokémon.'),
    (10003, 'white-2', 'An alien virus that fell to earth on a meteor underwent a DNA mutation to become this Pokémon.'),
    (10003, 'x', 'An alien virus that fell to earth on a meteor underwent a DNA mutation to become this Pokémon.'),
    (10003, 'y', 'DNA from a space virus mutated and became a Pokémon. It appears where auroras are seen.'),
    (10004, 'legends-arceus', 'Its earthen skin is reasonably hard—it has no problem repelling a Starly''s pecking, at least.'),
    (10005, 'legends-arceus', 'Its body, composed of refuse, blends in to the scenery so much as to be inconspicuous. This seems to be the perfect way for the Pokémon to evade the detection of predators.'),
    (10006, 'legends-arceus', 'Upon taking in the scent of a particular rare flower, Shaymin is enveloped in light, and its tiny body transforms. I took a whiff of the flower myself, but alas, my body remained unchanged.'),
    (10007, 'legends-arceus', 'Giratina loses its legs upon changing into this form. I believe this Pokémon must hail from a world where the heavens and the earth are as one, though I have no way of proving it.'),
    (10008, 'legends-arceus', 'A form in which Rotom lurks within a strange cauldron. The cauldron''s origin is unknown. A bothersome Pokémon, causing trouble with the flames it spits.'),
    (10008, 'legends-za', 'This Rotom has possessed a convection microwave oven that uses a special motor. It has a flair for manipulating flames.'),
    (10008, 'scarlet', 'If the convection microwave oven is not working properly, then the Rotom inhabiting it will become lethargic.'),
    (10008, 'shield', 'This form of Rotom enjoys making mischief by turning up the heat. It will gleefully burn your favorite outfit.'),
    (10008, 'sword', 'This Rotom has possessed a convection microwave oven that uses a special motor. It also has a flair for manipulating flames.'),
    (10008, 'violet', 'This Rotom has possessed a convection microwave oven. It will sear the surrounding area with its burning heat, then smile in delight.'),
    (10009, 'legends-arceus', 'A form in which Rotom lurks within an odd bureau. The bureau''s purpose is unknown. A bothersome Pokémon, causing trouble by splashing cold water everywhere.'),
    (10009, 'legends-za', 'This Rotom has possessed a washing machine that uses a special motor. It blasts out water to intimidate opponents.'),
    (10009, 'scarlet', 'This Rotom has entered a washing machine. It nods with satisfaction after it floods the surrounding area.'),
    (10009, 'shield', 'This Rotom has possessed a washing machine that uses a special motor. It blasts out water to get enemies to back down.'),
    (10009, 'sword', 'This form of Rotom enjoys coming up with water-based pranks. Be careful with it if you don''t want your room flooded.'),
    (10009, 'violet', 'The model of washing machine that Rotom can inspirit has been discontinued, so these appliances are now traded at high prices.'),
    (10010, 'legends-arceus', 'A form in which Rotom lurks within a bizarre cupboard. The cupboard''s composition is unknown. A bothersome Pokémon, causing trouble by frosting everything over.'),
    (10010, 'legends-za', 'This Rotom has possessed a refrigerator that uses a special motor. It battles by spewing cold air.'),
    (10010, 'scarlet', 'This Rotom has entered a refrigerator. It leaps around gleefully after it uses cold air to freeze the area around it.'),
    (10010, 'shield', 'When it''s like this, Rotom likes to play pranks that are freezing cold. You may find it''s turned the bath you just filled to solid ice!'),
    (10010, 'sword', 'Rotom assumes this form when it takes over a refrigerator powered by a special motor. It battles by spewing cold air.'),
    (10010, 'violet', 'The special motor within the refrigerator is the key to bringing about Rotom''s change in form.'),
    (10011, 'legends-arceus', 'A form in which Rotom lurks within a mysterious contraption. The contraption''s purpose is unknown. A bothersome Pokémon, causing trouble by stirring up powerful winds.'),
    (10011, 'legends-za', 'This Rotom has possessed an electric fan that uses a special motor. It sends its enemies flying with gusts of wind.'),
    (10011, 'scarlet', 'This Rotom has entered an electric fan. It smirks with satisfaction over a prank well pulled after it blows away everything around it.'),
    (10011, 'shield', 'This Rotom has taken over a fan that has a special motor. Its gusts of wind blow its opponents away!'),
    (10011, 'sword', 'In this form, Rotom applies its new power over wind to its love of pranks. It will happily blow away any important documents it can find.'),
    (10011, 'violet', 'There are several appliances that Rotom can inspirit, but the first one to be developed was the electric fan.'),
    (10012, 'legends-arceus', 'A form in which Rotom lurks within a misshapen wheelbarrow. The wheelbarrow''s mechanisms are bizarre. It''s a bothersome Pokémon, causing trouble by mowing down grass and trees.'),
    (10012, 'legends-za', 'This Rotom has possessed a lawn mower that uses a special motor. As it mows down grass, it scatters the clippings everywhere.'),
    (10012, 'scarlet', 'The lawn mower is one of the household appliances that led to the development of the Rotom Dex.'),
    (10012, 'shield', 'In this form, Rotom focuses its antics on plants. Any flowers you were growing are going to get mowed down.'),
    (10012, 'sword', 'This is Rotom after it''s seized control of a lawn mower that has a special motor. As it mows down grass, it scatters the clippings everywhere.'),
    (10012, 'violet', 'This Rotom has possessed a lawn mower. It will mow down grass and flowers, then swagger around with pride at its accomplishments.'),
    (10013, 'moon', 'This is Castform''s form when basking in fair weather. Its body is warm and toasty.'),
    (10013, 'sun', 'This is the form Castform takes on the brightest of days. Its skin is unexpectedly hot to the touch, so approach with care.'),
    (10013, 'ultra-moon', 'Castform changes to this form when it basks in bright sunlight. When you touch its glowing skin, it feels all dried out!'),
    (10013, 'ultra-sun', 'This is the form Castform takes on bright days. In an experiment where Castform was placed in front of a heater, it didn''t change to this form.'),
    (10014, 'moon', 'This is Castform''s form during a downpour of rain. Its body retains moisture and gets slippery.'),
    (10014, 'sun', 'This is the form Castform takes when soaked with rain. When its body is compressed, water will seep out as if from a sponge.'),
    (10014, 'ultra-moon', 'This is Castform''s form when pelted by rain. In an experiment where it was placed in a shower, this Pokémon didn''t change to this form.'),
    (10014, 'ultra-sun', 'Castform changes to this form when rain hits it. Its body is soft and slightly swollen with water.'),
    (10015, 'brilliant-diamond', 'Its appearance changes with the weather. Recently, its molecules were found to be just like water.'),
    (10015, 'moon', 'This is Castform''s form when caught in a hailstorm. Its cold skin is as smooth as ice.'),
    (10015, 'shining-pearl', 'Its appearance changes with the weather. Recently, its molecules were found to be just like water.'),
    (10015, 'sun', 'This is the form Castform takes when covered in snow. Its body becomes an ice-like material, with a temperature near 23 degrees Fahrenheit.'),
    (10015, 'ultra-moon', 'This is Castform''s form when caught in a hailstorm. Its whole body is chilled, and its skin is partially frozen!'),
    (10015, 'ultra-sun', 'This is the form Castform takes when hit by hail. In an experiment where it was placed in a freezer, it didn''t change to this form.'),
    (10016, 'scarlet', 'These Pokémon form schools with others of the same color. The greatest foe of a school of blue Basculin is a school of red Basculin.'),
    (10016, 'shield', 'Known for their violence, these Pokémon have the most fights with schools of red-striped Basculin.'),
    (10016, 'sword', 'Blue-striped Basculin used to be a common food source. They apparently have an inoffensive, light flavor.'),
    (10016, 'ultra-moon', 'Some people call it “the thug of the lake.” Whether the differences in color are meaningful is not yet known.'),
    (10016, 'ultra-sun', 'Even Basculin, which devours everything it can with its huge jaws, is nothing more than food to organisms stronger than itself.'),
    (10016, 'violet', 'The power of its jaws is immense—enough to leave teeth marks in iron sheets. Its personality is also extremely vicious.'),
    (10017, 'shield', 'When wounded, it stops moving. It goes as still as stone to meditate, sharpening its mind and spirit.'),
    (10017, 'sword', 'Through meditation, it calms its raging spirit and hones its psychic powers.'),
    (10018, 'legends-za', 'Now that it has reclaimed a long-forgotten song, Meloetta captivates everyone with its enchanting dance steps.'),
    (10019, 'legends-arceus', 'An example of what is known as a “form change,” though I suspect this strange avian guise to be Tornadus''s true form. Tornadus has been sighted crossing the ocean while in this form.'),
    (10020, 'legends-arceus', 'Quick as a flash, it materializes out of nowhere. It pulverizes foes into nothingness with showers of devastatingly powerful lightning bolts launched from the string of orbs on its tail.'),
    (10021, 'legends-arceus', 'Landorus soars through the sky in this form, bestowing plentiful harvests upon the land and earning the people''s reverence. It can traverse the whole of Hisui in a mere couple of hours.'),
    (10022, 'shield', 'The sameness of Zekrom''s and Kyurem''s genes allowed Kyurem to absorb Zekrom. Kyurem can now use the power of both electricity and ice.*'),
    (10022, 'sword', 'It''s said that this Pokémon battles in order to protect the ideal world that will exist in the future for people and Pokémon.*'),
    (10023, 'shield', 'It has foreseen that a world of truth will arrive for people and Pokémon. It strives to protect that future.*'),
    (10023, 'sword', 'The sameness of Reshiram''s and Kyurem''s genes allowed Kyurem to absorb Reshiram. Kyurem can now use the power of both fire and ice.*'),
    (10024, 'legends-za', 'Keldeo''s magnificent horn is proof of its resolve. Its allies provided guidance, and their hopes became Keldeo''s tricolored plume of feathers.'),
    (10024, 'shield', 'The power that lay hidden in its body now covers its horn, turning it into a sword that can slice through anything.*'),
    (10024, 'sword', 'Keldeo has strengthened its resolve for battle, filling its body with power and changing its form.*'),
    (10025, 'legends-za', 'Females are a bit more selfish and aggressive than males. If they don''t get what they want, they will torment you with their psychic abilities.'),
    (10025, 'scarlet', 'Female Meowstic are more aggressive than males. Their expression remains blank even while they''re wielding immense psychic power.'),
    (10025, 'shield', 'If it doesn''t hold back when it unleashes its psychic power, it can tear apart a tanker. Its unfriendliness is part of its charm.'),
    (10025, 'sword', 'Females are a bit more selfish and aggressive than males. If they don''t get what they want, they will torment you with their psychic abilities.'),
    (10025, 'violet', 'When they sense danger, they exert their psychic power at its maximum output. They have no regard for their opponents.'),
    (10026, 'legends-za', 'This stance is dedicated to offense. It can cleave any opponent with the strength and weight of its steel blade.'),
    (10026, 'shield', 'Once upon a time, a king with an Aegislash reigned over the land. His Pokémon eventually drained him of life, and his kingdom fell with him.'),
    (10026, 'sword', 'This stance is dedicated to offense. It can cleave any opponent with the strength and weight of its steel blade.'),
    (10033, 'brilliant-diamond', 'After a rainy day, the flower on its back smells stronger. The scent attracts other Pokémon.'),
    (10033, 'legends-za', 'In order to support its flower, which has grown larger due to Mega Evolution, its back and legs have become stronger.'),
    (10033, 'shield', 'A bewitching aroma wafts from its flower. The fragrance becalms those engaged in a battle.'),
    (10033, 'shining-pearl', 'After a rainy day, the flower on its back smells stronger. The scent attracts other Pokémon.'),
    (10033, 'sword', 'Its plant blooms when it is absorbing solar energy. It stays on the move to seek sunlight.'),
    (10034, 'legends-za', 'The overwhelming power that fills its entire body causes it to turn black and creates intense blue flames.'),
    (10035, 'brilliant-diamond', 'It is said that Charizard''s fire burns hotter if it has experienced harsh battles.'),
    (10035, 'legends-za', 'Its bond with its Trainer is the source of its power. It boasts speed and maneuverability greater than that of a jet.'),
    (10035, 'shield', 'Its wings can carry this Pokémon close to an altitude of 4,600 feet. It blows out fire at very high temperatures.'),
    (10035, 'shining-pearl', 'It is said that Charizard''s fire burns hotter if it has experienced harsh battles.'),
    (10035, 'sword', 'It spits fire that is hot enough to melt boulders. It may cause forest fires by blowing flames.'),
    (10036, 'brilliant-diamond', 'The jets of water it spouts from the rocket cannons on its shell can punch through thick steel.'),
    (10036, 'legends-za', 'The cannon on its back is as powerful as a tank gun. Its tough legs and back enable it to withstand the recoil from firing the cannon.'),
    (10036, 'shield', 'The rocket cannons on its shell fire jets of water capable of punching holes through thick steel.'),
    (10036, 'shining-pearl', 'The jets of water it spouts from the rocket cannons on its shell can punch through thick steel.'),
    (10036, 'sword', 'It crushes its foe under its heavy body to cause fainting. In a pinch, it will withdraw inside its shell.'),
    (10037, 'brilliant-diamond', 'Its superb memory lets it recall everything it has experienced from birth. Its IQ exceeds 5,000.'),
    (10037, 'legends-arceus', 'The longer Alakazam lives, the larger and heavier its head becomes. Our tests have shown that the strength of its psychic powers correlates positively to the weight of its head.'),
    (10037, 'legends-za', 'Alakazam has traded away its muscles, unleashing its true power. With its psychic powers, it can foresee all things.'),
    (10037, 'legends-za', 'Its brain cells multiply continually until it dies. As a result, it remembers everything.'),
    (10037, 'moon', 'Its hidden psychic power has been unleashed. A glance at someone gives it knowledge of the course of that person''s life, from birth to death.'),
    (10037, 'shield', 'Alakazam wields potent psychic powers. It''s said that this Pokémon used these powers to create the spoons it holds.'),
    (10037, 'shining-pearl', 'Its highly developed brain is on par with a supercomputer. It can use all forms of psychic abilities.'),
    (10037, 'sun', 'As a result of Mega Evolution, its power has been entirely converted into psychic energy, and it has lost all strength in its muscles.'),
    (10037, 'sword', 'It has an incredibly high level of intelligence. Some say that Alakazam remembers everything that ever happens to it, from birth till death.'),
    (10037, 'ultra-moon', 'Having traded away its muscles, Alakazam''s true power has been unleashed. With its psychic powers, it can foresee all things.'),
    (10037, 'ultra-sun', 'It sends out psychic power from the red organ on its forehead to foresee its opponents'' every move.'),
    (10038, 'brilliant-diamond', 'It hides in shadows. It is said that in rooms where Gengar is hiding, the temperature drops by nearly 10 degrees Fahrenheit.'),
    (10038, 'legends-arceus', 'Possesses potential victims'' shadows in an effort to steal away the victims'' lives. If your shadow begins to laugh, you must take hold of a protective charm posthaste!'),
    (10038, 'legends-za', 'It can pass through other dimensions and appear anywhere. It caused a stir one time when it stuck just one leg out of a wall.'),
    (10038, 'moon', 'The energy of Mega Evolution awakened it. It sinks into another dimension, where it keeps a patient watch for its chance to attack.'),
    (10038, 'shield', 'It is said to emerge from darkness to steal the lives of those who become lost in mountains.'),
    (10038, 'shining-pearl', 'Lurking in the shadowy corners of rooms, it awaits chances to steal its prey''s life-force.'),
    (10038, 'sun', 'Gengar''s relationships are warped. It has no interest in opponents unless it perceives them as prey.'),
    (10038, 'sword', 'On the night of a full moon, if shadows move on their own and laugh, it must be Gengar''s doing.'),
    (10038, 'ultra-moon', 'Mega Evolution has made it possible for Gengar to access other dimensions. Its entire body is brimming with strange power.'),
    (10038, 'ultra-sun', 'It tries to take the lives of anyone and everyone. It will even try to curse the Trainer who is its master!'),
    (10039, 'brilliant-diamond', 'It raises its offspring in its belly pouch. It lets its baby out to play only when it feels safe to do so.'),
    (10039, 'legends-za', 'Its child has grown rapidly, thanks to the energy of Mega Evolution. Mother and child show off their harmonious teamwork in battle.'),
    (10039, 'legends-za', 'It raises its offspring in its belly pouch. It lets its baby out to play only when it feels safe to do so.'),
    (10039, 'moon', 'Thanks to Mega Evolution, its child grows. But as the child is good only at fighting and nothing else, its mother feels uneasy about its future.'),
    (10039, 'shield', 'There are records of a lost human child being raised by a childless Kangaskhan.'),
    (10039, 'shining-pearl', 'It raises its offspring in its belly pouch. It lets its baby out to play only when it feels safe to do so.'),
    (10039, 'sun', 'Mega Kangaskhan''s strength derives from the mother''s happiness about her child''s growth. Watching it grow up keeps her spirits high.'),
    (10039, 'sword', 'Although it''s carrying its baby in a pouch on its belly, Kangaskhan is swift on its feet. It intimidates its opponents with quick jabs.'),
    (10039, 'ultra-moon', 'When the mother sees the back of her Mega-Evolved child, it makes her think of the day when her child will inevitably leave her.'),
    (10039, 'ultra-sun', 'The explosive energy the child is bathed in causes temporary growth. The mother is beside herself with worry about it.'),
    (10040, 'brilliant-diamond', 'It grips prey with its pincers until the prey is torn apart. What it can''t tear, it tosses far away.'),
    (10040, 'legends-za', 'It swings its long pincers wildly to attack. During cold periods, it hides deep in forests.'),
    (10040, 'legends-za', 'After Mega Evolution, it becomes able to fly. Perhaps because it''s so happy, it rarely touches the ground.'),
    (10040, 'moon', 'Bathed in the energy of Mega Evolution, its wings become unusually developed. It flies at speeds of approximately 30 mph.'),
    (10040, 'shield', 'This Pokémon clamps its pincers down on its prey and then either splits the prey in half or flings it away.'),
    (10040, 'shining-pearl', 'It grips prey with its pincers until the prey is torn apart. What it can''t tear, it tosses far away.'),
    (10040, 'sun', 'The influence of Mega Evolution leaves it in a state of constant excitement. It pierces enemies with its two large horns before shredding them.'),
    (10040, 'sword', 'These Pokémon judge one another based on pincers. Thicker, more impressive pincers make for more popularity with the opposite gender.'),
    (10040, 'ultra-moon', 'It zips around at blistering speeds, looking for an opening to skewer its opponent on its giant pincers.'),
    (10040, 'ultra-sun', 'After Mega Evolution, it becomes able to fly. Perhaps because it''s so happy, it rarely touches the ground.'),
    (10041, 'brilliant-diamond', 'Once Gyarados appears, its rage never settles until the Pokémon has razed the fields and mountains around it.'),
    (10041, 'legends-arceus', 'I suspect this Pokémon to be the true identity of a dragon written of in ancient texts, which claimed that it razed an entire village with white-hot beams from its maw.'),
    (10041, 'legends-za', 'In ancient literature, there is a record of a Gyarados that razed a village when violence flared.'),
    (10041, 'legends-za', 'It jets water from the orifices on its sides, streaking above the water surface at supersonic speed.'),
    (10041, 'moon', 'It jets water from the orifices on its sides, streaking above the water surface at supersonic speed.'),
    (10041, 'scarlet', 'Once it appears, it goes on a rampage. It remains enraged until it demolishes everything around it.'),
    (10041, 'shield', 'Once it begins to rampage, a Gyarados will burn everything down, even in a harsh storm.'),
    (10041, 'shining-pearl', 'In ancient literature, there is a record of a Gyarados that razed a village when violence flared.'),
    (10041, 'sun', 'Mega Evolution also affects its brain, leaving no other function except its destructive instinct to burn everything to cinders.'),
    (10041, 'sword', 'It has an extremely aggressive nature. The Hyper Beam it shoots from its mouth totally incinerates all targets.'),
    (10041, 'ultra-moon', 'It zooms out of the water at Mach speeds. Even large ships caught in its path are split cleanly in two!'),
    (10041, 'ultra-sun', 'Mega Evolution places a burden on its body. The stress causes it to become all the more ferocious.'),
    (10041, 'violet', 'It appears whenever there is world conflict, burning down any place it travels through.'),
    (10042, 'brilliant-diamond', 'It''s a Pokémon that roamed the skies in the dinosaur era. Its teeth are like saw blades.'),
    (10042, 'legends-za', 'It was regenerated from a pterosaur''s genetic matter that was found in amber. It flies with high- pitched cries.'),
    (10042, 'legends-za', 'Parts of its body have become stone. Some scholars claim that this is Aerodactyl''s true appearance.'),
    (10042, 'moon', 'When it Mega Evolves, it becomes more vicious than ever before. Some say that''s because its excess of power is causing it pain.'),
    (10042, 'shield', 'Aerodactyl''s sawlike fangs can shred skin to tatters—even the skin of Steel-type Pokémon.'),
    (10042, 'shining-pearl', 'It''s a Pokémon that roamed the skies in the dinosaur era. Its teeth are like saw blades.'),
    (10042, 'sun', 'Part of its body has become stone. Some scholars claim that this is Aerodactyl''s true appearance.'),
    (10042, 'sword', 'This is a ferocious Pokémon from ancient times. Apparently even modern technology is incapable of producing a perfectly restored specimen.'),
    (10042, 'ultra-moon', 'Mega Evolution awakened some dormant genes, bringing back the sharp rocks that once covered Aerodactyl''s entire body.'),
    (10042, 'ultra-sun', 'It will attack anything that moves. Mega Evolution is a burden on its body, so it''s incredibly irritated.'),
    (10043, 'legends-za', 'Psychic power has augmented its muscles. It has a grip strength of one ton and can sprint 100 meters in two seconds flat!'),
    (10044, 'brilliant-diamond', 'Mewtwo was created by recombining Mew''s genes. It''s said to have the most savage heart among Pokémon.'),
    (10044, 'legends-za', 'It was created by a scientist after years of horrific gene-splicing and DNA-engineering experiments.'),
    (10044, 'legends-za', 'Despite its diminished size, its mental power has grown phenomenally. With a mere thought, it can smash a skyscraper to smithereens.'),
    (10044, 'shield', 'The research efforts of [[Mr. Fuji|a certain scientist]] ultimately resulted in this Pokémon. Its powers are dedicated to battling.*'),
    (10044, 'shining-pearl', 'Mewtwo was created by recombining Mew''s genes. It''s said to have the most savage heart among Pokémon.'),
    (10044, 'sword', 'Created from the DNA of Mew, this Pokémon is a dangerous combination of overwhelming power and a savage heart.*'),
    (10045, 'brilliant-diamond', 'The tip of its tail shines brightly. In the olden days, people sent signals using the light from this Pokémon''s tail.'),
    (10045, 'legends-za', 'Massive amounts of energy intensely stimulated Ampharos''s cells, apparently awakening its long-sleeping dragon''s blood.'),
    (10045, 'legends-za', 'The tail''s tip shines brightly and can be seen from far away. It acts as a beacon for lost people.'),
    (10045, 'scarlet', 'The bright light on its tail can be seen far away. It has been treasured since ancient times as a beacon.'),
    (10045, 'shining-pearl', 'The tip of its tail shines brightly. In the olden days, people sent signals using the light from this Pokémon''s tail.'),
    (10045, 'ultra-moon', 'Massive amounts of energy intensely stimulated Ampharos''s cells, apparently awakening its long-sleeping dragon''s blood.'),
    (10045, 'ultra-sun', 'Excess energy from Mega Evolution stimulates its genes, and the wool it had lost grows in again.'),
    (10045, 'violet', 'When it gets dark, the light from its bright, shiny tail can be seen from far away on the ocean''s surface.'),
    (10046, 'brilliant-diamond', 'It has a steel-hard body. It intimidates foes by upraising its eye-patterned pincers.'),
    (10046, 'legends-arceus', 'Evolved by way of [[Metal Coat|a curious item]]. The shell covering its body has been shown to be stronger than forged steel.'),
    (10046, 'legends-za', 'Due to the effects of Mega Evolution, its pincers have taken on a more diabolical form, ripping anything they pinch to shreds.'),
    (10046, 'legends-za', 'It has a steel-hard body. It intimidates foes by upraising its eye-patterned pincers.'),
    (10046, 'moon', 'Due to the effects of Mega Evolution, its pincers have taken on a more diabolical form, ripping anything they pinch to shreds.'),
    (10046, 'scarlet', 'This Pokémon’s pincers, which contain steel, can crush any hard object they get ahold of into bits.'),
    (10046, 'shield', 'Though its body is slim, Scizor has tremendous attacking power. Even Scizor''s muscles are made of metal.'),
    (10046, 'shining-pearl', 'It has a steel-hard body. It intimidates foes by upraising its eye-patterned pincers.'),
    (10046, 'sun', 'The excess energy that bathes this Pokémon keeps it in constant danger of overflow. It can''t sustain a battle over long periods of time.'),
    (10046, 'sword', 'Bulky pincers account for one third of Scizor''s body weight. A single swing of one of these pincers will crush a boulder completely.'),
    (10046, 'ultra-moon', 'It''s better at beating things than grasping them. When it battles for a long time, the weight of its pincers becomes too much to bear.'),
    (10046, 'ultra-sun', 'It stores the excess energy from Mega Evolution, so after a long time passes, its body starts to melt.'),
    (10046, 'violet', 'It swings its eye-patterned pincers up to scare its foes. This makes it look like it has three heads.'),
    (10047, 'brilliant-diamond', 'It gathers in forests to search for tree sap, its favorite food. It''s strong enough to hurl foes.'),
    (10047, 'legends-arceus', 'This Pokémon has an unparalleled horn. Heracross itself demonstrates tremendous power—it''s capable of throwing several people trained in the traditional arts of war at once.'),
    (10047, 'legends-za', 'This powerful Pokémon thrusts its prized horn under its enemies'' bellies, then lifts and throws them.'),
    (10047, 'legends-za', 'It can grip things with its two horns and lift 500 times its own body weight.'),
    (10047, 'scarlet', 'It loves sweet nectar. To keep all the nectar to itself, it hurls rivals away with its prized horn.'),
    (10047, 'shield', 'This Pokémon takes pride in its strength, which allows it to lift things 100 times heavier than itself with no trouble at all.'),
    (10047, 'shining-pearl', 'Its powerful legs and claws give it enough power to hurl foes over great distances.'),
    (10047, 'sword', 'Heracross loves sweet sap and will go looking through forests for it. The Pokémon uses its two antennae to pick up scents as it searches.'),
    (10047, 'ultra-moon', 'A tremendous influx of energy builds it up, but when Mega Evolution ends, Heracross is bothered by terrible soreness in its muscles.'),
    (10047, 'ultra-sun', 'It can grip things with its two horns and lift 500 times its own body weight.'),
    (10047, 'violet', 'With its herculean powers, it can easily throw around an object that is 100 times its own weight.'),
    (10048, 'brilliant-diamond', 'Long ago, people imagined its eerie howls to be the call of the grim reaper.'),
    (10048, 'legends-za', 'Houndoom''s entire body generates heat when it Mega Evolves. Its intense, fiery breath turns its opponents to charcoal.'),
    (10048, 'legends-za', 'The flames it breathes when angry contain toxins. If they cause a burn, it will hurt forever.'),
    (10048, 'scarlet', 'If you are burned by the flames it shoots from its mouth, the pain will never go away.'),
    (10048, 'shining-pearl', 'Long ago, people imagined its eerie howls to be the call of the grim reaper.'),
    (10048, 'ultra-moon', 'Houndoom''s entire body generates heat when it Mega Evolves. Its fearsome fiery breath turns its opponents to ash.'),
    (10048, 'ultra-sun', 'Its red claws and the tips of its tail are melting from high internal temperatures that are painful to Houndoom itself.'),
    (10048, 'violet', 'Upon hearing its eerie howls, other Pokémon get the shivers and head straight back to their nests.'),
    (10049, 'brilliant-diamond', 'If it rampages, it knocks down mountains and buries rivers. Maps must be redrawn afterward.'),
    (10049, 'legends-za', 'The effects of Mega Evolution make it more ferocious than ever. It''s unclear whether it can even hear its Trainer''s orders.'),
    (10049, 'legends-za', 'If it rampages, it knocks down mountains and buries rivers. Maps must be redrawn afterward.'),
    (10049, 'scarlet', 'Extremely strong, it can change the landscape. It is so insolent that it doesn''t care about others.'),
    (10049, 'shield', 'The quakes caused when it walks make even great mountains crumble and change the surrounding terrain.'),
    (10049, 'shining-pearl', 'If it rampages, it knocks down mountains and buries rivers. Maps must be redrawn afterward.'),
    (10049, 'sword', 'Its body can''t be harmed by any sort of attack, so it is very eager to make challenges against enemies.'),
    (10049, 'ultra-moon', 'The effects of Mega Evolution make it more ferocious than ever. It''s unclear whether it can even hear its Trainer''s orders.'),
    (10049, 'ultra-sun', 'Due to the colossal power poured into it, this Pokémon''s back split right open. Its destructive instincts are the only thing keeping it moving.'),
    (10049, 'violet', 'In just one of its mighty hands, it has the power to make the ground shake and mountains crumble.'),
    (10050, 'legends-za', 'Boiling-hot blood courses through its entire body, doubling the sharpness of its moves. It subdues opponents in the blink of an eye.'),
    (10051, 'legends-za', 'When it opens the red plate on its chest and unleashes its heart, its strongest psychic power is released.'),
    (10052, 'brilliant-diamond', 'Attached to its head is a huge set of jaws formed by horns. It can chew through iron beams.'),
    (10052, 'legends-za', 'Attached to its head is a huge set of jaws formed by horns. It can chew through iron beams.'),
    (10052, 'legends-za', 'Its two sets of jaws thrash about violently as if they each had a will of their own. One gnash from them can turn a boulder to dust.'),
    (10052, 'shield', 'It chomps with its gaping mouth. Its huge jaws are actually steel horns that have been transformed.'),
    (10052, 'shining-pearl', 'Attached to its head is a huge set of jaws formed by horns. It can chew through iron beams.'),
    (10052, 'sword', 'It uses its docile-looking face to lull foes into complacency, then bites with its huge, relentless jaws.'),
    (10052, 'ultra-moon', 'Its two sets of jaws thrash about violently as if they each had a will of their own. One gnash from them can turn a boulder to dust.'),
    (10052, 'ultra-sun', 'It has an extremely vicious disposition. It grips prey in its two sets of jaws and tears them apart with raw power.'),
    (10053, 'legends-za', 'Energy from Mega Evolution has turned the iron inside this Pokémon into steel armor that covers Mega Aggron''s whole body.'),
    (10054, 'legends-za', 'Thanks to Mega Evolution, its mental power is limitless. It conjures up arms imbued with malice to defeat its enemies.'),
    (10055, 'brilliant-diamond', 'It discharges electricity from its mane. The Pokémon creates a thundercloud overhead from which to drop lightning bolts.'),
    (10055, 'legends-za', 'Mega Evolution fills its body with a tremendous amount of electricity, but it''s too much for Manectric to fully control.'),
    (10055, 'legends-za', 'It discharges electricity from its mane. The Pokémon creates a thundercloud overhead from which to drop lightning bolts.'),
    (10055, 'shield', 'It rarely appears before people. It is said to nest where lightning has fallen.'),
    (10055, 'shining-pearl', 'It discharges electricity from its mane. The Pokémon creates a thundercloud overhead from which to drop lightning bolts.'),
    (10055, 'sword', 'It stimulates its own muscles with electricity, so it can move quickly. It eases its soreness with electricity, too, so it can recover quickly as well.'),
    (10055, 'ultra-moon', 'Too much electricity has built up in its body, irritating Manectric. Its explosive speed is equal to that of a lightning bolt.'),
    (10055, 'ultra-sun', 'Mega Evolution fills its body with a tremendous amount of electricity, but it''s too much for Manectric to fully control.'),
    (10056, 'brilliant-diamond', 'A doll bore a grudge over being junked, and it became a Pokémon. It seeks the child that disowned it.'),
    (10056, 'legends-za', 'Mega Evolution increases its vindictiveness, and the cursing power that was held back by its zipper comes spilling out.'),
    (10056, 'legends-za', 'A doll bore a grudge over being junked, and it became a Pokémon. It seeks the child that disowned it.'),
    (10056, 'scarlet', 'This Pokémon developed from an abandoned doll that amassed a grudge. It is seen in dark alleys.'),
    (10056, 'shining-pearl', 'A doll bore a grudge over being junked, and it became a Pokémon. It seeks the child that disowned it.'),
    (10056, 'ultra-moon', 'Mega Evolution increases its vindictiveness, and the cursing power that was held back by its zipper comes spilling out.'),
    (10056, 'ultra-sun', 'Extraordinary energy amplifies its cursing power to such an extent that it can''t help but curse its own Trainer.'),
    (10056, 'violet', 'Strong feelings of hatred turned a puppet into a Pokémon. If it opens its mouth, its cursed energy escapes.'),
    (10057, 'brilliant-diamond', 'It senses coming disasters and appears before people only to warn them of impending danger.'),
    (10057, 'legends-za', 'When this Pokémon whips the winglike fur on its back as though beating its wings, it sends an intimidating aura flying at its opponents.'),
    (10057, 'legends-za', 'It senses coming disasters and appears before people only to warn them of impending danger.'),
    (10057, 'moon', 'As the energy of Mega Evolution fills it, its fur bristles. What you see on its back are not true wings, and this Pokémon isn''t able to fly.'),
    (10057, 'shield', 'Because of this Pokémon''s ability to detect danger, people mistook Absol as a bringer of doom.'),
    (10057, 'shining-pearl', 'It senses coming disasters and appears before people only to warn them of impending danger.'),
    (10057, 'sun', 'When this Pokémon whips the winglike fur on its back as though beating its wings, it sends an intimidating aura flying at its opponents.'),
    (10057, 'sword', 'Swift as the wind, Absol races through fields and mountains. Its curved, bow-like horn is acutely sensitive to the warning signs of natural disasters.'),
    (10057, 'ultra-moon', 'It converts the energy from Mega Evolution into an intimidating aura. Fainthearted people expire from shock at the sight of it.'),
    (10057, 'ultra-sun', 'Normally, it dislikes fighting, so it really hates changing to this form for battles.'),
    (10058, 'brilliant-diamond', 'When it folds up its body and extends its wings, it looks like a jet plane. It flies at sonic speed.'),
    (10058, 'legends-arceus', 'Soars across the heavens at blinding speed—a magnificent sight! It has a feral disposition. Utmost caution is required if one meets a Garchomp out in the wilds.'),
    (10058, 'legends-za', 'It flies at speeds equal to a jet fighter plane. It never allows its prey to escape.'),
    (10058, 'legends-za', 'Its disposition is more vicious than before its Mega Evolution. Garchomp carves its opponents up with the scythes on both arms.'),
    (10058, 'moon', 'Its vaunted wings become scythes, sending it mad with rage. It swings its scythes wildly and slices the ground to pieces.'),
    (10058, 'scarlet', 'It is said that when one runs at high speed, its wings create blades of wind that can fell nearby trees.'),
    (10058, 'shield', 'Garchomp is fast both underground and above. It can bring down prey and return to its den before its body has chilled from being outside.'),
    (10058, 'shining-pearl', 'It flies at speeds equal to a jet fighter plane. It never allows its prey to escape.'),
    (10058, 'sun', 'Excess energy melted its arms and wings, transforming them into giant scythes.'),
    (10058, 'sword', 'Garchomp makes its home in volcanic mountains. It flies through the sky as fast as a jet airplane, hunting down as much prey as it can.'),
    (10058, 'ultra-moon', 'Its disposition is more vicious than before its Mega Evolution. Garchomp carves its opponents up with the scythes on both arms.'),
    (10058, 'ultra-sun', 'Its arms and wings melted into something like scythes. Mad with rage, it rampages on and on.'),
    (10058, 'violet', 'The protuberances on its head serve as sensors. It can even detect distant prey.'),
    (10059, 'brilliant-diamond', 'It has the ability to sense the auras of all things. It understands human speech.'),
    (10059, 'legends-arceus', 'A most gallant-looking creature. It emits energy waves and controls them with precision, using them to sense even faraway beings. [[Professor Laventon|I]] have given the name “aura” to this power.'),
    (10059, 'legends-za', 'By reading the auras of all things, it can tell how others are feeling from over half a mile away.'),
    (10059, 'legends-za', 'Black streaks all over its body show where its auras and the energy of Mega Evolution intermingled and raced through it.'),
    (10059, 'moon', 'It readies itself to face its enemies by focusing its mental energies. Its fighting style can be summed up in a single word: heartless.'),
    (10059, 'scarlet', 'It’s said that no foe can remain invisible to Lucario, since it can detect auras—even those of foes it could not otherwise see.'),
    (10059, 'shield', 'It can tell what people are thinking. Only {{pkmn|Trainer}}s who have justice in their hearts can earn this {{OBP|Pokémon|species}}''s trust.'),
    (10059, 'shining-pearl', 'By sensing the aura emanating from others, it can read their thoughts and movements.'),
    (10059, 'sun', 'Black streaks all over its body show where its auras and the energy of Mega Evolution intermingled and raced through it.'),
    (10059, 'sword', 'It controls waves known as auras, which are powerful enough to pulverize huge rocks. It uses these waves to take down its prey.'),
    (10059, 'ultra-moon', 'Bathed in explosive energy, its combative instincts have awakened. For its enemies, it has no mercy whatsoever.'),
    (10059, 'ultra-sun', 'Its aura has expanded due to Mega Evolution. Governed only by its combative instincts, it strikes enemies without mercy.'),
    (10059, 'violet', 'A well-trained one can use its aura to identify and take in the feelings of creatures over half a mile away.'),
    (10060, 'legends-za', 'The buds on its back have sprouted into impressive icicles that can whip up massive blizzards of −22 degrees Fahrenheit.'),
    (10061, 'legends-za', 'This rare Floette holds a plant that died out in ancient times. The Pokémon is said to harbor an incredible power.'),
    (10061, 'ultra-moon', 'Terrifying energy is concealed within its ominous flower, but Floette still swings it about innocently.'),
    (10061, 'ultra-sun', 'The flower it''s holding can no longer be found blooming anywhere. It''s also thought to contain terrifying power.'),
    (10062, 'legends-za', 'Both its flying capabilities and its attack power have increased. It scatters transparent down to confuse its enemies.'),
    (10063, 'legends-za', 'It flies at speeds exceeding Mach 4. It is among the top tier of all Pokémon in terms of aerial combat capability.'),
    (10064, 'legends-za', 'The water within its body further strengthens its already enlarged muscles, using the same principles as a hydraulic pump.'),
    (10065, 'legends-za', 'The seeds on its back are filled with energy from Mega Evolution. The Pokémon detonates these seeds to launch the tip of its tail.'),
    (10066, 'brilliant-diamond', 'It hides in the darkness of caves. Its diet of gems has transformed its eyes into gemstones.'),
    (10066, 'legends-za', 'The jewel from its chest, which has grown gigantic due to the effects of Mega Evolution, can turn back any attack.'),
    (10066, 'legends-za', 'It hides in the darkness of caves. Its diet of gems has transformed its eyes into gemstones.'),
    (10066, 'moon', 'Supporting a giant heavy jewel, it can''t change direction very nimbly and is vulnerable to attack from behind.'),
    (10066, 'scarlet', 'It dwells in the darkness of caves. It uses its sharp claws to dig up gems to nourish itself.'),
    (10066, 'shield', 'It feeds on gemstone crystals. In darkness, its eyes sparkle with the glitter of jewels.'),
    (10066, 'shining-pearl', 'It hides in the darkness of caves. Its diet of gems has transformed its eyes into gemstones.'),
    (10066, 'sun', 'The jewel from its chest, which has grown gigantic due to the effects of Mega Evolution, can turn back any attack.'),
    (10066, 'sword', 'This Pokémon is feared. When its gemstone eyes begin to glow with a sinister shine, it''s believed that Sableye will steal people''s spirits away.'),
    (10066, 'ultra-moon', 'It blocks any and all attacks with its giant-sized gemstone. However, the stone''s a heavy burden, and it limits Mega Sableye''s movements.'),
    (10066, 'ultra-sun', 'Bathed in the energy of Mega Evolution, the gemstone on its chest expands, rips through its skin, and falls out.'),
    (10066, 'violet', 'Materials from gems it has eaten float to the surface of its body and can form an infinite number of patterns among individuals.'),
    (10067, 'legends-za', 'Its down is so soft, it seems as if a touch could melt it. But it''s strong enough that just a few strands could be used to hoist a dump truck.'),
    (10068, 'legends-za', 'It gets power from the bond it has with its Trainer. Mega Evolution has given it plates to slice its enemies and a cape to protect its body.'),
    (10069, 'legends-za', 'Anyone who touches the secondary feelers that have sprouted from the base of its throat will fall into a deep sleep.'),
    (10070, 'brilliant-diamond', 'Its fangs rip through sheet iron. It swims at 75 mph and is known as the Bully of the Sea.'),
    (10070, 'legends-za', 'The spines sprouting from its head are transformed fangs. If they''re injured or broken off, the spines will regenerate countless times.'),
    (10070, 'legends-za', 'It can swim at speeds of 75 mph by jetting seawater through its body. It is the bandit of the sea.'),
    (10070, 'moon', 'As a consequence of Mega Evolution, its combative instincts exploded. The yellow marks it bears are scars from a long history of battles.'),
    (10070, 'shield', 'This Pokémon is known as the Bully of the Sea. Any ship entering the waters Sharpedo calls home will be attacked—no exceptions.'),
    (10070, 'shining-pearl', 'Its fangs rip through sheet iron. It swims at 75 mph and is known as the Bully of the Sea.'),
    (10070, 'sun', 'The spines sprouting from its head are transformed fangs. If they''re injured or broken off, the spines will regenerate countless times.'),
    (10070, 'sword', 'As soon as it catches the scent of its prey, Sharpedo will jet seawater from its backside, hurtling toward the target to attack at 75 mph.'),
    (10070, 'ultra-moon', 'The moment it charges into its opponent, sharp spikes pop out of Sharpedo''s head, leaving its opponent with deep wounds.'),
    (10070, 'ultra-sun', 'The yellow patterns it bears are old scars. The energy from Mega Evolution runs through them, causing it sharp pain and suffering.'),
    (10071, 'brilliant-diamond', 'Though usually dim-witted, it seems to become inspired if the Shellder on its tail bites down.'),
    (10071, 'legends-za', 'When bathed in the energy of Mega Evolution, Shellder converts into impregnable armor. There is virtually no change in Slowpoke.'),
    (10071, 'moon', 'When bathed in the energy of Mega Evolution, Shellder converts into impregnable armor. There is virtually no change in Slowpoke.'),
    (10071, 'shield', 'Being bitten by a Shellder shocked this Pokémon into standing on two legs. If the Shellder lets go, it seems Slowbro will turn back into a Slowpoke.'),
    (10071, 'shining-pearl', 'Though usually dim-witted, it seems to become inspired if the Shellder on its tail bites down.'),
    (10071, 'sun', 'All the energy from Mega Evolution poured into the Shellder on its tail, leaving Slowpoke to be swallowed whole.'),
    (10071, 'sword', 'Slowpoke became Slowbro when a Shellder bit on to its tail. Sweet flavors seeping from the tail make the Shellder feel as if its life is a dream.'),
    (10071, 'ultra-moon', 'Having been swallowed whole by Shellder, Slowbro now has an iron defense. It''s pretty comfortable in there, too.'),
    (10071, 'ultra-sun', 'Tremendous energy strengthened the power of the Shellder on its tail, but it doesn''t really affect Slowpoke.'),
    (10072, 'legends-za', 'To protect itself from opponents'' attacks, it uses magnetism to control pieces of its hard outer shell that have flaked off.'),
    (10073, 'brilliant-diamond', 'By flapping its wings with all its might, Pidgeot can make a gust of wind capable of bending tall trees.'),
    (10073, 'legends-za', 'It flies over water as it hunts, skimming along the surface to catch Magikarp and other such prey.'),
    (10073, 'legends-za', 'With its muscular strength now greatly increased, it can fly continuously for two weeks without resting.'),
    (10073, 'shining-pearl', 'By flapping its wings with all its might, Pidgeot can make a gust of wind capable of bending tall trees.'),
    (10074, 'brilliant-diamond', 'To protect itself, it clad its body in an armor of ice, made by freezing moisture in the air.'),
    (10074, 'legends-arceus', 'It covers its body with an armor of ice harder than steel. Uses its breath to freeze prey, which it then devours as if they were frozen desserts.'),
    (10074, 'legends-za', 'When it spews stupendously cold air from its broken mouth, the entire area around it gets whited out.'),
    (10074, 'legends-za', 'To protect itself, it clad its body in an armor of ice, made by freezing moisture in the air.'),
    (10074, 'moon', 'It envelops prey in its mouth, freezing them instantly. But its jaw is dislocated, so it''s unable to eat them.'),
    (10074, 'scarlet', 'Its prey is instantaneously frozen stiff by the cold air it exhales from its huge mouth. While they’re in that frozen state, it gobbles them up.'),
    (10074, 'shield', 'It can instantly freeze moisture in the atmosphere. It uses this power to freeze its foes.'),
    (10074, 'shining-pearl', 'To protect itself, it clad its body in an armor of ice, made by freezing moisture in the air.'),
    (10074, 'sun', 'The excess energy from Mega Evolution spilled over from its mouth, breaking its jaw. It spews endless blizzards.'),
    (10074, 'sword', 'It has a body of ice that won''t melt, even with fire. It can instantly freeze moisture in the atmosphere.'),
    (10074, 'ultra-moon', 'The power of Mega Evolution was so strong that it smashed Glalie''s jaw. Its inability to eat very well leaves Glalie irritated.'),
    (10074, 'ultra-sun', 'When it spews stupendously cold air from its broken mouth, the entire area around it gets whited out.'),
    (10074, 'violet', 'It prevents prey from escaping by instantaneously freezing moisture in the air.'),
    (10075, 'legends-za', 'This Pokémon is also known as the Royal Pink Princess. The dazzling, sparkling diamond on its forehead is a whopping 2,000 carats.'),
    (10076, 'brilliant-diamond', 'Metang combined to form it. With four brains, it has the intelligence of a supercomputer.'),
    (10076, 'legends-za', 'Metang combined to form it. With four brains, it has the intelligence of a supercomputer.'),
    (10076, 'legends-za', 'This form results from one Metagross, one Metang, and two Beldum linking up.'),
    (10076, 'moon', 'Mega Evolution stimulated its brain. It emerged as a ruthless Pokémon that will clutch at any means of ensuring its victories.'),
    (10076, 'scarlet', 'It folds its four legs when flying. Its four brains are said to be superior to a supercomputer.'),
    (10076, 'shield', 'Metagross is the result of the fusion of two Metang. This Pokémon defeats its opponents through use of its supercomputer-level brain.'),
    (10076, 'shining-pearl', 'Metang combined to form it. With four brains, it has the intelligence of a supercomputer.'),
    (10076, 'sun', 'This form results from one Metagross, one Metang, and two Beldum linking up.'),
    (10076, 'sword', 'Because the magnetic powers of these Pokémon get stronger in freezing temperatures, Metagross living on snowy mountains are full of energy.'),
    (10076, 'ultra-moon', 'When it knows it can''t win, it digs the claws on its legs into its opponent and starts the countdown to a big explosion.'),
    (10076, 'ultra-sun', 'Its intellect surpasses its previous level, resulting in battles so cruel, they''ll make you want to cover your eyes.'),
    (10076, 'violet', 'It firmly pins its prey using its four claws and large body. Then Metagross uses the mouth on its stomach to chew its prey to bits.'),
    (10077, 'legends-za', 'Kyogre reverted to this state via the [[Blue Orb]], which contains the energy of the primordial world. Kyogre''s body resembles seawater.'),
    (10078, 'legends-za', 'This is Groudon''s true form, restored using the [[Red Orb]]. Energy spills from its body in the form of magma.'),
    (10079, 'legends-za', 'A shooting star streaking across the night sky may, in fact, be Mega Rayquaza flying gracefully after a meteoroid.'),
    (10086, 'legends-za', 'This is Hoopa''s true form, in which it has regained its sealed powers. The hole in its chest is said to connect to another dimension.'),
    (10087, 'legends-za', 'When this Pokémon''s rage reaches a boiling point, the huge volcano in the hump on its back erupts violently, spewing molten lava.'),
    (10088, 'brilliant-diamond', 'An extremely cautious Pokémon that cloaks its body with its fluffy ear fur when it senses danger.'),
    (10088, 'legends-arceus', 'Its fur is warm and yet remarkably light. This Pokémon kicks as though it were a master of karate, driving back its opponents with ease.'),
    (10088, 'legends-za', 'It swings its ears like whips and strikes its enemies with them. It has an intensely combative disposition.'),
    (10088, 'legends-za', 'This Pokémon''s ears are apparently very delicate. They must be handled gently and with care, or else Lopunny will kick you with its graceful legs.'),
    (10088, 'shield', 'Once hot seasons are over, Lopunny''s coat will be replaced with fur that holds a lot of insulating air in preparation for colder weather.'),
    (10088, 'shining-pearl', 'It likes to keep itself clean and never fails to groom its ears. It runs with sprightly jumps.'),
    (10088, 'sword', 'Lopunny is constantly monitoring its surroundings. If dangers approaches, this Pokémon responds with superdestructive kicks.'),
    (10088, 'ultra-moon', 'Mega Evolution awakens its combative instincts. It has shed any fur that got in the way of its attacks.'),
    (10088, 'ultra-sun', 'It swings its ears like whips and strikes its enemies with them. It has an intensely combative disposition.'),
    (10089, 'brilliant-diamond', 'As a result of its long-held dream of flying, its cellular structure changed, and wings grew out.'),
    (10089, 'legends-za', 'To streamline itself for flight, it pulls its forelegs into its shell. Salamence flies at high speeds even when faced with complex topographical features.'),
    (10089, 'legends-za', 'It''s uncontrollable if enraged. It flies around spouting flames, scorching fields and mountains.'),
    (10089, 'moon', 'Mega Evolution fuels its brutality, and it may even turn on the Trainer who raised it. It''s been dubbed "the blood-soaked crescent."'),
    (10089, 'scarlet', 'It flies around on its wings, which have grown in at last. In its happiness, it gushes hot flames, burning up everything it passes over.'),
    (10089, 'shield', 'While basking in the joy of flight generally keeps this Pokémon in high spirits, Salamence turns into an uncontrollable menace if something angers it.'),
    (10089, 'shining-pearl', 'As a result of its long-held dream of flying, its cellular structure changed, and wings grew out.'),
    (10089, 'sun', 'Anyone standing in its path gets sliced right in two, while this Pokémon continues its flight without interruption.'),
    (10089, 'sword', 'Salamence is an unusual Pokémon in that it was able to evolve a body with wings just by constantly wishing to be able to fly.'),
    (10089, 'ultra-moon', 'It puts its forelegs inside its shell to streamline itself for flight. Salamence flies at high speeds over all kinds of topographical features.'),
    (10089, 'ultra-sun', 'The stress of its two proud wings becoming misshapen and stuck together because of strong energy makes it go on a rampage.'),
    (10089, 'violet', 'It becomes uncontrollable if it is enraged. It destroys everything with shredding claws and fire.'),
    (10090, 'brilliant-diamond', 'Its best attack involves flying around at high speed, striking with poison needles, then flying off.'),
    (10090, 'legends-za', 'They may appear in a swarm. Beedrill flies at violent speeds, all the while stabbing with the toxic stinger on its rear.'),
    (10090, 'legends-za', 'Its legs have become poison stingers. It stabs its prey repeatedly with the stingers on its limbs, dealing the final blow with the stinger on its rear.'),
    (10090, 'shining-pearl', 'Its best attack involves flying around at high speed, striking with poison needles, then flying off.'),
    (10091, 'brilliant-diamond', 'It''s cautious in the extreme, and its hardy vitality lets it live in any kind of environment.'),
    (10091, 'moon', 'When the sun goes down, it becomes active. It runs around town on a chase for good food for the boss of its nest—Raticate.'),
    (10091, 'shining-pearl', 'It''s cautious in the extreme, and its hardy vitality lets it live in any kind of environment.'),
    (10091, 'sun', 'With its incisors, it gnaws through doors and infiltrates [[Human|people]]''s homes. Then, with a twitch of its whiskers, it steals whatever food it finds.'),
    (10091, 'ultra-moon', 'Night after night, they sneak into people''s homes seeking food. A massive outbreak of them has become an issue of public concern.'),
    (10091, 'ultra-sun', 'It shows no interest in anything that isn''t fresh. If you take it shopping with you, it will help you pick out ingredients.'),
    (10092, 'brilliant-diamond', 'It whittles down its constantly growing fangs by gnawing on hard things. It can chew apart cinder block walls.'),
    (10092, 'moon', 'This gourmet Pokémon is particular about the taste and freshness of its food. Restaurants where Raticate live have a good reputation.'),
    (10092, 'shining-pearl', 'It whittles down its constantly growing fangs by gnawing on hard things. It can chew apart cinder block walls.'),
    (10092, 'sun', 'It forms a group of Rattata, which it assumes command of. Each group has its own territory, and disputes over food happen often.'),
    (10092, 'ultra-moon', 'It commands a nest of Rattata. Different nests don''t get along, whipping up severe fights over feeding grounds.'),
    (10092, 'ultra-sun', 'It has an incredibly greedy personality. Its nest is filled with so much food gathered by Rattata at its direction, it can''t possibly eat it all.'),
    (10100, 'brilliant-diamond', 'It turns aggressive if it has too much electricity in its body. It discharges power through its tail.'),
    (10100, 'legends-arceus', 'It can discharge bursts of electricity exceeding 100,000 volts—a single strike with that amount of power would incapacitate one of the Copperajah of [[Professor Laventon|my]] [[Galar|homeland]].'),
    (10100, 'legends-za', 'It uses psychokinesis to control electricity. It hops aboard its own tail, using psychic power to lift the tail and move about while riding it.'),
    (10100, 'legends-za', 'When its electricity builds, its muscles are stimulated, and it becomes more aggressive than usual.'),
    (10100, 'moon', 'It uses psychokinesis to control electricity. It hops aboard its own tail, using psychic power to lift the tail and move about while riding it.'),
    (10100, 'scarlet', 'Its tail discharges electricity into the ground, protecting it from getting shocked.'),
    (10100, 'shield', 'If its electric pouches run empty, it raises its tail to gather electricity from the atmosphere.'),
    (10100, 'shield', 'This Pokémon rides on its tail while it uses its psychic powers to levitate. It attacks with star-shaped thunderbolts.'),
    (10100, 'shining-pearl', 'It can loose 100,000-volt bursts of electricity, instantly downing foes several times its size.'),
    (10100, 'sun', 'It only [[Evolution|evolves]] to this form in the [[Alola]] [[region]]. According to researchers, its diet is one of the causes of this change.'),
    (10100, 'sword', 'Its long tail serves as a ground to protect itself from its own high-voltage power.'),
    (10100, 'sword', 'It''s believed that the weather, climate, and food of the Alola region all play a part in causing Pikachu to evolve into this form of Raichu.'),
    (10100, 'ultra-moon', 'When you rub its cheeks, a sweet fragrance comes wafting out. However, you''ll also get a light shock!'),
    (10100, 'ultra-sun', 'It focuses psychic energy into its tail and rides it like it''s surfing. Another name for this Pokémon is "hodad."'),
    (10100, 'violet', 'If the electric pouches in its cheeks become fully charged, both ears will stand straight up.'),
    (10101, 'brilliant-diamond', 'To protect itself from attackers, it curls up into a ball. It lives in arid regions with minimal rainfall.'),
    (10101, 'moon', 'An ancient tradition of Alolan festivals, still carried on to this day, is a competition to slide Sandshrew across ice as far as one can.'),
    (10101, 'scarlet', 'It digs deep burrows to live in. When in danger, it rolls up its body to withstand attacks.'),
    (10101, 'scarlet', 'It lives on snowy mountains. Its steel shell is very hard—so much so, it can’t roll its body up into a ball.'),
    (10101, 'shield', 'It burrows into the ground to create its nest. If hard stones impede its tunneling, it uses its sharp claws to shatter them and then carries on digging.'),
    (10101, 'shield', 'It lives in snowy mountains on southern islands. When a blizzard rolls in, this Pokémon hunkers down in the snow to avoid getting blown away.'),
    (10101, 'shining-pearl', 'To protect itself from attackers, it curls up into a ball. It lives in arid regions with minimal rainfall.'),
    (10101, 'sun', 'It lives on snowy mountains. Its steel shell is very hard—so much so, it can''t roll its body up into a ball.'),
    (10101, 'sword', 'Life on mountains covered with deep snow has granted this Pokémon a body of ice that''s as hard as steel.'),
    (10101, 'sword', 'It loves to bathe in the grit of dry, sandy areas. By sand bathing, this Pokémon rids itself of dirt and moisture clinging to its body.'),
    (10101, 'ultra-moon', 'The skin on its back is as hard as steel. Predators go after its soft belly, so it clings to the ground desperately.'),
    (10101, 'ultra-sun', 'After fleeing a volcanic eruption, it ended up moving to an area of snowy mountains. Its ice shell is as hard as steel.'),
    (10101, 'violet', 'No matter how high a place it falls from, this Pokémon can save itself by rolling in a ball and bouncing.'),
    (10101, 'violet', 'An ancient tradition of Alolan festivals, still carried on to this day, is a competition to slide Sandshrew across ice as far as one can.'),
    (10102, 'brilliant-diamond', 'It curls up, then rolls into foes with its back. Its sharp spines inflict severe damage.'),
    (10102, 'moon', 'This Pokémon''s steel spikes are sheathed in ice. Stabs from these spikes cause deep wounds and severe frostbite as well.'),
    (10102, 'scarlet', 'This Pokémon’s steel spikes are sheathed in ice. Stabs from these spikes cause deep wounds and severe frostbite as well.'),
    (10102, 'scarlet', 'It is adept at attacking with the spines on its back and its sharp claws while quickly scurrying about.'),
    (10102, 'shield', 'It climbs trees by hooking on with its sharp claws. Sandslash shares the berries it gathers, dropping them down to Sandshrew waiting below the tree.'),
    (10102, 'shield', 'Many people climb snowy mountains, hoping to see the icy spikes of these Pokémon glistening in the light of dawn.'),
    (10102, 'shining-pearl', 'It curls up, then rolls into foes with its back. Its sharp spines inflict severe damage.'),
    (10102, 'sun', 'Fleeing a volcanic eruption, it settled on a snowy mountain. As it races through the snowfields, it sends up a spray of snow.'),
    (10102, 'sword', 'The drier the area Sandslash lives in, the harder and smoother the Pokémon''s spikes feel when touched.'),
    (10102, 'sword', 'It uses large, hooked claws to cut a path through deep snow as it runs. On snowy mountains, this Sandslash is faster than any other Pokémon.'),
    (10102, 'ultra-moon', 'A long, long time ago, it lived in the desert. With its sharp claws fully extended, it can climb right up an iceberg without slipping.'),
    (10102, 'ultra-sun', 'It runs across snow-covered plains at high speeds. It developed thick, sharp claws to plow through the snow.'),
    (10102, 'violet', 'A long, long time ago, it lived in the desert. With its sharp claws fully extended, it can run right up an iceberg without slipping.'),
    (10102, 'violet', 'The spikes on its body are made up of its hardened hide. It rolls up and attacks foes with its spikes.'),
    (10103, 'brilliant-diamond', 'It controls balls of fire. As it grows, its six tails split from their tips to make more tails.'),
    (10103, 'legends-arceus', 'In its belly burns a fire, which Vulpix spits out in the form of fireballs. When young, this Pokémon has but one white tail. As the Pokémon matures, this single tail splits into six.'),
    (10103, 'legends-arceus', 'These Pokémon live in packs in the snowy mountains and defend themselves with icy breath. I suspect this species changed its form to adapt to the frigid climate.'),
    (10103, 'moon', 'In hot weather, this Pokémon makes ice shards with its six tails and sprays them around to cool itself off.'),
    (10103, 'scarlet', 'They live together in a skulk, helping one another. Before eating their prey, they freeze it solid with their −58 degree Fahrenheit breath.'),
    (10103, 'scarlet', 'If it is attacked by an enemy that is stronger than itself, it feigns injury to fool the enemy and escapes.'),
    (10103, 'shield', 'If you observe its curly hairs through a microscope, you''ll see small ice particles springing up.'),
    (10103, 'shield', 'As each tail grows, its fur becomes more lustrous. When held, it feels slightly warm.'),
    (10103, 'shining-pearl', 'It controls balls of fire. As it grows, its six tails split from their tips to make more tails.'),
    (10103, 'sun', 'It exhales air colder than -58 degrees Fahrenheit. Elderly people in Alola call this Pokémon by an older name—Keokeo.'),
    (10103, 'sword', 'After long years in the ever-snowcapped mountains of Alola, this Vulpix has gained power over ice.'),
    (10103, 'sword', 'While young, it has six gorgeous tails. When it grows, several new tails are sprouted.'),
    (10103, 'ultra-moon', 'They live together in a skulk, helping one another. Before eating their prey, they freeze it solid with their –58<!--U+2013 EN DASH in-game--> degree Fahrenheit breath.'),
    (10103, 'ultra-sun', 'If you carelessly approach it because it''s cute, the boss of the pack, Ninetales, will appear and freeze you.'),
    (10103, 'violet', 'In hot weather, this Pokémon makes ice shards with its six tails and sprays them around to cool itself off.'),
    (10103, 'violet', 'As its body grows larger, its six warm tails become more beautiful, with a more luxurious coat of fur.'),
    (10104, 'brilliant-diamond', 'Its nine tails are said to be imbued with a mystic power. The Pokémon is said to live for 1,000 years.'),
    (10104, 'legends-arceus', 'Dwells on sacred peaks perpetually covered in snow. Said to appear to virtuous people who have lost their way on mountain paths—it then guides them back down to the mountain''s base.'),
    (10104, 'legends-arceus', 'The coat of gleaming golden fur is quite magnificent. This species is said to store sacred power in its nine long tails and to live for a millennium.'),
    (10104, 'moon', 'Possessing a calm demeanor, this Pokémon was revered as a deity incarnate before it was identified as a regional variant of Ninetales.'),
    (10104, 'scarlet', 'Some legends claim that each of its nine tails has its own unique type of special mystical power.'),
    (10104, 'scarlet', 'Possessing a calm demeanor, this Pokémon was revered as a deity incarnate before it was identified as a regional variant of Ninetales.'),
    (10104, 'shield', 'While it will guide travelers who get lost on a snowy mountain down to the mountain''s base, it won''t forgive anyone who harms nature.'),
    (10104, 'shield', 'Very smart and very vengeful. Grabbing one of its many tails could result in a 1,000-year curse.'),
    (10104, 'shining-pearl', 'Its nine tails are said to be imbued with a mystic power. The Pokémon is said to live for 1,000 years.'),
    (10104, 'sun', 'It creates drops of ice in its coat and showers them over its enemies. Anyone who angers it will be frozen stiff in an instant.'),
    (10104, 'sword', 'It is said to live 1,000 years, and each of its tails is loaded with supernatural powers.'),
    (10104, 'sword', 'A deity resides in the snowy mountains where this Pokémon lives. In ancient times, it was worshiped as that deity''s incarnation.'),
    (10104, 'ultra-moon', 'Some said that deities visited mountains where Ninetales live, so in times long past, no one was allowed to go into those mountains.'),
    (10104, 'ultra-sun', 'The reason it guides people all the way down to the mountain''s base is that it wants them to hurry up and leave.'),
    (10104, 'violet', 'It creates drops of ice in its coat and showers them over its enemies. Anyone who angers it will be frozen stiff in an instant.'),
    (10104, 'violet', 'It has nine long tails and fur that gleams gold. It is said to live for 1,000 years.'),
    (10105, 'brilliant-diamond', 'This Pokémon lives underground. Because of its dark habitat, it is repelled by bright sunlight.'),
    (10105, 'moon', 'Its golden hairs function as sensors. It pokes them out of its burrow to monitor its surroundings.'),
    (10105, 'scarlet', 'It lives about one yard underground, where it feeds on plant roots. It sometimes appears aboveground.'),
    (10105, 'scarlet', 'The things growing from its head are whiskers that have become metallic. Diglett communicates with its comrades by waving them.'),
    (10105, 'shield', 'Its three hairs change shape depending on Diglett''s mood. They''re a useful communication tool among these Pokémon.'),
    (10105, 'shield', 'It burrows through the ground at a shallow depth. It leaves raised earth in its wake, making it easy to spot.'),
    (10105, 'shining-pearl', 'This Pokémon lives underground. Because of its dark habitat, it is repelled by bright sunlight.'),
    (10105, 'sun', 'Its head sports an altered form of whiskers made of metal. When in communication with its comrades, its whiskers wobble to and fro.'),
    (10105, 'sword', 'The metal-rich geology of this Pokémon''s habitat caused it to develop steel whiskers on its head.'),
    (10105, 'sword', 'If a Diglett digs through a field, it leaves the soil perfectly tilled and ideal for planting crops.'),
    (10105, 'ultra-moon', 'The need to dig through volcanic rock in the ground has made them more powerful than the Diglett of other regions.'),
    (10105, 'ultra-sun', 'Although it''s powerful enough to dig right through volcanic rock, it doesn''t allow itself to be seen very often.'),
    (10105, 'violet', 'Its skin is very thin. If it is exposed to light, its blood heats up, causing it to grow weak.'),
    (10105, 'violet', 'Its golden whiskers function as sensors. It pokes them out of its burrow to monitor its surroundings.'),
    (10106, 'brilliant-diamond', 'Its three heads move alternately, driving it through tough soil to depths of over 60 miles.'),
    (10106, 'moon', 'These Pokémon are cherished in the Alola region, where they are thought to be feminine deities of the land incarnate.'),
    (10106, 'scarlet', 'Its shining gold whiskers are advanced sensors that can detect vibrations from sounds several miles away.'),
    (10106, 'scarlet', 'Its three heads bob separately up and down to loosen the soil nearby, making it easier for it to burrow.'),
    (10106, 'shield', 'The three of them get along very well. Through their formidable teamwork, they defeat powerful opponents.'),
    (10106, 'shield', 'These Diglett triplets dig over 60 miles below sea level. No one knows what it''s like underground.'),
    (10106, 'shining-pearl', 'Its three heads move alternately, driving it through tough soil to depths of over 60 miles.'),
    (10106, 'sun', 'Its shining gold hair provides it with protection. It''s reputed that keeping any of its fallen hairs will bring bad luck.'),
    (10106, 'sword', 'Their beautiful, metallic whiskers create a sort of protective helmet on their heads, and they also function as highly precise sensors.'),
    (10106, 'sword', 'A team of Diglett triplets. It triggers huge earthquakes by burrowing 60 miles underground.'),
    (10106, 'ultra-moon', 'Its shining gold whiskers are advanced sensors that can detect vibrations from sounds several miles away.'),
    (10106, 'ultra-sun', 'Its metallic whiskers are heavy, so it''s not very fast, but it has the power to dig through bedrock.'),
    (10106, 'violet', 'In battle, it digs through the ground and strikes the unsuspecting foe from an unexpected direction.'),
    (10106, 'violet', 'Its metallic whiskers are heavy, so it’s not very fast, but it has the power to dig through even the hardest bedrock.'),
    (10107, 'brilliant-diamond', 'It is nocturnal by nature. If it spots something shiny, its eyes glitter as brightly as the shiny object.'),
    (10107, 'legends-za', 'It''s fickle, selfish, and easily bored. This species is very popular with certain Trainers-ones who prefer fulfilling others'' needs over their own.'),
    (10107, 'moon', 'When its delicate pride is wounded, or when the gold coin on its forehead is dirtied, it flies into a hysterical rage.'),
    (10107, 'shield', 'It washes its face regularly to keep the coin on its forehead spotless. It doesn''t get along with Galarian Meowth.'),
    (10107, 'shield', 'Deeply proud and keenly smart, this Pokémon moves with cunning during battle and relentlessly attacks enemies'' weak points.'),
    (10107, 'shining-pearl', 'It is nocturnal by nature. If it spots something shiny, its eyes glitter as brightly as the shiny object.'),
    (10107, 'sun', 'This Pokémon was not originally found in Alola. Human actions caused a surge in their numbers, and they went feral. They''re prideful and crafty.'),
    (10107, 'sword', 'It loves to collect shiny things. If it''s in a good mood, it might even let its Trainer have a look at its hoard of treasures.'),
    (10107, 'sword', 'It''s accustomed to luxury because it used to live with Alolan royalty. As a result, it''s very picky about food.'),
    (10107, 'ultra-moon', 'A royal house that flourished in the distant past brought it here from another region. Meowth is both selfish and prideful.'),
    (10107, 'ultra-sun', 'It''s impulsive, selfish, and fickle. It''s very popular with some Trainers who like giving it the attention it needs.'),
    (10108, 'brilliant-diamond', 'It is a very haughty Pokémon. Among fans of Persian, the size of the jewel in its forehead is a topic of much talk.'),
    (10108, 'legends-za', 'Many admire Persian for the dignity it exudes from every inch of its body. However, it will lash out with its claws given the slightest provocation.'),
    (10108, 'legends-za', 'Its round face is a symbol of wealth. Persian that have bigger, plumper faces are considered more beautiful.'),
    (10108, 'moon', 'It looks down on everyone other than itself. Its preferred tactics are sucker punches and blindside attacks.'),
    (10108, 'scarlet', 'Although its fur has many admirers, it is tough to raise as a pet because of its fickle meanness.'),
    (10108, 'shield', 'This Pokémon is one tough opponent. Not only does it have formidable physical abilities, but it''s also not above fighting dirty.'),
    (10108, 'shield', 'Its elegant and refined behavior clashes with that of the barbaric Perrserker. The relationship between the two is one of mutual disdain.'),
    (10108, 'shining-pearl', 'It is a very haughty Pokémon. Among fans of Persian, the size of the jewel in its forehead is a topic of much talk.'),
    (10108, 'sun', 'Its round face and smooth coat—softer than the most high-class velvet—have made this a very popular Pokémon in Alola.'),
    (10108, 'sword', 'Getting this prideful Pokémon to warm up to you takes a lot of effort, and it will claw at you the moment it gets annoyed.'),
    (10108, 'sword', 'The round face of Alolan Persian is considered to be a symbol of prosperity in the Alola region, so these Pokémon are very well cared for.'),
    (10108, 'ultra-moon', 'Its round face is a symbol of wealth. Persian that have bigger, plumper faces are considered more beautiful.'),
    (10108, 'ultra-sun', 'In contrast to its lovely face, it''s so brutal that it tortures its weakened prey rather than finishing them off.'),
    (10108, 'violet', 'It has a vicious temperament. Beware if it raises its tail straight up. This is a signal that it is about to pounce and bite.'),
    (10109, 'brilliant-diamond', 'Many live on mountain trails and remain half-buried while keeping an eye on climbers.'),
    (10109, 'legends-arceus', 'Makes its home in mountainous regions, using its arms to climb along harsh mountain roads. Can be troublesome—carelessly kicking one will cause it to fly into a rage and chase after you.'),
    (10109, 'moon', 'If you accidentally step on a Geodude sleeping on the ground, you''ll hear a crunching sound and feel a shock ripple through your entire body.'),
    (10109, 'scarlet', 'Its body is a magnetic stone. Iron sand attaches firmly to the portions of its body that are particularly magnetic.'),
    (10109, 'scarlet', 'At rest, it looks just like a rock. Carelessly stepping on it will make it swing its fists angrily.'),
    (10109, 'shining-pearl', 'It is impossible to distinguish from rocks. It slams against others in contests of toughness.'),
    (10109, 'sun', 'Its body is a magnetic stone. Iron sand attaches firmly to the portions of its body that are particularly magnetic.'),
    (10109, 'ultra-moon', 'Geodude compete against each other with headbutts. The iron sand on their heads will stick to whichever one has stronger magnetism.'),
    (10109, 'ultra-sun', 'If you mistake it for a rock and step on it, it will headbutt you in anger. In addition to the pain, it will also zap you with a shock.'),
    (10109, 'violet', 'If you step on a Geodude sleeping on the ground, you’ll hear a zapping sound and feel a tingling shock throughout your entire body.'),
    (10109, 'violet', 'Most people may not notice, but a closer look should reveal that there are many Geodude around.'),
    (10110, 'brilliant-diamond', 'Graveler make their homes on sheer cliff faces that have numerous holes in them.'),
    (10110, 'legends-arceus', 'Dwells in holes dug into sheer walls of stone. It enjoys rolling down slopes as though it were a boulder during a rockfall, so keep an eye upward while traversing mountain roads.'),
    (10110, 'moon', 'They eat rocks and often get into a scrap over them. The shock of Graveler smashing together causes a flash of light and a booming noise.'),
    (10110, 'scarlet', 'A slow walker, it rolls to move. It pays no attention to any object that happens to be in its path.'),
    (10110, 'scarlet', 'They eat rocks and often get into a scrap over them. The impact of Graveler smashing together causes a flash of light and a booming noise.'),
    (10110, 'shining-pearl', 'It tumbles down slopes, heedless of any body parts chipping off. It eats a ton of rocks daily.'),
    (10110, 'sun', 'Its preferred food is {{wp|dravite}}. After it has eaten this mineral, crystals form inside the Pokémon, rising to the surface of part of its body.'),
    (10110, 'ultra-moon', 'Graveler''s entire body is tinged with electricity due to the stones it likes to eat. It''s very quick-tempered.'),
    (10110, 'ultra-sun', 'When two Graveler fight each other, it fills the surroundings with flashes of light and sound. People call it the "fireworks of the earth."'),
    (10110, 'violet', 'Graveler''s entire body is electrically charged due to the stones it likes to eat. It is a very quick-tempered Pokémon.'),
    (10110, 'violet', 'Moss-covered rocks are Graveler''s favorite food. It consumes over a ton of them a day, crunching loudly while it eats.'),
    (10111, 'brilliant-diamond', 'It sheds its hide once a year. Its boulder-like body is so tough, even dynamite can''t harm it.'),
    (10111, 'legends-arceus', 'The rocklike shell is shed each year. The cast-off shell then crumbles, reverting to a mass of soil, which can be spread across fields to promote crop growth.'),
    (10111, 'moon', 'Because it can''t fire boulders at a rapid pace, it''s been known to seize nearby Geodude and fire them from its back.'),
    (10111, 'scarlet', 'It is enclosed in a hard shell that is as rugged as slabs of rock. It sheds skin once a year to grow larger.'),
    (10111, 'scarlet', 'It’s grumpy and stubborn. If you upset it, it discharges electricity from the surface of its body and growls with a voice like thunder.'),
    (10111, 'shining-pearl', 'It tumbles down mountains, leaving grooves from peak to base. Stay clear of these grooves.'),
    (10111, 'sun', 'It fires rocks charged with electricity. Even if the rock isn''t fired that accurately, just grazing an opponent will cause numbness and fainting.'),
    (10111, 'ultra-moon', 'It shoots large rocks that are charged with electricity. Tremendous electric shocks are flung out across the whole area of impact.'),
    (10111, 'ultra-sun', 'It''s grumpy and stubborn. If you upset it, it discharges electricity from the surface of its body and growls with a voice like thunder.'),
    (10111, 'violet', 'It fires rocks charged with electricity. Even if the rock isn’t fired that accurately, just grazing an opponent will cause numbness and fainting.'),
    (10111, 'violet', 'It deliberately blows itself up, then uses this explosive force to jump from mountain to mountain.'),
    (10112, 'brilliant-diamond', 'It was born when sludge in a dirty stream was exposed to the moon''s X-rays. It appears among filth.'),
    (10112, 'moon', 'The crystals on Grimer''s body are lumps of toxins. If one falls off, lethal poisons leak out.'),
    (10112, 'scarlet', 'Born from sludge, these Pokémon now gather in polluted places and increase the bacteria in their bodies.'),
    (10112, 'scarlet', 'They store their toxins inside their bodies, so unlike Grimer from other regions, they don’t smell bad even up close.'),
    (10112, 'shining-pearl', 'It was born when sludge in a dirty stream was exposed to the moon''s X-rays. It appears among filth.'),
    (10112, 'sun', 'A Grimer, which had been brought in to solve a problem with garbage, developed over time into this form.'),
    (10112, 'ultra-moon', 'Brought to Alola to solve the garbage problem, Grimer seems to relish any and all kinds of trash.'),
    (10112, 'ultra-sun', 'There are a hundred or so of them living in Alola''s waste-disposal site. They''re all hard workers who eat a lot of trash.'),
    (10112, 'violet', 'Alolan Grimer will gladly gobble up any kind of trash, making it a widely used and popular Pokémon at garbage disposal facilities.'),
    (10112, 'violet', 'When two of these Pokémon''s bodies are combined together, new poisons are created.'),
    (10113, 'brilliant-diamond', 'A toxic fluid seeps from its body. The fluid kills plants and trees immediately upon contact.'),
    (10113, 'moon', 'While it''s unexpectedly quiet and friendly, if it''s not fed any trash for a while, it will smash its Trainer''s furnishings and eat up the fragments.'),
    (10113, 'scarlet', 'It’s thickly covered with a filthy, vile sludge. It is so toxic, even its footprints contain poison.'),
    (10113, 'scarlet', 'There are over a hundred kinds of poison inside its body. Chemical reactions between different poisons are the source of its vitality.'),
    (10113, 'shining-pearl', 'A toxic fluid seeps from its body. The fluid kills plants and trees immediately upon contact.'),
    (10113, 'sun', 'The garbage it eats causes continuous chemical changes in its body, which produce its exceedingly vivid coloration.'),
    (10113, 'ultra-moon', 'What look like fangs and claws are actually crystallized poison that will afflict you at a mere touch, so don''t get too close.'),
    (10113, 'ultra-sun', 'There are over a hundred kinds of poison inside its body. Chemical reactions between different poisons are the source of its vitality.'),
    (10113, 'violet', 'It''s so stinky! Muk''s body contains toxic elements, and any plant will wilt when it passes by.'),
    (10113, 'violet', 'What look like fangs and claws are actually crystallized poison that will afflict you at a mere touch, so don’t get too close.'),
    (10114, 'brilliant-diamond', 'It is called the Walking Jungle. If a head grows too big, it falls off and becomes an Exeggcute.'),
    (10114, 'moon', 'As it grew taller and taller, it outgrew its reliance on psychic powers, while within it awakened the power of the sleeping dragon.'),
    (10114, 'scarlet', 'It swings its long neck like a whip and smacks its head into opponents. This makes Exeggutor itself a little dizzy too.'),
    (10114, 'scarlet', 'It is called the Walking Jungle. Each of the nuts has a face and a will of its own.'),
    (10114, 'shield', 'This Pokémon''s psychic powers aren''t as strong as they once were. The head on this Exeggutor''s tail scans surrounding areas with weak telepathy.'),
    (10114, 'shield', 'When they work together, Exeggutor''s three heads can put out powerful psychic energy. Cloudy days make this Pokémon sluggish.'),
    (10114, 'shining-pearl', 'It is called the Walking Jungle. If a head grows too big, it falls off and becomes an Exeggcute.'),
    (10114, 'sun', 'Alola is the best environment for this Pokémon. Local people take pride in its appearance, saying this is how Exeggutor ought to look.'),
    (10114, 'sword', 'Blazing sunlight has brought out the true form and powers of this Pokémon.'),
    (10114, 'sword', 'Each of Exeggutor''s three heads is thinking different thoughts. The three don''t seem to be very interested in one another.'),
    (10114, 'ultra-moon', 'It swings its long neck like a whip and smacks its opponents. This makes Exeggutor itself dizzy, too.'),
    (10114, 'ultra-sun', 'Exeggutor is the pride of the Alolan people. Its image is carved into historical buildings and murals.'),
    (10114, 'violet', 'It is said that on rare occasions, one of its heads will drop off and continue on as an Exeggcute.'),
    (10114, 'violet', 'As it grew taller and taller, it outgrew its reliance on psychic powers, while within it awakened the power of the sleeping dragon.'),
    (10115, 'brilliant-diamond', 'The bones it uses have been in its possession since it was born. It has a ferocious nature.'),
    (10115, 'legends-za', 'It has transformed the spirit of its dear departed mother into flames, and tonight it will once again dance in mourning of others of its kind.'),
    (10115, 'legends-za', 'It carries a bone that it collected from someplace unknown. Rumor has it that somewhere in the world, there is a graveyard only for Marowak.'),
    (10115, 'moon', 'Its custom is to mourn its lost companions. Mounds of dirt by the side of the road mark the graves of the Marowak.'),
    (10115, 'shield', 'When this Pokémon evolved, the skull of its mother fused to it. Marowak''s temperament also turned vicious at the same time.'),
    (10115, 'shield', 'The cursed flames that light up the bone carried by this Pokémon are said to cause both mental and physical pain that will never fade.'),
    (10115, 'shining-pearl', 'The bones it uses have been in its possession since it was born. It has a ferocious nature.'),
    (10115, 'sun', 'The bones it possesses were once its mother''s. Its mother''s regrets have become like a vengeful spirit protecting this Pokémon.'),
    (10115, 'sword', 'This Pokémon sets the bone it holds on fire and dances through the night as a way to mourn its fallen allies.'),
    (10115, 'sword', 'This Pokémon overcame its sorrow to evolve a sturdy new body. Marowak faces its opponents bravely, using a bone as a weapon.'),
    (10115, 'ultra-moon', 'When it beats opponents with its bone, the cursed flames spread to them. No amount of water will stop those flames from burning.'),
    (10115, 'ultra-sun', 'The rich greenery of the Alola region is hard on Marowak. It controls fire to stay alive.'),
    (10120, 'legends-za', 'Born when all of Zygarde''s cells have been gathered together, it uses force to neutralize those who harm the ecosystem.'),
    (10120, 'moon', 'This is Zygarde''s 100% form. It has enough power to overwhelm even Xerneas or Yveltal.'),
    (10120, 'sun', 'This is Zygarde''s form at times when it uses its overwhelming power to suppress those who endanger the ecosystem.'),
    (10120, 'ultra-moon', 'Born when all of Zygarde''s cells have been gathered together, it uses force to neutralize those who harm the ecosystem.'),
    (10120, 'ultra-sun', 'This is Zygarde''s perfected form. From the orifice on its chest, it radiates high-powered energy that eliminates everything.'),
    (10123, 'moon', 'It creates an electric charge by rubbing its feathers together. It dances over to its enemies and delivers shocking electrical punches.'),
    (10123, 'scarlet', 'This form of Oricorio has sipped yellow nectar. It uses nimble steps to approach opponents, then knocks them out with electric punches.'),
    (10123, 'sun', 'This Oricorio has sipped bright yellow nectar. Its bright, cheerful dance melts the hearts of its enemies.'),
    (10123, 'ultra-moon', 'This Oricorio has drunk bright yellow nectar. When it sees someone looking glum, it will try to cheer them up with a dance.'),
    (10123, 'ultra-sun', 'It lifts its opponents'' spirits with its cheerful dance moves. When they let their guard down, it electrocutes them with a jolt.'),
    (10123, 'violet', 'The energetic, cheerful dance of these Oricorio is popular with children, but the Oricorio themselves are hard to find in Paldea.'),
    (10124, 'moon', 'This Oricorio has sipped pink nectar. Its enemies'' hearts melt at the sight of its gently swaying hips.'),
    (10124, 'scarlet', 'The airy dance of these Oricorio is popular as a means of maintaining good health, but the Oricorio themselves are hard to find in Paldea.'),
    (10124, 'sun', 'This Oricorio relaxes by swaying gently. This increases its psychic energy, which it then fires at its enemies.'),
    (10124, 'ultra-moon', 'This Oricorio has sipped pink nectar. It gets so caught up in its dancing that it sometimes doesn''t hear its Trainer''s orders.'),
    (10124, 'ultra-sun', 'It relaxes its opponents with its elegant dancing. When they let their guard down, it showers them with psychic energy.'),
    (10124, 'violet', 'This form of Oricorio has sipped pink nectar. It elevates its mind with the gentle steps of its dance, then unleashes its psychic energy.'),
    (10125, 'moon', 'It summons the dead with its dreamy dancing. From their malice, it draws power with which to curse its enemies.'),
    (10125, 'scarlet', 'This form of Oricorio has sipped purple nectar. It uses ethereal dance steps to call forth the spirits of the dead.'),
    (10125, 'sun', 'This Oricorio has sipped purple nectar. Its elegant, attractive dance will send the minds and hearts of its enemies to another world.'),
    (10125, 'ultra-moon', 'This Oricorio has sipped purple nectar. Some dancers use its graceful, elegant dancing as inspiration.'),
    (10125, 'ultra-sun', 'It charms its opponents with its refined dancing. When they let their guard down, it places a curse on them that will bring on their demise.'),
    (10125, 'violet', 'The elegant, attractive dance of these Oricorio is popular with adults, but the Oricorio themselves are hard to find in Paldea.'),
    (10126, 'moon', 'It goads its enemies into attacking, withstands the hits, and in return, delivers a headbutt, crushing their bones with its rocky mane.'),
    (10126, 'scarlet', 'This Pokémon uses its rocky mane to slash any who approach. It will even disobey its Trainer if it dislikes the orders it was given.'),
    (10126, 'shield', 'It''s invigorated by powerful opponents–the stronger the better. A full-force headbutt from one of these Lycanroc can shatter giant boulders.'),
    (10126, 'sun', 'The more intimidating the opponent it faces, the more this {{OBP|Pokémon|species}}''s blood boils. It will attack with no regard for its own safety.'),
    (10126, 'sword', 'This form of Lycanroc is reckless. It charges headlong at its opponents, attacking without any care about what injuries it might receive.'),
    (10126, 'ultra-moon', 'They live alone without forming packs. They will only listen to orders from Trainers who can draw out their true power.'),
    (10126, 'ultra-sun', 'It has no problem ignoring orders it doesn''t like. It doesn''t seem to mind getting hurt at all—as long as it can finish off its opponent.'),
    (10126, 'violet', 'This Lycanroc has an extremely vicious temperament. It will happily sustain injuries for the sake of taking down its opponent.'),
    (10127, 'moon', 'At their appearance, even Gyarados will flee. When they team up to use Water Gun, its power exceeds that of Hydro Pump.'),
    (10127, 'shield', 'When facing tough opponents, they get into formation. But if they get wounded in battle, they''ll scatter and become solitary again.'),
    (10127, 'sun', 'Weak Wishiwashi school together to concentrate their power. Their united force makes them the demon of the sea, feared near and far.'),
    (10127, 'sword', 'On their own, they''re very weak. But when Wishiwashi pool their power together in a school, they become a demon of the sea.'),
    (10127, 'ultra-moon', 'Called “demon of the sea” by some, when Wishiwashi are injured in battle and their numbers dwindle, they become a regular school.'),
    (10127, 'ultra-sun', 'Wishiwashi assemble in this formation to face off against strong foes. It boasts a strength that earned it the name “demon of the sea.”'),
    (10136, 'moon', 'If its core stays exposed, it will soon die off. It''s possible that it may survive if it''s put into a [[Poké Ball]] quickly enough.'),
    (10136, 'scarlet', 'Minior that fall to the ground try to return to space, but their wish will not come true—all they can do is fade away.'),
    (10136, 'sun', 'It eats dust in the atmosphere. The composition of the dust determines the color of its core.'),
    (10136, 'ultra-moon', 'This is its form when its shell has fallen off. The color of its core depends on the materials that made up the food it ate.'),
    (10136, 'ultra-sun', 'Places where Minior fall from the night sky are few and far between, with Alola being one of the precious few.'),
    (10136, 'violet', 'It feeds on dust in the atmosphere. The color of its core is said to be determined by the composition of the dust it eats.'),
    (10147, 'legends-za', 'This Magearna looks as it did at the time of its invention. Its magnificent ornamentation delighted the king''s daughter.'),
    (10147, 'legends-za', 'This Pokémon was built by a scientist roughly 500 years ago. The part called the Soul-Heart is the actual life-form.'),
    (10147, 'moon', 'This gorgeous Magearna looks as it did at the time of its invention. Its luxurious decoration pleased the king''s daughter.'),
    (10147, 'sun', 'This beautiful form reflects Magearna''s appearance when first presented to a king''s daughter 500 years ago.'),
    (10147, 'ultra-moon', 'It functions thanks to its artificial soul. The vivid decoration is proof that it was presented as a gift to royalty.'),
    (10147, 'ultra-sun', 'This is its form from almost 500 years ago. Its body is nothing more than a container—its artificial heart is the actual life-form.'),
    (10152, 'scarlet', 'Normally this Pokémon doesn''t even bark, but once it enters battle, it will relentlessly drive the opponent into a corner.'),
    (10152, 'shield', 'These Pokémon have both calm and ferocious qualities. Their temperamental nature makes them a difficult species to raise.'),
    (10152, 'sword', 'This form of Lycanroc is normally calm and quiet. Once a {{pkmn|battle}} begins, however, this Pokémon displays a ferocious fighting spirit.'),
    (10152, 'ultra-moon', 'This strange form is the result of its evolving at dusk. It''s very rare in Alola.'),
    (10152, 'ultra-sun', 'Bathed in the setting sun of evening, Lycanroc has undergone a special kind of evolution. An intense fighting spirit underlies its calmness.'),
    (10152, 'violet', 'These Pokémon have both calm and ferocious qualities. It''s said that this form of Lycanroc is the most troublesome to raise.'),
    (10155, 'shield', 'Necrozma has attached itself to Solgaleo. It siphons away its host''s limitless energy, exploiting that energy to fuel a rampage.*'),
    (10155, 'sword', 'When it dominates Solgaleo, it takes on this form. It''s a vicious Pokémon, mangling prey with its many claws—including those on its back.*'),
    (10155, 'ultra-moon', 'This is Necrozma''s form while it''s absorbing the power of Solgaleo, making it extremely ferocious and impossible to control.'),
    (10155, 'ultra-sun', 'This is its form while it is devouring the light of Solgaleo. It pounces on foes and then slashes them with the claws on its four limbs and back.'),
    (10156, 'shield', 'When Necrozma latches on to Lunala, it becomes vicious, seeing enemies everywhere it looks. It will burn the world with lasers.*'),
    (10156, 'sword', 'Necrozma has subjugated Lunala entirely, forcing the unfortunate {{OBP|Pokémon|species}} to emit its light energy for Necrozma to consume.*'),
    (10156, 'ultra-moon', 'This is its form while it''s devouring the light of Lunala. It grasps foes in its giant claws and rips them apart with brute force.'),
    (10156, 'ultra-sun', 'Lunala no longer has a will of its own. Now under the control of Necrozma, it continuously expels all of its energy.'),
    (10157, 'shield', 'It needs light to survive, and it goes on a rampage seeking it out. Its laser beams will cut anything to pieces.*'),
    (10157, 'sword', 'It survives by absorbing light. After a long time spent slumbering underground, impurities accumulated within it, causing its body to darken.*'),
    (10157, 'ultra-moon', 'The light pouring out from all over its body affects living things and nature, impacting them in various ways.'),
    (10157, 'ultra-sun', 'This is its form when it has absorbed overwhelming light energy. It fires laser beams from all over its body.'),
    (10161, 'legends-za', 'Its unkempt beard is a vestige from living in cold climes. It fights dauntlessly using its steel claws.'),
    (10161, 'shield', 'These daring Pokémon have coins on their foreheads. Darker coins are harder, and harder coins garner more respect among Meowth.'),
    (10161, 'sword', 'Living with a savage, seafaring people has toughened this Pokémon''s body so much that parts of it have turned to iron.'),
    (10162, 'shield', 'This Pokémon will look into your eyes and read the contents of your heart. If it finds evil there, it promptly hides away.'),
    (10162, 'sword', 'Its small horn hides a healing power. With a few rubs from this Pokémon''s horn, any slight wound you have will be healed.'),
    (10163, 'shield', 'Brave and prideful, this Pokémon dashes airily through the forest, its steps aided by the psychic power stored in the fur on its fetlocks.'),
    (10163, 'sword', 'Little can stand up to its Psycho Cut. Unleashed from this Pokémon''s horn, the move will punch a hole right through a thick metal sheet.'),
    (10164, 'legends-za', 'It lazes vacantly near water. If something bites its tail, it won''t even notice for a whole day.'),
    (10164, 'legends-za', 'Although this Pokémon is normally zoned out, its expression abruptly sharpens on occasion. The cause for this seems to lie in Slowpoke''s diet.'),
    (10164, 'scarlet', 'It gives off a stimulating scent because of chemicals that have seeped into its body from the spice that it eats as its staple food.'),
    (10164, 'scarlet', 'It is incredibly slow and dopey. It takes five seconds for it to feel pain when under attack.'),
    (10164, 'shield', 'Because Galarian Slowpoke eat the seeds of a plant that grows only in Galar, their tails have developed a spicy flavor.'),
    (10164, 'sword', 'Although this Pokémon is normally zoned out, its expression abruptly sharpens on occasion. The cause for this seems to lie in Slowpoke''s diet.'),
    (10164, 'violet', 'It is always vacantly lost in thought, but no one knows what it is thinking about. It is good at fishing with its tail.'),
    (10164, 'violet', 'It uses its tail to fish, but the scent of the spice emanating from its tail ensures its catches are always lacking.'),
    (10165, 'legends-za', 'A Shellder bite set off a chemical reaction with the spices inside Slowbro''s body, causing Slowbro to become a Poison-type Pokémon.'),
    (10165, 'legends-za', 'An attached Shellder won''t let go because of the tasty flavor that oozes out of Slowbro''s tail.'),
    (10165, 'scarlet', 'When a Slowpoke went hunting in the sea, its tail was bitten by a Shellder. That made it evolve into Slowbro.'),
    (10165, 'scarlet', 'Shellder seems blissful over the taste of Slowbro even though the toxins seeping from the bite have caused Shellder to faint.'),
    (10165, 'shield', 'If this Pokémon squeezes the tongue of the Shellder biting it, the Shellder will Shell Side Arm.'),
    (10165, 'sword', 'A Shellder bite set off a chemical reaction with the spices inside Slowbro''s body, causing Slowbro to become a Poison-type Pokémon.'),
    (10165, 'violet', 'Shellder bites down hard on Slowbro’s arm to suck out more poison. This seems to cause itching, so Slowbro occasionally lashes out.'),
    (10165, 'violet', 'If the tail-biting Shellder is thrown off in a harsh battle, this Pokémon reverts to being an ordinary Slowpoke.'),
    (10166, 'legends-za', 'Wielding a thick, heavy leek has strengthened its body. In battle, it bets everything on a single destructive blow.'),
    (10166, 'legends-za', 'The plant stalk it holds is also its beloved weapon. Farfetch''d can swing the stalk like a katana to cut all sorts of things.'),
    (10166, 'shield', 'The stalks of leeks are thicker and longer in the Galar region. Farfetch''d that adapted to these stalks took on a unique form.'),
    (10166, 'sword', 'The Farfetch''d of the Galar region are brave warriors, and they wield thick, tough leeks in battle.'),
    (10167, 'scarlet', 'Top-grade perfume is made using its internal poison gases by diluting them to the highest level.'),
    (10167, 'shield', 'Long ago, during a time when droves of factories fouled the air with pollution, Weezing changed into this form for some reason.'),
    (10167, 'sword', 'This Pokémon consumes particles that contaminate the air. Instead of leaving droppings, it expels clean air.'),
    (10167, 'violet', 'When it inhales poisonous gases from garbage, its body expands, and its insides smell much worse.'),
    (10168, 'legends-za', 'It uses its tap-dancing steps to rapidly chill the surrounding area and form a splendid stage made of ice.'),
    (10168, 'legends-za', 'It uses the mysterious power that emanates from its fingers to solidify the air around it into invisible walls.'),
    (10168, 'shield', 'It can radiate chilliness from the bottoms of its feet. It''ll spend the whole day tap-dancing on a frozen floor.'),
    (10168, 'sword', 'Its talent is tap-dancing. It can also manipulate temperatures to create a floor of ice, which this Pokémon can kick up to use as a barrier.'),
    (10169, 'shield', 'Known as Articuno, this Pokémon fires Freezing Glare that can {{status|Freeze|immobilize}} opponents as if they had been frozen solid.'),
    (10169, 'sword', 'Its feather-like blades are composed of psychic energy and can shear through thick iron sheets as if they were paper.'),
    (10170, 'shield', 'One kick from its powerful legs will pulverize a dump truck. Supposedly, this Pokémon runs through the mountains at over 180 mph.'),
    (10170, 'sword', 'When its feathers rub together, they produce a crackling sound like the zapping of electricity. That''s why this Pokémon is called Zapdos.'),
    (10171, 'shield', 'The sinister aura that blazes like molten fire around this Pokémon is what inspired the name Moltres.'),
    (10171, 'sword', 'This Pokémon''s sinister, flame-like aura will consume the spirit of any creature it hits. Victims become burned-out shadows of themselves.'),
    (10172, 'legends-za', 'It has incredible intellect and intuition. Whatever the situation, it remains calm and collected.'),
    (10172, 'legends-za', 'A combination of toxins and the shock of evolving has increased Shellder''s intelligence to the point that Shellder now controls Slowking.'),
    (10172, 'scarlet', 'It administers its potions to weakened Pokémon it sees. These potions are derived from poison and secreted from holes in Slowking’s horns.'),
    (10172, 'scarlet', 'When its head was bitten, toxins entered Slowpoke’s head and unlocked an extraordinary power.'),
    (10172, 'shield', 'While chanting strange spells, this Pokémon combines its internal toxins with what it''s eaten, creating strange potions.'),
    (10172, 'sword', 'A combination of toxins and the shock of evolving has increased Shellder''s intelligence to the point that Shellder now controls Slowking.'),
    (10172, 'violet', 'It has incredible intellect and intuition. Whatever the situation, it remains calm and collected.'),
    (10172, 'violet', 'It creates potions by mixing toxins with the food it’s eaten. Not even Slowking itself knows what effects the potions will have.'),
    (10173, 'shield', 'Sudden climate change wiped out this ancient kind of Corsola. This Pokémon absorbs others'' life-force through its branches.'),
    (10173, 'sword', 'Watch your step when wandering areas oceans once covered. What looks like a stone could be this Pokémon, and it will curse you if you kick it.'),
    (10174, 'shield', 'Thought to be the oldest form of Zigzagoon, it moves in zigzags and wreaks havoc upon its surroundings.'),
    (10174, 'sword', 'Its restlessness has it constantly running around. If it sees another Pokémon, it will purposely run into them in order to start a fight.'),
    (10175, 'shield', 'This very aggressive Pokémon will recklessly challenge opponents stronger than itself.'),
    (10175, 'sword', 'It uses its long tongue to taunt opponents. Once the opposition is enraged, this Pokémon hurls itself at the opponent, tackling them forcefully.'),
    (10176, 'shield', 'The colder they get, the more energetic they are. They freeze their breath to make snowballs, using them as ammo for playful snowball fights.'),
    (10176, 'sword', 'It lived in snowy areas for so long that its fire sac cooled off and atrophied. It now has an organ that generates cold instead.'),
    (10178, 'shield', 'Darmanitan takes this form when enraged. It won''t stop spewing flames until its rage has settled, even if its body starts to melt.'),
    (10178, 'sword', 'Anger has reignited its atrophied flame sac. This Pokémon spews fire everywhere as it rampages indiscriminately.'),
    (10179, 'legends-za', 'Each Yamask carries a mask representing the face it had when it was still human. Sometimes it gazes at the mask and weeps.'),
    (10179, 'legends-za', 'A cursed clay slab and a departed spirit have become bound together. This Pokémon swings its slab around with malicious intent.'),
    (10179, 'shield', 'It''s said that this Pokémon was formed when an ancient clay tablet was drawn to a vengeful spirit.'),
    (10179, 'sword', 'A clay slab with cursed engravings took possession of a Yamask. The slab is said to be absorbing the Yamask''s dark power.'),
    (10180, 'legends-za', 'Living in mud with a high iron content has given it a strong steel body.'),
    (10180, 'legends-za', 'It conceals itself in the mud of the seashore. Then it waits. When prey touch it, it delivers a jolt of electricity.'),
    (10180, 'shield', 'Its conspicuous lips lure prey in as it lies in wait in the mud. When prey gets close, Stunfisk clamps its jagged steel fins down on them.'),
    (10180, 'sword', 'Living in mud with a high iron content has given it a strong steel body.'),
    (10181, 'legends-za', 'This is Zygarde when about 10% of its pieces have been assembled. It leaps at its opponent''s chest and sinks its sharp fangs into them.'),
    (10181, 'moon', 'This is Zygarde''s form when about 10% of its cells have been gathered. It runs across the land at speeds greater than 60 mph.'),
    (10181, 'sun', 'Its sharp fangs make short work of finishing off its enemies, but it''s unable to maintain this body indefinitely. After a period of time, it falls apart.'),
    (10181, 'ultra-moon', 'Born when around 10% of Zygarde''s cells have been gathered from all over, this form is skilled in close-range combat.'),
    (10181, 'ultra-sun', 'This is Zygarde when about 10% of its pieces have been assembled. It leaps at its opponent''s chest and sinks its sharp fangs into them.'),
    (10182, 'scarlet', 'Cramorant is constantly on the hunt for food along riverbanks. It loves Arrokuda—when it finds them, it swallows them whole without a thought.'),
    (10182, 'shield', 'The slightest shock is sometimes enough to get this Pokémon to {{a|Gulp Missile|spit out the Arrokuda lodged in its throat}}.'),
    (10182, 'sword', 'Cramorant''s gluttony led it to try to swallow an Arrokuda whole, which in turn led to Cramorant getting an Arrokuda stuck in its throat.'),
    (10182, 'violet', 'Cramorant takes advantage of Arrokuda''s frantic thrashing to help spit Arrokuda out at high speed.'),
    (10183, 'scarlet', 'Cramorant instinctively swallow everything whole. They''re at their most formidable when they''re struggling to swallow overly large prey.'),
    (10183, 'scarlet', 'Its throat is clearly not wide enough to swallow a Pikachu, and yet Cramorant makes no move to release its catch.'),
    (10183, 'shield', 'The half-swallowed Pikachu is so startled that it isn''t struggling yet, but it''s still looking for a chance to strike back.'),
    (10183, 'sword', 'This Cramorant has accidentally gotten a Pikachu lodged in its gullet. Cramorant is choking a little, but it isn''t really bothered.'),
    (10183, 'violet', 'It''s an incredibly poor learner because it uses the bare minimum amount of energy for its brain. It focuses on battling instead.'),
    (10183, 'violet', 'With a Pikachu stuck in its throat, Cramorant can use Pikachu''s prickling electricity to give its opponents a shock.'),
    (10184, 'legends-za', 'On its chest is an electricity-generating organ. A sound like that of a bass guitar echoes all around while this organ produces electricity.'),
    (10184, 'scarlet', 'Many youths admire the way this Pokémon listlessly picks fights and keeps its cool no matter what opponent it faces.'),
    (10184, 'shield', 'It has an electrical organ on its chest. While generating electricity, it fills its surroundings with what sounds like the strumming of a bass guitar.'),
    (10184, 'sword', 'Capable of generating 15,000 volts of electricity, this Pokémon looks down on all that would challenge it.'),
    (10184, 'violet', 'As it gulps down stagnant water and generates electricity in its body, a sound like a rhythm played by a bass guitar reverberates all around.'),
    (10185, 'scarlet', 'The ice that was covering this Eiscue’s face has shattered. Eiscue emits cold air from the tip of its hair to protect its head, which is sensitive to heat.'),
    (10185, 'shield', 'The hair on its head connects to the surface of its brain. When this Pokémon has something on its mind, its hair chills the air around it.'),
    (10185, 'sword', 'The ice covering this Pokémon''s face has shattered, revealing a slightly worried expression that many people are enamored with.'),
    (10185, 'violet', 'Contrary to its looks, Eiscue is a poor swimmer. It creates ice balls at the tip of its single hair to lure prey in and fish them up.'),
    (10186, 'legends-za', 'These Pokémon are highly intelligent. They touch horns with their fellow Indeedee to share information with one another.'),
    (10186, 'scarlet', 'It dislikes conflict. If a fight occurs in its territory, it uses psychic power to throw things at the combatants in an effort to drive them away.'),
    (10186, 'shield', 'They diligently serve people and Pokémon so they can gather feelings of gratitude. The females are particularly good at babysitting.'),
    (10186, 'sword', 'These intelligent Pokémon touch horns with each other to share information between them.'),
    (10186, 'violet', 'In search of happy feelings—such as joy and gratitude—Indeedee bustles around, taking diligent care of people and other Pokémon.'),
    (10187, 'legends-za', 'Intense hunger drives it to extremes of violence, and the electricity in its cheek sacs has converted into a Dark-type energy.'),
    (10187, 'scarlet', 'Even after using up all its dark energy, this violent ruffian will keep running riot until its hunger is appeased.'),
    (10187, 'shield', 'Hunger hormones affect its temperament. Until its hunger is appeased, it gets up to all manner of evil deeds.'),
    (10187, 'sword', 'Intense hunger drives it to extremes of violence, and the electricity in its cheek sacs has converted into a {{type|Dark}} energy.'),
    (10187, 'violet', 'Hunger has disrupted this Pokémon''s hormonal balance. The {{type|Electric}} energy stored in its cheek sacs has turned into Dark-type energy.'),
    (10188, 'shield', 'Able to cut down anything with a single strike, it became known as the Fairy King''s Sword, and it inspired awe in friend and foe alike.'),
    (10188, 'sword', 'Now armed with a weapon it used in ancient times, this Pokémon needs only a single strike to fell even [[Gigantamax]] Pokémon.'),
    (10189, 'shield', 'Now that it''s equipped with its shield, it can shrug off impressive blows, including the attacks of [[Dynamax]] Pokémon.'),
    (10189, 'sword', 'Its ability to deflect any attack led to it being known as the Fighting Master''s Shield. It was feared and respected by all.'),
    (10190, 'shield', 'Infinite amounts of energy pour from this Pokémon''s enlarged core, warping the surrounding space-time.'),
    (10190, 'sword', 'As a result of [[Rose]]''s meddling, Eternatus absorbed all the energy in the Galar region. It''s now in a state of power overload.'),
    (10191, 'shield', 'This form of Urshifu is a strong believer in defeating foes by raining many blows down on them. Its strikes are nonstop, flowing like a river.'),
    (10191, 'sword', 'It''s believed that this Pokémon modeled its fighting style on the flow of a river—sometimes rapid, sometimes calm.'),
    (10192, 'shield', 'This Zarude''s special strength stems from its love and care for an orphaned human child that the Pokémon has raised since the child''s infancy.'),
    (10192, 'sword', 'This Zarude left its pack to raise {{OBP|Koko|M23|a human child}}. The cloth Zarude would wrap the child with has a comforting scent that calmed the child''s crying.'),
    (10193, 'shield', 'It''s said that this Pokémon once moved a large forest—and all the Pokémon living there—to a new location overnight.'),
    (10193, 'sword', 'According to lore, this Pokémon showed no mercy to those who got in its way, yet it would heal its opponents'' wounds after battle.'),
    (10194, 'shield', 'Legend says that by using its power to see all events from past to future, this Pokémon saved the creatures of a forest from a meteorite strike.'),
    (10194, 'sword', 'It''s said that Calyrex and a Spectrier that had bonded with it ran all across the Galar region to bring green to the wastelands.'),
    (10195, 'legends-za', 'After a rainy day, the flower on its back smells stronger. The scent attracts other Pokémon.'),
    (10195, 'scarlet', 'While it basks in the sun, it can convert the light into energy. As a result, it is more powerful in the summertime.'),
    (10195, 'shield', 'Huge amounts of pollen burst from it with the force of a volcanic eruption. Breathing in too much of the pollen can cause fainting.'),
    (10195, 'sword', 'In battle, this Pokémon swings around two thick vines. If these vines slammed into a 10-story building, they could easily topple it.'),
    (10195, 'violet', 'By spreading the broad petals of its flower and catching the sun’s rays, it fills its body with power.'),
    (10196, 'legends-za', 'Its wings can carry this Pokémon close to an altitude of 4,600 feet. It blows out fire at very high temperatures.'),
    (10196, 'scarlet', 'If Charizard becomes truly angered, the flame at the tip of its tail burns in a light blue shade.'),
    (10196, 'shield', 'The flame inside its body burns hotter than 3,600 degrees Fahrenheit. When Charizard roars, that temperature climbs even higher.'),
    (10196, 'sword', 'This colossal, flame-winged figure of a Charizard was brought about by Gigantamax energy.'),
    (10196, 'violet', 'It uses its wings to fly sky-high. The more experience it gains in battle, the greater the temperature at which its flames burn.'),
    (10197, 'legends-za', 'It crushes its foe under its heavy body to cause fainting. In a pinch, it will withdraw inside its shell.'),
    (10197, 'scarlet', 'It deliberately increases its body weight so it can withstand the recoil of the water jets it fires.'),
    (10197, 'shield', 'Water fired from this Pokémon''s central main cannon has enough power to blast a hole into a mountain.'),
    (10197, 'sword', 'It''s not very good at precision shooting. When attacking, it just fires its 31 cannons over and over and over.'),
    (10197, 'violet', 'It has jet nozzles on its shell. This impressive Pokémon uses these jets to charge toward foes with all the force of a rocket.'),
    (10198, 'shield', 'Once it has opponents trapped in a tornado that could blow away a 10-ton truck, it finishes them off with its poisonous scales.'),
    (10198, 'sword', 'Crystallized Gigantamax energy makes up this Pokémon''s blindingly bright and highly toxic scales.'),
    (10199, 'legends-za', 'It has small electric sacs on both its cheeks. When in a tough spot, this Pokémon discharges electricity.'),
    (10199, 'scarlet', 'When it is angered, it immediately discharges the energy stored in the pouches in its cheeks.'),
    (10199, 'shield', 'When it smashes its opponents with its bolt-shaped tail, it delivers a surge of electricity equivalent to a lightning strike.'),
    (10199, 'sword', 'Its Gigantamax power expanded, forming its supersized body and towering tail.'),
    (10199, 'violet', 'When several of these Pokémon gather, their electricity can build and cause lightning storms.'),
    (10200, 'legends-za', 'It loves anything that shines. It especially adores coins, which it will pick up and stash somewhere.'),
    (10200, 'scarlet', 'All it does is sleep during the daytime. At night, it patrols its territory with its eyes aglow.'),
    (10200, 'shield', 'Its body has grown incredibly long and the coin on its forehead has grown incredibly large—all thanks to Gigantamax power.'),
    (10200, 'sword', 'The pattern that has appeared on its giant coin is thought to be the key to unlocking the secrets of the Dynamax phenomenon.'),
    (10200, 'violet', 'It loves things that sparkle. When it sees a shiny object, the gold coin on its head shines, too.'),
    (10201, 'legends-za', 'It uses its four powerful arms to pin the limbs of its foe, then throws the victim over the horizon.'),
    (10201, 'shield', 'One of these Pokémon once used its immeasurable strength to lift a large ship that was in trouble. It then carried the ship to port.'),
    (10201, 'sword', 'The Gigantamax energy coursing through its arms makes its punches hit as hard as bomb blasts.'),
    (10202, 'legends-za', 'It hides in shadows. It is said that in rooms where Gengar is hiding, the temperature drops by nearly 10 degrees Fahrenheit.'),
    (10202, 'scarlet', 'To steal the life of its target, it slips into the prey’s shadow and silently waits for an opportunity.'),
    (10202, 'shield', 'It lays traps, hoping to steal the lives of those it catches. If you stand in front of its mouth, you''ll hear your loved ones'' voices calling out to you.'),
    (10202, 'sword', 'Rumor has it that its gigantic mouth leads not into its body, filled with cursed energy, but instead directly to the afterlife.'),
    (10202, 'violet', 'Hiding in people''s shadows at night, it absorbs their heat. The chill it causes makes the victims shake.'),
    (10203, 'shield', 'The bubbles it spews out are strongly alkaline. Any opponents hit by them will have their bodies quickly melted away.'),
    (10203, 'sword', 'The flow of Gigantamax energy has spurred this Pokémon''s left pincer to grow to an enormous size. That claw can pulverize anything.'),
    (10204, 'scarlet', 'It ferries people across the sea on its back. It may sing an enchanting cry if it is in a good mood.'),
    (10204, 'shield', 'It surrounds itself with a huge ring of gathered ice particles. It uses the ring to smash any icebergs that might impede its graceful swimming.'),
    (10204, 'sword', 'Over 5,000 people can ride on its shell at once. And it''s a very comfortable ride, without the slightest shaking or swaying.'),
    (10204, 'violet', 'Able to understand human speech and very intelligent, it loves to swim in the sea with people on its back.'),
    (10205, 'legends-za', 'Thanks to its unstable genetic makeup, this special Pokémon conceals many different possible evolutions.'),
    (10205, 'scarlet', 'Its ability to evolve into many forms allows it to adapt smoothly and perfectly to any environment.'),
    (10205, 'shield', 'Having gotten even friendlier and more innocent, Eevee tries to play with anyone around, only to end up crushing them with its immense body.'),
    (10205, 'sword', 'Gigantamax energy upped the fluffiness of the fur around Eevee''s neck. The fur will envelop a foe, capturing its body and captivating its mind.'),
    (10205, 'violet', 'Its genetic code is irregular. It may mutate if it is exposed to radiation from element stones.'),
    (10206, 'scarlet', 'This gluttonous Pokémon eats constantly, apart from when it''s asleep. It devours nearly 900 pounds of food per day.'),
    (10206, 'shield', 'Terrifyingly strong, this Pokémon is the size of a mountain—and moves about as much as one as well.'),
    (10206, 'sword', 'Gigantamax energy has affected stray seeds and even pebbles that got stuck to Snorlax, making them grow to a huge size.'),
    (10206, 'violet', 'Its stomach''s digestive juices can dissolve any kind of poison. Eating things off the ground doesn''t bother it at all.'),
    (10207, 'legends-za', 'Consuming garbage makes new kinds of poison gases and liquids inside their bodies.'),
    (10207, 'shield', 'It sprays toxic gas from its mouth and fingers. If the gas engulfs you, the toxins will seep in all the way down to your bones.'),
    (10207, 'sword', 'Due to Gigantamax energy, this Pokémon''s toxic gas has become much thicker, congealing into masses shaped like discarded toys.'),
    (10208, 'legends-za', 'It was worshipped long ago for its capacity to produce iron. For some reason, it has come back to life after 3,000 years.'),
    (10208, 'shield', 'It can send electric beams streaking out from the hole in its belly. The beams'' tremendous energy can vaporize an opponent in one shot.*'),
    (10208, 'sword', 'In a distant land, there are legends about a cyclopean giant. In fact, the giant was a Melmetal that was flooded with Gigantamax energy.*'),
    (10209, 'scarlet', 'Though it has a calm disposition, it won’t tolerate those who drum up discord. It strictly disciplines offenders until they learn their lesson.'),
    (10209, 'shield', 'Rillaboom has become one with its forest of drums and continues to lay down beats that shake all of Galar.'),
    (10209, 'sword', 'Gigantamax energy has caused Rillaboom''s stump to grow into a drum set that resembles a forest.'),
    (10209, 'violet', 'When one Rillaboom challenges another who leads a troop, a drumming battle commences. The victor becomes the troop’s new boss.'),
    (10210, 'scarlet', 'Although Cinderace loses its cool easily, it will battle flawlessly for a Trainer it trusts.'),
    (10210, 'shield', 'Gigantamax energy can sometimes cause the diameter of this Pokémon''s fireball to exceed 300 feet.'),
    (10210, 'sword', 'Infused with Cinderace''s fighting spirit, the G-Max Fireball never misses its targets and completely roasts opponents.'),
    (10210, 'violet', 'Using a ball that it made out of flames, Cinderace blinds its opponents and keeps them at bay.'),
    (10211, 'scarlet', 'It uses special lenses in its eyes to sense things about its opponents—like their body heat—then attacks once it identifies a weak spot.'),
    (10211, 'shield', 'It has excellent sniping skills. Shooting a berry rolling along over nine miles away is a piece of cake for this Pokémon.'),
    (10211, 'sword', 'Gigantamax Inteleon''s [[Water Gun]] move fires at Mach 7. As the Pokémon takes aim, it uses the crest on its head to gauge wind and temperature.'),
    (10211, 'violet', 'It may present itself as being well-mannered, but deep down, it still has a lazy side. It will slack off when its Trainer isn’t looking.'),
    (10212, 'legends-za', 'Its wings, now made of steel, are extremely tough. Even if it''s attacked mid-flight, Corviknight flies on mightily through the sky, unbothered.'),
    (10212, 'scarlet', 'Corviknight can’t serve as a taxi service in [[Paldea]] because the Pokémon’s Tinkatons will attack it while it flies, endangering the customer.'),
    (10212, 'shield', 'The eight feathers on its back are called blade birds, and they can launch off its body to attack foes independently.'),
    (10212, 'sword', 'Imbued with [[Gigantamax]] energy, its wings can whip up winds more forceful than any a hurricane could muster. The gusts blow everything away.'),
    (10212, 'violet', 'Although its wings have partly turned to steel and become heavy as a result, this Pokémon flies through the skies with ease.'),
    (10213, 'shield', 'If it were to utilize every last bit of its power, it could control the minds of every living being in its vicinity.'),
    (10213, 'sword', 'Its brain has grown to a gargantuan size, as has the rest of its body. This Pokémon''s intellect and psychic abilities are overpowering.'),
    (10214, 'scarlet', 'Its massive, jagged teeth can crush a boulder in a single bite. This Pokémon has an extremely vicious disposition.'),
    (10214, 'shield', 'In the Galar region, there''s a tale about this Pokémon chewing up a mountain and using the rubble to stop a flood.'),
    (10214, 'sword', 'It responded to Gigantamax energy by becoming bipedal. First it comes crashing down on foes, and then it finishes them off with its massive jaws.'),
    (10214, 'violet', 'Drednaw lurks along the shoreline. When prey come to drink water, Drednaw stretches its neck out and chomps down on them.'),
    (10215, 'scarlet', 'To intimidate its opponents, Coalossal will vigorously shake its body, scattering coal from its smoldering back.'),
    (10215, 'shield', 'When Galar was hit by a harsh cold wave, this Pokémon served as a giant heating stove and saved many lives.'),
    (10215, 'sword', 'Its body is a colossal stove. With Gigantamax energy stoking the fire, this Pokémon''s flame burns hotter than 3,600 degrees Fahrenheit.'),
    (10215, 'violet', 'It''s gentle usually but fearsome when angered. With a body that burns at over 2,700 degrees Fahrenheit, it crushes foes and turns them to ash.'),
    (10216, 'scarlet', 'It flutters around while seeking an opening in the opponent’s guard, then attacks by spitting acidic liquid strong enough to melt metal.'),
    (10216, 'shield', 'If it stretches its neck, the strong aroma of its nectar pours out. The scent is so sickeningly sweet that one whiff makes other Pokémon faint.'),
    (10216, 'sword', 'Under the influence of Gigantamax energy, it produces much more sweet nectar, and its shape has changed to resemble a giant apple.'),
    (10216, 'violet', 'It uses its own body fluid to repair its apple. Strong Flapple that have won many battles have apples that are clay colored all over.'),
    (10217, 'scarlet', 'It feeds mainly on sweet apples. It will also eat small bug Pokémon that are attracted by its sweet nectar.'),
    (10217, 'shield', 'Due to Gigantamax energy, this Pokémon''s nectar has thickened. The increased viscosity lets the nectar absorb more damage than before.'),
    (10217, 'sword', 'It blasts its opponents with massive amounts of sweet, sticky nectar, drowning them under the deluge.'),
    (10217, 'violet', 'When some Lechonk come along to lick the sweet nectar on Appletun''s back, Appletun will spew sticky nectar at them to drive them away.'),
    (10218, 'scarlet', 'It will expand its body as much as it can and then contract itself, blasting out sand with enough force to wash away a dump truck.'),
    (10218, 'shield', 'Sand swirls around its body with such speed and power that it could pulverize a skyscraper.'),
    (10218, 'sword', 'Its sand pouch has grown to tremendous proportions. More than 1,000,000 tons of sand now swirl around its body.'),
    (10218, 'violet', 'The sand it spews contains sharp, pointy gravel, which is actually just sand that Sandaconda''s saliva has hardened into irregular shapes.'),
    (10219, 'shield', 'Out of control after its own poison penetrated its brain, it tears across the land in a rampage, contaminating the earth with toxic sweat.'),
    (10219, 'sword', 'Its excessive electric energy is its weapon. This Pokémon can build up more electricity than any thundercloud.'),
    (10220, 'shield', 'The heat that comes off a Gigantamax Centiskorch may destabilize air currents. Sometimes it can even cause storms.'),
    (10220, 'sword', 'Gigantamax energy has evoked a rise in its body temperature, now reaching over 1,800 degrees Fahrenheit. Its heat waves incinerate its enemies.'),
    (10221, 'scarlet', 'Hatterene knocks out those that intrude in its home forest by blasting them with a beam, then slashing with claws enhanced by psychic power.'),
    (10221, 'shield', 'Beams like lightning shoot down from its tentacles. It''s known to some as the Raging Goddess.'),
    (10221, 'sword', 'This Pokémon can read the emotions of creatures over 30 miles away. The minute it senses hostility, it goes on the attack.'),
    (10221, 'violet', 'Beware of forests that show no signs of living creatures within. You may have wandered into Hatterene''s territory.'),
    (10222, 'scarlet', 'This Pokémon has complete control over its hair. Grimmsnarl normally keeps its hair wrapped around its body to support its muscles.'),
    (10222, 'shield', 'Gigantamax energy has caused more hair to sprout all over its body. With the added strength, it can jump over the world''s tallest building.'),
    (10222, 'sword', 'By transforming its leg hair, this Pokémon delivers power-packed drill kicks that can bore huge holes in Galar''s terrain.'),
    (10222, 'violet', 'It lives deep within the forest. Even after evolving into this splendid form, it hasn''t given up on its petty misdeeds and pranks.'),
    (10223, 'shield', 'It launches swarms of missiles, each made of cream and loaded with 100,000 kilocalories. Get hit by one of these, and your head will swim.'),
    (10223, 'sword', 'Cream pours endlessly from this Pokémon''s body. The cream stiffens when compressed by an impact. A harder impact results in harder cream.'),
    (10224, 'scarlet', 'This Pokémon was brought to Paldea long ago by people from a faraway land. It’s so strong that it can easily pull an airplane.'),
    (10224, 'shield', 'After this Pokémon has Gigantamaxed, its massive nose can utterly demolish large structures with a single smashing blow.'),
    (10224, 'sword', 'So much power is packed within its trunk that if it were to unleash that power, the resulting blast could level mountains and change the landscape.'),
    (10224, 'violet', 'Copperajah are prideful, cantankerous Pokémon. Specimens with vibrant green skin command the respect of others of their kind.'),
    (10225, 'scarlet', 'Duraludon’s body is comprised of a special metal that’s lightweight and scratch resistant. It’s also smooth, as though it was given a mirror finish.'),
    (10225, 'shield', 'The hardness of its cells is exceptional, even among Steel types. It also has a body structure that''s resistant to earthquakes.'),
    (10225, 'sword', 'It''s grown to resemble a skyscraper. Parts of its towering body glow due to a profusion of energy.'),
    (10225, 'violet', 'Its metal body is durable but prone to retaining heat. It vents this heat from the slits in its tail.'),
    (10226, 'shield', 'The energy released by this Pokémon''s fists forms shock waves that can blow away [[Dynamax]] Pokémon in just one hit.'),
    (10226, 'sword', 'People call it the embodiment of rage. It''s said that this Pokémon''s terrifying expression and shout will rid the world of malevolence.'),
    (10227, 'shield', 'All it takes is a glare from this Pokémon to take the lives of those with evil in their hearts—or so they say.'),
    (10227, 'sword', 'As it waits for the right moment to unleash its Gigantamax power, this Pokémon maintains a perfect one-legged stance. It won''t even twitch.'),
    (10229, 'legends-arceus', 'They patrol their territory in pairs. I believe the igneous rock components in the fur of this species are the result of volcanic activity in its habitat.'),
    (10229, 'scarlet', 'It has a brave and trustworthy nature. It fearlessly stands up to bigger and stronger foes.'),
    (10229, 'violet', 'It''s very friendly and faithful to people. It will try to repel enemies by barking and biting.'),
    (10230, 'legends-arceus', 'Snaps at its foes with fangs cloaked in blazing flame. Despite its bulk, it deftly feints every which way, leading opponents on a deceptively merry chase as it all but dances around them.'),
    (10230, 'scarlet', 'An ancient picture scroll shows that people were captivated by its movement as it ran through prairies.'),
    (10230, 'violet', 'Its magnificent bark conveys a sense of majesty. Anyone hearing it can''t help but grovel before it.'),
    (10231, 'legends-arceus', 'An enigmatic Pokémon that happens to bear a resemblance to a Poké Ball. When excited, it discharges the electric current it has stored in its belly, then lets out a great, uproarious laugh.'),
    (10231, 'scarlet', 'It rolls to move. If the ground is uneven, a sudden jolt from hitting a bump can cause it to explode.'),
    (10231, 'violet', 'It''s usually found in power plants. Easily mistaken for a Poké Ball, it has zapped many people.'),
    (10232, 'legends-arceus', 'The tissue on the surface of its body is curiously similar in composition to an [[Apricorn]]. When irritated, this Pokémon lets loose an electric current equal to 20 lightning bolts.'),
    (10232, 'scarlet', 'The more energy it charges up, the faster it gets. But this also makes it more likely to explode.'),
    (10232, 'violet', 'It explodes in response to even minor stimuli. It is feared, with the nickname of the Bomb Ball.'),
    (10233, 'legends-arceus', 'Said to purify lost, forsaken souls with its flames and guide them to the afterlife. I believe its form has been influenced by the energy of the sacred mountain towering at Hisui''s center.'),
    (10233, 'scarlet', 'It has a secret, devastating move. It rubs its blazing fur to cause huge explosions.'),
    (10233, 'violet', 'If its rage peaks, it becomes so hot that anything that touches it will instantly go up in flames.'),
    (10234, 'legends-arceus', 'Fishers detest this troublesome Pokémon because it sprays poison from its spines, getting it everywhere. A different form of Qwilfish lives in other regions.'),
    (10234, 'legends-za', 'This Pokémon eats toxic minerals to build up poison within itself. Get jabbed by it, and you''ll face three days and three nights of misery.'),
    (10234, 'legends-za', 'To fire off the poison spikes covering its body, it inflates itself by sucking in over 2.6 gallons of water all at once.'),
    (10234, 'scarlet', 'Be cautious if this Pokémon starts sucking in water—it will soon attack by scattering the toxic spikes that grow all over its body.'),
    (10234, 'scarlet', 'It lives just offshore in cold parts of the world. Its poisonous spikes are thicker and shorter than those of other regions’ Qwilfish.'),
    (10234, 'violet', 'Experienced fishers say they try to catch Qwilfish in the brief moment that these Pokémon become defenseless just after launching poisonous spikes.'),
    (10234, 'violet', 'It absorbs toxins from the food it eats. The distinct purple spikes on its body are evidence of its potent poison.'),
    (10235, 'legends-arceus', 'Its sturdy, curved claws are ideal for traversing precipitous cliffs. From the tips of these claws drips a venom that infiltrates the nerves of any prey caught in Sneasel''s grasp.'),
    (10235, 'scarlet', 'This cunning Pokémon hides under the cover of darkness, waiting to attack its prey.'),
    (10235, 'violet', 'This is a smart and sneaky Pokémon. A pair may work together to steal eggs by having one lure the parents away.'),
    (10236, 'legends-arceus', 'Hard of heart and deft of blade, this rare form of Samurott is a product of the Pokémon''s evolution in the region of [[Hisui]]. Its turbulent blows crash into foes like ceaseless pounding waves.'),
    (10236, 'scarlet', 'A master of a sword-drawing art called iaijutsu, Samurott settles its battles with a single swing of either large sword sheathed in its foreleg armor.'),
    (10236, 'violet', 'Samurott leads its group strictly. Those who do not follow its rules receive a merciless thrashing.'),
    (10237, 'legends-arceus', 'I suspect that its well-developed legs are the result of a life spent on mountains covered in deep snow. The scent it exudes from its flower crown heartens those in proximity.'),
    (10237, 'scarlet', 'The fragrance of the garland on its head has a relaxing effect, but taking care of it is very difficult.'),
    (10237, 'violet', 'No matter how much time and money is spent raising it, its flowers are the most beautiful when they bloom in the wild.'),
    (10238, 'legends-arceus', 'A once-departed soul, returned to life in Hisui. Derives power from resentment, which rises as energy atop its head and takes on the forms of foes. In this way, Zorua vents lingering malice.'),
    (10238, 'scarlet', 'It changes into the forms of others to surprise them. Apparently, it often transforms into a silent child.'),
    (10238, 'violet', 'To protect themselves from danger, they hide their true identities by transforming into people and Pokémon.'),
    (10239, 'legends-arceus', 'With its disheveled white fur, it looks like an embodiment of death. Heedless of its own safety, Zoroark attacks its nemeses with a bitter energy so intense, it lacerates Zoroark''s own body.'),
    (10239, 'scarlet', 'Stories say those who tried to catch Zoroark were trapped in an illusion and punished.'),
    (10239, 'violet', 'Each has the ability to fool a large group of people simultaneously. They protect their lair with illusory scenery.'),
    (10240, 'legends-arceus', 'Screaming a bloodcurdling battle cry, this huge and ferocious bird Pokémon goes out on the hunt. It blasts lakes with shock waves, then scoops up any prey that float to the water''s surface.'),
    (10240, 'scarlet', 'The more scars they have, the more respect these brave soldiers of the sky get from their peers.'),
    (10240, 'violet', 'For the sake of its friends, this brave warrior of the sky will not stop battling, even if injured.'),
    (10241, 'legends-arceus', 'A creature given to melancholy. I suspect its metallic shell developed as a result of the mucus on its skin reacting with the iron in Hisui''s water.'),
    (10241, 'legends-za', 'Its four horns are a high-performance radar system. It uses them to sense sounds and smells, rather than using ears or a nose.'),
    (10241, 'legends-za', 'The iron in Sliggoo''s drinking water turned its shell metallic. The Pokémon doesn''t come out of its shell on sunny days.'),
    (10241, 'scarlet', 'The swirly protrusion on its back is filled with all its vital organs, such as its brain and heart.'),
    (10241, 'violet', 'When Sliggoo senses danger, the mucus coating its entire body becomes more concentrated— it''ll dissolve anything.'),
    (10242, 'legends-arceus', 'Able to freely control the hardness of its metallic shell. It loathes solitude and is extremely clingy—it will fume and run riot if those dearest to it ever leave its side.'),
    (10242, 'legends-za', 'If anything bad happens to it, Goodra retreats into its shell and bounces around like a rubber ball, knocking down trees and boring into mountains.'),
    (10242, 'legends-za', 'This very friendly dragon Pokémon will hug its beloved Trainer, leaving that Trainer covered in sticky slime.'),
    (10242, 'scarlet', 'It loves the rain. This mellow Pokémon can be seen walking around on the plains and in the mountains on rainy days.'),
    (10242, 'violet', 'This Pokémon is uncontrollable when enraged. It rampages on and on, lashing its tail with enough power to send a dump truck flying.'),
    (10243, 'legends-arceus', 'The armor of ice covering its lower jaw puts steel to shame and can shatter rocks with ease. This Pokémon barrels along steep mountain paths, cleaving through the deep snow.'),
    (10243, 'legends-za', 'With its icy jaw, it swiftly plows across snowy fields and mountains, in search of nutritious vegetables people have stored in the snow.'),
    (10243, 'legends-za', 'Its ice-covered body is as hard as steel. Its enormous frame crushes anything that stands in its way.'),
    (10243, 'scarlet', 'As Avalugg walks along with Bergmite on its back, it comes across pods of Cetitan. It lets them pass to avoid conflict.'),
    (10243, 'violet', 'This Pokémon uses its massive icy body to flatten anything that gets in its way. When it''s floating out on the ocean, it looks exactly like drift ice.'),
    (10244, 'legends-arceus', 'The air stored inside the rachises of Decidueye''s feathers insulates the Pokémon against [[Hisui]]''s extreme cold. This is firm proof that evolution can be influenced by environment.'),
    (10244, 'scarlet', 'It cunningly conceals arrow quills in its wings. It launches these quills with such precision that they can pierce a pebble at over a hundred yards.'),
    (10244, 'violet', 'It nocks its arrow quills and looses them at opponents. When it needs to hit, it pulls the vines on its hood to narrow its view and focus.'),
    (10245, 'legends-arceus', 'Radiant light caused Dialga to take on a form bearing a striking resemblance to Arceus. Dialga now wields such colossal strength that one must conclude this is its true form.'),
    (10246, 'legends-arceus', 'It soars across the sky in a form that greatly resembles the creator of all things. Perhaps this imitation of appearance is Palkia''s strategy for gaining Arceus''s powers.'),
    (10247, 'legends-arceus', 'Though it differs from other Basculin in several respects, including demeanor—this one is gentle—[[Professor Laventon|I]] have categorized it as a [[regional form]] given the vast array of shared qualities.'),
    (10247, 'scarlet', 'They live in frigid seas, forming schools and sharing food among themselves. When the time comes, they return to the river they were born in.'),
    (10247, 'violet', 'Its ecology is starkly different from that of other Basculin, so theories that it''s a totally different species have gained traction in recent years.'),
    (10248, 'scarlet', 'The souls of its comrades cloak its body and propel it effortlessly through even raging rapids.'),
    (10248, 'violet', 'It can afflict a target with terrifying illusions that are under its control. The deeper the sadness in its friends'' souls, the paler Basculegion becomes.'),
    (10249, 'legends-arceus', 'A different guise from its feminine humanoid form. From the clouds, it descends upon those who treat any form of life with disrespect and metes out wrathful, ruthless punishment.'),
    (10250, 'scarlet', 'This Pokémon has a muscular body and excels at close-quarters combat. It uses its short horns to strike the opponent’s weak spots.'),
    (10250, 'violet', 'This kind of Tauros, known as the Combat Breed, is distinguished by its thick, powerful muscles and its fierce disposition.'),
    (10251, 'scarlet', 'When heated by fire energy, its horns can get hotter than 1,800 degrees Fahrenheit. Those gored by them will suffer both wounds and burns.'),
    (10251, 'violet', 'People call this kind of Tauros the Blaze Breed due to the hot air it snorts from its nostrils. Its three tails are intertwined.'),
    (10252, 'scarlet', 'This Pokémon blasts water from holes on the tips of its horns—the high-pressure jets pierce right through Tauros’s enemies.'),
    (10252, 'violet', 'It swims by jetting water from its horns. The most notable characteristic of the Aqua Breed is its high body fat, which allows it to float easily.'),
    (10253, 'scarlet', 'After losing a territorial struggle, Wooper began living on land. The Pokémon changed over time, developing a poisonous film to protect its body.'),
    (10253, 'violet', 'It''s dangerous for Wooper to travel alone. They line up in groups of three or four and help each other as they walk around the wetlands.'),
    (10254, 'scarlet', 'This Pokémon sends a flowerlike scent wafting about. Well-developed muscles in its legs allow it to leap more than 16 feet with no trouble at all.'),
    (10254, 'violet', 'This is a meticulous Pokémon that likes to keep things tidy. It shrouds itself in a floral aroma that soothes the Pokémon around it.'),
    (10255, 'scarlet', 'The gentle Dudunsparce will put Pokémon that wander into its nest onto its back and carry them to the entrance.'),
    (10255, 'scarlet', 'This Pokémon uses its hard tail to make its nest by boring holes into bedrock deep underground. The nest can reach lengths of over six miles.'),
    (10255, 'violet', 'A recent study uncovered that the number of segments a Dudunsparce’s body has is determined by the Pokémon’s genes.'),
    (10255, 'violet', 'It drives enemies out of its nest by sucking in enough air to fill its long, narrow lungs, then releasing the air in an intense blast.'),
    (10256, 'scarlet', 'This Pokémon''s ancient genes have awakened. It is now so extraordinarily strong that it can easily lift a cruise ship with one fin.'),
    (10256, 'violet', 'This hero of the ocean swims at a speed of 50 knots and saves drowning [[Human|people]] and Pokémon.'),
    (10257, 'scarlet', 'The two little ones just appeared one day. The group might be a family of related Pokémon, but nobody knows for sure.'),
    (10257, 'scarlet', 'They build huge nests with many rooms that are used for different purposes, such as eating and sleeping.'),
    (10257, 'violet', 'The little one just appeared one day. They all live together like a family, but the relationship between the three is still unclear.'),
    (10257, 'violet', 'The larger pair protects the little ones during {{pkmn|battle}}s. When facing strong opponents, the whole group will join the fight.'),
    (10258, 'legends-za', 'Even if swallowed by a foe, Tatsugiri will try to make its escape through various means, such as by inflating its throat sac.'),
    (10258, 'scarlet', 'This species'' differing colors and patterns are apparently the result of Tatsugiri changing itself to suit the preferences of the prey it lures in.'),
    (10258, 'violet', 'This Pokémon tricks its opponents by playing dead. It is small and weak, but it uses its smarts to survive.'),
    (10259, 'legends-za', 'Tatsugiri assesses situations using its sharp intellect. If it determines there is no hope of winning, it flees as fast as it can.'),
    (10259, 'scarlet', 'Bird Pokémon are its main prey. This Pokémon knows it''s weak, so it hunts with a partner.'),
    (10259, 'violet', 'It''s one of the most intelligent dragon Pokémon. It camouflages itself by inflating its throat sac.'),
    (10260, 'legends-za', 'Squawkabilly with blue plumage are the second most populous variety after their green counterparts, which they view as foes.'),
    (10260, 'scarlet', 'The largest of their flocks can contain more than 50 individuals. They fly around towns and forests, searching for food and making a racket.'),
    (10260, 'violet', 'Blue-feathered Squawkabilly view their green-feathered counterparts as rivals, since the latter make up the largest, most powerful groups.'),
    (10261, 'legends-za', 'Squawkabilly with yellow plumage grew increasingly aggressive in order to be taken seriously by the more populous varieties.'),
    (10261, 'scarlet', 'These Squawkabilly are hotheaded, and their fighting style is vicious. They’ll leap within reach of their foes to engage in close combat.'),
    (10261, 'violet', 'The yellow Squawkabilly are especially fierce. They''ve even been known to drive other bird Pokémon out of town.'),
    (10262, 'legends-za', 'This is the least populous variety of Squawkabilly. They don''t like conflict, but when they have to fight, they do so valiantly and resolutely.'),
    (10262, 'scarlet', 'This Pokémon dislikes being alone. It has a strong sense of community and survives by cooperating with allies.'),
    (10262, 'violet', 'Though these Squawkabilly are the fewest in number, they have no trouble living in towns since they blend in with the white buildings.'),
    (10263, 'legends-za', 'If it senses it''s about to be found by a human or a Pokémon, Gimmighoul will turn invisible to protect itself, leaving only its coin visible.'),
    (10263, 'scarlet', 'This Pokémon was born from passion that seeped into a coin. It wanders, apparently seeking to return to the treasure chest it once inhabited.'),
    (10263, 'violet', 'It wanders around, carrying an old coin on its back. It survives by draining the life-force from humans who try to pick up its coin.'),
    (10272, 'scarlet', 'It crossed the sea and drifted ashore in [[Kitakami|a new land]]. Surviving in this place led it to take on a unique appearance and gain special powers.'),
    (10272, 'violet', 'This special Ursaluna can see in the dark with its left eye and protects itself with mud that is as hard as iron.'),
    (10273, 'scarlet', 'This form excels in both attack and defense. It ceaselessly unleashes moves like a spring gushes water.'),
    (10273, 'violet', 'In this form, it draws on the power of water. It attacks unrelentingly with kicks and ivy strikes.'),
    (10274, 'scarlet', 'This form is the most aggressive, bombarding enemies with the intensity of flames blazing within a hearth.'),
    (10274, 'violet', 'In this form, it draws on the power of fire. It spears its enemies with thorn-covered ivy.'),
    (10275, 'scarlet', 'This form has excellent defenses, absorbing impacts solidly like the cornerstones that support houses.'),
    (10275, 'violet', 'In this form, it draws on the power of stone. Its body is rock-solid, protecting it from all manner of attacks.'),
    (10276, 'scarlet', 'Upon sensing danger, it prepares itself for {{pkmn|battle}} by creating a sturdy shell of crystallized [[Terastal energy]].'),
    (10276, 'violet', 'The shell is made of crystallized Terastal energy. When struck by a move, this shell absorbs the [[move]]''s energy and transfers it to Terapagos.'),
    (10277, 'scarlet', 'In this form, Terapagos resembles the world as the ancients saw it, and its Terastal energy is abnormally amplified.'),
    (10277, 'violet', 'An old expedition [[Scarlet Book|jou]][[Violet Book|rnal]] describes the sight of this Pokémon buried in the depths of the earth as resembling a planet floating in space.'),
    (10278, 'legends-za', 'It flies by using the power of moonlight to control gravity within a radius of over 32 feet around it.'),
    (10279, 'legends-za', 'The volume of this Pokémon''s acid has increased due to Mega Evolution, filling its mouth. If it''s not careful, the acid will overflow and spill out.'),
    (10280, 'legends-za', 'Its movements have become more humanlike. Whether it''s simply trying to communicate or wants to supplant humanity is unclear.'),
    (10281, 'legends-za', 'Mega Evolution has excessively powered up this Pokémon''s feelings of kindness. It finishes off its opponents with mercy in its heart.'),
    (10282, 'legends-za', 'This Pokémon can fire a tremendously powerful Solar Beam from its four flowers. Another name for this is {{a|Mega Sol}} Cannon.'),
    (10283, 'legends-za', 'With its arms and hoodlike fin, this Pokémon forms a gigantic set of jaws with a bite 10 times as powerful as Mega Feraligatr''s actual jaws.'),
    (10284, 'legends-za', 'It flies faster than the speed of sound. After whipping up shock waves to send enemies flying, it finishes them off with its talons.'),
    (10285, 'legends-za', 'This Pokémon can use eerie cold air imbued with ghost energy to freeze even insubstantial things, such as flames or the wind.'),
    (10286, 'legends-za', 'Brandishing a blazing flame shaped like a serpentine spear, it rushes in to rescue its imperiled allies.'),
    (10287, 'legends-za', 'If this Pokémon brings its arms and head together to form a streamlined shape and spins at high speeds, it can destroy anything.'),
    (10288, 'legends-za', 'Its deadly venom gives off a faint glow. The venom affects Scolipede''s mind, honing its viciousness.'),
    (10289, 'legends-za', 'Mega Evolution has caused Scrafty''s shed skin to turn white, growing tough and supple. Of course, this Pokémon is still as feisty as ever.'),
    (10290, 'legends-za', 'It now generates 10 times the electricity it did before Mega Evolving. It discharges this electricity from its false Eelektrik, which are made of mucus.'),
    (10291, 'legends-za', 'One of its eyes is a window linking our world with the afterlife. This Pokémon draws in hatred and converts it into power.'),
    (10292, 'legends-za', 'It has fortified armor and a will to defend at all costs. Both are absurdly strong.'),
    (10293, 'legends-za', 'It wields flaming branches to dazzle its opponents before incinerating them with a huge fireball.'),
    (10294, 'legends-za', 'This Pokémon spins a giant shuriken at high speed to make it float, then clings to it upside down to catch opponents unawares.'),
    (10295, 'legends-za', 'This Pokémon spews flames hotter than 18,000 degrees Fahrenheit. It swings around its grand, blazing mane as it protects its allies.'),
    (10296, 'legends-za', 'The Eternal Flower has absorbed all the energy from Mega Evolution. The flower now attacks enemies on its own.'),
    (10297, 'legends-za', 'It uses its colorful lights to overwrite the personalities and memories of others—and to control them.'),
    (10298, 'legends-za', 'It uses its many arms to toy with its opponents. This keeps the head extremely busy.'),
    (10299, 'legends-za', 'It spits a liquid that causes the regenerative power of cells to run wild. The liquid is deadly poison to everything other than itself.'),
    (10300, 'legends-za', 'Mega Evolution has pumped up all its muscles. Hawlucha flexes to show off its strength.'),
    (10301, 'legends-za', 'In response to people''s emotions during an unprecedented crisis, Zygarde Mega Evolves and calms the situation with its unmatched power.'),
    (10302, 'legends-za', 'Drampa''s cells have been invigorated, allowing it to regain its youth. It manipulates the atmosphere to summon storms.'),
    (10303, 'legends-za', 'Mega Falinks has taken on the ultimate battle formation, which can be achieved only if the troopers and brass have the strongest of bonds.'),
    (10304, 'legends-za', 'It resembles an X as it flies through the air with 50 million volts of electricity sparking from its ears and forked tail.'),
    (10305, 'legends-za', 'It fires bolts of electricity from the tip of its tail and from the spiky tufts of fur growing out of its temples. This electricity forms the letter Y.'),
    (10306, 'legends-za', 'It vibrates its entire body to attack in all directions using sound waves. Any who hear the vibrations get so confused, they forget who they are.'),
    (10307, 'legends-za', 'Using fur that it has made into sharp, clawlike shapes, it cuts down foes with a single blow. This is an act of kindness to keep them from suffering.'),
    (10308, 'legends-za', 'Mega Staraptor is a top-class flier. It can easily soar through the sky while gripping a Steelix that weighs more than 880 lbs.'),
    (10309, 'legends-za', 'Garchomp has gained a new Mega-Evolved form. It flies around foes at Mach speed and cuts them to shreds with its sinister wing claws.'),
    (10310, 'legends-za', 'By completely cloaking itself in its aura, Mega Lucario Z can parry all manner of attacks, battling as if it were gracefully dancing.'),
    (10311, 'legends-za', 'It''s said that if it goes all out, it can heat its body up to temperatures over 1.8 million degrees Fahrenheit. This heat keeps enemies at bay.'),
    (10312, 'legends-za', 'Its dark power blocks out the sun, plunging the surrounding area into darkness. There is no escaping its evil eye.'),
    (10313, 'legends-za', 'The energy within Golurk has been stimulated by Mega Evolution. The Pokémon could explode at any moment.'),
    (10315, 'legends-za', 'It can pulverize reinforced concrete with a light swing of one of its fists, each of which is covered in a thick layer of ice.'),
    (10316, 'legends-za', 'It uses four of its arms to fiercely assail its foes. Once they''ve been pushed to the brink of defeat, it finishes them off with the arms it kept hidden.'),
    (10317, 'legends-za', 'This is Magearna once a previously hidden mode activates. The emotions Magearna had begun to feel now hide away as it fells foe after foe.'),
    (10318, 'legends-za', 'A mechanism to remove Magearna''s limitations has lain secretly within Magearna for 500 years. This mechanism is triggered by a Mega Stone.'),
    (10319, 'legends-za', 'It stores up 10 lightning strikes'' worth of electricity. When it stops limiting itself, it''s in the strongest class of electric Pokémon.'),
    (10320, 'legends-za', 'Mega Evolution has dialed up this Pokémon''s spiciness. It swings its "necktie" around to wallop its foes.'),
    (10321, 'legends-za', 'Glimmora''s petals—now larger and separated from its main body—rotate around it to provide defense while scattering poisonous fragments.'),
    (10322, 'legends-za', 'Tatsugiri''s brain has been invigorated by [[Mega Evolution]], making it even wilier. It can create and command copies of itself.'),
    (10322, 'legends-za', 'Tatsugiri will battle furiously among themselves to determine which of them will get to partner with a particular Dondozo.'),
    (10322, 'scarlet', 'This is a small dragon Pokémon. It lives inside the mouth of Dondozo to protect itself from enemies on the outside.'),
    (10322, 'violet', 'Tatsugiri is an extremely cunning Pokémon. It feigns weakness to lure in prey, then orders its partner to attack.'),
    (10323, 'legends-za', 'It solidifies the energy of Mega Evolution, building up an overflowing pile to launch as projectiles. These projectiles explode on contact.'),
    (10324, 'legends-za', 'Using the energy of Mega Evolution, it creates a dish to ride upon, allowing it to move with total freedom-even through the air.'),
    (10325, 'legends-za', 'Baxcalibur''s dorsal blade has grown even more massive thanks to Mega Evolution. This Pokémon fires beams from the hilt at its solar plexus.')
